    <node id="&quot;KLYUYERA SP.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dominant bacterial species found in the gut microbiome of T. molitor larvae fed polypropylene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-92bf00317a1d0d9ffccab121661a18a8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENTEROBACTER SP.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Enterobacter sp. is a bacterium isolated from the gut of greater wax moths that aids in polyethylene degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacter sp. is a genus isolated from Indian mealmoth larvae with LDPE-degradation capabilities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Isolated from the gut of greater wax moth, potentially involved in PE degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacter sp. is a genus of bacteria linked to polypropylene diets in the gut microbiome of Zophobas atratus larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacter sp. is another gut microbe linked to the PP-fed microbiome of Z. atratus larvae, possibly involved in PP degradation."</data>
