    <node id="&quot;EXIGUOBACTERIUM SP. STRAIN YT2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A bacterial strain capable of converting ingested polystyrene into CO2 and biomass."&lt;SEP&gt;"Isolated from yellow mealworms, contributing to PS degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exiguobacterium sp. strain YT2 is a bacterial strain capable of degrading PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exiguobacterium sp. strain YT2 is a bacterium isolated from Tenebrio molitor larvae gut that degrades polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exiguobacterium sp. strain YT2 is a bacterial isolate from mealworms capable of significant polystyrene degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exiguobacterium sp. strain YT2 is a bacterial strain isolated from mealworm guts that demonstrates the ability to degrade PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exiguobacterium sp. strain YT2 is a PS-degrading bacterial strain isolated from the intestine of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exiguobacterium sp. strain YT2 is a PS-degrading bacterial strain isolated from the guts of mealworms, capable of forming biofilm on PS surfaces."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exiguobacterium sp. strain YT2, isolated from yellow mealworms, participates in polystyrene degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exiguobacterium sp. strain YT2 is a microorganism found in the digestive tract of Tenebrio molitor that enables the degradation of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exiguobacterium sp. strain YT2 is a bacterial strain isolated from the gut of mealworms that plays a significant role in degrading polystyrene."</data>
