    <node id="&quot;PSEUDOMONAS SP.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A bacterial species isolated from the gut of superworms capable of biodegrading polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Isolated from superworms, involved in PS degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas sp. refers to a bacterial species isolated from the gut of superworms, capable of degrading polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas sp. is a genus of gram-negative bacteria capable of degrading polystyrene, isolated from the gut of superworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas sp. is a bacterial species belonging to the Pseudomonadaceae family, found in the gut microbiome of T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas sp. is a bacterium involved in the enzymatic transformation of styrene into phenylacetate, contributing to the biological degradation of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas sp. refers to a genus of gram-negative bacteria capable of degrading various types of plastics, including polyurethane foams."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas sp. is a bacterial species capable of degrading polystyrene, as observed in the gut of superworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas sp. is a genus of bacteria isolated from the gut of superworms that contributes to the biodegradation of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas sp., isolated from superworms, contributes to polystyrene degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas sp. is a bacterial species capable of degrading PE wax in sterilized compost conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas sp. isolated from the gut of superworms contributes to the biodegradation of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas sp. refers to various species within the Pseudomonas genus that contribute to polystyrene degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas sp. refers to a genus of gram-negative bacteria capable of degrading various synthetic polymers, including plastics."</data>
