hunk-158317f8eba5f6198135df044d385935&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-beb3c133fa4d5851f0feff55507c6874&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51f749234fed052c982d79f81b93cc29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd3cec3addc1bee202783dff1583ba54</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;G. MELLONELLA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"G. mellonella is a genus of larvae that showed preference for certain types of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"G. mellonella, or greater waxworms, were studied for their gut microbiome changes upon PE feeding."&lt;SEP&gt;"G. mellonella is a species of moth whose larvae were studied for their ability to degrade plastics and beeswax."&lt;SEP&gt;"G. mellonella larvae are capable of degrading plastics such as polystyrene through enzymatic pathways."&lt;SEP&gt;"G. mellonella is an insect involved in the biodegradation of plastics, similar to T. molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"G. mellonella is a species of larvae used in experiments involving the degradation of Styrofoam, with its gut microbial community analyzed."&lt;SEP&gt;"G. mellonella refers to the greater wax moth larvae used in the study for gut microbial community analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"G. mellonella is a species involved in LDPE degradation, similar to other larvae species."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-158317f8eba5f6198135df044d385935&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dfcb3f2424bd027b5888293a0d01d3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31f2ee9a779791fef2da810debc12720&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79c11bccb4ef9bd152bdae9b5c2c5c8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5a94048d4a1499a73a50e74a59245e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a3e42eecd3967a9e53cfadc926363ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6dce72fccb3df94ec407aba3d4df8eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93d5b1c190fdca6b5e456b1513515be4</data>
    </node>
