    <node id="&quot;ZOPHOBAS ATRATUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">**Zophobas atratus**, commonly referred to as superworms, are the larvae of a species of darkling beetle belonging to the family Tenebrionidae. These insects have garnered significant attention due to their unique ability to consume and biodegrade various types of plastics, including polystyrene (PS), polypropylene (PP), low-density polyethylene (PE), polyethylene terephthalate (PET), and PVC. Their plastic-degrading capability is attributed to gut-microbe-dependent mechanisms, where bacteria residing in their digestive systems play a crucial role in breaking down the polymers.

Superworms exhibit the ability to mineralize polystyrene and contribute to the depolymerization of other plastics such as PE and PP. Studies have demonstrated that their survival rates during experiments involving plastic consumption are generally high, though they may be lower compared to other species like *Tenebrio molitor* when fed exclusively on certain plastics like PP. When provided with additional nutrients like wheat bran, their consumption and degradation of polystyrene increase, enhancing their effectiveness in plastic waste management.

The biodegradation process involves both enzymatic activities and oxidative processes. The larvae can degrade polystyrene through the combined effect of reactive oxygen species (ROS) and extracellular oxidase from gut microbes. Additionally, they contribute to the biodegradation of polypropylene via gut-microbe-dependent depolymerization. During this process, distinct changes occur in their gut microbiome, further supporting their role in plastic degradation.

**Zophobas atratus** has been extensively studied in experiments aimed at understanding and enhancing the biodegradation of synthetic polymers. Their potential applications extend beyond environmental remediation, as they have also been evaluated for their nutritional content. While **Zophobas atratus** shares some similarities with the *Tenebrio* species, it is distinct in its larval form and plastic-degrading capabilities. Overall, **Zophobas atratus** represents an important species in ongoing research into sustainable solutions for plastic waste management, demonstrating both enzymatic activities within their gut microbiota and the potential for contributing to the biodegradation of various plastics. They are widely used in studies involving microbial biodegradation and microbiome investigations, particularly focusing on plastic degradation.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-779ca6b59945309c6bf5040c9fb474ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-104d99248e84b2776ff5ca17c285a7bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d068dbad68e3ecd909a551f43f82b893&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df045e015825dac8935c9c6d8a402cda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-260d8c268067de32e5ac98d66ab70a6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-939f85d52d9301668deab282264e5fd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-032b3b0fe0366e6e76e86abf8c48d200&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-550dde13ffd2abcf536dd87f7d4c1b40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30a7209d626a6319ba5600bea7f27299&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfd8d6b8105d9868a4ffadf5779d0df5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec1a5b2913dd6782ff1e0533dd57325f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e127a4930b6154498b93c2e94f2b7c20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-566d464a7713ef7ca266f3d5f24a1a59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0881f766e34a5d97ee711cd2edd793f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-551c06d3562ff01465354b3a954b1145&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4265fd894f71345b4ef09c26e6adbda5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-422e833d3381bd5fd0b5a3d63d9047f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e3ac1a351ece6e7f29ea15d8b1c721d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f91ffc7c76e8e0a1757d91f7cf62f568&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3667703f7416ebab666e65b375dd8582&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c0c246e98a503a16ace92f28394b584&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7232abef4870641de7945afeb6a4bf93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21bee96879472a1c6df454d862dc9e90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce7cf71b094ef4329d3da3b628438bec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-694aaaa7c2839ea048d46b6a2bb13748&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d642e5476221b3ea202c68d7e6070b96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a1fbf409e74e27aa2b223e54f2e0def&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cede90fd3b3eee0bd12d582eaa7d54c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3fe22bd6c91507d8d1e60d24886e0eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38283df790b03806f99ca90272a1000f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9095195e9cf06b9887c03abde6284d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa1a88a43b40afd043514c5f6898ee71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffb4e34985ec90215629dc19750c8bdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-411368ddb6a73777c1dd4c683bd389c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53d382cbd1392dbcf9530428c2eb8584&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64a060d0c9650ae8bed2ca9b44eef10c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0caad5c42a4b470a8c41ac3fb68c1f64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eaf641df5c55c7ff41895611514cdd22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-937d9d4e1671351e8e90f0bd2647f321&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d85ab9c6af7915311ccbb4804160be5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cff93a2e1d68c6ed1fcd9f720197238f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4b3c26a06ad850bb97d0ca2d9217be1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d5261cecf34dd62f3f6ee6f6c3e7834&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4304c39ef3427872131caf77e7cdb438&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5279ebea7d4d5e22eebe3106de3ba1c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae42540a18795e5e2ad9054b7a0edfc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5613b129e38cb777855c04f228fe7e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5caa980be616efa237401a957b69019&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1d76ad321e1c68d5f139cdb94d5bf42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-014a80fd61677e73708fa28913d7fc56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1f0f043d44950fae05e8207a298d4a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bc3253e8d41785f994d1c6fcc2b6c47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dafca19c0156f11127587dba3673503&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9fcb421212175a148a0a1858582cfb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6eb7955dc484d5f656e1be7b406abb3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54215690a971d0637c3a6fa61d10f685&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a47a21d3773bb9ea3318d47bb077597f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5050676818c53a0ef6d691d3049e923c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1006283f24aba2aa605f9e719f36cf9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56f83fc7c1ea25f2ead74aceccfe4cf2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d7500fe4985cb2b885f9eb244ed3c2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5251cc2ed910c3785b2c7242b7cbc11e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22e4b8000531766cffd145ef32353af2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-566afea8a2a89bd188f68d0afa1bb173&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59defb995f5b0409c31d1922916c2f22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a31a12c930b59b872c94dda484d0db4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00a6288e1109e01eac1ce7ecb35f2eda</data>
