    <node id="&quot;KLEBSIELLA PNEUMONIAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Klebsiella pneumoniae is a bacterial strain also isolated from mealworm guts with capabilities in PS degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Klebsiella pneumoniae is a bacterial strain isolated from mealworm guts that aids in PS degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Klebsiella pneumoniae is a bacterial strain isolated from mealworm guts capable of growing on PS, belonging to Family Enterobacteriaceae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Klebsiella pneumoniae is a bacterium present in the gut microbiome of mealworms and contributes to plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Klebsiella pneumoniae is a nitrogen-fixing bacterium found in the guts of various insects, including termites."&lt;SEP&gt;"Klebsiella pneumoniae is a bacterium previously identified for its role in degrading polystyrene."</data>
