    <node id="&quot;TETRAHYDROFURAN (THF)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL COMPOUND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An organic compound used as a solvent in various chemical reactions, including those involved in plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"THF extracts PS and PVC during degradation experiments."&lt;SEP&gt;"THF is added to stop biological activity before final analysis using ATR-FTIR."&lt;SEP&gt;"THF is used as a solvent for extracting Styrofoam degradation products from frass samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"THF is used as a solvent for extracting components from fresh fecula in the Soxhlet extractor."&lt;SEP&gt;"THF is an anhydrous solvent with a purity of ≥99.9% used in LC-MS grade applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"THF is a solvent used to extract residual plastic from frass for further analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tetrahydrofuran is an organic solvent used to extract polystyrene from frass samples for analysis of residual PS content."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tetrahydrofuran (THF) is a solvent used in the extraction process to determine the mass of polystyrene residue in frass samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tetrahydrofuran is used to dissolve Styrofoam and frass samples for GPC analysis."</data>
