      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A method used to measure changes in physical and chemical properties of materials as a function of increasing temperature."&lt;SEP&gt;"TGA is a thermal analysis method used to measure the thermal stability and decomposition behavior of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"TGA is a thermal analysis technique used to measure changes in physical and chemical properties of materials as a function of temperature."&lt;SEP&gt;"TGA is a technique used to measure changes in weight with temperature, applied here to study pyrolysis of polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"TGA is a thermal analysis technique used to study the decomposition and thermal stability of materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"TGA measured thermal variation between control PS/CS samples and frass from PS- and CS-fed larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thermogravimetric analysis evaluates the thermal stability and degradation characteristics of materials under controlled conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thermogravimetric analysis measures weight changes in materials as a function of temperature, providing insights into thermal stability and decomposition behaviors."</data>
