    <node id="&quot;TENEBRIO OBSCURUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"INSECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">**Tenebrio obscurus**, commonly known as the dark mealworm, is a species of beetle belonging to the family of darkling beetles and part of the genus Tenebrio. This species exhibits widespread distribution across the world, highlighting its ecological adaptability and significance. The larval stage of **Tenebrio obscurus**, referred to as dark mealworms, has garnered significant attention for its remarkable ability to biodegrade various types of plastics, making it an important subject in scientific research focused on reducing plastic pollution.

These larvae have been extensively studied for their capability to degrade plastics such as low-density polyethylene (LDPE), linear low-density polyethylene (LLDPE), high-density polyethylene (HDPE), expanded polystyrene (EPS), polystyrene (PS), polyvinyl chloride (PVC), and polypropylene (PP). Notably, **Tenebrio obscurus** larvae are particularly efficient at degrading polystyrene compared to **Tenebrio molitor**, another closely related species whose larvae also exhibit plastic-degrading abilities. Despite similarities in mechanisms between the two species, differences in degradation efficiency have been observed.

The degradation process exhibited by **Tenebrio obscurus** larvae is noteworthy due to its dual capacity: it can occur both independently of gut microbes and with the assistance of their gut microbiome. This indicates that the larvae possess inherent enzymatic or biochemical mechanisms for breaking down polymers, setting them apart in the realm of plastic-degrading insects. Evidence suggests that these larvae may even exhibit increased survival rates when fed polystyrene, further emphasizing their adaptability and potential utility in addressing plastic waste.

In summary, **Tenebrio obscurus**, or dark mealworms, are insects with larvae that exhibit significant ecological importance due to their dual capacity for degrading plastics through both microbe-dependent and -independent processes. Their ability to ingest and biodegrade plastic materials underscores their potential role in combating environmental challenges posed by plastic pollution, offering promising solutions for plastic waste management.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e340b8704554cdc28486ac37e78ab0fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-104d99248e84b2776ff5ca17c285a7bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-acbe3a2cb3a17985d07d15bed638bd90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e3058d086d89f1ce9baa29cbc29bb48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-260d8c268067de32e5ac98d66ab70a6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30a7209d626a6319ba5600bea7f27299&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c3165b5b483903ac54f813f43b4076d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-566d464a7713ef7ca266f3d5f24a1a59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-915331bc1ae85fe139629eaebc4042cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0881f766e34a5d97ee711cd2edd793f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44e006d8af33633a06dac6789334329d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-207d77d551e893eda6578be68ca3d0db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-422e833d3381bd5fd0b5a3d63d9047f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-326a8dda1cdd196236b9c836192c76f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d908d878ed4e7fc36f3af71a5be7f2ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9528beb2e85a7fb89449a9233eb979bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3667703f7416ebab666e65b375dd8582&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7232abef4870641de7945afeb6a4bf93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21bee96879472a1c6df454d862dc9e90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68c274a59cd5db4cd675bca51f11adb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cede90fd3b3eee0bd12d582eaa7d54c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8c6850a83a1c6efd4f1a3a37a0a8181&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa1a88a43b40afd043514c5f6898ee71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd73d3cca5434181ee9dd1ad1b8f8ab9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3351564dbd6a0ee6a8b97f6687378ffc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc744f6fa5a9ea876a0423d37eedfc87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6464a2f3ca18442f70e254b9341a3e1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64a060d0c9650ae8bed2ca9b44eef10c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d85ab9c6af7915311ccbb4804160be5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ddf4b13293dd3d8d0887af10fc52c98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95142a3f585446bd848eeedadd1ab713&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b74f16813537103549cdcb6770abaea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b50c5a85182344022614ffe10dc9382&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c7b499dc783c21f764eb35989a449f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d5261cecf34dd62f3f6ee6f6c3e7834&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5279ebea7d4d5e22eebe3106de3ba1c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ac276660dd76d0ef97a8a0b1a59664c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-276c82b9935756a3e668c788458ff922&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5caa980be616efa237401a957b69019&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3c4d027474e8769f550ce290c9391ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1d76ad321e1c