      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A plastic-degrading bacterium isolated from the gut microbiome of Galleria mellonella, another insect species."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacter Sp. D1 is a bacterial strain isolated from the guts of Galleria Mellonella larvae, capable of degrading polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacter sp. D1 is a bacterial strain isolated from the guts of wax moth Galleria mellonella, effective in degrading polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacter sp. D1 is a bacterium isolated from the gut of Galleria mellonella, capable of degrading polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacter sp. D1 is a bacterium isolated from the gut microbiome of Galleria mellonella that contributes to plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacter Sp. D1 is a bacterium isolated from the guts of wax moth larvae that participates in the biodegradation of polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacter sp. D1 is a bacterium isolated from the gut of wax moth larvae, capable of degrading polyethylene."</data>
