    <node id="&quot;ACHATINA FULICA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Achatina Fulica, or the giant African snail, contributes to the biodegradation of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Achatina fulica is a species of land snail that demonstrates the adverse effects of microplastic exposure through uptake studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Achatina fulica is a species of land snail that demonstrates the effects of microplastic exposure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Achatina fulica, a land snail, is capable of disintegrating polystyrene regardless of intestinal microflora composition."&lt;SEP&gt;"Achatina fulica, land snails, have been found to contribute to the biodegradation and disintegration of expanded polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Achatina fulica, or land snails, have been shown to degrade expanded polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Achatina fulica, or land snails, exhibit limited extent depolymerization of EPS through gut-microbe independent mechanisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Achatina fulica, or the giant African land snail, has demonstrated the capacity to biodegrade expanded polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Land snails (Achatina fulica) are soil animals that consume plastics and harbor gut microbes involved in plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Achatina fulica, or land snails, can ingest and degrade polystyrene plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Achatina fulica, commonly known as land snails, can degrade expanded polystyrene through their digestive processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Achatina fulica, or land snails, are researched for their uptake and adverse effects of microplastic fibers after soil exposure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Achatina fulica, or land snails, are involved in the biodegradation and disintegration of expanded polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-53d382cbd1392dbcf9530428c2eb8584&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-825c2784fa66ce67114e4173ed0702f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfd8d6b8105d9868a4ffadf5779d0df5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a47a21d3773bb9ea3318d47bb077597f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49ebafd73759fc2bf3d4a642ccad96e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa9972450967f344c19cb747d7ce649e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c4652e08c4ac6887914d0deebe761b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5251cc2ed910c3785b2c7242b7cbc11e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8e18d03240e025c60621d616f1de85b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-566afea8a2a89bd188f68d0afa1bb173&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5073433ee060ce75e140a6626619108b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bd2f7b94f62fa18de9e02426577d241</data>
    </node>
