      <data key="d1">"A microbial community consists of all microorganisms inhabiting a specific environment or niche."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbial communities encompass the collective populations of microorganisms that interact within specific environments, such as the gut."&lt;SEP&gt;"PICRUSt2 predicted metagenomic functions based on microbial community data obtained from mealworm gut samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"The microbial community refers to the collective microorganisms present in a specific environment, such as the gut of Tenebrio Molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"The microbial community refers to the diverse group of microorganisms present in the gut of mealworms, aiding in biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The microbial community encompasses all microorganisms inhabiting a specific environment, such as the guts of superworms and mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"A microbial community consists of various microorganisms coexisting in a specific environment, contributing to processes like biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbial communities within larval guts are analyzed to understand their role in PS degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The microbial community consists of microorganisms involved in the degradation of polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"The microbial community in the gut of T. molitor larvae plays a crucial role in adhering to and breaking down plastic polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"The microbial community refers to the microorganisms present in the gut of T. molitor larvae that aid in the degradation of microplastics."</data>
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
    </node>
