    <node id="&quot;BIODEGRADABILITY&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-2741fab96df80d452d2d4cc651730521&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-648afbc8ee82935d4026f5915152491c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3667703f7416ebab666e65b375dd8582&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5740f0973ff804cae61f6fc12f3e3753&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a47a21d3773bb9ea3318d47bb077597f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-718900b924b6910a58e8ead81c01c723</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biodegradability is the ability of a substance to be broken down through biological processes, often involving microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodegradability refers to the ability of plastics to be broken down by biological processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ecotoxicity assessments are crucial for understanding the environmental impact of biodegradable materials and ensuring their safe use."&lt;SEP&gt;"The capability of a substance to be broken down by biological organisms into simpler compounds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodegradability refers to the capability of materials to be decomposed by biological processes, such as those involving microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodegradability refers to the ability of a material, such as PS, to be broken down by biological processes."</data>
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DEGRADATION ANALYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-a47a21d3773bb9ea3318d47bb077597f</data>
      <data key="d1">"GC-MS is utilized to analyze degradation products, providing insights into the mechanisms and outcomes of biodegradation processes."</data>
      <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
    </node>
