    <node id="&quot;MEALWORM LARVAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Larvae capable of degrading plastics like polystyrene and polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworm larvae are capable of digesting unconventional materials like polystyrene and cellulose, utilizing their gut microbiota for decomposition."&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworm larvae, specifically the larval stage of the Tenebrio molitor beetle, are an important subject in scientific research due to their unique capabilities and versatile roles as model organisms. These larvae represent the immature form of Tenebrio molitor beetles and are extensively studied for their ability to degrade plastics such as polystyrene (PS), polyethylene (PE), expanded polystyrene, and polypropylene. Their gut microbiota plays a critical role in metabolizing unconventional materials like plastics, cellulose, and lignocellulose, enabling them to break down these substances into valuable insect biomass while exhibiting varying physiological responses depending on diet composition.

As primary organisms in studies focused on microbial interactions, enzymatic activities, and physiological responses to dietary conditions, mealworm larvae contribute significantly to understanding the mechanisms behind plastic degradation. Research has demonstrated their capacity to ingest and biodegrade plastic polymers, forming degradation products under different feeding strategies. Studies also show that changes in weight and development occur when larvae consume diets containing plastics, indicating their adaptability to unconventional food sources. Mealworm larvae, particularly the yellow mealworm, have been identified as key contributors to efforts addressing plastic waste management, showing promise in breaking down PE microplastics and other forms of plastic pollution.

Beyond plastic degradation, mealworm larvae are used as model organisms to study fatty acid content under various feeding conditions. They are critical for evaluating growth, development, and metabolic processes under diverse experimental conditions, making them ideal test subjects for investigating the effects of different diets on their fatty acid profiles. Additionally, they exhibit oxidative stress due to microplastic ingestion, providing insights into the potential environmental and biological impacts of plastic exposure.

Overall, mealworm larvae (Tenebrio molitor L.) play a pivotal role in scientific investigations aimed at exploring sustainable solutions for environmental challenges and advancing knowledge about microbial interactions, enzymatic activities, and physiological responses in insects. Their active feeding stage makes them indispensable for studying growth, development, and metabolic processes in response to varied dietary conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-779ca6b59945309c6bf5040c9fb474ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dd9a0647afad70038c8052c24eb5a67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e3058d086d89f1ce9baa29cbc29bb48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a708f09b97ac93da05bd1d20bdfe174&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47c76e5149ac059b1960b533c9e99a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6cc0afd02f25b584d6e3a755fc7272b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77a9d70651c9f13362e4c1e3ce10eab0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a660790845c6a68ed38b428a7756fc84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fccc204d8a48c645da49bd7b3175c262&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f44f9d05edb3efaf7fdb8f0f1517549&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e56bce8206396081e0b7dccc47a10c9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56604c68c2f6221f63a4afa5d457e8ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a54e547b0e77432a65a8a9804c44c5d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-728d6b0b96814c5c3c7b93042e9b9856&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba22196a59b67cbf67af7d76a039af1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e25fe1af3bede4605e7b94d457c9634&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a2991bc47bdc7fe9bc0d7c0d3e23f60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-246606838d14d58d03d733b6250a0460&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa1a88a43b40afd043514c5f6898ee71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19bc661af07a194ef5a3f48c337c8d59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f8516b10110f884279870c2ef887f64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f38f2f3673b813b3a817c014229c9565&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4af956dbe737dee68ab6b9834fe2fcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f26c2702cadbaabe34c0d0e5cd2ec9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d7e47d05442ff6cd0cf042db9974f2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56f83fc7c1ea25f2ead74aceccfe4cf2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f54f1dd7372cfa3dc5f348864eed2261&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1175f4bdc5e5c267806fa6c0ff19fcc4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f7d44b3f99233bb4389ceea0cd62617&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e32e296ef016e2403df45f75eedee219&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c810740a381d4d9e829e28c01e62564</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYETHYLENE (PE) MICROPLASTICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polyethylene microplastics are plastic particles that undergo biodegradation by mealworm larvae, leading to weight loss and oxidative stress."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4f7d44b3f99233bb4389ceea0cd62617</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OXIDATIVE STRESS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A condition caused by excessive production of reactive oxygen species (ROS) leading to oxidative damage and metabolic dysbiosis in organisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oxidative stress occurs due to an imbalance between antioxidants and reactive oxygen species, caused here by plastics exposure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic exposure caused oxidative stress in BSF larvae, leading to upregulated stress response pathways like glutathione metabolism."&lt;SEP&gt;Oxidative stress is a biological condition characterized by an imbalance between the production of free radicals, such as reactive oxygen species (ROS), and the body's ability to counteract their harmful effects through antioxidants. This imbalance can lead to cellular damage at physiological or biochemical levels, potentially impacting health and survival. Oxidative stress has been studied in various contexts, including its effects on Tenebrio larvae and other invertebrates when exposed to microplastics like polyethylene (PE) and polystyrene (Styrofoam). Investigations have shown that oxidative stress parameters in insect cells may not always result in adverse effects, depending on the type of exposure. It has also been noted as a potential cause for the upregulation of lipid metabolic pathways in response to microplastic exposure. Furthermore, oxidative stress is recognized as a physiological response triggered by toxic substances, including certain polymers like PVC, which affect organisms' health. Overall, oxidative stress represents a critical process influenced by environmental factors, particularly plastic degradation processes, highlighting its significance in understanding the impacts of pollutants on living systems.&lt;SEP&gt;"Oxidative stress occurs in organisms exposed to microplastics and associated contaminants."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oxidative stress refers to the imbalance between free radicals and antioxidants in the body, causing cellular damage."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oxidative stress is induced in mealworms due to the presence of ultrahigh-MW polymers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7e67971bdf45c447f2409fddb80e0d8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-104d99248e84b2776ff5ca17c285a7bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d068dbad68e3ecd909a551f43f82b893&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fb491e686c96e54f8ea43a9f1ba97eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17052974ec1c317689bf07f0684f130f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b30daa90b5c91314e1d65e87f191166&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf697c73d05470fb4a143aa0e4700787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae2c294948460ef392ceeec82d5e81f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90367ecb21e0f14b2e548acf307a2628&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdb235a6eddd0a0e69be356e83362fc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8f677b3b4d06e07d3a58446375133fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fccc204d8a48c645da49bd7b3175c262&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f44f9d05edb3efaf7fdb8f0f1517549&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5d8df2e13d3902379597b08eb0e08db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b693d867918f89c9b28997fe94fc830&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ac1b1db6ffab6f4cfea7a525785a2fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8c6850a83a1c6efd4f1a3a37a0a8181&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcf2bd0dbdce4d7299bfc35487eaf0f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22ae90a77be18cbac99e5441d47ce2d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19bc661af07a194ef5a3f48c337c8d59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-939800f545beed77f5a7d1c026c250fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e356bad5f8c2dd9188b38c0d9462b9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b74f16813537103549cdcb6770abaea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a24fcfbc571e8620a1fc59b215b42e56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0efd7a9e4443dc5d3dfe588c7f7efc13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf54b3c2c01c935a178261a31b8ed897&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fbbfcf279533f78737706f5751ee5a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1175f4bdc5e5c267806fa6c0ff19fcc4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70eb294c60e73338ed59a2eddf057c1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f7d44b3f99233bb4389ceea0cd62617&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e32e296ef016e2403df45f75eedee219</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REACTIVE OXYGEN SPECIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MARKER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Reactive Oxygen Species (ROS) are chemically reactive molecules containing oxygen, playing a role in oxidative degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reactive oxygen species are chemically reactive molecules containing oxygen, often associated with oxidative stress."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reactive oxygen species levels increase in mealworm larvae fed with pure PE, indicating oxidative stress."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reactive oxygen species are molecules involved in oxidative degradation processes within biological systems."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reactive oxygen species are markers of oxidative stress observed in mealworms fed with microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reactive oxygen species mediate toxic effects of imidazolium-based ionic liquids on Caenorhabditis elegans."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-779ca6b59945309c6bf5040c9fb474ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fccc204d8a48c645da49bd7b3175c262&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf54b3c2c01c935a178261a31b8ed897&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59879670a8110deb87c1843ffdb71c75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f7d44b3f99233bb4389ceea0cd62617&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3fe22bd6c91507d8d1e60d24886e0eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANTIOXIDANT ENZYME ACTIVITIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL FUNCTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Antioxidant enzyme activities are elevated in response to oxidative stress induced by exposure to MPs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antioxidant enzyme activities refer to enzymatic processes that neutralize harmful reactive oxygen species."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antioxidant enzyme activities, including SOD, GST, and CAD, indicate the organism's ability to counteract oxidative stress."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antioxidant enzymes are upregulated in mealworm larvae to counteract the effects of oxidative stress caused by PE ingestion."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antioxidant enzymes play a role in neutralizing ROS and protecting cells from oxidative damage."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-104d99248e84b2776ff5ca17c285a7bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fccc204d8a48c645da49bd7b3175c262&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19bc661af07a194ef5a3f48c337c8d59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f7d44b3f99233bb4389ceea0cd62617&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44bfda02e6c219cb097ec88543433798</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIPID PEROXIDATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL REACTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lipid Peroxidation is the oxidative degradation of lipids, which is a marker for oxidative stress in biological systems."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipid peroxidation increases as plastic degradability decreases, reflecting oxidative damage in mealworms exposed to MPs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipid peroxidation is a chain reaction involving the oxidation of lipids, leading to cellular damage."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipid peroxidation is a chain reaction that damages cell membranes and other structures due to oxidative stress."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipid peroxidation is a chain reaction that damages cell membranes, increased in larvae fed with pure PE."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipid peroxidation is a process where free radicals damage cell membranes, contributing to oxidative stress."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipid peroxidation measures the oxidative degradation of lipids, serving as an indicator of oxidative stress."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipid peroxidation is the oxidative degradation of lipids, often used as a marker of oxidative stress."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-104d99248e84b2776ff5ca17c285a7bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fccc204d8a48c645da49bd7b3175c262&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22ae90a77be18cbac99e5441d47ce2d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19bc661af07a194ef5a3f48c337c8d59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1175f4bdc5e5c267806fa6c0ff19fcc4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f7d44b3f99233bb4389ceea0cd62617&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e32e296ef016e2403df45f75eedee219&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44bfda02e6c219cb097ec88543433798</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DEPOLYMERIZATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">Depolymerization is a critical biological and chemical process in which polymers, such as polypropylene (PP), polystyrene (PS), polyethylene (PE), polyethylene terephthalate (PET), and low-density polyethylene (LDPE), are broken down into smaller units, including monomers or low-molecular-weight fragments. This process plays a pivotal role in the biodegradation of synthetic polymers, enabling their environmental processing and assimilation by ecosystems.

As the first essential step in the biodegradation of plastics, depolymerization involves the breakdown of polymer chains through both chemical reactions and biological mechanisms. The process reduces the molecular weights of polymers, facilitating their structural decomposition. Biological depolymerization is particularly effective in certain organisms, such as mealworms (*Tenebrio molitor*) and superworms, which possess specialized gut microbiomes capable of breaking down polymers like PS, PE, PP, and LDPE into simpler components. Evidence of this activity is found in the frass excreted by these larvae, especially older mealworm larvae, highlighting the efficiency of their digestive systems in polymer degradation. The effectiveness of depolymerization may vary depending on factors such as the life stage of the organism, with optimal larval stages showing higher efficiency compared to mature stages.

Extracellular enzymes secreted by microorganisms in the guts of these organisms play a key role in enzymatic depolymerization, breaking down long-chain polymer molecules into simpler compounds. Observations have shown that depolymerization contributes to the degradation of various plastics, including PS, PE, and LDPE, reducing the molecular weight of polymers and impacting their structure. This facilitates further degradation and assimilation by natural systems, significantly contributing to the environmental breakdown of synthetic materials and supporting ecosystem health.

In addition, depolymerization exhibits two distinct patterns during the biodegradation of polystyrene microplastics (PS MPs): broad depolymerization (BD) and limited-extent depolymerization (LD). Overall, depolymerization is an essential step in transforming complex polymer structures into simpler compounds, playing a crucial role in reducing plastic waste in the environment. It is particularly notable in the gut of *Tenebrio* species fed PE and PS, resulting in reduced molecular weights and contributing to the reduction of plastic pollution.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e340b8704554cdc28486ac37e78ab0fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf697c73d05470fb4a143aa0e4700787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-422e833d3381bd5fd0b5a3d63d9047f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-326a8dda1cdd196236b9c836192c76f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705bf68703e5d236b2ffabb7ecb3de5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02a57c5d6ee92292f1b1bd3dbe76e612&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22d348f5320f96e129128362b6e0407c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3eb3742a8be739a1146cbf15e6b7ae5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21bee96879472a1c6df454d862dc9e90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49ebafd73759fc2bf3d4a642ccad96e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f79f3fee16e3f983c9f04a66e4d50760&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89344d5b5d9debdca45ab8c7c963a585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-640f0655e17fab473cca3b460c2795de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ab754d1dc0a02ee3f869d2b082a710e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc908e62eec4d1d05265c6e451cca84c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b759b81206d0e33e320f2d61e540ae47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c1e1694d44433fcf53dc8120c479ca4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cff93a2e1d68c6ed1fcd9f720197238f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-444b8acd02a76616457012e1ac0db23b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e155a60beeedb5736450fdc1ffa4699e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25f3365d0b08e5e77183d813ce6a1049&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3380732c060363504db5f6e4b8610b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-490fdb90ad8a65d35f3c2cd42a8c4c8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af801199dfd68205bddcbe0bcda26eef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfe58fb1bbaa5c35e9c6c837d0b1050f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-395b01f15fd97b70e2368941120e9a37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99f8bb992751f8875d9449507e9c46ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f370c2f246a6c8a776ae90277a5aacc8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30a7209d626a6319ba5600bea7f27299&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c818a01113d8c07554629cc5edfd28f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05b7bf66b11c66f02e73a07fb823b8fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e24cc3865ed97850c3f25795ff514e8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f91df729b04e3d570337e02872cf1c38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56604c68c2f6221f63a4afa5d457e8ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c343b12adf5bbce5bf80b96909fe66d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31ad3152e855d5b8085e1e61af57515d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd4d84d6de496440fcabc6616d1c96ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e1faf524e6fabeb512a07b13f37e51e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd73d3cca5434181ee9dd1ad1b8f8ab9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98f748ef0b9e55c370617ad91bcf219c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21c07a838ff0a