c39ef3427872131caf77e7cdb438&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-276c82b9935756a3e668c788458ff922&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5613b129e38cb777855c04f228fe7e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15323ef47e29f2927f95274e49f4e5bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-beb3c133fa4d5851f0feff55507c6874&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7fa795762aa89809d8221dc9dda92fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5caa980be616efa237401a957b69019&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-846559469c70e081884fea2f9a4b7317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e97dc712df43805c553423ceb65cd6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f7d44b3f99233bb4389ceea0cd62617&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b673e7590aa1d03b7721694ed73cd74</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THERMAL DECOMPOSITION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Thermal decomposition involves breaking down materials into gaseous compounds under programmed temperature conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thermal decomposition is the process by which materials break down under high temperatures, producing various gaseous and solid products."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thermal decomposition signals indicate the biodegradation of PE microplastics in mealworm larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thermal decomposition involves breaking down materials through heat, often used for plastic waste management but generating harmful byproducts."</data>
