    <node id="&quot;HYDROPHOBICITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hydrophobicity describes the extent to which a material repels water, with PS film surface showing reduced hydrophobicity due to microbial action."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hydrophobicity describes the tendency of a material to repel water, impacting microbial adhesion and degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hydrophobicity describes the tendency of a substance to repel water, assessed here via contact angle analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hydrophobicity describes the water-repellent nature of PET, influenced by crystallinity and affecting its biodegradability."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hydrophobicity refers to the property of a surface or material to repel water, measured here for gut mealworm isolates."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hydrophobicity refers to the tendency of bacteria to repel water, impacting their ability to adhere to surfaces and degrade non-polar polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hydrophobicity refers to the water-repellent nature of polyethylene, further hindering microbial attack."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hydrophobicity refers to the tendency of a substance to repel water, measured using contact angle analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hydrophobicity refers to the water-repellent property of materials, which decreases during the degradation of polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hydrophobicity refers to the water-repellent nature of polymers, influencing their interaction with microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hydrophobicity is a physical property of polystyrene that decreases during its degradation by gut bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hydrophobicity refers to the water-repellent property of a material's surface, which was altered by biofilm formation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hydrophobicity describes the reduced water-repellent property of aged PE due to surface oxidation, enhancing microbial adhesion."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hydrophobicity describes the water-repellent characteristic of aged polymers, which decreases with surface oxidation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hydrophobicity describes the water-repellent nature of plastics, which decreases with aging and affects microbial adhesion."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-361c5d4ba2e879627f4eb7fc4011ee3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-939fc2ea222a49f84f9bdc11f9801367&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06ba9ca61fb4f42582bbf7bd00ff0005&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-582f48080aab075de76c9c590558639f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffb4e34985ec90215629dc19750c8bdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8eca628f2d85c664191a5205194ec475&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16a478461d1471ca083f90b3f8e7456e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4443da1fe36ec7133cd5add18d1957a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dfcb17715cb4e5148b33061c1b6cbf1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-902ed6a67c601276c5dbf43c35dd824f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40357516e3f9dd4b2969b73efe444c28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-668212da3bf356132cadb63df6ce09b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f7d44b3f99233bb4389ceea0cd62617&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31ad3152e855d5b8085e1e61af57515d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b673e7590aa1d03b7721694ed73cd74</data>
    </node>
