    <node id="&quot;INFLAMMATORY RESPONSES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"IMMUNE RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Inflammatory responses are part of the immune system's reaction to micro(nano)plastics, indicating potential health risks."&lt;SEP&gt;"Inflammatory responses are reactions of the immune system to harmful stimuli, potentially induced by nanoplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Inflammatory responses occur in macroinvertebrates ingesting plastic debris or MPs, contributing to physiological stress."&lt;SEP&gt;"Inflammatory responses result from imbalances or mechanical stimulation of the gut microbiota."&lt;SEP&gt;"Inflammatory responses are triggered by the ingestion of microplastics, indicating an immune reaction to foreign particles."</data>
