    <node id="&quot;PHENANTHRENE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TOXIN"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An organic pollutant affecting earthworm mortality, growth, and antioxidant systems under laboratory conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phenanthrene is a polycyclic aromatic hydrocarbon that can adsorb onto microplastics, contributing to environmental contamination."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phenanthrene is a PAH effectively degraded by Achromobacter sp. LH-1, showcasing high degradability."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phenanthrene is a polycyclic aromatic hydrocarbon degraded by certain bacteria like Achromobacter sp. LH-1."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phenanthrene is a toxic compound that affects earthworm mortality, growth, and antioxidant systems."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-779ca6b59945309c6bf5040c9fb474ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3934e2c5488a209e54e10ba4c0335a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26138366e1d9310732edc569ba338bfe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a53d37e7ff6850fc55177f325e49861&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f7d44b3f99233bb4389ceea0cd62617</data>
