      <data key="d1">"Antarctic krill are capable of fragmenting microplastics into nanoplastics through digestive processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antarctic krill are small crustaceans that have been found to biofragment ingested plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antarctic krill are marine crustaceans that do not possess significant plastic-degrading capabilities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antarctic krill are microorganisms that can fragment microplastics into nanoplastics through digestion."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antarctic krill is a macroinvertebrate studied for its ability to fragment plastics, though lacking significant plastic-degrading abilities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antarctic krill is a species studied for its digestive fragmentation of microplastics into nanoplastics."</data>
