    <node id="&quot;GLASS CONTAINERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Glass containers are used to house mealworm larvae during breeding and experimentation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Glass containers are used to house mealworm larvae during breeding and experimentation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Glass containers were used in the experimental setup to house mealworm larvae and collect frass."&lt;SEP&gt;"Glass containers with a volume of 300 mL were used to rear mealworms under controlled conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Glass containers were used to house mealworms during the experiment, ensuring controlled conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Glass containers were used to house mealworms during the experiment, with specific dimensions and population density."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f267b48449a40d614a2f325799752dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1283355f048671359adcde7d3137af9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e56bce8206396081e0b7dccc47a10c9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9af0d95fd5f52d02b9cb33387951963&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a2991bc47bdc7fe9bc0d7c0d3e23f60</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REACTIVE OXYGEN SPECIES (ROS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MARKER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Highly reactive molecules containing oxygen, produced excessively during microplastic digestion in mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"ROS are chemically reactive molecules containing oxygen, often associated with oxidative stress in biological systems."&lt;SEP&gt;"ROS levels increase as plastic degradability decreases, indicating oxidative stress in mealworms exposed to MPs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reactive Oxygen Species (ROS) are molecules that can cause oxidative stress in cells, indicative of cellular damage or stress."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reactive oxygen species are chemical species that include free radicals and peroxides, measured to assess oxidative stress in mealworm larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reactive oxygen species are chemically reactive molecules containing oxygen, indicative of oxidative stress in cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reactive oxygen species are chemically reactive molecules containing oxygen, which were measured in the gut cells of the insects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reactive oxygen species are chemically reactive molecules containing oxygen, often associated with oxidative stress and cellular damage."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reactive Oxygen Species are molecules involved in the degradation process of polystyrene by Zophobas atratus larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"ROS levels rise in organisms exposed to microplastic contaminants, indicating oxidative stress responses."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reactive Oxygen Species (ROS) is a biological marker that indicates oxidative stress levels in organisms, represented by fluorescence intensity per mg of protein."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-104d99248e84b2776ff5ca17c285a7bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe381daaa91bbff20758798e5baf82b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8f677b3b4d06e07d3a58446375133fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f44f9d05edb3efaf7fdb8f0f1517549&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6cbb8ccec16f4756fa7a1fb365886d9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6eb7955dc484d5f656e1be7b406abb3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fbbfcf279533f78737706f5751ee5a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17052974ec1c317689bf07f0684f130f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f54f1dd7372cfa3dc5f348864eed2261&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf697c73d05470fb4a143aa0e4700787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44bfda02e6c219cb097ec88543433798</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MALONDIALDEHYDE (MDA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A marker of lipid peroxidation and oxidative damage, elevated in mealworms fed on plastic diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"MDA is a biomarker for lipid peroxidation, which increases in response to oxidative stress induced by microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Malondialdehyde (MDA) is a metabolite used to assess oxidative damage, measured in nanomoles per gram of fresh weight."&lt;SEP&gt;"Malondialdehyde (MDA) is a reactive aldehyde and one of the final products of lipid peroxidation, serving as a biomarker for oxidative stress."&lt;SEP&gt;"Malondialdehyde is a product of lipid peroxidation, used as an indicator of oxidative damage in biological systems."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fe381daaa91bbff20758798e5baf82b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22ae90a77be18cbac99e5441d47ce2d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f44f9d05edb3efaf7fdb8f0f1517549&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17052974ec1c317689bf07f0684f130f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f54f1dd7372cfa3dc5f348864eed2261</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUPEROXIDE DISMUTASE (SOD)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An antioxidant enzyme responsible for eliminating superoxide anions (\(O_2^-\)) in organisms, showing increased activity in plastic-fed mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"SOD is an enzyme that helps neutralize superoxide radicals, playing a role in combating oxidative stress caused by microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Superoxide Dismutase (SOD) is an enzyme that converts superoxide radicals into hydrogen peroxide and oxygen, acting as an antioxidant."&lt;SEP&gt;"Superoxide dismutase is an enzyme that catalyzes the dismutation of superoxide radicals into oxygen and hydrogen peroxide, acting as an antioxidant."&lt;SEP&gt;"Superoxide Dismutase (SOD) is an enzyme that serves as a physiological stress response marker, measured in units per gram of fresh weight."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fe381daaa91bbff20758798e5baf82b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22ae90a77be18cbac99e5441d47ce2d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f44f9d05edb3efaf7fdb8f0f1517549&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17052974ec1c317689bf07f0684f130f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f54f1dd7372cfa3dc5f348864eed2261</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GLUTATHIONE-S-TRANSFERASE (GST)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Glutathione-S-Transferase (GST) is an enzyme involved in detoxification processes by catalyzing the conjugation of glutathione to various substrates."&lt;SEP&gt;"Glutathione-S-transferase is an enzyme involved in detoxification processes, contributing to the antioxidant defense system."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-22ae90a77be18cbac99e5441d47ce2d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f54f1dd7372cfa3dc5f348864eed2261</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CATALASE (CAT)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Catalase (CAT) is an enzyme that catalyzes the decomposition of hydrogen peroxide into water and oxygen, protecting cells from oxidative damage."&lt;SEP&gt;"Catalase is an enzyme that catalyzes the decomposition of hydrogen peroxide into water and oxygen, protecting cells from oxidative damage."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-22ae90a77be18cbac99e5441d47ce2d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f54f1dd7372cfa3dc5f348864eed2261</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;H2O2 SOLUTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL REACTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hydrogen peroxide solution is used to digest organic matter in frass samples, allowing for the recovery of residual plastic particles."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f54f1dd7372cfa3dc5f348864eed2261</data>
    </node>
