    <node id="&quot;SPCRS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Specific Plastic Consumption Rates (SPCRs) measure how much plastic T. molitor larvae consume over time."&lt;SEP&gt;"Specific consumption rates, indicating the amount of feed consumed by mealworm larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fa1a88a43b40afd043514c5f6898ee71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f61cd3a131593ce6b058802713d43ddb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MW, MN, MZ&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Molecular weight parameters used to characterize the depolymerization of PE microplastics after biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mw (Weight-average molecular weight), Mn (Number-average molecular weight), and Mz (Z-average molecular weight) are metrics used to describe polymer size distribution."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mw, Mn, Mz represent molecular weight parameters analyzed using GPC."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1d39fc863538a777920c4eafb37bcf8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa1a88a43b40afd043514c5f6898ee71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c84ac252cb9ce906354bda2ad1113aba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHYSIOLOGICAL RESPONSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Changes in survival rate (SR) and activity weight (AW) of mealworm larvae under different diet conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Physiological responses are reactions or adaptations of an organism to environmental stimuli, potentially observed in mealworms under study."&lt;SEP&gt;"Physiological response refers to the measurable changes in mealworms' health and growth due to exposure to polystyrene microplastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fa1a88a43b40afd043514c5f6898ee71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35eed7e10fb1cc08baaecab1b1cffad0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e136b8a35c0d60811b9daf0cbd5729f5</data>
    </node>
