      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL FUNCTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biomacromolecule function involves the roles of large biological molecules like proteins and lipids in mealworm physiology."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e32e296ef016e2403df45f75eedee219</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;APOPTOSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Apoptosis biomarkers increase in Tenebrio molitor when consuming polystyrene, suggesting cellular stress."&lt;SEP&gt;"Apoptosis is the process of programmed cell death, which may be triggered by oxidative damage in mealworm larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Apoptosis, or programmed cell death, is triggered in zebrafish exposed to toxic microplastics, affecting their development."&lt;SEP&gt;"Apoptosis refers to programmed cell death, observed in the study but showing no differences between control and Styrofoam groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"Programmed cell death indicated by changes in the lipidome of mealworms consuming PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Programmed cell death triggered by severe oxidative stress and mitochondrial dysfunction."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e5caa980be616efa237401a957b69019&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0d2f43eebe2309fba46c5335d76df56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8f677b3b4d06e07d3a58446375133fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f44f9d05edb3efaf7fdb8f0f1517549&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5922f60fcd06ac6ffa27018026871346&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e32e296ef016e2403df45f75eedee219</data>
    </node>
