      <data key="d0">"PHYSIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Abnormal development refers to deviations from normal growth patterns in mealworm larvae due to oxidative stress."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e32e296ef016e2403df45f75eedee219</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENE EXPRESSION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENETIC CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Changes in gene expression are observed in organisms exposed to microplastics and chemicals."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gene expression is the process by which genetic information is converted into functional products like proteins in mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gene expression refers to the transcriptional activity measured through RNA sequencing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gene expression refers to the process by which genetic information is converted into functional products, such as proteins, often influenced by environmental conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e32e296ef016e2403df45f75eedee219&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-718900b924b6910a58e8ead81c01c723&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a7768b61a3d166f2cd01d4e87ac88cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fb491e686c96e54f8ea43a9f1ba97eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DNA DAMAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"DNA damage refers to structural abnormalities in the DNA molecule caused by oxidative stress in mealworm larvae."</data>
