    <node id="&quot;METABOLITES OF LIPID PEROXIDATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Metabolites of lipid peroxidation are breakdown products generated during oxidative damage to lipids."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e32e296ef016e2403df45f75eedee219</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;O₂⁻&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"O₂⁻ is a reactive oxygen species (ROS) that can cause oxidative stress and damage in organisms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1175f4bdc5e5c267806fa6c0ff19fcc4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MDA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"MDA (malondialdehyde) is a metabolite marker for lipid peroxidation and oxidative damage."&lt;SEP&gt;"MDA is a marker of lipid peroxidation, indicating oxidative stress in the organism."&lt;SEP&gt;"Malondialdehyde (MDA) is a biomarker for lipid peroxidation and oxidative damage in cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Malondialdehyde (MDA) is a lipid peroxidation product used to determine oxidative damage to membrane lipids."&lt;SEP&gt;"Malondialdehyde is a marker of lipid peroxidation and oxidative stress in organisms exposed to plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Malondialdehyde (MDA) content was determined to indicate lipid peroxidation levels."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-90367ecb21e0f14b2e548acf307a2628&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a27dff473ed210517e6461ad3e5d783&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e98fb757cb68ae45626058d9c3a15cb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b693d867918f89c9b28997fe94fc830&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1175f4bdc5e5c267806fa6c0ff19fcc4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a24fcfbc571e8620a1fc59b215b42e56</data>
    </node>
