    <node id="&quot;RESIDUAL POLYMERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Remaining polymer structures extracted from frass after biodegradation by larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Residual polymers are the leftover polymer chains after the larvae have processed the original plastic material."&lt;SEP&gt;"Residual polymers are the remaining plastic materials after partial biodegradation within the digestive system of Tenebrio larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Residual polymers are undigested microplastics found in the frass of mealworm larvae after biodegradation, indicating incomplete digestion of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Residual polymers are the remaining polymer fragments after partial biodegradation of PS MPs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Residual polymers refer to the undigested PS fragments remaining in the frass after ingestion by mealworms."</data>
