    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEXABROMOCYCLODODECANE (HBCD)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TOXIN"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HBCD is a flame retardant commonly found in polystyrene and studied for its environmental impact."&lt;SEP&gt;"HBCD is a flame retardant commonly found in polystyrene materials. It can be processed by mealworms without bioaccumulation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hexabromocyclododecane is a flame retardant found in polystyrene and studied for its fate during plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hexabromocyclododecane is a flame retardant compound found in polystyrene, which can accumulate during its degradation process."&lt;SEP&gt;"HBCD is a flame retardant found in PS foam and other plastics, which does not negatively impact T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hexabromocyclododecane (HBCD) is a flame retardant whose fate in polyethylene-degrading mealworms has been investigated."&lt;SEP&gt;"HBCD is a flame retardant commonly found in polystyrene, impacting its degradation process."&lt;SEP&gt;"HBCD is a flame retardant found in polystyrene, with potential bioaccumulation concerns."&lt;SEP&gt;"HBCD is a flame retardant found in polystyrene, with elevated levels in egested polymer but no bioaccumulation in mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9a882603f777986db9d8fc65cea91dce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79e833cbc3a0a6e2c80e1b69da50317e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e3058d086d89f1ce9baa29cbc29bb48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91831340731171413dc4c412a325e034&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5d8df2e13d3902379597b08eb0e08db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fb491e686c96e54f8ea43a9f1ba97eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5338aa2127367c868a3e7331e1f66225&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ee089593160e720e507848fa8c917a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-694aaaa7c2839ea048d46b6a2bb13748</data>
