    <node id="&quot;CARBON METABOLISM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL FUNCTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Carbon Metabolism involves the processes by which organisms utilize carbon-based compounds for energy and growth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon metabolism encompasses the processes through which carbon atoms are incorporated into organic molecules, supporting energy production and biosynthesis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon metabolism involves the breakdown of carbon-based compounds, which is essential for the biodegradation of plastics in mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon metabolism refers to the biochemical processes involved in the assimilation and transformation of carbon compounds within living organisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon metabolism pathways are enriched in PP-fed larvae, facilitating the assimilation of PP intermediates."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon metabolism is necessary for energy acquisition during plastic degradation."</data>
