    <node id="&quot;INSECTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CLASS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Insects are a class of arthropods, some of which interact with packaging materials and may contribute to biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Insects are a class of invertebrates that include species like mealworms and wax moths, some of which can degrade plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Insects are considered a potential source of food and feed, providing essential nutrients that could contribute to global food security."&lt;SEP&gt;"Insects such as yellow mealworms and dark mealworms serve as hosts for gut microbes that facilitate polymer degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Insects are organisms studied for their ability to consume and degrade polystyrene, with potential implications for human health."&lt;SEP&gt;"Insects like mealworms are studied for their ability to consume plastics and their physiological responses to starvation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Insects are organisms that undergo metabolic stress due to consuming plastic as part of their diet."&lt;SEP&gt;"The primary subject of the study, focusing on their development and dietary impacts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Insects are organisms capable of biotransforming specific plastic types, contributing to the development of fit-for-purpose insect biotransformers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Insects play a role in the degradation of PS through their gut microbiome and enzymatic activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Insects are arthropods that include darkling beetles and pest moths, known for their ability to chew and ingest plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Insects are small arthropods with three body segments, playing critical roles in ecosystems, including decomposition and pollination."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a097963ab8ec0ad6b1d51685fc359027&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5caa980be616efa237401a957b69019&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c8dab62f56f2bfabf08bfe99049386a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ead6f17ad517015b638608c5bfe6852&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3eb3742a8be739a1146cbf15e6b7ae5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41635122b30ee45048cc885b38fff6ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0caad5c42a4b470a8c41ac3fb68c1f64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00a6288e1109e01eac1ce7ecb35f2eda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b47eb2d42413e11dbd4e9bb9f2df12f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf8041a3cdcd6091f6c96b8b67229df2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d76cb64e0aa4e4039b70799a0df8943d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b50c5a85182344022614ffe10dc9382</data>
    </node>
