      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PLA is a biodegradable and bioactive thermoplastic derived from renewable resources."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polylactic acid (PLA) is a biodegradable plastic analyzed in the experiment to assess its influence on insect metabolism."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polylactic acid (PLA) is a biodegradable polymer that can be processed by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polylactic acid is a biodegradable polymer whose photolytic degradation can increase toxicity to zebrafish by causing mitochondrial dysfunction and apoptosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polylactic acid is a biodegradable thermoplastic derived from renewable resources like corn starch or sugarcane."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polylactic acid is a biodegradable plastic that can be degraded by yellow mealworms as part of sustainable waste management strategies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polylactic acid is a biodegradable polymer that can be degraded by mealworms as part of sustainable waste management strategies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polylactic acid is a biodegradable thermoplastic derived from renewable resources, studied for microbial adhesion and oxytetracycline interactions."</data>
