      <data key="d1">"Groups of microorganisms involved in nitrogen conversion and amino acid synthesis within the digestive system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hydrophobicity of polyethylene limits microbial colonization and enzymatic activity, reducing its biodegradability."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microorganisms refer to the bacterial communities isolated from the digestive tracts of mealworm larvae fed different substrates."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microorganisms are small living organisms, often unicellular, that play a crucial role in environmental processes and metabolic activities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microorganisms are present in the intestines of insects and play a role in the biodegradation of plastics through enzymatic activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microorganisms are living entities capable of degrading polystyrene and other materials, often influenced by environmental factors."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microorganisms aggregate into a large symbiotic organ called the bacteriome and play a significant role in the digestive process to provide essential nutrients for host insects. They are also involved in detoxification of toxic compounds and production of volatile substances."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microorganisms are living entities capable of biodegrading plastics, offering a potential solution to plastic pollution."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microorganisms are tiny living organisms that may play a role in degrading plastics and were mentioned as a potential solution to plastic pollution."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microorganisms in the gut of Tenebrio molitor larvae play a significant role in the digestive process and provide essential nutrients for the host insects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Living organisms capable of degrading PU external parts via extracellular enzymes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microorganisms from diverse environmental sources, such as sludge, soil, landfill, seawater, and compost, play a role in the biodegradation of PE products."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microorganisms in the gut of Coleoptera and Lepidoptera larvae play a crucial role in breaking down nanoplastic particles ingested during digestion."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microorganisms refer to the bacterial strains isolated from mealworms that degrade NPS and EPS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microorganisms include bacteria and fungi that are capable of degrading plastics like PE under specific conditions such as photo- or thermo-oxidation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microorganisms are living organisms involved in the limited biodegradation of PE after pretreatment processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microorganisms are the focus of the study, isolated from mealworms' intestines and tested for their ability to degrade polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microorganisms are tiny living entities responsible for breaking down plastics through biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microorganisms refer to the bacterial communities isolated from the digestive tracts of mealworm larvae fed different substrates."</data>
      <data key="d0">"MICROBE"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLASTIC BIODEGRADATION&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-323c02b97d9365a25761a155d358b17a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19bc661af07a194ef5a3f48c337c8d59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74e2601f950d62c093ceb86612b2374f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c39e41f4f36c9c6854fa71508c35a08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d33654bada6ddaf4917586dd5fd41e9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bd3778dedc6a0463017df9f8d6396eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d7500fe4985cb2b885f9eb244ed3c2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-896c5c0e4d1805ded38b335876a02f78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcc545cfe4d6e8e04c3698a149d4101a</data>
      <data key="d1">"Plastic biodegradation involves the breakdown of plastic materials into simpler compounds by living organisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The darkling beetle family includes species capable of voluntarily masticating and fragmenting plastics, contributing to biodegradation efforts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic biodegradation is a biological process where microorganisms break down plastics into simpler compounds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic biodegradation refers to the breakdown of plastic materials by microorganisms, such as those found in the mealworm gut."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic biodegradation is the process by which microorganisms break down plastic polymers into simpler compounds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic biodegradation refers to the breakdown of plastic materials into simpler compounds through biological processes, particularly involving insect gut microbes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic biodegradation involves the enzymatic depolymerization of various plastics by microorganisms such as fungi and bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic biodegradation refers to the process by which microorganisms break down plastic materials into simpler compounds."&lt;SEP&gt;"The breakdown of plastic materials by living organisms, particularly microbes."</data>
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HT-GPC&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-bd73d3cca5434181ee9dd1ad1b8f8ab9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17b1e554820493d86eb8bc96ba8bef37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3380732c060363504db5f6e4b8610b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26a193cc62c03cb6460b0434df42d8c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af682f78e3e8970d7d70b027a8f79116&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-566d464a7713ef7ca266f3d5f24a1a59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa9972450967f344c19cb747d7ce649e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-718900b924b6910a58e8ead81c01c723&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-843d5746868067bce1a2f15dfc1571e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4cdbea1d06006b95d57c8b628d9e3f8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05b7bf66b11c66f02e73a07fb823b8fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a2991bc47bdc7fe9bc0d7c0d3e23f60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ab754d1dc0a02ee3f869d2b082a710e</data>
      <data key="d1">"HT-GPC (High-Temperature Gel Permeation Chromatography) is a method used to determine molecular weight changes in residual polymers after biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"HT-GPC (High-Temperature Gel Permeation Chromatography) is a technique used to analyze molecular weight distributions of polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"HT-GPC (High-Temperature Gel Permeation Chromatography) quantifies molecular weight of LDPE."&lt;SEP&gt;"HT-GPC analysis verifies the depolymerization and biodegradation of PE microplastics ingested by mealworm larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"HT-GPC, or high-temperature gel permeation chromatography, is a specialized form of GPC used for analyzing high-molecular-weight polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"High-temperature gel permeation chromatography (HT-GPC) is a method used to determine molecular weights of plastics like PP, LDPE, and LLDPE."&lt;SEP&gt;"HT-GPC is a chromatographic technique used to determine the molecular weight distribution of polyethylene in mulching films."&lt;SEP&gt;"High-Temperature Gel Permeation Chromatography (HT-GPC) is a technique used to analyze molecular weights of polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"High-Temperature Gel Permeation Chromatography (HT-GPC) is a method used to analyze the molecular weight distribution of residual polymers after ingestion by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"HT-GPC (High-Temperature Gel Permeation Chromatography) is a technique used to analyze the molecular weight distributions of polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"HT-GPC is a technique used for analyzing molecular weights of residual polymers from frass samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"HT-GPC is a process used to analyze the molecular weight distribution of polymers in this study."&lt;SEP&gt;"High-temperature gel permeation chromatography, a technique used to analyze molecular weight distributions of polymers."</data>
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
    </node>
