    <node id="&quot;MICROBIOME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Microbiome refers to the community of microorganisms associated with Tenebrio molitor larvae, which plays a role in the biodegradation of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbiome refers to the community of microorganisms living in the gut of T. molitor larvae, which plays a crucial role in degrading plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbiome refers to the community of microorganisms living in the gut of Tenebrio molitor larvae, which plays a key role in the degradation of different types of waste materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"The microbial community supporting styrene degradation and polymer biotransformation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The microbiome refers to the community of microorganisms living in the gut of T. molitor, which plays a role in biodegrading plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"The gut microbiome of certain insects like caterpillars contributes significantly to the degradation of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"The microbiome refers to the community of microorganisms present in the gut of insects, potentially contributing to LDPE degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The microbiome refers to the community of microorganisms residing in the gut of the greater wax moth, which may play a role in the degradation of LDPE."&lt;SEP&gt;"The core gut microbiome plays a role in the biodegradation processes of plastics within insect larvae, as influenced by dietary supplements."&lt;SEP&gt;"The microbiome represents the community of microorganisms residing in a specific environment, such as the gut of insects."&lt;SEP&gt;"The community of microorganisms associated with the insects, influenced by diet."&lt;SEP&gt;"The microbiome represents the community of microorganisms living within a specific environment, such as the gut of insect larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"The microbiome represents the microbial community associated with larval diet and host-specificity."&lt;SEP&gt;"The microbiome refers to the microbial community in the insect gut that contributes to the enzymatic activity and degradation of PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"The microbiome refers to the community of microorganisms in the mealworm gut involved in digesting plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"The microbiome encompasses all the microorganisms present in a particular environment, such as the gut of insects, playing a role in material degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The microbiome refers to the community of microorganisms inhabiting a specific environment, such as the gut of Tenebrio molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbiome refers to the community of microorganisms living in the gut of Tenebrio molitor larvae, which plays a key role in the degradation of different types of waste materials."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dc31a0931fceb1446bc6ec4d0c587f7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a214d2b1c90aeb78e6e8562679d4963&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3891caf14683493be3d8709ced467492&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ead6f17ad517015b638608c5bfe6852&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-681ece0a8beca8b22f3c6aa11a564f63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bc3253e8d41785f994d1c6fcc2b6c47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3eb3742a8be739a1146cbf15e6b7ae5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fd138e047a780efd715a5ab4701b58c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3815960770483b9c0a1579ca8442e3a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5dc0ba5d8a1abfb746af0dedb7d575b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a603837ad5b989bafd614f5eeb8504c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b693d867918f89c9b28997fe94fc830&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b47eb2d42413e11dbd4e9bb9f2df12f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33180d5b7e1ebfedf8de59ba1a2a2d04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95142a3f585446bd848eeedadd1ab713&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c42631c88da011b836666dae04cfa11a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53f87a406d4812c07e783e6cbfc09606</data>
