      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A bacterial genus linked to Diet 3 conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacteroides is a bacterial class distributed similarly to Alphaproteobacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacteroides is a bacterial genus present in the gut microbiome of Tenebrio molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacteroides is a genus of gram-negative bacteria within the order Bacteroidales."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacteroides is a dominant bacterial phylum in the gut microbiome of mealworms contributing to plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacteroides is a genus of gram-negative bacteria found in the gut microbiome contributing to plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacteroides was found in low abundance in the mealworm gut microbiome, showing variability in bacterial composition across studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacteroides is a bacterial class distributed similarly to Alphaproteobacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacteroides is a bacterial genus present in the gut microbiome of Tenebrio molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacteroides is a genus of gram-negative bacteria within the order Bacteroidales."</data>
