    <node id="&quot;LACTOCOCCUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A bacterial genus showing varying responses to different diets, potentially involved in EPS degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lactococcus is a genus of bacteria found in larvae fed on plastic diets, participating in decomposition processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lactococcus is a genus of bacteria unique to each plastic diet in Tenebrio molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lactococcus is a genus of bacteria that increased significantly in both PS-fed superworms and yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"A genus of bacteria found in T. molitor larvae fed PE and PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lactococcus is a bacterial genus noted in the mealworm gut microbiome, contributing to its microbial diversity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lactococcus is a genus of bacteria identified as predominant in the gut microbiome of Tenebrio molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"A genus within Firmicutes consistently associated with the PU diet throughout the experiment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lactococcus is a genus of bacteria associated with the degradation of polyurethane throughout the experiment described in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lactococcus is a genus of bacteria found predominantly in the anterior gut of mealworms when fed a standard diet."&lt;SEP&gt;"A genus of lactic acid bacteria that plays a role in maintaining gut health."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lactococcus is a common genus in the mealworm gut microbiome, found throughout the gut."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lactococcus is a genus of bacteria present in the gut of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lactococcus is a bacterial genus whose relative abundance increased in the gut microbial community of yellow mealworms fed on mask layers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lactococcus is a genus of bacteria common in insect guts, contributing to gut health and associated with PP degradation in T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lactococcus is a genus of bacteria present in the core gut microbiome of superworms and yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lactococcus is a common genus in all groups, representing a consistent component of the gut bacterial community."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lactococcus is a genus of lactic acid bacteria, exhibiting variations in relative abundance across treatments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lactococcus is a bacterial genus found in larvae fed on plastic diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lactococcus is a genus of bacteria unique to each plastic diet in Tenebrio molitor larvae."</data>
