    <node id="&quot;CARBON DIOXIDE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Carbon dioxide is a byproduct of the biodegradation process of plastics into simpler molecules."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon dioxide is a byproduct of the chemical reactions involved in the digestion of polystyrene by mealworm larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon dioxide is a metabolic product generated from the degradation of plastics by gut microbes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon dioxide is a gas evolved from the mineralization process of ingested Styrofoam by superworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon dioxide is another decomposition product identified in the fecula, also formed within the temperature range of 175 to 480°C."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon dioxide is a byproduct of the plastic degradation process carried out by yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon dioxide is a product of the EPS biodegradation process in the mealworm gut."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon dioxide is one of the products of EPS biodegradation by mealworm gut bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon dioxide is a byproduct of the chemical reactions involved in the digestion of polystyrene by mealworm larvae."</data>
