      <data key="d1">"Bacilli is a bacterial class containing genera such as Virgibacillus and Pseudogracilbacillus that appeared overrepresented in PS samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacilli is a bacterial class widely distributed across analyzed feeding variants."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacilli is an order within the class Clostridia, encompassing genera like Enterococcus."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacilli is a class of aerobic bacteria within the Firmicutes phylum found in the gut microbiota of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacilli is a class within the phylum Firmicutes, to which Exiguobacterium sp. YT2 belongs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacilli is a class of bacteria found abundantly in the gut microbiome of Tenebrio molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacilli is a bacterial class widely distributed across analyzed feeding variants."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacilli is an order within the class Clostridia, encompassing genera like Enterococcus."</data>
