    <node id="&quot;BACTEROIDALES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORDER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An order prominent in OAT groups, associated with carbohydrate metabolism."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacteroidales is a bacterial order commonly found in the larval microbiome, with mean abundance of 17.4%."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacteroidales is an order in the phylum Bacteroidetes, including genera such as Bacteroides."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacteroidales is an order of bacteria that includes ectosymbionts associated with gut flagellates in dry-wood termites."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacteroidales is an order of bacteria with a mean abundance of 17.4%, higher in OAT and CEL diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacteroidales is an order in the phylum Bacteroidetes, including genera such as Bacteroides."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacteroidales is an order of bacteria that includes ectosymbionts associated with gut flagellates in dry-wood termites, influencing nitrogen fixation."</data>
