    <node id="&quot;NITROSOMONADALES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORDER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An order characteristic of PS diets, involved in ammonia oxidation."&lt;SEP&gt;"An order of bacteria positively correlated with the PS diet and the second ordination axis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrosomonadales is a bacterial order contributing to ammonia oxidation in mealworm gut environments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrosomonadales is an order of bacteria contributing to nitrogen cycling and fixation in insect digestive systems."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrosomonadales is an order within the class Gammaproteobacteria, containing genera like Nitrosomonas."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrosomonadales is an order of bacteria involved in the nitrification process, oxidizing ammonia to nitrite."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrosomonadales is an order with an average abundance of 1.6%, highest in the PS variant."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrosomonadales includes bacteria like Nitrosomonas sp., contributing to ammonia oxidation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrosomonadales is an order within the class Gammaproteobacteria, containing genera like Nitrosomonas."</data>
