    <node id="&quot;TENERICUTES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CLASS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A bacterial phylum dominant in the mealworm gut microbiome, with decreasing proportions over time on PU diet."&lt;SEP&gt;"One of the dominant bacterial phyla found in other studies on mealworms fed with polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenericutes is a bacterial class commonly found in the mealworm gut microbiome, contributing significantly to microbial diversity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenericutes is a class of bacteria that includes orders such as Entomoplasmatales."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenericutes is a phylum of bacteria that dominated in PE-fed yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenericutes is another dominant bacterial phylum found in the gut microbiota of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenericutes is a bacterial phylum whose relative abundance increased in PS- and CS-fed groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenericutes are a phylum of bacteria identified as indicator taxa in the gut microbiomes of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenericutes is a bacterial phylum that shows increased abundance in PP-fed yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenericutes is the dominant phylum in PP-fed groups, highlighting its role in shaping the gut bacterial community with specific diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenericutes is a bacterial phylum identified in the gut microbiota of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenericutes is a class of bacteria that includes orders such as Entomoplasmatales."</data>
