    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENTOMOPLASMATALES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORDER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An order commonly found in insects, potentially pathogenic when increased in PE-oxo diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Entomoplasmatales has an average abundance of 1.1%, significantly higher in the PE-oxo variant."&lt;SEP&gt;"Entomoplasmatales is a bacterial order found in mealworm guts, contributing to digestion and nutrient processing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Entomoplasmatales is a bacterial order found in the gut microbiome of mealworms, influencing digestion and nutrient uptake."&lt;SEP&gt;"Entomoplasmatales is an order of bacteria commonly found in insect gut microbiomes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Entomoplasmatales is an order of bacteria commonly found in insect symbiosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Entomoplasmatales is an order of bacteria implicated in symbiotic relationships with insects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Entomoplasmatales is an order within the class Tenericutes, containing genera like Spiroplasma."&lt;SEP&gt;"Entomoplasmatales are bacterial orders involved in insect symbiosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Entomoplasmatales is a bacterial order involved in insect symbiosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Entomoplasmatales is an order within the class Tenericutes, containing genera like Spiroplasma."</data>
