    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPIROPLASMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A bacterial genus associated with the control diet and Diet 3 in the gut microbiome of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Spiroplasma is a genus of bacteria associated with polyethylene degradation in the gut of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Spiroplasma is a genus of bacteria found in the order Entomoplasmatales."&lt;SEP&gt;"Spiroplasma is a genus of bacteria associated with the degradation of PET polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Spiroplasma is a genus found at higher levels in normal diet bran-fed larvae compared to those fed with PE and PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"A genus within Tenericutes that decreased throughout the experiment but was not harmful in the mealworm gut."&lt;SEP&gt;"Spiroplasma is a genus found in high abundance in both PS- and CS-fed larvae compared to CB-fed larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Spiroplasma is a predominant genus found in the gut of mealworms across all diet groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"Spiroplasma is commonly detected in both Tenebrio species across all treatments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Spiroplasma is a genus of anaerobic bacteria present in the posterior gut of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Spiroplasma is a genus of gut-associated microbes commonly found in yellow mealworms and dark mealworms, contributing significantly to the gut microbiome."&lt;SEP&gt;"Spiroplasma is a predominant bacterium in the mealworm gut microbiome, potentially aiding digestion."&lt;SEP&gt;"Spiroplasma is a genus of bacteria identified in the gut of mealworms, some species of which are insect pathogens but do not harm T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Spiroplasma becomes dominant in PP-fed groups, accounting for 52.61%, linking it closely to PP degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Spiroplasma is a genus of bacteria found significantly in the gut microbiome of PP-fed T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Spiroplasma is a genus that was significantly higher in PP-fed groups, strongly associated with PP degradation and common in the yellow mealworm gut microbiome."&lt;SEP&gt;"Spiroplasma is a genus of bacteria with observed relative abundance changes in the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"Spiroplasma is a genus of bacteria found in the order Entomoplasmatales."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a3f07da33b55bf8a25fe06beee23e90e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25f3365d0b08e5e77183d813ce6a1049&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-630e33352368a0c7f34d56ad45a38e56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54f22136b514092aeeb2f431170b6ed6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5982537ede5118840b65596ee2a04896&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eaf1f7b81bc271c665d7776cc3114a92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-476e13b69587aa4e81395e2fd00a9d5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df045e015825dac8935c9c6d8a402cda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49ebafd73759fc2bf3d4a642ccad96e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2122660fcfebecf752000198a16f222&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bd3778dedc6a0463017df9f8d6396eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d7500fe4985cb2b885f9eb244ed3c2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e127a4930b6154498b93c2e94f2b7c20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6746a90a5be233f46211ddf406c02e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32f340b7166025be3c56178a94ae480d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81f09d7c1a5d91a7a0b4766ca0e47f56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e1faf524e6fabeb512a07b13f37e51e</data>
    </node>
