    <node id="&quot;TRYPSIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Trypsin is a proteolytic enzyme responsible for breaking down proteins into smaller peptides."&lt;SEP&gt;"Trypsin is a serine protease enzyme responsible for breaking down proteins into smaller peptides."&lt;SEP&gt;"Trypsin is an enzyme used to detach cells during passaging in cell culture."&lt;SEP&gt;"Trypsin is an enzyme that plays a role in digestion, particularly in breaking down proteins into smaller peptides."&lt;SEP&gt;"Trypsin is a serine protease enzyme responsible for breaking down proteins into smaller peptides."&lt;SEP&gt;"Trypsin was a proteolytic enzyme analyzed in the study but did not show significant differences across experimental variants."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2aeb4d96b02258056c16688ea13a9e90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1c9087e78bc6ba94c2b63fd88d2ca66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54f22136b514092aeeb2f431170b6ed6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c0c246e98a503a16ace92f28394b584&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db672d5836dfe372ee7c47ee4dd6fbd3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;Z-CHYMOTRYPSIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"z-Chymotrypsin is a serine protease enzyme that cleaves peptide bonds at aromatic amino acids."&lt;SEP&gt;"z-Chymotrypsin is a serine protease enzyme that cleaves peptide bonds at aromatic amino acids."&lt;SEP&gt;"z-Chymotrypsin is an enzyme with measured activity levels in the digestive tract and bacterial consortia, showing consistent values across different variants."&lt;SEP&gt;"z-Chymotrypsin is an enzyme with measured activity levels in the digestive tract and bacterial consortia, showing consistent values across different variants."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-54f22136b514092aeeb2f431170b6ed6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ce1f7a057da80b206f8354c70d120c9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OAT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DIET"</data>
      <data key="d1">"OAT refers to oatmeal waste, which serves as a substrate for bacterial activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"OAT refers to oatmeal waste, which serves as a substrate for bacterial activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"OAT refers to oatmeal, used as one of the diets for Tenebrio molitor larvae in the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"OAT represents a diet based on oatmeal, with specific protein and fatty acid content as shown in the table."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oatmeal diet fed to insect larvae, associated with low larval counts but high metamorphosis rates and fewer dead insects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oat is a dietary supplement added to the larval diet in some experimental groups, providing additional nutrition but not fully restoring growth and reproduction."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oat is a dietary supplement provided to larvae to improve their survival and growth conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oat refers to a dietary supplement provided alongside PS to enhance nutritional value for the larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a38885f67ed46b97bb84086f575fd43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ead6f17ad517015b638608c5bfe6852&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54f22136b514092aeeb2f431170b6ed6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02f21478b87845df31740b3dab37d197&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5740f0973ff804cae61f6fc12f3e3753&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f71fddc259d51158d5c79f38bf41523f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CEL refers to cardboard, another diet tested for its effects on Tenebrio molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"CEL refers to cardboard, used as a nutrient source in microbial studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"CEL represents a diet based on cardboard, showing specific protein and fatty acid content as indicated in the table."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cardboard diet, similar in development pattern to PE-oxo group and showing moderate results in terms of larval development and metamorphosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"CEL refers to cardboard, used as a nutrient source in microbial studies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-54f22136b514092aeeb2f431170b6ed6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a38885f67ed46b97bb84086f575fd43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02f21478b87845df31740b3dab37d197&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ead6f17ad517015b638608c5bfe6852</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PE-OXO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Oxo-degradable polyethylene diet, associated with low metamorphosis rates and high mortality."&lt;SEP&gt;"PE-oxo represents a diet based on oxo-degradable polyethylene, forming part of a homogeneous group with PE-reg."&lt;SEP&gt;"PE-oxo represents oxo-degradable polyethylene, a plastic-based diet included in the experiment."&lt;SEP&gt;"PE-oxo represents oxo-degradable polyethylene, a type of plastic material."&lt;SEP&gt;"PE-oxo represents oxo-degradable polyethylene, a type of plastic material."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-54f22136b514092aeeb2f431170b6ed6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a38885f67ed46b97bb84086f575fd43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02f21478b87845df31740b3dab37d197&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ead6f17ad517015b638608c5bfe6852</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PE-REG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PE-reg denotes polyethylene regranulate, another plastic-based diet tested for its impact on Tenebrio molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"PE-reg refers to polyethylene regranulate, a recycled plastic material."&lt;SEP&gt;"PE-reg represents a diet based on polyethylene regranulate, similar to PE-oxo and forming a homogeneous group."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene regranulate diet, showing development patterns similar to OAT diet but with moderate mortality and relatively high adult production."&lt;SEP&gt;"PE-reg refers to polyethylene regranulate, a recycled plastic material."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-54f22136b514092aeeb2f431170b6ed6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a38885f67ed46b97bb84086f575fd43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02f21478b87845df31740b3dab37d197&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ead6f17ad517015b638608c5bfe6852</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIGESTIVE TRACT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Digestive Tract refers to the location where enzymatic activities are measured in the context of enzymatic functionality."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Digestive Tract refers to the location where enzymatic activities are measured in the context of enzymatic functionality."&lt;SEP&gt;"The digestive tract is the part of the body involved in digestion and absorption of nutrients."&lt;SEP&gt;"The digestive tract of T. molitor larvae was dissected to isolate gut bacteria under sterile conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The digestive tract is a part of the body responsible for digestion and nutrient absorption, here specifically referring to the larval digestive system."&lt;SEP&gt;"The digestive tract of mealworm larvae was excised for DNA extraction and microbial community analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"The digestive tract is the part of the body involved in digestion and absorption of nutrients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-39c4ff9e5812f88117b37503a70b0479&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54f22136b514092aeeb2f431170b6ed6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-512840a413df7ae3d881389c5cf1feb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-246606838d14d58d03d733b6250a0460&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ce1f7a057da80b206f8354c70d120c9</data>
    </node>
