    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENZYME ACTIVITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Enzyme activity in both the mealworm and its gut microbiome is investigated for understanding plastic degradation mechanisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzyme activity refers to the catalytic capability of enzymes, influencing biological processes like phosphatase activity in soils."&lt;SEP&gt;"The enzymatic activity of bacterial consortia was observed and measured, with significant differences noted across various experimental variants."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzyme activity refers to the rate at which enzymes catalyze biochemical reactions, influencing processes like plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzyme activity refers to the catalytic action of enzymes involved in breaking down complex molecules like plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"The activity of enzymes was characterized by significantly lower values in bacterial consortia across variants CEL, PE-oxo, and PS. The activity reduction in variant PE-reg was the highest at 29 pmol."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2aeb4d96b02258056c16688ea13a9e90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1c9087e78bc6ba94c2b63fd88d2ca66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e3058d086d89f1ce9baa29cbc29bb48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07aae06c64778453da4bda48f5347de5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3667703f7416ebab666e65b375dd8582&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7a49f1c1e76d6e987e0aa499923d3f3</data>
    </node>
