      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"\(\beta\)-Glucuronidase was highly active and showed no significant differences across experimental variants."&lt;SEP&gt;"\(\beta\)-glucuronidase is another highly active enzyme in the group, playing a role in carbohydrate breakdown."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2aeb4d96b02258056c16688ea13a9e90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1c9087e78bc6ba94c2b63fd88d2ca66</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ESTERASE C4&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Esterase C4 is correlated with the CEL variant and contributes to fat hydrolysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Esterase C4 was correlated with variant CEL, indicating its secretion in that dietary condition."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2aeb4d96b02258056c16688ea13a9e90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1c9087e78bc6ba94c2b63fd88d2ca66</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\(\ALPHA\)-CHYMOTRYPSIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"\(\alpha\)-Chymotrypsin was clearly correlated with variant CEL, suggesting its role in protein breakdown under this condition."&lt;SEP&gt;"\(\alpha\)-chymotrypsin is associated with the CEL variant and participates in protein digestion."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2aeb4d96b02258056c16688ea13a9e90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1c9087e78bc6ba94c2b63fd88d2ca66</data>
    </node>
