      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"\(\beta\)-Glucosidase was one of the enzymes analyzed and showed no significant differences across experimental variants."&lt;SEP&gt;"\(\beta\)-glucosidase is an enzyme involved in carbohydrate metabolism, showing activity across various experimental variants."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2aeb4d96b02258056c16688ea13a9e90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1c9087e78bc6ba94c2b63fd88d2ca66</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;N-ACETYL-\(\BETA\)-GLUCOSAMINIDASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"N-acetyl-\(\beta\)-Glucosaminidase was analyzed as part of the study and showed no significant differences across experimental variants."&lt;SEP&gt;"N-acetyl-\(\beta\)-glucosaminidase is an enzyme active in the group of studied enzymes, participating in carbohydrate breakdown."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2aeb4d96b02258056c16688ea13a9e90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1c9087e78bc6ba94c2b63fd88d2ca66</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\(\ALPHA\)-GLUCOSIDASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"\(\alpha\)-Glucosidase was involved in carbohydrate metabolism and was studied for its enzymatic activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"\(\alpha\)-glucosidase is an enzyme contributing to carbohydrate hydrolysis within the studied variants."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2aeb4d96b02258056c16688ea13a9e90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1c9087e78bc6ba94c2b63fd88d2ca66</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\(\ALPHA\)-MANNOSIDASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"\(\alpha\)-Mannosidase was involved in glycoprotein metabolism and was included in the enzymatic analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"\(\alpha\)-mannosidase is an enzyme playing a role in glycoprotein degradation and carbohydrate metabolism."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2aeb4d96b02258056c16688ea13a9e90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1c9087e78bc6ba94c2b63fd88d2ca66</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\(\ALPHA\)-FUCOSIDASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"\(\alpha\)-Fucosidase was involved in fucose-containing glycan metabolism and was analyzed in the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"\(\alpha\)-fucosidase is an enzyme involved in the breakdown of fucose-containing glycans."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2aeb4d96b02258056c16688ea13a9e90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1c9087e78bc6ba94c2b63fd88d2ca66</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CYSTINE ARYLAMIDASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cystine arylamidase is an enzyme involved in sulfur-containing amino acid metabolism."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cystine arylamidase was involved in sulfur-containing amino acid metabolism and was part of the analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2aeb4d96b02258056c16688ea13a9e90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1c9087e78bc6ba94c2b63fd88d2ca66</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHOSPHORUS BONDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL BOND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Phosphorus bonds are chemical bonds that are broken down by specific enzymes, such as phosphatases."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2aeb4d96b02258056c16688ea13a9e90</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INDOXACARB INSECTICIDE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TOXIN"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Indoxacarb insecticide is degraded by esterase-producing bacteria found in the digestive tracts of insects."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2aeb4d96b02258056c16688ea13a9e90</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PSEUDOMONAS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pseudomonas is a bacterial genus known to produce esterases, contributing to the degradation of complex compounds like indoxacarb insecticide and potentially plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas is a genus identified in the gut microbiota of mealworms for nitrogen fixation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas is another genus of bacteria involved in the degradation process of PP films."&lt;SEP&gt;Pseudomonas is a versatile bacterial genus within the γ-proteobacteria class of the phylum Proteobacteria. Known for its metabolic versatility, Pseudomonas includes Gram-negative, rod-shaped, and aerobic bacteria that play significant roles in the degradation of various synthetic polymers and complex compounds. This genus is particularly noted for its ability to degrade plastics such as polystyrene (PS), polyethylene, polyurethane, and bioplastics, often through enzymatic processes like esterase production.

Pseudomonas has been detected in the gut microbiome of several insect species, including Tenebrio molitor (mealworms) and superworms, where it contributes to the breakdown of plastics ingested by these organisms. Studies indicate that Pseudomonas becomes significantly more abundant in the gut microbiomes of larvae fed with plastic substrates, such as PS or polypropylene (PP), suggesting an adaptive response to the diet. For instance, Pseudomonas accounted for a substantial proportion (7.68%) in PP-fed groups and was also observed as a dominant genus in polyolefin-fed larvae, highlighting its role in degrading these materials.

Research has shown that Pseudomonas exhibits variability in bacterial communities depending on the type of plastic substrate consumed, with two distinct species identified in some studies. Additionally, Pseudomonas chlororaphis, a member of this genus, exemplifies the group's metabolic flexibility. The genus is consistently over-represented in samples from insects fed plastics, with log2-fold changes ranging from 4.1 to 6.5, further emphasizing its importance in plastic degradation.

Beyond plastic degradation, Pseudomonas is involved in styrene degradation and contributes to the assembly factors of gut microbiomes. Its presence in the gut microbiota of T. molitor larvae has been confirmed through 16S ribosomal RNA gene sequencing, reinforcing its ecological significance in both natural and engineered environments. Overall, Pseudomonas represents a key player in microbial-driven plastic biodegradation and highlights the potential of harnessing bacterial metabolism for environmental remediation.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-67425e341a5b2c8102281581fa148554&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e127a4930b6154498b93c2e94f2b7c20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93d5b1c190fdca6b5e456b1513515be4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1c9087e78bc6ba94c2b63fd88d2ca66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b42ef7860e1f056d47955d0d13a15cd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2961e2aad708e7b78a585260097b4d2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e81871d41a32fbdcbbd4f699efae3d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6ddf9dd30d7258964408f9a915d3478&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3815960770483b9c0a1579ca8442e3a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14f9f0280098bb86719394a4bd53e5bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa10245aaff722ac7d69e73bed8afe74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1070f8c33eb8afcfcffac95df9012d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa9972450967f344c19cb747d7ce649e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-188daf7716cd1d683a79562bf4d6ab90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c02a8ea5e75c58dcb9cfbbcd64f37d82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e1faf524e6fabeb512a07b13f37e51e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2aeb4d96b02258056c16688ea13a9e90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0caad5c42a4b470a8c41ac3fb68c1f64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2122660fcfebecf752000198a16f222&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6746a90a5be233f46211ddf406c02e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81f09d7c1a5d91a7a0b4766ca0e47f56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-681a7143730d41e569d0d76a926eb069&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3f07da33b55bf8a25fe06beee23e90e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-476e13b69587aa4e81395e2fd00a9d5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b4b45d826a6a7956015e680f5fb8ee6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d7500fe4985cb2b885f9eb244ed3c2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-001e8f54368c9a236f702fd09cddf4a8</data>
    </node>
