      <data key="d1">"Enzymatic activity involves the catalytic action of enzymes in breaking down complex molecules, including plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzymatic activity is involved in the breakdown of PS, influenced by the presence of water and bran in the diet."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzymatic activity is modified due to the incorporation of PS into the insects' diet."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzymatic activity pertains to the catalytic action of enzymes in biochemical reactions, essential for polymer degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzymatic activity refers to the rate at which enzymes catalyze biochemical reactions in the bacterial community."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzymatic activity refers to the biochemical reactions catalyzed by enzymes, contributing to the breakdown of plastics in insect larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzymatic activity refers to the catalytic action of enzymes that facilitate biochemical reactions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzymatic activity refers to the action of enzymes involved in the breakdown of complex molecules like plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzymatic activity refers to the metabolic processes occurring in T. molitor larvae that contribute to the breakdown of PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzymatic activity refers to the rate at which enzymes catalyze biochemical reactions, such as the degradation of PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzymatic activity refers to the biochemical reactions catalyzed by enzymes, enabling microorganisms to degrade plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"The action of enzymes in facilitating chemical reactions, such as the degradation of plastics by gut microbiota."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzymatic activity refers to the rate at which enzymes catalyze biochemical reactions within a bacterial community."</data>
