    <node id="&quot;PSEUDOMONADALES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORDER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pseudomonadales forms a small part of microbial communities, with an average of 1.4%, higher in PE-reg and PS variants."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonadales is a bacterial order present in mealworm guts, playing roles in nutrient breakdown."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonadales is an order of bacteria involved in symbiotic relationships with insects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonadales is an order of bacteria often associated with diverse metabolic activities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonadales include bacteria that enter into symbiotic relationships with insects."</data>
