      <data key="d0">"ORDER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Xanthomonadales contribute to symbiotic relationships with insects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Xanthomonadales is a bacterial order associated with symbiotic relationships contributing to nitrogen fixation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Xanthomonadales is an order of bacteria associated with symbiotic relationships and enzymatic activities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Xanthomonadales is an order of bacteria involved in symbiotic relationships with insects."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-edad11f4e8936fcfb69f8616ad364f18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47c76e5149ac059b1960b533c9e99a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d13e8c770c847882a94a6b78b0979cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0855091c2b50520d68971a532789a9a2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WOLBACHIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Wolbachia is a genus of bacteria known for its symbiotic relationship with various insects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wolbachia is a genus of bacteria often found as endosymbionts in insects, influencing metabolic and reproductive processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wolbachia is a genus of intracellular bacteria commonly found in arthropods and implicated in symbiotic interactions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wolbachia is a genus of bacteria that form symbiotic relationships with insects."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-edad11f4e8936fcfb69f8616ad364f18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47c76e5149ac059b1960b533c9e99a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d13e8c770c847882a94a6b78b0979cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0855091c2b50520d68971a532789a9a2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NASUTITERMES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nasutitermes is a genus of termites harboring a stable microbial community responsible for cellulose degradation, nitrogen cycling, and fermentation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-edad11f4e8936fcfb69f8616ad364f18</data>
