    <node id="&quot;DIAZOTROPHS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Diazotrophs are microorganisms capable of fixing atmospheric nitrogen, contributing to nutrient distribution in insect-hosted environments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diazotrophs are nitrogen-fixing bacteria that supplement the nitrogen supply for insects on low-nitrogen diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diazotrophs are microorganisms capable of nitrogen fixation, often found in the guts of various organisms such as earthworms and insects."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-edad11f4e8936fcfb69f8616ad364f18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0817d79fa27f2f5b078e09086250c6e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fa884bb7540491e8ab975e29c46d1f1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OBIALES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORDER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Obiales is an order of fungi or microorganisms that may play a role in nitrogen fixation and enzymatic processes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d47c76e5149ac059b1960b533c9e99a5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;N-FIXING BACTERIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"N-fixing Bacteria are microorganisms capable of nitrogen fixation, providing nitrogen to larvae consuming plastic diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrogen-fixing bacteria are microorganisms capable of converting atmospheric nitrogen into ammonia, essential for nitrogen assimilation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrogen-fixing bacteria are microorganisms capable of converting atmospheric nitrogen into ammonia."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d290a6a81802d3048c35d2a2fb1252c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47c76e5149ac059b1960b533c9e99a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0855091c2b50520d68971a532789a9a2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NITROGENASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nitrogenase is an enzyme responsible for catalyzing the reduction of N₂ to NH₃ in nitrogen fixation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrogenase is an enzyme responsible for the reduction of molecular nitrogen (N2) to ammonia (NH3), requiring trace elements like iron, sulfur, vanadium, and manganese."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrogenase is the enzyme responsible for converting nitrogen gas into ammonia, a key process in nitrogen fixation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrogenase is an enzyme responsible for nitrogen fixation, requiring trace elements such as iron, sulfur, vanadium, and manganese."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d47c76e5149ac059b1960b533c9e99a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53ab7dd83bf51674598c6a5bdd146b90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b12451ba2a22e6f74c543f982a0a7b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0855091c2b50520d68971a532789a9a2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IRON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Iron is a trace element critical for the function of nitrogenase and other biochemical processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Iron is a trace element essential for the activity of nitrogenase enzyme."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d47c76e5149ac059b1960b533c9e99a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0855091c2b50520d68971a532789a9a2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SULFUR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sulfur is a trace element required for the functionality of nitrogenase enzyme."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sulfur is a trace element required for the structure and function of enzymes such as nitrogenase."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d47c76e5149ac059b1960b533c9e99a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0855091c2b50520d68971a532789a9a2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VANADIUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Vanadium is a trace element involved in enzymatic processes, including nitrogen fixation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vanadium is a trace element that contributes to the active site of nitrogenase enzyme."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d47c76e5149ac059b1960b533c9e99a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0855091c2b50520d68971a532789a9a2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MANGANESE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Manganese is a trace element important for enzymatic activity and biological functions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Manganese is a trace element necessary for the activity of nitrogenase enzyme."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d47c76e5149ac059b1960b533c9e99a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0855091c2b50520d68971a532789a9a2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PARABACTEROIDES SPP.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Parabacteroides is a genus of anaerobic bacteria capable of degrading complex polymers like hemicellulose and polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Parabacteroides is a genus of anaerobic bacteria involved in the decomposition of hemicellulose and polyethylene."</data>
