    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ATMOSPHERIC NITROGEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Atmospheric Nitrogen is a critical nutrient source for organisms capable of nitrogen fixation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Atmospheric nitrogen (N2) is a primary source of nitrogen for nitrogen-fixing bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Atmospheric nitrogen is a critical nutrient that is converted into bioavailable forms through nitrogen fixation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d47c76e5149ac059b1960b533c9e99a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-813b71242f366f10218c10631cd7dee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20a69982e6abe36c2a0d4a70b78720ec</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRACE ELEMENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Trace Elements are vital nutrients required for long-term survival and growth, not present in PP."&lt;SEP&gt;"Trace elements such as iron, sulfur, vanadium, and manganese are essential for enzymatic activities like nitrogen fixation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Trace elements are micronutrients present in bran, necessary for the overall health of T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Trace elements are essential micronutrients required for various biological processes, including enzyme production."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cd3092744be0c66dad5833977dedd913&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47c76e5149ac059b1960b533c9e99a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdc8398efba587929eebd0a0842f6e69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77a9d70651c9f13362e4c1e3ce10eab0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WATER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An essential component added to some diets to enhance PS consumption by larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Water forms during the metabolic process in frass collected from mealworms from Guangzhou when fed with PVC."&lt;SEP&gt;"Water is a critical component in nutrient-deficient habitats, influencing metabolic processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Water is critical for larval growth and survival. Its presence or absence affects the degradation of PS by larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Water is an essential nutrient included in the diets of mealworm larvae during the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"Water is essential for the growth and survival of T. molitor larvae, influencing their feeding behavior and PS degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tap water used to wet the paper towels and mix with protein powder for supplemental nutrition."&lt;SEP&gt;"Water is an essential component of all living organisms, included in one of the experimental diets to study its effects on insect metabolism."&lt;SEP&gt;"Water plays a crucial role in enhancing the degradation of PS when present in the diet of insects, particularly in Diet 2."&lt;SEP&gt;"Water is essential for maintaining hydration and supporting metabolic processes in larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c810740a381d4d9e829e28c01e62564&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e25fe1af3bede4605e7b94d457c9634&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c4244cae75095bda7fb526c3d0c9d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3eb3742a8be739a1146cbf15e6b7ae5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84f576487c8d473c1524eb1141730a12&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c11c77665793ac79aecfb19a89dd1f52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a708f09b97ac93da05bd1d20bdfe174&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47c76e5149ac059b1960b533c9e99a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ed721221326657b60aadb09faeeac92</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEMICELLULOSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A polysaccharide found in plant materials, degraded by T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hemicellulose is a polysaccharide found in plant cell walls, degraded by anaerobic bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hemicellulose is a polysaccharide found in plant cell walls, degraded alongside cellulose and lignin."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hemicellulose is a polysaccharide found in plant cell walls, digested to a lesser extent compared to cellulose."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hemicellulose is a complex carbohydrate degraded by specific gut bacteria in mealworm larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-158317f8eba5f6198135df044d385935&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0855091c2b50520d68971a532789a9a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d39fc863538a777920c4eafb37bcf8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5dc0ba5d8a1abfb746af0dedb7d575b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47c76e5149ac059b1960b533c9e99a5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HYDROLYTIC ENZYMES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hydrolytic enzymes are involved in the breakdown of polymers in the digestive tract of T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hydrolytic enzymes are involved in the breakdown of polymers into simpler compounds."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d47c76e5149ac059b1960b533c9e99a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0855091c2b50520d68971a532789a9a2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANAEROBIC BACTERIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROBE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Anaerobic bacteria assist in the decomposition of PET under oxygen-depleted conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anaerobic bacteria thrive in oxygen-deprived environments and participate in the degradation of complex polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacteria that thrive in the absence of oxygen, participating in the breakdown of PET."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d47c76e5149ac059b1960b533c9e99a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b715dc0bf578795b387fe1255d07f22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df5e2448d1e9703b511b85725469467e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROTEIN SYNTHESIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Protein synthesis is a biological process where amino acids are polymerized to form proteins, facilitated by nitrogen assimilation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d47c76e5149ac059b1960b533c9e99a5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GUT FLAGELLATES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gut Flagellates are microorganisms found in the guts of termites, hosting Bacteroidales ectosymbionts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut flagellates are microorganisms found in the digestive system of termites, interacting with Bacteroidales ectosymbionts to shape the nitrogen-fixing community."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-412d934721b214c2cd0565531172171c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7a49f1c1e76d6e987e0aa499923d3f3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NITROGEN-FIXING COMMUNITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Nitrogen-fixing Community refers to microorganisms involved in nitrogen fixation within the termite gut environment."&lt;SEP&gt;"The nitrogen-fixing community refers to microorganisms involved in converting atmospheric nitrogen into a usable form within the termite gut ecosystem."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-412d934721b214c2cd0565531172171c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7a49f1c1e76d6e987e0aa499923d3f3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DRY-WOOD TERMITES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dry-wood Termites are insects whose gut microbiota plays a role in nitrogen fixation and involves symbiotic relationships."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dry-wood termites are insects known for their ability to digest wood and host specific gut microbiota that facilitate nitrogen fixation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-412d934721b214c2cd0565531172171c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7a49f1c1e76d6e987e0aa499923d3f3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLASTIC DEBRIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"POLLUTANT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Plastic Debris represents polymeric materials that pose a threat to marine environments due to their persistence and potential toxicity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic debris includes various forms of plastic waste found in the environment, contributing to pollution."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic debris refers to waste materials derived from plastic consumption by larvae, used for calculating PS or PU consumption."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic debris refers to waste materials made of plastic that pollute natural environments, particularly marine ecosystems."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a38c714e7f1f701ec1149e25910e16e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d76cb64e0aa4e4039b70799a0df8943d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7a49f1c1e76d6e987e0aa499923d3f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aface14c9ee7dd5ccd25e7094ed5c1c7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYMERIC MATERIALS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polymeric Materials include plastics that drift in marine environments, causing ecological concerns."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polymeric materials encompass a wide range of synthetic polymers subject to microbiological degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polymeric materials refer to synthetic polymers such as plastics that pose environmental threats when not properly disposed of, particularly in marine environments."</data>
