      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mealworms are insects used in the study to biodegrade polystyrene, showing changes in their lipidome and protein content."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms, specifically Tenebrio molitor, are insects studied for their ability to consume styrofoam waste."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms are larvae of the darkling beetle, capable of biodegrading polystyrene and other plastics through gut microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms are the larvae of Tenebrio molitor, capable of digesting plastics such as PS and PE with the help of their gut microbiota."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor larvae, commonly known as mealworms, are insects studied for their gut microbiota's ability to degrade plastics."</data>
