      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Advanced sequencing technology used to analyze complex microbial communities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Next-Generation Sequencing is a high-throughput sequencing technology used to analyze metagenomic data."&lt;SEP&gt;"Next-generation sequencing is a technology used to analyze differentially expressed genes in mealworms fed on plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Next-generation sequencing is a technology used to explore the larval gut microbiome and investigate the effects of PS diets on microbial communities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Next-generation sequencing refers to advanced technologies that enable rapid and cost-effective DNA sequencing, widely used in genomic research."&lt;SEP&gt;"Next-generation sequencing is a modern technique used to analyze changes in the genetic composition of microbial communities, such as the mealworm gut microbiome."&lt;SEP&gt;"Next-generation sequencing is a technology used to analyze the gut microbiome of mealworms, identifying key bacterial species involved in plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Next-generation sequencing is used to analyze the gut microbiome, revealing specific OTUs associated with PP-fed microbiomes in Z. atratus and T. molitor larvae."</data>
