    <node id="&quot;CARBOXYLESTERASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Carboxylesterase enzymes are active toward PET oligomers and play a role in their degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carboxylesterase hydrolyzes ester bonds in various substrates, including those found in plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carboxylesterase is an enzyme involved in the degradation of indoxylcarb, found in gut bacterial flora isolated from diamondback moth, Plutella xylostella."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carboxylesterase is an enzyme involved in the hydrolysis of carboxylic esters and exhibits amide-related activities, playing a role in metabolizing drugs and xenobiotics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carboxylesterase plays a role in the breakdown of ester bonds found in polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carboxylesterase is an enzyme involved in the hydrolysis of ester bonds, contributing to the degradation of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carboxylesterase is an enzyme that hydrolyzes carboxylic esters."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carboxylesterase is an enzyme that was reported to be very active toward PET oligomers, indicating its role in the degradation of plastics."</data>
