      <data key="d1">"Diverse microbial communities from soils, seawater, sediments, sludge, and compost are involved in the biodegradation of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbial Communities encompass the diverse range of microorganisms involved in processes such as dark fermentation and enzymatic hydrolysates."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbial communities consist of various microorganisms interacting within specific environments, such as gut flora or fuel cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"The microbial communities within the gut of mealworms play a key role in the biodegradation process of plastics like polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbial communities are crucial in maintaining stable environments for effective plastic biodegradation processes."</data>
