      <data key="d1">"Diet affects the development time and survival rate of mealworms, indicating its importance in their growth and polystyrene degradation ability."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diet refers to the food consumed by an organism, which influences the composition and activity of the gut microbiome."&lt;SEP&gt;"The activity of \(\beta\)-glucosidase varies depending on the diet variant, indicating dietary influence on enzymatic activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diet refers to the types of food consumed by an organism, with mealworms being explored as a sustainable dietary component."&lt;SEP&gt;"Different compositions of food provided to mealworm larvae during the experiment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Different diets were tested to observe their effects on the growth and survival of T. molitor larvae, with Diet 3 requiring the least handling."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diet significantly influences the gut microbiota composition in T. molitor, affecting bacterial diversity and functionality."&lt;SEP&gt;"The diet consisted of bran food supplemented with antibiotics, fed to larvae for 8 days."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diet represents the types of food consumed by organisms, influencing their physiological responses and microbial composition."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diet refers to the food consumed by organisms, influencing their growth, development, and overall health."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diet refers to the different food compositions fed to the insects, influencing their growth and metabolic outputs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Different diets, including PE, PS, PVC, and wheat bran, were provided to mealworms during the experiment."</data>
