    <node id="&quot;HDPE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"High-density polyethylene (HDPE) serves as a comparative material in the study of LDPE biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;High-density polyethylene (HDPE) is a type of plastic polymer characterized by its high strength-to-density ratio, durability, and resistance to microbial degradation due to its high molecular weight, polymer structure without functional groups, and hydrophobicity. HDPE contributes approximately 12.9% of total plastics globally and exhibits higher crystallinity and density compared to low-density polyethylene (LDPE), which significantly affects its physical properties, biodegradability, and stability. It is widely used in commercial applications such as packaging, containers, and bags because of its strength and durability. Its specific oriented structures result in anisotropic properties, making it distinct from other types of polyethylene like LDPE and linear low-density polyethylene (LLDPE).

Despite its general resistance to microbial degradation, HDPE undergoes biodegradation under certain conditions. Studies have shown that organisms such as mealworms (*Tenebrio* larvae) and insect larvae like *Achroia grisella* can consume and degrade HDPE. This biodegradation process leads to the loss of carbon and hydrogen, weight reduction, and structural changes, often facilitated by bacterial strains like PM S1 or PELW2042. Research has demonstrated that HDPE consumption by mealworms results in relatively low consumption rates compared to polystyrene and causes significant mass reduction during 10- and 30-day intervals, although less mass gain was observed during the 20-day interval.

HDPE is frequently employed in scientific studies for microbial degradation analysis, typically in the form of plastic beads or microplastics. These experiments aim to understand how HDPE influences gut microbiome composition differently compared to other plastics and assess its effects on larval health, including inducing varying levels of oxidative stress and ecotoxicity. HDPE's role in metabolic dysfunction and its potential as a dietary component for studying gut microbiome effects continue to be explored in various studies. Molecular weights of HDPE used in such studies range from 105,000 to 132,700 Da. While HDPE degrades more slowly than LDPE, it remains an important subject in research focused on plastic degradation and its ecological impacts.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-939fc2ea222a49f84f9bdc11f9801367&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-602bba09eb2c308c400b412f39f4adb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff201df58dec460c49cd31920c29f11a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-475b22fe6100b14cced604f739663fe4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fd075a78abe1dca64ddea928d3f94b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8eca628f2d85c664191a5205194ec475&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb16cd27b6682965375050748ee77862&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30a7209d626a6319ba5600bea7f27299&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16a478461d1471ca083f90b3f8e7456e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6675480dfd01dcb533166d01b8e5482e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b30daa90b5c91314e1d65e87f191166&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa33fb34ba06610c290cdfd8a5b4e916&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90367ecb21e0f14b2e548acf307a2628&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2169963c4d6dae9b98da331d39eaa72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b42ef7860e1f056d47955d0d13a15cd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9528beb2e85a7fb89449a9233eb979bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26a193cc62c03cb6460b0434df42d8c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3646a65acc7cbdc1d20742888b17613a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd4d84d6de496440fcabc6616d1c96ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ab754d1dc0a02ee3f869d2b082a710e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ac1b1db6ffab6f4cfea7a525785a2fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e1faf524e6fabeb512a07b13f37e51e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8c6850a83a1c6efd4f1a3a37a0a8181&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd73d3cca5434181ee9dd1ad1b8f8ab9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98d4ea946a931acf7e5a8292c30ea4c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffb4e34985ec90215629dc19750c8bdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc908e62eec4d1d05265c6e451cca84c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21d8b17fc7993bee31f7e07e4db97cfa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b21eb0db725b38c3e0b5c01526ce90b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f75b58db5211fc7348ccca8206b9bbae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a24fcfbc571e8620a1fc59b215b42e56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-262bed73e929944e03b9f72769b8196c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-361c5d4ba2e879627f4eb7fc4011ee3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-970b4f5f0c494fbc90aab36156ecc044&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3380732c060363504db5f6e4b8610b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c6c5d405260e0a6f512a9504195dc0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70bab3579af07d0f99a5f948a90fe1e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1006283f24aba2aa605f9e719f36cf9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22e4b8000531766cffd145ef32353af2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b387da8298c55673284dca93ea82fc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-988ef11180899