      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"S1 is a bacterial isolate that showed effective growth, high adhesion, hydrophobicity, and potential in degrading LDPE, HDPE, and PS beads."&lt;SEP&gt;"S1 is a bacterium with potential for breaking down polystyrene and enhancing plant growth, exhibiting biopesticidal and antifungal properties."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ed48dc66abf9c27721101b1adac15e7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-939fc2ea222a49f84f9bdc11f9801367</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXTRACELLULAR ENZYMES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Enzymes secreted by fungi that play a crucial role in breaking down polyurethane (PU) plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzymes secreted by microorganisms that facilitate the degradation of PU."&lt;SEP&gt;"Extracellular enzymes are produced by bacteria like S1 to break down polymers such as LDPE, HDPE, and PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Extracellular enzymes, including hydrolases and oxidases, are secreted by microbes and the host to initiate PET degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Extracellular enzymes are secreted outside cells and play a role in breaking down external substrates like PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Extracellular enzymes are secreted by gut microbiota and catalyze the depolymerization of polystyrene fragments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Extracellular enzymes are secreted by gut bacteria to break down polystyrene polymer chains, playing a critical role in biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Extracellular enzymes are proteins secreted by microorganisms that facilitate the breakdown of polyurethane bonds during biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Extracellular enzymes are proteins secreted by microorganisms to degrade external substrates like lignin or plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Secreted by the host and microbiota, these enzymes play a role in PET depolymerization."&lt;SEP&gt;"Extracellular enzymes are hypothesized to play a role in the degradation of polyethylene by A. grisella larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Extracellular enzymes are proteins secreted by organisms that may play a role in the degradation of polyethylene by A. grisella larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Extracellular enzymes are produced by gut microbes in Tenebrio molitor larvae to facilitate the breakdown of microplastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-effe1e87d51e126ff4ec5cf9e49d6524&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2c62bcfb28547d6b2336f142d27a326&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab6b219720db5a6e3384c884c280984c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e34d58a20a707b35e8fcd5658ba2924&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-939fc2ea222a49f84f9bdc11f9801367&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e81871d41a32fbdcbbd4f699efae3d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21c07a838ff0a489c73c8319e5011134&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d3b3c7bbc61318a9728caff13ac5b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7367fc6115c08ae427a6e9e91eaa1de3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df5e2448d1e9703b511b85725469467e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-652bf0615ec39fba0cedd113ec87a78a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af5eb6a8326b4977801e2f7694a2c750&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b19ac5bdc755bb8e9deb8e317ce365dd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARBON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A primary energy source and structural component in organic molecules, important for metabolic processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon is an element found in LDPE, HDPE, and PS beads, whose percentage decreases during the degradation process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon serves as a nutrient source for bacteria under carbon-starved conditions, influencing their hydrophobicity and degradation capabilities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon is an essential element derived from the breakdown of polystyrene and incorporated into metabolic processes within mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon is a chemical element detected in the surface analysis of polystyrene using X-ray photoelectron spectroscopy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon is a nutrient derived from plastic consumption, supporting the life activities of yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon is an element present in PP and serves as an energy source for larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-939fc2ea222a49f84f9bdc11f9801367&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06ba9ca61fb4f42582bbf7bd00ff0005&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d0e4cb4324bc684ebb2ca6136c04ad0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd3092744be0c66dad5833977dedd913&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c343b12adf5bbce5bf80b96909fe66d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b30daa90b5c91314e1d65e87f191166&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-262bed73e929944e03b9f72769b8196c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;16S RRNA SEQUENCING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"16S rRNA Sequencing is a molecular method used to identify bacterial isolates like S1."&lt;SEP&gt;"16S rRNA sequencing identifies bacterial species involved in PS degradation from mixed microbial enrichments."&lt;SEP&gt;"A method used to identify bacterial species by analyzing their ribosomal RNA genes."&lt;SEP&gt;"16S rRNA sequencing is a molecular technique used to identify bacterial isolates by comparing their genetic sequences with databases."&lt;SEP&gt;"16S rRNA Sequencing is a technique used to identify and compare bacterial species based on their ribosomal RNA sequences."&lt;SEP&gt;"16S rRNA sequencing is a method used to determine the taxonomic relationships of bacterial strains."&lt;SEP&gt;"16S rRNA sequencing is a technique used to identify bacterial species present in the gut microbiome of the larvae, revealing specific bacteria associated with polypropylene degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"A method used for taxonomic identification of microorganisms based on their ribosomal RNA sequences."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f5613b129e38cb777855c04f228fe7e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-939fc2ea222a49f84f9bdc11f9801367&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39c4ff9e5812f88117b37503a70b0479&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10f59d5d10f08e8107f36bff5a4c93ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe29ef34ad1e5ab11c4ec7f5270fa94d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c310f4f7adc3c5b8340e973a5af45e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eba752cb179633f5dd054ee7c9ee2cba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eda80cb027c8107defa00011d491b002</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NUTRIENT AGAR MEDIUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nutrient agar medium is used as a growth substrate for bacterial isolates in experiments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-939fc2ea222a49f84f9bdc11f9801367</data>
