    <node id="&quot;WEIGHT LOSS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"HEALTH MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A measure of PS degradation determined by comparing initial and residual weights."&lt;SEP&gt;"Weight Loss is a physiological response observed in Tenebrio molitor larvae after ingestion of microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Weight Loss is the reduction in body mass of mealworms due to insufficient nutrients when consuming PU Foam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Weight Loss refers to the reduction in mass of LDPE, HDPE, and PS beads during biodegradation by PM S1."&lt;SEP&gt;"Weight loss indicates the reduction in mass of plastics due to bacterial degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Weight loss measured by DSC-TGA reflects the extent of plastic degradation and the presence of biodegradation byproducts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Weight loss is a physiological response observed in mealworms fed with MPS at older larval stages."&lt;SEP&gt;"Weight loss refers to the reduction in body mass of mealworms due to microplastic exposure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Weight loss is an essential indicator used in the gravimetric determination of biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Weight loss refers to the reduction in mass of PE mulching films due to microbial degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Weight loss is a metric used in biodegradation assays to quantify HDPE degradation by bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Weight loss is an important indicator of HDPE biodegradation, measured as mass reduction during microbial treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Weight loss refers to the reduction in mass of PS samples due to the degradation activity of strain YT2."&lt;SEP&gt;"Weight loss refers to the reduction in mass of polystyrene samples due to microbial degradation by strain YT2."&lt;SEP&gt;"Measurement of polystyrene degradation based on weight reduction."&lt;SEP&gt;"Weight Loss refers to the reduction in mass of a substrate due to microbial degradation processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Weight loss is a measurable indicator of the extent of PE and WC degradation by A. grisella larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Weight loss refers to the reduction in weight of mealworm groups over time due to biodegradation activities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Weight loss is a health measure indicating the decrease in mass of mealworms over the experimental period."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-68041096d198a27b4ed526281746b7f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fd075a78abe1dca64ddea928d3f94b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9a869d17d470cb9ca00328986147a3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-939f85d52d9301668deab282264e5fd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af5eb6a8326b4977801e2f7694a2c750&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02a57c5d6ee92292f1b1bd3dbe76e612&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af682f78e3e8970d7d70b027a8f79116&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-640f0655e17fab473cca3b460c2795de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22ae90a77be18cbac99e5441d47ce2d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5b6629e8c030ab3162553d83aa6eca4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-262bed73e929944e03b9f72769b8196c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55bdcf1b4859e82ab15050837ab539dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06ba9ca61fb4f42582bbf7bd00ff0005&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc88563632a3abf926bf4e4ac16973fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c39e41f4f36c9c6854fa71508c35a08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e38968f22c4cd9bef3f1562e4ca47e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70bab3579af07d0f99a5f948a90fe1e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2338bb97657d74ab5d8a444849037692&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6675480dfd01dcb533166d01b8e5482e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BACILLUS CEREUS NJDI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bacillus cereus NJDI is a strain isolated from dumpsites capable of degrading polymers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2fd075a78abe1dca64ddea928d3f94b7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HIPS (High Impact Polystyrene) is a type of plastic degraded by some Enterobacteriaceae species."&lt;SEP&gt;"HIPS (High Impact Polystyrene) is a type of plastic with an amorphous structure, showing high consumption rates by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"HIPS (High-Impact Polystyrene) is a plastic product used in the experiment to assess degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"HIPS (High-Impact Polystyrene) is a type of plastic tested for degradation by Bacillus strains."&lt;SEP&gt;"HIPS, or high-impact polystyrene, is a type of polystyrene copolymer with improved toughness."&lt;SEP&gt;"High-impact polystyrene (HIPS) is a type of PS containing rubber as an additive, used for comparison in plastic degradation studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"HIPS (High Impact Polystyrene) is a type of polystyrene used in various products."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d9095195e9cf06b9887c03abde6284d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96aac7c9638ee245b9db5df3ec1d2a1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fd075a78abe1dca64ddea928d3f94b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-566d464a7713ef7ca266f3d5f24a1a59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-718900b924b6910a58e8ead81c01c723&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-188daf7716cd1d683a79562bf4d6ab90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4cdbea1d06006b95d57c8b628d9e3f8f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ELEMENTAL ANALYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Elemental analysis determines the composition of elements like carbon and hydrogen in materials."</data>
