    <node id="&quot;PLASTIC-EATING MEALWORMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mealworms capable of consuming and degrading plastics such as polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms capable of consuming and degrading plastics such as polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms, particularly Tenebrio molitor, have been studied for their ability to degrade plastics like polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic-eating mealworms are larvae of Tenebrio molitor capable of breaking down plastics like polystyrene through metabolic processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic-eating mealworms refer to larvae of Tenebrio molitor that have been observed to consume and biodegrade plastics such as polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic-eating mealworms refer to Tenebrio molitor larvae capable of consuming and degrading plastic materials like polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic-Eating Mealworms are insects capable of consuming and degrading plastic materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic-eating mealworms are insects whose gut microbiota have the ability to degrade plastic materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic-eating mealworms possess the ability to digest and biodegrade plastics like polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic-eating mealworms refer to larvae capable of biodegrading plastic materials such as polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms capable of consuming various types of plastic, including Styrofoam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic-Eating Mealworms refer to the larvae of Tenebrio molitor L., capable of degrading non-hydrolyzable vinyl plastics as their sole diet."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic-eating mealworms are insects capable of consuming plastic materials while utilizing their gut microbiota for essential nutrient acquisition."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic-eating mealworms are larvae of Tenebrio molitor with the ability to degrade various types of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic-eating mealworms (larvae of Tenebrio genus) possess the ability to biodegrade plastics like polystyrene through gut microbial activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic-eating mealworms possess gut microorganisms capable of degrading plastic materials such as polystyrene."</data>
