    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYMERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polymers are large molecules composed of repeated subunits, forming the basis of most plastic materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polymers are large molecules composed of repeating structural units, commonly used in the production of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polymers are large molecules composed of repeating structural units, including plastics and other synthetic materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polymers are large molecules composed of repeating structural units, such as polystyrene, which can be biodegraded by certain organisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polymers refer to the plastic materials being studied, including PS, PE, and PU foams, which undergo biodegradation due to microbial activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polymers are large molecules composed of repeating structural units, such as those found in polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polymers such as polystyrene and polyethylene serve as alternative nutrient sources for mealworm larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polymers are large molecules composed of repeating structural units, often studied for their environmental impact and biodegradability."</data>
