    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOOD WASTE VALORISATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Food waste valorisation involves converting food waste into valuable products, promoting sustainable practices in insect rearing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Food waste valorisation refers to the process of converting food waste into valuable resources, aligning with circular economy principles."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-95142a3f585446bd848eeedadd1ab713&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85d18d5d86ed1c061dc44d69e9c09ffc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOW-DENSITY POLYETHYLENE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Low-density polyethylene (LDPE) is a thermoplastic that can be degraded by specific microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Low-density polyethylene is a plastic material that undergoes biodegradation by Zophobas atratus larvae, resulting in fragmentation into microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;**Low-Density Polyethylene (LDPE)** is a thermoplastic polymer derived from petroleum, known for its flexibility, durability, and widespread use in films, packaging materials, and flexible containers. As a specific form of polyethylene, LDPE is characterized by its low density and unique molecular weight, making it suitable for various applications such as plastic bags and other forms of packaging.

Research has shown that **low-density polyethylene** undergoes biodegradation under specific conditions, though this process is limited. Certain organisms, including Tenebrio molitor larvae (commonly known as mealworms), superworms, greater wax worms, and microorganisms like bacteria of the genus Pantoea, contribute to the degradation of LDPE. These microorganisms may be associated with caterpillar larvae or earthworm guts, facilitating the breakdown of the plastic. Studies indicate that biodegradation can occur through gut microbe-independent mechanisms, enabling mineralization and depolymerization of the polymer.

Despite its reputation for persistence in the environment, LDPE has been confirmed to undergo partial degradation by both insect larvae and microbial processes. However, during biodegradation, LDPE may fragment into microplastics, which raises environmental concerns. The material's susceptibility to biodegradation under certain conditions makes it an important subject of study in efforts to reduce plastic waste and develop sustainable solutions.

In summary, **low-density polyethylene** is a versatile yet environmentally significant material, commonly used in films and packaging, whose biodegradability continues to be explored for reducing plastic pollution. It represents a balance between utility and ecological impact, with ongoing research aimed at enhancing its degradation potential.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d068dbad68e3ecd909a551f43f82b893&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfd8d6b8105d9868a4ffadf5779d0df5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c3165b5b483903ac54f813f43b4076d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3aaf626f7d7f62d0cee4a0e5efafeb69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-915331bc1ae85fe139629eaebc4042cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdf2753a9a78b282c1ca2c0539e3203d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88659f9848d30be72c37a99b551a9a0a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bd2f7b94f62fa18de9e02426577d241&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-422e833d3381bd5fd0b5a3d63d9047f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d40b7debb6497167fa1aec874ebce45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f91df729b04e3d570337e02872cf1c38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9528beb2e85a7fb89449a9233eb979bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3667703f7416ebab666e65b375dd8582&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21bee96879472a1c6df454d862dc9e90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56604c68c2f6221f63a4afa5d457e8ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1d3c25b9affee2f535cb531a09a2384&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d642e5476221b3ea202c68d7e6070b96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c4804d2c00d1d5fff2b89eaf6da26da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59dab99372af01b60a073d8eac17870f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3fe22bd6c91507d8d1e60d24886e0eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db579d338d8f90574e3ac67a3ae9938d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5d6035f4b0686837c8c4319bab80d70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecf2c478d08c7bc8e491f630aa289881&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85d18d5d86ed1c061dc44d69e9c09ffc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64a060d0c9650ae8bed2ca9b44eef10c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-937d9d4e1671351e8e90f0bd2647f321&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af9ad6e808e93b61ec40d6ba4131fda7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9bd8cf0d5102bbca724e0773be0eeae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b74f16813537103549cdcb6770abaea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5073433ee060ce75e140a6626619108b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ac276660dd76d0ef97a8a0b1a59664c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-276c82b9935756a3e668c788458ff922&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0cba3b06dd82e87d3b582bc21c475868&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79e833cbc3a0a6e2c80e1b69da50317e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bc3253e8d41785f994d1c6fcc2b6c47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03f2fc4d98412efb8a792474cc47e558&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a31a12c930b59b872c94dda484d0db4</data>
