    <node id="&quot;COLEOPTERA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORDER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Coleoptera is an order of insects that includes Tenebrio molitor, a species with exceptional plastic-degrading abilities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Coleoptera is an order of insects that includes beetles such as Tenebrio molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;**COLEOPTERA** is an order of insects commonly known as beetles, characterized by their hard exoskeleton and hardened forewings. This diverse group includes numerous species such as *Tenebrio molitor* (yellow mealworm), *Zophobas morio* (superworm), *Holotrichia parallela*, *Zophobas atratus*, and *Tenebrio obscurus*. Members of the order also include darkling beetles, which belong to the family **Tenebrionidae**.

Species within the Coleoptera order play significant ecological roles and have been extensively studied for their unique capabilities. Notably, the larvae of certain beetles, including those of mealworms and superworms, have demonstrated the ability to degrade plastics such as polystyrene styrofoam. This process involves gut microorganisms that aid in the digestion of plastic materials like expanded polystyrene (EPS). Additionally, research into the gut microbiota of beetles has provided insights into their digestive processes and potential applications for biodegradation.

Overall, **Coleoptera** represents a vital component of global insect biodiversity, with members contributing to various ecological processes and playing critical roles in ecosystems worldwide.&lt;SEP&gt;"Coleoptera is an order of insects, including beetles, observed taking plastics as a food supply and able to decompose them in vivo."&lt;SEP&gt;"Coleoptera is the order containing Tenebrionidae, comprising approximately 20,000 species worldwide."&lt;SEP&gt;"Coleoptera is the order that includes beetles, such as Tenebrio molitor, which have shown plastic-degrading capabilities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8c8dab62f56f2bfabf08bfe99049386a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5cbd81fc528c18f42514a2a74d4921e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9859524b7a6851b786570d2a704e34f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-550dde13ffd2abcf536dd87f7d4c1b40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30a7209d626a6319ba5600bea7f27299&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bd2f7b94f62fa18de9e02426577d241&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-422e833d3381bd5fd0b5a3d63d9047f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f91df729b04e3d570337e02872cf1c38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21bee96879472a1c6df454d862dc9e90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35eed7e10fb1cc08baaecab1b1cffad0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d1301f6942d17092ef7b22ac40f19f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed48dc66abf9c27721101b1adac15e7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c343b12adf5bbce5bf80b96909fe66d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df24ea37743c236d369911024fc20bfc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d97be338c51b4c4354e2d0f8de9c9dc8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db672d5836dfe372ee7c47ee4dd6fbd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cede90fd3b3eee0bd12d582eaa7d54c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3351564dbd6a0ee6a8b97f6687378ffc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbf098ec253f99187f3c98d5d0589f7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0caad5c42a4b470a8c41ac3fb68c1f64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af9ad6e808e93b61ec40d6ba4131fda7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cff93a2e1d68c6ed1fcd9f720197238f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4b3c26a06ad850bb97d0ca2d9217be1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3569d74f8a4c9d0851777a5a66284a00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b74f16813537103549cdcb6770abaea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5613b129e38cb777855c04f228fe7e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-302543e7a2fdb3596cc8a10e7072ec01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0014171c7ef07a60c6be3b57e791688c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fd138e047a780efd715a5ab4701b58c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6eb7955dc484d5f656e1be7b406abb3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ff228c7711f94fb27152b187b1fa3eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06a44b308af148551c5b7feef324d88b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59453e4c878e72ac6985a08043cdf126&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02e6f7bbb2c1ef92c57b423020b0cc5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22e4b8000531766cffd145ef32353af2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd1ab39969c669dba42f162e8497c23f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-694aaaa7c2839ea048d46b6a2bb13748&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a81144d30653377d6d90e26c4497eb0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TENEBRIONIDAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FAMILY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tenebrionidae is a family of beetles that includes Tenebrio molitor, known for its plastic-degrading capabilities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrionidae is a family of beetles that includes Tenebrio molitor, known for its plastic-degrading potential."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrionidae is a family of beetles that includes species like Tenebrio molitor, known for their larvae's plastic-degrading abilities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrionidae is the family of darkling beetles to which Tenebrio molitor and Zophobas atratus belong, known for their ability to degrade plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrionidae is the family that includes darkling beetles capable of plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrionidae is a large and diverse family of beetles within the Coleoptera order, commonly referred to as darkling beetles. This family encompasses over 20,000 species, including notable members such as *Tenebrio molitor* (mealworm beetle), *Zophobas atratus* (superworms), *Zophobas morio*, and *Tenebrio obscurus*. Members of Tenebrionidae are renowned for their adaptability and ecological significance.

The larvae of certain species, particularly *Tenebrio molitor* (yellow mealworm) and *Zophobas atratus* (superworms), have gained attention due to their ability to consume and degrade plastics, making them potential candidates for addressing plastic waste in industrial applications. While some members contribute positively to biodegradation processes, others are known to cause damage to plastic packaging. 

*Tenebrio molitor* has also been recognized as an edible insect due to its high nutritional value and suitability for industrialized production, contributing to food security and human nutrition. Additionally, the larval stages of these beetles play important roles in ecosystems, serving as decomposers and forming part of the food chain.

Overall, Tenebrionidae represents a significant group of beetles with promising applications in environmental management, biodegradation, and sustainable food sources. The family's adaptability and ecological contributions make it a key focus in both scientific research and practical applications.&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrionidae is the family of darkling beetles, seventh-most speciose taxon in Order Coleoptera."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrionidae is the family to which both T. molitor and Alphitobius diaperinus Panzer belong."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b5cbd81fc528c18f42514a2a74d4921e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fc215d3abb38f76b4ee0d22c4f1eb11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98d7ae4d155085781614411da5564816&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-550dde13ffd2abcf536dd87f7d4c1b40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30a7209d626a6319ba5600bea7f27299&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-918d0788c95399a6714bd40c688594de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa27760a0a889fe7b58360dbb150cdf3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bd2f7b94f62fa18de9e02426577d241&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4b03ca32b0efbf0ca6a3c8761c0d03d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-422e833d3381bd5fd0b5a3d63d9047f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f91df729b04e3d570337e02872cf1c38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21bee96879472a1c6df454d862dc9e90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35eed7e10fb1cc08baaecab1b1cffad0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d1301f6942d17092ef7b22ac40f19f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed48dc66abf9c27721101b1adac15e7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c343b12adf5bbce5bf80b96909fe66d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df24ea37743c236d369911024fc20bfc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d97be338c51b4c4354e2d0f8de9c9dc8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db672d5836dfe372ee7c47ee4dd6fbd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cede90fd3b3eee0bd12d582eaa7d54c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f71fddc259d51158d5c79f38bf41523f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3351564dbd6a0ee6a8b97f6687378ffc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64a060d0c9650ae8bed2ca9b44eef10c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0caad5c42a4b470a8c41ac3fb68c1f64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af9ad6e808e93b61ec40d6ba4131fda7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cff93a2e1d68c6ed1fcd9f720197238f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4b3c26a06ad850bb97d0ca2d9217be1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3569d74f8a4c9d0851777a5a66284a00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b74f16813537103549cdcb6770abaea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4304c39ef3427872131caf77e7cdb438&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5613b129e38cb777855c04f228fe7e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-302543e7a2fdb3596cc8a10e7072ec01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e05bc34fccfca5e177064daf8346866&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0014171c7ef07a60c6be3b57e791688c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fd138e047a780efd715a5ab4701b58c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af801199dfd68205bddcbe0bcda26eef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ff228c7711f94fb27152b187b1fa3eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1679027e80b766e0469f7323db15b497&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32e10966ec80ea585746639b6be7e04e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22e4b8000531766cffd145ef32353af2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02e6f7bbb2c1ef92c57b423020b0cc5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd1ab39969c669dba42f162e8497c23f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-694aaaa7c2839ea048d46b6a2bb13748</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENVIRONMENTAL POLLUTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ECOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Environmental Pollution focuses on pollutants and their impact on ecosystems."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environmental pollution encompasses harmful substances introduced into the environment, including microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environmental pollution refers to the contamination of natural environments by waste materials, such as plastic, affecting ecosystems."&lt;SEP&gt;"The harmful impact of plastic waste on ecosystems and organisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The contamination of the natural environment by harmful substances, often caused by human activities."&lt;SEP&gt;"The contamination of natural environments by harmful substances, such as microplastics, affecting ecosystems."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environmental pollution refers to the contamination of natural environments by harmful substances, including plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environmental pollution refers to the contamination of natural environments by harmful substances, such as plastics and microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environmental pollution involves the contamination of the physical environment by harmful substances, often resulting from human activities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environmental pollution refers to the contamination of natural environments by harmful substances, such as plastics and hydrocarbons."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environmental Pollution involves the contamination of the environment by harmful substances, such as toxic pollutants from plastic waste."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environmental Pollution is a journal that published a study on microbiome diversity in Tenebrio molitor fed with polystyrene waste."&lt;SEP&gt;"The contamination of natural environments by pollutants such as plastics and chemicals, affecting ecological balance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environmental Pollution refers to the contamination of the environment by harmful substances, including plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environmental pollution arises from mismanaged plastic waste, posing risks to ecosystems and potentially human health."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environmental pollution refers to the contamination of the environment by harmful substances, often resulting from human activities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environmental pollution refers to the contamination of natural environments by synthetic plastics, leading to ecological harm."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environmental pollution refers to the contamination of natural environments by harmful substances, such as plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environmental pollution encompasses the contamination of natural environments by substances such as plastics and microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environmental pollution refers to the contamination of the environment by harmful substances, including microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environmental pollution refers to the contamination of natural environments by substances like microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environmental pollution refers to the presence of harmful substances in the environment, including plastics like polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eada60ee606520104bb515c4896d6b0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5cbd81fc528c18f42514a2a74d4921e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f45bee9c7111e3b95e966d23c3a6223d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63813cc5cb4812528045bd8f1ced4313&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b8cc3aa81b03290b589ccf0a1548ca0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f2fd4b2e978e6745e0dde602114a826&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-630d06d8ab372b4cadd7e3772d8fa1fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f91df729b04e3d570337e02872cf1c38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-648afbc8ee82935d4026f5915152491c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3667703f7416ebab666e65b375dd8582&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b77d05458a2050e3057c427cf81e24ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56604c68c2f6221f63a4afa5d457e8ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d1301f6942d17092ef7b22ac40f19f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d642e5476221b3ea202c68d7e6070b96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bd3778dedc6a0463017df9f8d6396eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85fe36521680f0d09a603eab04706561&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71372e333b39cee7eea0c53f89bec5c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d9491734042920c5911740665415835&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b50c5a85182344022614ffe10dc9382&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fd138e047a780efd715a5ab4701b58c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a3d3cf8ea423f7e0f637dddade1bbf1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5050676818c53a0ef6d691d3049e923c</data>
