      <data key="d2">chunk-8518832c2d3e002c8acf71795e306144&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff1127258b5df378d8b32fff2a93eb84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-383865d9c2a2b8a7cabd754f1193b8f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-648afbc8ee82935d4026f5915152491c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa2e818c436fabed80b9d3d720ebf491&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7432cb0d6c74fd2dd80b065fbad26b4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1679027e80b766e0469f7323db15b497&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc6c2706bd609f920aa61d5ef2310db6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-827853316f7304c444884dc82f757802&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e540abd667582c77f4d2222836147ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56af57b5211422531c03b0cbcfded1b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e77298fbeb95f87269261b74c2158d5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-463ac9dfa68274d35700c61208f4ea85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a4712059883b356b4aea23cb7ef1514</data>
      <data key="d1">"Free-living fungi have been identified as efficient in breaking down synthetic polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fungi are a diverse group of eukaryotic organisms, often involved in decomposition and nutrient cycling."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fungi are a group of microorganisms that have been found to degrade certain types of plastic waste."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fungi are eukaryotic organisms that produce enzymes with various biotechnological applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fungi play a critical role in the biodegradation of plastics, breaking them down into simpler components through enzymatic processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Various species of fungi have been tested for their ability to biodegrade polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbes capable of degrading various substances, including bioplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fungi are microorganisms capable of breaking down complex organic materials and are part of the gut microbiome."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fungi identified from Dandora dumpsite in Nairobi have shown potential for biodegrading polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microorganisms responsible for the degradation of soil-buried polyester polyurethane across various soil water holding capacities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fungi are eukaryotic organisms that include species capable of degrading PET."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fungi are eukaryotic organisms found in the gut of Tenebrio molitor, involved in lignocellulolytic activities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fungi are eukaryotic organisms that include yeasts, molds, and mushrooms, some of which can degrade polymers like polypropylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fungi are eukaryotic microorganisms that contribute to the biodegradation of various polymers."</data>
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALGAE&quot;">
