      <data key="d1">"Wax moths are another example of omnivorous insect larvae capable of degrading plastics, indicating potential for broader plastic degradation by insects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wax moths contribute to the biodegradation of plastics, breaking them down into smaller components within their digestive systems."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wax moths are insects whose larvae, known as waxworms, have shown the ability to consume and degrade plastics."</data>
