    <node id="&quot;CHITIN&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-15323ef47e29f2927f95274e49f4e5bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-078b6698be699eb7105b7cffadf709af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0627e3f1b0fb440795f73c4fa33093c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ee6535da22915c7094098e016b19d80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa2e818c436fabed80b9d3d720ebf491&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44565f26e7290c5eb0f26935608a5f16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32e10966ec80ea585746639b6be7e04e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5251cc2ed910c3785b2c7242b7cbc11e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a81144d30653377d6d90e26c4497eb0</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chitin derived from insect exoskeletons can be utilized in the circular economy as a renewable resource for producing biomaterials and other products."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chitin is a component of T. molitor exoskeletons and a precursor for chitosan production."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chitin is a complex carbohydrate found in the exoskeletons of insects, providing structural support and having various industrial applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chitin is a structural component found in the exoskeleton of worms, potentially promoting plant growth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chitin is a structural component in worm frass, contributing to its value as a fertilizer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chitin is reported to support rooting in plants and is present in superworm frass."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chitin is a component found in the insect cuticle, identified through NMR analysis in the fecula spectrum."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chitin is a long-chain polymer found in the exoskeletons of arthropods and plays structural roles."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chitin is a component of the exoskeleton of arthropods, found in melted skeletons consumed by starvation mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHITOSAN&quot;">
