      <data key="d1">"Cell-surface hydrophobicity describes the extent to which bacterial surfaces repel water, influencing adhesion and colonization on hydrophobic substrates."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cell-surface hydrophobicity determines the adhesion of bacteria to hydrocarbons, impacting their role in biodegradation processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cell-surface hydrophobicity is a characteristic of bacterial cells that influences their ability to degrade hydrocarbons."</data>
