    <node id="&quot;RHODOTORULA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNGUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A genus of yeast-like fungi strongly associated with the biodegradation of plastics such as PP, PU, and EVA."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rhodotorula is a fungal genus associated with plastic degradation, showing higher relative abundances in PS- and PE-fed yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rhodotorula is a genus of fungi linked to polyethylene degradation in the gut of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rhodotorula is a fungal genus that dominates the gut fungal communities across all plastics-fed groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rhodotorula showed increased relative abundance in plastic-fed groups, being specifically associated with plastic degradation."</data>
