      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A genus of fungi involved in the biodegradation of plastics, specifically associated with PE and PS degradation in yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cryptococcus had a high relative abundance in plastic-fed groups, uniquely associated with plastic degradation processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cryptococcus is a fungal genus associated with plastic degradation, showing higher relative abundances in PS- and PE-fed yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cryptococcus is a genus of fungi associated with polystyrene degradation in the gut of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cryptococcus is a genus of encapsulated yeast-like fungi."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cryptococcus is another dominant fungal genus observed in the gut microbiome of plastics-fed larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a3f07da33b55bf8a25fe06beee23e90e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e34d58a20a707b35e8fcd5658ba2924&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de9904e6f38706256e15c7957f8f0527&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d7500fe4985cb2b885f9eb244ed3c2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e127a4930b6154498b93c2e94f2b7c20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbb6f13dbe3de759712fa3a0c9780470</data>
