    <node id="&quot;CITROBACTER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Citrobacter is a bacterial genus associated with PE and PP diets in superworms and strongly associated with both PE and PS diets in mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Citrobacter is a genus of bacteria associated with both polyethylene and polystyrene diets in the gut of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Citrobacter is involved in nitrogen metabolism and found in T. obscurus larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Citrobacter is a genus of bacteria showing fluctuations in abundance based on the experimental conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Citrobacter is a genus of gram-negative bacteria often associated with infections and environmental processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Citrobacter is a genus of bacteria identified in mealworms with nitrogen-fixing capabilities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Citrobacter is a genus of bacteria involved in nitrogen fixation within insect gut microbiota."</data>
