    <node id="&quot;KLEBSIELLA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A bacterial genus found predominantly in the gut microbiome of mealworms consuming the control diet."&lt;SEP&gt;"Klebsiella is a bacterial genus associated with the PS diet in mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Klebsiella is a genus of bacteria associated with polystyrene degradation in the gut of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Klebsiella is a type of bacteria present in certain diets that do not support gut health."&lt;SEP&gt;"Klebsiella is a bacterial genus noted in the mealworm gut microbiome, contributing to the diversity of microbial communities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Klebsiella is a genus of bacteria capable of degrading bioplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Klebsiella is a genus of bacteria to which WJ2020 belongs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Klebsiella is a genus of bacteria to which strain WJ2020 belongs."&lt;SEP&gt;"A genus of bacteria identified as an important nitrogen-fixing symbiont in Styrofoam-eating mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Klebsiella is a genus of bacteria identified as an important nitrogen-fixing symbiont within the gut microbiota of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Klebsiella is a genus of gram-negative bacteria identified as nitrogen-fixing gut bacteria in mealworms."</data>
