    <node id="&quot;ASPERGILLUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNGI"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A genus of fungi observed in PU-fed groups, known for its ability to degrade plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aspergillus exhibited high abundance in PS- and CS-fed larvae, associated with lignocellulose or plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aspergillus is a fungal genus involved in PS plastic degradation in mealworm guts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aspergillus is a fungal genus known for its potential in LDPE degradation and has been reported in the gut of wax moth larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aspergillus is a genus of fungi containing several species of medical and industrial importance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aspergillus produces galactosaminogalactan, which mediates adherence to host constituents."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aspergillus is a fungal genus known for its plastic biodegradation capacity, such as A. flavus PEDX3 from Galleria mellonella larvae for PE degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aspergillus is a fungal genus known for its plastic biodegradation capacity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aspergillus is a genus of fungi known for its plastic biodegradation capacity, such as A. flavus PEDX3 degrading PE and A. tubingenis degrading PU."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aspergillus is a genus of fungi, including species like Aspergillus niger, involved in the biodegradation of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aspergillus is a fungal genus identified in the gut microbiota of polystyrene-fed larvae, known for its potential role in plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aspergillus is a fungal genus significantly enriched in PS samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aspergillus is a fungal genus that appeared overrepresented in PS samples with a Log2-fold change of 13.9 and was recovered with a sizeable frequency in resamples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aspergillus is a fungal genus with species capable of degrading several plastic materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aspergillus is a fungal genus associated with plastic degradation abilities, found in the gut microbiome."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1d40b7debb6497167fa1aec874ebce45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9095195e9cf06b9887c03abde6284d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e34d58a20a707b35e8fcd5658ba2924&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6ddf9dd30d7258964408f9a915d3478&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eaf1f7b81bc271c665d7776cc3114a92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de9904e6f38706256e15c7957f8f0527&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1070f8c33eb8afcfcffac95df9012d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d33654bada6ddaf4917586dd5fd41e9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1d3c25b9affee2f535cb531a09a2384&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a91a3c11281861b559c31c3107c72e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d7500fe4985cb2b885f9eb244ed3c2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec1a5b2913dd6782ff1e0533dd57325f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbb6f13dbe3de759712fa3a0c9780470&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-001e8f54368c9a236f702fd09cddf4a8</data>
    </node>
