    <node id="&quot;LARVAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LIFE STAGE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Larvae are the immature forms of insects that experienced weight reduction during the experiment, possibly due to stressful rearing conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Larvae refer to the immature stages of insects used in the study."&lt;SEP&gt;Larvae are the immature, feeding stages of certain insects, such as *Tenebrio molitor* (mealworms), *Galleria mellonella*, and *Zophobas morio*. Specifically, they represent an essential developmental stage in the life cycles of these organisms, playing a critical role in scientific research. Larvae, including those of *Tenebrio molitor*, focus on consuming and degrading organic materials, and have been extensively studied for their ability to consume and metabolize various types of plastics, such as polystyrene (PS), polyethylene (PE), polypropylene (PP), and polyethylene terephthalate (PET). 

In experimental settings, larvae are often fed specific diets, such as PS microplastics mixed with wheat bran, while researchers monitor their survival rates, weight changes, frass production, and plastic consumption over periods of up to 45 days. These studies reveal that larvae exhibit behaviors and capabilities like activating digestive enzymes and altering gene expression in both gut bacteria and the host organism, facilitating the breakdown of synthetic polymers. Additionally, under nutrient-deficient conditions, larvae may rely on body reserves for survival and can even display cannibalistic behavior.

Larvae are also utilized in experiments to evaluate growth dynamics, nutritional values (such as crude protein and fat content), and the effects of different diets or environmental conditions on biodegradation abilities. Some studies involve dividing larvae into groups based on factors like antibiotic treatment or feedstock type. Furthermore, larvae contribute to nitrogen fixation during digestion, enhancing their role in breaking down complex materials. Overall, larvae serve as key subjects in addressing plastic pollution through biological means, making them vital components in the study of insect development and environmental science.&lt;SEP&gt;"Larvae refer to the immature forms of certain organisms, such as Tenebrio molitor, which exhibit plastic-degrading abilities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Larvae represent an early developmental stage in the life cycle of certain organisms, here specifically referring to T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Larvae represent the early developmental stage of T. molitor, characterized by growth and feeding behaviors."&lt;SEP&gt;"Larvae represent the juvenile life stage of T. molitor, which is the focus of the study for analyzing growth and reserve dynamics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98d7ae4d155085781614411da5564816&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-032b3b0fe0366e6e76e86abf8c48d200&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df5e2448d1e9703b511b85725469467e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf697c73d05470fb4a143aa0e4700787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6dce72fccb3df94ec407aba3d4df8eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee46611b24ea3848df979ded841f06b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d5a9fbe4803ded646c6a5e4d23ca93a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d908d878ed4e7fc36f3af71a5be7f2ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0638e0fe93dc27e678672a164e6088c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6ddf9dd30d7258964408f9a915d3478&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8a706f2bd66291a3ef925114ffd9300&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5740f0973ff804cae61f6fc12f3e3753&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89344d5b5d9debdca45ab8c7c963a585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5540fc6fe4d3ef0fd986ec36a589c77f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c4804d2c00d1d5fff2b89eaf6da26da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c426315f0f412528b9c6fb2a82dff2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c16f995987af72f86486559556052e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcf2bd0dbdce4d7299bfc35487eaf0f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-697bf99ecf19f99243f3b5a4ef5b334c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c84ac252cb9ce906354bda2ad1113aba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16810fc8beb169dfca32904d41bd992b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eed90a978852274ead3771418cd60bed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b759b81206d0e33e320f2d61e540ae47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af9ad6e808e93b61ec40d6ba4131fda7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32f340b7166025be3c56178a94ae480d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-531058c4540bd4e6a50d141db01d4d11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc31a0931fceb1446bc6ec4d0c587f7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a38c714e7f1f701ec1149e25910e16e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ead6f17ad517015b638608c5bfe6852&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20395efa1299dc8b777774e765ad1159&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5134944e002326fa5ca136c470d99e2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd3cec3addc1bee202783dff1583ba54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54049db5a67a6464f459ccc427765140&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d290a6a81802d3048c35d2a2fb1252c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a170da66288c73388872b8a43fa51e33</data>
    </node>
