    <node id="&quot;SURVIVAL RATES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"HEALTH MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Survival Rates refer to the percentage of larvae that survive under different dietary conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Survival Rates were calculated to assess the impact of plastic diets on different larval groups over the 45-day period."&lt;SEP&gt;"Survival rates indicate the proportion of insects surviving under specific dietary conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Survival rates (SRs) indicate the percentage of organisms surviving under specific conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Survival rates indicate how well larvae survived over the 6-week period under various diet conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Survival rates of larvae fed with polyethylene reflect the overall health impact of the material."&lt;SEP&gt;"Survival rates are a measure of the health and viability of larvae under different dietary conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Survival rates represent the proportion of living larvae over time, indicating the impact of plastic diets on their viability."&lt;SEP&gt;"Survival rates indicate the viability of waxworms when fed on different diets, including polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Survival rates are health measures indicating the proportion of larvae surviving under different dietary conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Survival rates refer to the proportion of mealworm larvae that survive during the experiment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Survival rates of larvae are measured every 5 days to assess the effects of Styrofoam consumption."&lt;SEP&gt;"Survival rates indicate the viability of larvae under different dietary conditions, including PP-only and co-fed diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Survival rates of mealworm larvae were measured every 4 days to assess their health."&lt;SEP&gt;"Survival rates represent the percentage of mealworms that survive under various feeding conditions, reflecting the impact of polystyrene microplastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a38c714e7f1f701ec1149e25910e16e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e415042ae4079ee5fe96c7105eb534c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-acbe3a2cb3a17985d07d15bed638bd90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d5a9fbe4803ded646c6a5e4d23ca93a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8bb63b06976c3a8e6f2cea85c1ecf518&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f267b48449a40d614a2f325799752dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c64d0f1648a87497fbcae56f3089b417&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eecad183fc5700f3d7e0a266e293de1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e136b8a35c0d60811b9daf0cbd5729f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16810fc8beb169dfca32904d41bd992b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c16dd402d0a926c1a975280e2b32e84e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0caad5c42a4b470a8c41ac3fb68c1f64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4df787efdb36123e3f2a76b5402278ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3aaf626f7d7f62d0cee4a0e5efafeb69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a3e42eecd3967a9e53cfadc926363ee</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PUPATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pupation is a developmental stage in the life cycle of larvae, influenced by dietary factors such as plastic consumption."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pupation is the biological process where mealworm larvae transform into pupae, influenced by diet and life stage."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pupation is the stage in the life cycle of mealworms where larvae transform into adult beetles, influenced by nutrition and environmental factors."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pupation is the stage in the life cycle of mealworms where they transform into adult beetles."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pupation is the stage in the life cycle of some insects during which they undergo transformation into adults."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pupation refers to the developmental stage where larvae transform into adults, affected by dietary conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pupation refers to the developmental stage where larvae transform into pupae, affected differently in superworms and yellow mealworms based on diet."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pupation refers to the transformation from larva to adult, used as an indicator of health and development in the experiment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pupation is the stage in the life cycle of T. molitor affected by diet quality, with control groups showing normal pupation while others do not."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pupation marks the developmental stage where larvae transition into adults, triggered by reaching a reproduction buffer threshold."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a38c714e7f1f701ec1149e25910e16e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02a57c5d6ee92292f1b1bd3dbe76e612&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a522a615bbcac2e06f97f2e4e61975b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84558838faaf585c61e883356c52c0e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16810fc8beb169dfca32904d41bd992b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c16dd402d0a926c1a975280e2b32e84e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f38f2f3673b813b3a817c014229c9565&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a97d5b092508f2e837932274d6b3282&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-640f0655e17fab473cca3b460c2795de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-998b63e5349034d477c2087c139669ed</data>
    </node>
