      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Benzene ring skeleton vibration is a characteristic peak of polystyrene that disappears during degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8a1fbf409e74e27aa2b223e54f2e0def</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HYDROXYL OR CARBOXYLIC ACID GROUPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNCTIONAL GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"These groups are identified at around 3370 cm\(^{-1}\), suggesting a change from hydrophobic to more hydrophilic surfaces in degraded plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c9a869d17d470cb9ca00328986147a3f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DSC-TGA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"DSC-TGA (Differential Scanning Calorimetry-Thermogravimetric Analysis) confirms the differences in thermal stability and decomposition rate of plastics after digestion by yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"DSC-TGA (Differential Scanning Calorimetry-Thermogravimetric Analysis) is a thermal analysis method used to study the degradation characteristics of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"DSC-TGA analyzes thermal properties and degradation behavior of polymers in larval frass."&lt;SEP&gt;"DSC-TGA is a method used to assess thermal stabilities of plastics and frass samples, showing differences in weight loss rates between feedstocks and larval frass."&lt;SEP&gt;"Differential Scanning Calorimetry - Thermogravimetric Analysis (DSC-TGA) is utilized to examine thermal stability and weight loss characteristics of plastics and frass samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Differential Scanning Calorimetry-Thermogravimetric Analysis (DSC-TGA) is used to confirm the modification and degradation of plastics after ingestion by larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"DSC-TGA is a thermal analysis method used to study weight loss and decomposition characteristics of materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"DSC-TGA is a method used to analyze the thermal properties and degradation of foam plastics after passing through the larval guts."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-705bf68703e5d236b2ffabb7ecb3de5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1f0f043d44950fae05e8207a298d4a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d0e4cb4324bc684ebb2ca6136c04ad0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9a869d17d470cb9ca00328986147a3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f370c2f246a6c8a776ae90277a5aacc8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2417ca11674320d88eecdf4cb66f9d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-444b8acd02a76616457012e1ac0db23b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BOTTOM SEDIMENTATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bottom sedimentation includes complex residues from plastic degradation and other biological digestive products."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c9a869d17d470cb9ca00328986147a3f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIODEGRADATION BYPRODUCTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
