    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHEMICAL BONDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chemical Bonds are interactions between atoms that hold them together in molecules, such as those found in polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chemical bonds within plastics are broken or altered during degradation processes, as evidenced by changes in functional groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chemical bonds in PE are modified during the biodegradation process by waxworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The forces holding atoms together in molecules, which are broken during the biodegradation of plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f15cc70e99a3287ced1a6cbb6c8d76a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9a869d17d470cb9ca00328986147a3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39598f698094d1663ca3438bc143bc90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b25215becbc007a60f24b86a2d6aaf26</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HYDROPHILIC SURFACE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL FEATURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A hydrophilic surface is formed due to the addition of hydroxyl or carboxylic acid groups during plastic degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c9a869d17d470cb9ca00328986147a3f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GUT-BACTERIAL MICROBIOME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The gut-bacterial microbiome refers to the bacterial community within the digestive system of superworms and yellow mealworms, which experiences significant changes when fed plastic diets."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c1f0f043d44950fae05e8207a298d4a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NUMBER AVERAGE WEIGHT (MN)&quot;">
