    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENBANK&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DATABASE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A comprehensive database of publicly available nucleotide sequences managed by NCBI."&lt;SEP&gt;"GenBank is a comprehensive database of publicly available DNA sequences maintained by NCBI."&lt;SEP&gt;"GenBank is a comprehensive database of publicly available nucleotide sequences and related information."&lt;SEP&gt;"GenBank is a comprehensive database of publicly available nucleotide sequences used for phylogenetic and molecular analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"GenBank is a comprehensive database that contains publicly available nucleotide sequences for all organisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"GenBank is a comprehensive database of publicly available nucleotide sequences and their protein translations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5b74e88d1f94354055e078b38af6a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1f0f043d44950fae05e8207a298d4a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aface14c9ee7dd5ccd25e7094ed5c1c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e9eb740edf53e540b468122b302cb82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d71b4e70d7c620ee64c709aaeae634a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51daa29515cc5a431055291627bcb199</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OPERATIONAL TAXONOMIC UNITS (OTUS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"OTUs are groups of closely related organisms defined by sequence similarity thresholds."&lt;SEP&gt;"OTUs represent clusters of closely related organisms, used to classify bacterial species in microbiome studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Operational taxonomic units (OTUs) are clusters of closely related organisms based on genetic similarity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1b673e7590aa1d03b7721694ed73cd74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1f0f043d44950fae05e8207a298d4a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-449dceb5649c6baa34ecc2218cd3e9e1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHAO ESTIMATOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chao Estimator provides an estimate of species richness in ecological samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Chao estimator is a statistical method to estimate species richness in a community."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c1f0f043d44950fae05e8207a298d4a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-013f364e92a266c0e922cb0582f7a997</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ACE ESTIMATOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ace Estimator is a method used to analyze taxonomic richness within a microbial community."&lt;SEP&gt;"The ACE estimator is another method for estimating species richness in microbial communities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c1f0f043d44950fae05e8207a298d4a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-013f364e92a266c0e922cb0582f7a997</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GUT BACTERIAL COMMUNITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gut Bacterial Community refers to the microbial population within the digestive tract, which is influenced by diet and plays a role in plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut bacterial community refers to the microorganisms inhabiting the digestive tract of the larvae, which were significantly affected by plastic diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"The gut bacterial community of yellow mealworms undergoes compositional changes depending on the type of surgical mask layer ingested."&lt;SEP&gt;"The gut bacterial community refers to the microorganisms inhabiting the digestive tract of yellow mealworms, influenced by dietary changes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-476e13b69587aa4e81395e2fd00a9d5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a91a3c11281861b559c31c3107c72e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93d5b1c190fdca6b5e456b1513515be4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e663286500e382f6d296e2b683bf542</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ASCOMYCOTA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYLUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ascomycota is a class of fungi, which includes unclassified members and genera like Taphrina and Aspergillus. These fungi are significantly associated with plastic degradation in the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ascomycota is a phylum of fungi predominant in bran-fed groups and PS-fed superworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ascomycota is a fungal phylum predominant in both PS and CT samples, particularly more abundant in CT samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ascomycota is a fungal phylum involved in polymer degradation, commonly found in the gut fungal community."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d33654bada6ddaf4917586dd5fd41e9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3f07da33b55bf8a25fe06beee23e90e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1070f8c33eb8afcfcffac95df9012d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93d5b1c190fdca6b5e456b1513515be4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BASIDIOMYCOTA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYLUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Basidiomycota is a fungal phylum better represented in PS samples but rare in CT samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Basidiomycota is a fungal phylum present at fairly high frequency in PS samples but almost absent in CT samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Basidiomycota is a phylum of fungi present at a high frequency in PS samples but nearly absent in CT samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Basidiomycota is a phylum of fungi strongly associated with plastics diets in yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Basidiomycota is a fungal phylum whose relative abundance increased in all plastics-fed groups, suggesting its association with plastic diets."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a3f07da33b55bf8a25fe06beee23e90e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6ddf9dd30d7258964408f9a915d3478&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b4b45d826a6a7956015e680f5fb8ee6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1070f8c33eb8afcfcffac95df9012d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93d5b1c190fdca6b5e456b1513515be4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SHANNON AND SIMPSON INDICES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Shannon and Simpson indices are measures of bacterial richness that showed significant decreases in plastic-fed superworms and yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"These indices measure the diversity and evenness of gut microbial communities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Shannon and Simpson indices are measures of diversity applied to estimate larval gut-fungi diversity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a91a3c11281861b559c31c3107c72e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93d5b1c190fdca6b5e456b1513515be4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2cfbb4289b0cc4c8b69884f6d57c447</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NMDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"NMDS (Non-metric Multidimensional Scaling) is a statistical method used to reveal clusters associated with different larval species and diets."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-93d5b1c190fdca6b5e456b1513515be4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRAY-CURTIS DISTANCES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bray-Curtis distances are used to analyze the similarity of gut bacterial communities between samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bray-Curtis distances are used to measure community diversity distance in gut microbiome analyses."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bfe58fb1bbaa5c35e9c6c837d0b1050f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93d5b1c190fdca6b5e456b1513515be4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNWEIGHTED UNIFRAC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ANALYTICAL TECHNIQUE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Unweighted Unifrac is a method used to analyze differences in microbial community composition between groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"Unweighted Unifrac is a method used to compare microbial community structures based on phylogenetic differences, applied here to analyze gut bacterial communities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Unweighted Unifrac is a metric used to compare microbial community compositions based on phylogenetic differences."&lt;SEP&gt;"Unweighted Unifrac measures beta-diversity based on phylogenetic differences without considering abundance."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7d0e4cb4324bc684ebb2ca6136c04ad0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1070f8c33eb8afcfcffac95df9012d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93d5b1c190fdca6b5e456b1513515be4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e663286500e382f6d296e2b683bf542</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALPHITOBIUS DIAPERINUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A beetle species studied for bacterial and fungal diversity in its gut when fed polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alphitobius diaperinus is one of the edible insects studied for nitrogen-protein conversion factors, indicating its potential as a food source."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alphitobius diaperinus, or lesser mealworms, were studied for their gut microbiome changes upon PS feeding."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alphitobius diaperinus, also known as the lesser mealworm, has been studied for its metabolic responses during food shortages and recovery at different temperatures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alphitobius diaperinus, also known as the lesser mealworm, is an insect species studied for its protein content."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alphitobius diaperinus is a coleopteran species, also known as the lesser mealworm, capable of feeding on and degrading polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alphitobius diaperinus, or lesser mealworm, is a pest known for its potential role in degrading polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-97444337eddb4e9e3d88bde93ce02aef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19868f1234aac10de61c710c8352c076&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56af57b5211422531c03b0cbcfded1b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56af93e805daf3987d95ff99ab8e891d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-001e8f54368c9a236f702fd09cddf4a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5279ebea7d4d5e22eebe3106de3ba1c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93d5b1c190fdca6b5e456b1513515be4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PEDIOCOCCUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A genus of lactic acid bacteria that may contribute to maintaining a healthy gut microbiome environment."&lt;SEP&gt;"A genus within Firmicutes associated with the PU diet at various stages of the experiment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pediococcus is a genus of bacteria present in control yellow mealworms but disappeared in PS-fed ones."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pediococcus exhibited high abundance in PS- and CS-fed larvae, associated with lignocellulose or plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pediococcus is a lactic acid bacterium whose abundance increases with bran supplementation in the diet."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-630e33352368a0c7f34d56ad45a38e56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eaf1f7b81bc271c665d7776cc3114a92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6746a90a5be233f46211ddf406c02e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93d5b1c190fdca6b5e456b1513515be4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64e35cb810117768309e5f4db5d7e6b8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WEISSELLA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A bacterial genus showing differential abundance between styrene and ethylene diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Weissella is a genus of bacteria present in control yellow mealworms but disappeared in PS-fed ones."&lt;SEP&gt;"Weissella is enriched in the gut of CS-fed larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Weissella is a genus of bacteria found in the gut of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Weissella, a gut-associated bacterium, disappears in plastic-fed groups, reflecting dietary shifts."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-476e13b69587aa4e81395e2fd00a9d5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32f340b7166025be3c56178a94ae480d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81f09d7c1a5d91a7a0b4766ca0e47f56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93d5b1c190fdca6b5e456b1513515be4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64e35cb810117768309e5f4db5d7e6b8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HYPHOPICHIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hyphopichia is a fungal genus that was predominant in the guts of bran-fed superworms and yellow mealworms but decreased or disappeared in plastic-fed groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hyphopichia is a genus of fungi predominant in bran-fed superworms and yellow mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dbb6f13dbe3de759712fa3a0c9780470&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93d5b1c190fdca6b5e456b1513515be4</data>
