    <node id="&quot;PENICILLIUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Penicillium is a fungal genus considered as a potential candidate for plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Penicillium is a genus of fungi, including species like Penicillium pinophilum, which participate in the biodegradation of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Penicillium is a fungal genus identified as significantly more abundant in PS samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Penicillium is a fungal genus including species capable of breaking C—C bonds in polyethylene and mineralizing polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Penicillium is a fungal genus that appeared overrepresented in PS samples with a Log2-fold change of 16.3, but was recovered rarely in resamples."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d9095195e9cf06b9887c03abde6284d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6ddf9dd30d7258964408f9a915d3478&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1070f8c33eb8afcfcffac95df9012d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1d3c25b9affee2f535cb531a09a2384&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbb6f13dbe3de759712fa3a0c9780470</data>
    </node>
