      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hydrogen Production refers to the biological process where hydrogen is generated as a byproduct, often linked with microbial activities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hydrogen production involves generating hydrogen gas, often using catalysts or other innovative methods."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hydrogen production is a biological process occurring in microbial electrolysis cells, influenced by factors like L-cysteine."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dc31a0931fceb1446bc6ec4d0c587f7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf54b3c2c01c935a178261a31b8ed897&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e77298fbeb95f87269261b74c2158d5e</data>
    </node>
