      <data key="d1">"Microbial Degradation involves the use of microorganisms to break down complex substances such as plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbial degradation is the process by which microorganisms break down complex organic substances, such as PET plastics, into simpler compounds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbial degradation processes target the breakdown of plastic wastes into simpler compounds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbial degradation refers to the breakdown of materials like PET by microorganisms or their enzymes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbial degradation involves the breakdown of complex substances, such as plastic waste, by microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbial degradation refers to the breakdown of materials by microorganisms, such as bacteria and fungi, often focusing on plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbial degradation refers to the breakdown of organic materials, including plastics like polystyrene, by microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The process by which microorganisms break down complex organic substances, such as plastics, into simpler compounds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbial degradation involves the breakdown of complex substances by microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbial degradation is the breakdown of organic materials by microorganisms, including bacteria and fungi, through enzymatic processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbial degradation refers to the breakdown of synthetic plastics by microorganisms, including bacteria and fungi, as a natural process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbial degradation refers to the breakdown of complex organic substances by microorganisms, such as in the case of starch-based polypropylene."</data>
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
    </node>
