      <data key="d1">"Cultural-dependent methods are used to study the gut-associated bacteria in Tenebrio molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut-associated bacteria are microorganisms living in the digestive tract of animals, playing roles in digestion and degradation of substances."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut-associated bacteria are microorganisms present in the digestive system of Tenebrio molitor larvae, playing roles in biodegradation processes."</data>
