    <node id="&quot;EXTRACELLULAR DEPOLYMERASES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Extracellular Depolymerases are secreted by gut bacteria to break down complex polymers like plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Extracellular depolymerases are enzymes secreted outside the cell that act on polymer chains to facilitate their breakdown."&lt;SEP&gt;"Extracellular depolymerases catalyze the depolymerization of plastic polymers, producing shorter linear chains."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e5a228b2d8328bdce2419d34f8f59bc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dea2d94de229e98ea99b0d40b7b077ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31f2ee9a779791fef2da810debc12720</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;XENOBIOTICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Foreign compounds not naturally present in the environment, often degraded by specific bacterial strains."&lt;SEP&gt;"Xenobiotics are foreign chemical substances that can be degraded by microbial communities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Xenobiotics are foreign compounds in an organism's body, such as plastic degradation intermediates treated as harmful substances."&lt;SEP&gt;"Xenobiotics are foreign compounds not naturally found in an organism's body, such as intermediates from plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Xenobiotics are foreign compounds not naturally produced or expected to be present in living organisms, often requiring special degradation mechanisms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0f2fd4b2e978e6745e0dde602114a826&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5a228b2d8328bdce2419d34f8f59bc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31f2ee9a779791fef2da810debc12720&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e3ac1a351ece6e7f29ea15d8b1c721d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a8b07ee5dc7a7af59a93d03311efe60</data>
