    <node id="&quot;LINEAR LOW-DENSITY POLYETHYLENE (LLDPE)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of polyethylene similar to LDPE but with improved strength and flexibility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Linear low-density polyethylene is a variant of polyethylene found in commercial mulching films."&lt;SEP&gt;"Linear low-density polyethylene is a variant of polyethylene with linear chains and improved strength."&lt;SEP&gt;"LLDPE is a type of polyethylene with medium crystallinity (20–60%) and more short chain branching than HDPE."&lt;SEP&gt;"LLDPE is a type of polyethylene with linear molecules and higher short chain branching compared to HDPE, leading to intermediate crystallinity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Linear Low-Density Polyethylene is a type of plastic that cannot be degraded by T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"LLDPE is a type of polyethylene that mealworms can ingest and oxidize."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e5a228b2d8328bdce2419d34f8f59bc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-326a8dda1cdd196236b9c836192c76f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-acbe3a2cb3a17985d07d15bed638bd90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe381daaa91bbff20758798e5baf82b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6eb7955dc484d5f656e1be7b406abb3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa9972450967f344c19cb747d7ce649e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-567c36cf69b624a7ec0d891d3bd15163</data>
    </node>
