      <data key="d1">"A bacterial strain isolated from the gut of waxworms capable of degrading PE."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacter asburiae YT1 is a PE-degrading bacterial strain isolated from the intestine of plodia interpunctella larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacter asburiae YT1 is a bacterial strain capable of degrading polyethylene films."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacter asburiae YT1 is another bacterial strain known for its ability to degrade LDPE."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacter asburiae YT1 is a gut bacterium able to remove approximately 6.1% of LDPE films after 60 days."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacter asburiae YT1 is a bacterium capable of degrading commercial LDPE film."</data>
