      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Another bacterial strain isolated from the gut of waxworms capable of degrading PE."&lt;SEP&gt;"Another bacterial strain present in the gut of waxworms capable of degrading polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus sp. YP1 is another bacterial strain isolated from waxworm gut that can degrade polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus sp. YP1 is a bacterial strain capable of degrading LDPE."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus sp. YP1 is a bacterium isolated from Plodia interpunctella that degrades LDPE."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus sp. YP1 is another gut bacterium capable of removing about 10.7% of LDPE films after 60 days."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus sp. YP1 is another PE-degrading bacterial strain isolated from the intestine of plodia interpunctella larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus sp. YP1 is a bacterium isolated from the gut of waxworms, capable of degrading polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus sp. YP1 is another bacterium involved in the degradation of commercial LDPE film."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus sp. YP1 is a bacterial strain capable of degrading polyethylene, isolated from the gut of PE plastic-eating waxworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus sp. YP1 is a polyethylene-degrading bacterial strain isolated from the gut of plastic-eating waxworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus sp. YP1 is a polyethylene-degrading bacterium isolated from the gut of plastic-eating waxworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus sp. YP1 is a bacterium that contributes to the degradation of commercial LDPE film."</data>
