    <node id="&quot;DIFFERENTIALLY EXPRESSED GENES (DEGS)">
      <data key="d0">GENE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Differentially expressed genes are identified through RNA sequencing to understand metabolic pathways and functional enzymes involved in plastic degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-566d464a7713ef7ca266f3d5f24a1a59</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LLDPE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">Linear Low-Density Polyethylene (LLDPE) is a type of polyethylene characterized by linear chains and shorter side branches compared to other variants like LDPE. It exhibits unique structural and anisotropic properties, contributing to its flexibility, strength, and specific applications in commercial products, often mixed with LDPE. LLDPE plays a significant role in global plastic production alongside LDPE, with differences in structure influencing their respective applications and biodegradability.

In studies focused on biodegradation, LLDPE has been included in experimental diets for mealworms and other insect larvae, such as *Tenebrio molitor* and *Tenebrio obscurus*. While it is consumed by these larvae, the extent of biodegradation is intermediate compared to other forms of polyethylene, such as LDPE and HDPE. The degradation process involves significant molecular weight changes, increased crystallinity, and limited depolymerization. Despite being less biodegradable than LDPE, LLDPE undergoes some level of breakdown when processed by larvae, inducing oxidative stress, ecotoxicity, and physiological impairments in the organisms.

The inclusion of LLDPE in the diet of larvae has also been observed to affect gut microbiome composition uniquely, suggesting an interaction between the plastic material and microbial functions within the digestive system. Further investigation into its biodegradability and potential ecological impacts remains necessary due to its persistence as a poorly biodegradable polymer. Overall, LLDPE represents a critical subject of study in understanding the environmental implications of plastic consumption by insects and the mechanisms underlying its breakdown.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-630e33352368a0c7f34d56ad45a38e56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8eca628f2d85c664191a5205194ec475&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30a7209d626a6319ba5600bea7f27299&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b30daa90b5c91314e1d65e87f191166&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa33fb34ba06610c290cdfd8a5b4e916&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-566d464a7713ef7ca266f3d5f24a1a59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90367ecb21e0f14b2e548acf307a2628&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2169963c4d6dae9b98da331d39eaa72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9528beb2e85a7fb89449a9233eb979bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26a193cc62c03cb6460b0434df42d8c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-718900b924b6910a58e8ead81c01c723&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4cdbea1d06006b95d57c8b628d9e3f8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ac1b1db6ffab6f4cfea7a525785a2fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd4d84d6de496440fcabc6616d1c96ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e1faf524e6fabeb512a07b13f37e51e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8c6850a83a1c6efd4f1a3a37a0a8181&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd73d3cca5434181ee9dd1ad1b8f8ab9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98d4ea946a931acf7e5a8292c30ea4c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffb4e34985ec90215629dc19750c8bdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc908e62eec4d1d05265c6e451cca84c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b21eb0db725b38c3e0b5c01526ce90b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f75b58db5211fc7348ccca8206b9bbae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a24fcfbc571e8620a1fc59b215b42e56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96aac7c9638ee245b9db5df3ec1d2a1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3380732c060363504db5f6e4b8610b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1006283f24aba2aa605f9e719f36cf9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-988ef111808996ddbe6e483d6505ab45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLESIOPHTHALIMUS DAVIDIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"INSECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Plesiophthalimus davidis is an insect reported to degrade plastics like PS, PE, PVC, and PP."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-566d464a7713ef7ca266f3d5f24a1a59</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLODIA INTERPUNCTELLA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">**Plodia interpunctella**, commonly known as the Indian meal moth, is a species of moth whose larvae have been extensively studied for their ability to degrade and penetrate various types of plastics. This insect species is capable of damaging packaging materials made from polyethylene (PE), polypropylene (PP), polyvinyl chloride (PVC), and polystyrene (PS). The larvae of **Plodia interpunctella**, often referred to as waxworms, have demonstrated the ability to chew through and consume PE films, contributing to the biodegradation of these materials.

The gut microbiota of **Plodia interpunctella** plays a significant role in this process. Microbes within the midgut of the larvae, including *Enterobacter absurcis YT1*, have been identified as contributors to the degradation of plastics. These microbes are capable of breaking down complex polymers, making **Plodia interpunctella** an intriguing subject for research into organic waste biodegradation and potential solutions for plastic pollution.

In addition to its role in plastic degradation, **Plodia interpunctella** is also known for its ability to penetrate and damage packaging films, posing challenges in food storage and preservation. Overall, the Indian meal moth represents a dual aspect: both a pest in stored food environments and a potential ally in addressing environmental issues related to plastic waste.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-086890e8567c60d8cfa7c03b0cc61f9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b27c93b39534612a0492f52ce1f3cd8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0c513c586aa89e48e9570525bfc5366&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-566d464a7713ef7ca266f3d5f24a1a59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7232abef4870641de7945afeb6a4bf93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa9972450967f344c19cb747d7ce649e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0462cccaa75cf13e553e16026939880b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-567c36cf69b624a7ec0d891d3bd15163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c02a8ea5e75c58dcb9cfbbcd64f37d82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24ba7d6b1b5275089cbabe56bc33b92e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffb4e34985ec90215629dc19750c8bdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4da90774e2e5cb1fea30fd5aa390760&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cb5478046e8b80ff49694ccdb8f92fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e05bc34fccfca5e177064daf8346866&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bd104d06a1ede06701ecfa96bccc2c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d7500fe4985cb2b885f9eb244ed3c2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-566afea8a2a89bd188f68d0afa1bb173&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd1ab39969c669dba42f162e8497c23f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-694aaaa7c2839ea048d46b6a2bb13748</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANTIBIOTICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Antibiotics are substances administered to suppress gut microbiota, affecting PS depolymerization rates in certain studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibiotics are substances that inhibit bacterial growth, used here to select resistant strains."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibiotics are substances used in the study to depress gut microbes, leading to inhibited polystyrene degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibiotics are used to suppress gut bacteria activity in mealworms, affecting their ability to degrade plastics such as PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibiotics such as gentamicin sulfate, erythrocin, chloramphenicol, tetracycline, ampicillin, and kanamycin suppress gut bacteria, enabling examination of larval PET biodegradation independent of microbial action."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibiotics like gentamicin inhibit gut microbes, affecting plastic depolymerization."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibiotics are substances used to inhibit the growth of bacteria. In this context, they were used to treat mealworms to test their residual effects on the gut microbiome."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibiotics are used to suppress the gut microbiome activity, highlighting its necessity in plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibiotics were used in some experiments to treat specimens, affecting their behavior and potentially altering the results."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibiotics can affect the gut microbiota of mealworms, potentially impacting their ability to biodegrade plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibiotics influence the microbial community and can have adverse effects on gut microbiota."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibiotics were added to the diet at a specific ratio to observe their effects on larvae and gut bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibiotics are substances used to suppress microbial gut communities, which disrupts the degradation of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibiotics are substances used to eliminate gut microbiota, revealing their role in nitrogen fixation within mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibiotics are substances that suppress the growth of microorganisms, used in experiments to inhibit gut microbiota involved in polystyrene degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2fb515eae7af2b662d5d600120e7001&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-196a7570e6cac531e94c1680c54f5491&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-681ece0a8beca8b22f3c6aa11a564f63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20395efa1299dc8b777774e765ad1159&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07aae06c64778453da4bda48f5347de5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-813b71242f366f10218c10631cd7dee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af682f78e3e8970d7d70b027a8f79116&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-566d464a7713ef7ca266f3d5f24a1a59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10474cc69c90eb0c245c8f55d1ec2834&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a221e0c62ecd5a2502ec0a4473ab0999&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-395b01f15fd97b70e2368941120e9a37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-668212da3bf356132cadb63df6ce09b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-001e8f54368c9a236f702fd09cddf4a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b673e7590aa1d03b7721694ed73cd74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2cfbb4289b0cc4c8b69884f6d57c447</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DENSITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A measure of mass per unit volume, negatively correlated with PS consumption but less influential than crystallinity."&lt;SEP&gt;"A physical characteristic of plastics, negatively correlated with PS consumption."&lt;SEP&gt;"Density is a physical property of plastics that influences their degradation by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Density is a physical property of the plastics being studied."&lt;SEP&gt;"A measure of mass per unit volume, relevant to the physical characteristics of EPS foam packaging."&lt;SEP&gt;"Density is a physical property that measures the mass per unit volume of materials, such as plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Density is a measure of mass per unit volume, used here as an indicator of material compactness."&lt;SEP&gt;"Density is a physical property that influences how easily mealworms can consume PS materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"Density refers to the mass per unit volume of materials, such as polystyrene products, which varies depending on their type and application."&lt;SEP&gt;"Density is the mass per unit volume of the polystyrene foam, measured as \(0.0197 \pm 0.0009 \, \text{g/cm}^3\)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The mass per unit volume of a substance, here referring to the density of PP foam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Density refers to the mass per unit volume, measured for larvae and PS chips during experiments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8bb63b06976c3a8e6f2cea85c1ecf518&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96aac7c9638ee245b9db5df3ec1d2a1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8ee8f544a1849c80a5a1524c4f2674c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53dd546535ef4247004faab1fa475889&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3815960770483b9c0a1579ca8442e3a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30a7209d626a6319ba5600bea7f27299&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5740f0973ff804cae61f6fc12f3e3753&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-718900b924b6910a58e8ead81c01c723&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fb9111bd088e1990cde867c6d85cf28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-566d464a7713ef7ca266f3d5f24a1a59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf662c8e784d14a3a4dba2e89041aa4a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SHORE HARDNESS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Shore hardness (HD) is a measure of the hardness of plastics, which affects their interaction with mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Shore hardness is a measure of the hardness of the studied plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Shore hardness is a measure used to assess the hardness of materials, with PSr and PS measured on the Shore D scale."&lt;SEP&gt;"Shore hardness is a measure used to characterize the physical properties of polystyrene materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"Shore hardness is a physical property used to measure the hardness of materials like PS and PSr."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3d47d39d364c5c66ef3fc32ef741ca63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41635122b30ee45048cc885b38fff6ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-718900b924b6910a58e8ead81c01c723&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-566d464a7713ef7ca266f3d5f24a1a59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06a44b308af148551c5b7feef324d88b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CRYSTALLINITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A measure of the degree of structural order in a solid, affecting plastic consumption and degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Crystallinity measures the degree of structural order in the plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Crystallinity refers to the degree of crystalline structure in plastics, impacting their degradation by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Crystallinity refers to the degree of structural order in a polymer, impacting the rate and extent of PET degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Crystallinity refers to the degree of structural order in polymers, which can be affected by biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Crystallinity refers to the degree of structural order in a polymer, which can change during digestion."&lt;SEP&gt;"The degree of structural order in polyethylene, affecting its susceptibility to biodegradation; lower crystallinity facilitates degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Crystallinity is the degree of structural order in a solid, reduced during the biodegradation of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Crystallinity measures the ordered structure of HDPE, which decreases due to microbial attack during biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Crystallinity refers to the degree of structural order in a polymer, which can be altered during biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Crystallinity refers to the degree of structural order in a polymer, affecting its biodegradability."&lt;SEP&gt;"Crystallinity refers to the degree of structural order in a polymer, affecting its susceptibility to enzymatic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Crystallinity describes the degree of structural order in a polymer, impacting its resistance to biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Crystallinity refers to the degree of structural order in polyethylene, affecting its physical properties and degradability."&lt;SEP&gt;"Crystallinity is a physical property of materials, indicating the degree of structural order in a solid."&lt;SEP&gt;"Crystallinity refers to the degree of long-range order in a material, affecting the hardness, density, and biodegradability of polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Crystallinity of plastics impacts their biodegradation efficiency."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1e45f9527e7b07e945435dae572dc387&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-acbe3a2cb3a17985d07d15bed638bd90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b42ef7860e1f056d47955d0d13a15cd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96aac7c9638ee245b9db5df3ec1d2a1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79c11bccb4ef9bd152bdae9b5c2c5c8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffb4e34985ec90215629dc19750c8bdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8eca628f2d85c664191a5205194ec475&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6eb7955dc484d5f656e1be7b406abb3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1679027e80b766e0469f7323db15b497&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b12468cce513394dbebb8b4ce27f62d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30a7209d626a6319ba5600bea7f27299&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1006283f24aba2aa605f9e719f36cf9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-718900b924b6910a58e8ead81c01c723&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-566d464a7713ef7ca266f3d5f24a1a59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-567c36cf69b624a7ec0d891d3bd15163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6675480dfd01dcb533166d01b8e5482e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b673e7590aa1d03b7721694ed73cd74</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RNA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MARKER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"RNA (ribonucleic acid) is indirectly analyzed through the study of bacterial 16S rRNA genes."&lt;SEP&gt;"RNA serves as a biomarker for understanding gene expression changes in mealworms when fed different diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"RNA extracted from bacterial samples serves as a biological marker for gene expression analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ribonucleic acid, a molecule involved in coding, decoding, regulation, and expression of genes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e81a4fde1bdef8287df342fc27193de6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53ab7dd83bf51674598c6a5bdd146b90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c426315f0f412528b9c6fb2a82dff2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-718900b924b6910a58e8ead81c01c723</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLASTICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Materials often derived from petrochemicals, subject to production, use, and environmental impact studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastics are materials that are mass-produced and often end up in landfills and oceans, causing environmental pollution."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastics are synthetic polymers that can enter the Antarctic marine system, posing potential environmental risks."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastics refer to synthetic materials whose molecular weight and functional groups were analyzed during the experiment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastics refer to synthetic materials derived from polymers, which are being studied for their biodegradability by microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastics, such as Styrofoam and LDPE, serve as a nutrient source for certain microorganisms in the larval gut."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastics are synthetic materials derived from polymers, widely used in various industries but posing environmental concerns."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastics are synthetic materials made from a wide range of organic polymers, often used in various applications due to their durability and versatility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastics are synthetic materials derived from polymers, widely used in various industries but posing environmental concerns due to their persistence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastics are synthetic polymers that undergo environmental cycling, including biodegradation and mineralization."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastics refer to materials such as HDPE, LDPE, PP, PVC, and PS that were tested for mealworm consumption. These materials lack essential nutrients like vitamins, minerals, and proteins."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastics are synthetic materials derived from polymers, widely used in various industries but posing significant environmental challenges."&lt;SEP&gt;"Synthetic materials made from polymers, which are often persistent in the environment and pose pollution challenges."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3891caf14683493be3d8709ced467492&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dad389953d78e790a40a9267c5b591c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df896f6505a6c800d1edd6c75fce9b4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20a69982e6abe36c2a0d4a70b78720ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19868f1234aac10de61c710c8352c076&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41635122b30ee45048cc885b38fff6ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eaf641df5c55c7ff41895611514cdd22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b50c5a85182344022614ffe10dc9382&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-718900b924b6910a58e8ead81c01c723&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03980ce7209ce3f1b1c62c6ed9961e27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b387da8298c55673284dca93ea82fc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81b6237c84f002117fbfe7575d9cdd6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44e006d8af33633a06dac6789334329d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PDI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PDI (Polydispersity Index) gives an indication of the broadness of the polymer distribution, which increases after PET passes through the larval gut."&lt;SEP&gt;"PDI (Polydispersity Index) measures the distribution of molecular weights in polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polydispersity index, indicating the range of molecular weights in a polymer sample."&lt;SEP&gt;"PDI (Polydispersity Index) measures the distribution of molecular weights in a polymer sample, with higher values indicating broader distributions."&lt;SEP&gt;"PDI (Polydispersity Index) measures the distribution of molecular weights in a polymer sample, indicating the heterogeneity of the polymer after degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polydispersity Index (PDI) quantifies the heterogeneity of polymer chain lengths, increasing during PS biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polydispersity index (PDI) measures the heterogeneity of molecular weights in polymer samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polydispersity index (PDI) measures the heterogeneity in chain-length distributions of polymers. An increase in PDI indicates endo-type depolymerization or random internal scission of polymer chains."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bd73d3cca5434181ee9dd1ad1b8f8ab9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-beb3c133fa4d5851f0feff55507c6874&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1536c14bdcd58ae9dabf3a49f6724cd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbc20d6948e6ca1157ecd7f80a183952&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67028993c2650049216602d03fb3f786&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-846559469c70e081884fea2f9a4b7317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-718900b924b6910a58e8ead81c01c723&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f545e57b1a2b3da8601b4d23e1260c94</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRANSCRIPTOME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A collection of all RNA molecules in a cell or population of cells, used here to study gene expression changes."&lt;SEP&gt;"The transcriptome refers to the complete set of RNA transcripts produced by the genome, reflecting gene expression changes during polypropylene biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Transcriptome encompasses all RNA molecules produced in the mealworms under different feeding conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Transcriptome refers to the set of all RNA molecules produced in one sample or cell."&lt;SEP&gt;"The transcriptome represents the complete set of RNA transcripts produced by an organism, providing insights into gene expression during plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The transcriptome represents the complete set of RNA transcripts produced by an organism under specific conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-91523cdd8f510a966e9b301a0adb96b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-152e743d95b64fab136afadf0304d459&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-718900b924b6910a58e8ead81c01c723&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbdeaa1a437ba819412de45788aa119c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-566afea8a2a89bd188f68d0afa1bb173&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcc545cfe4d6e8e04c3698a149d4101a</data>
    </node>
