    <node id="&quot;ANOVA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"STATISTICAL METHOD"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A statistical method used for pairwise analysis of identified components in frass fractions."&lt;SEP&gt;"A statistical technique used for analyzing variance among groups to identify significant differences."&lt;SEP&gt;"A statistical technique used to compare means across multiple groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"ANOVA, or analysis of variance, is a statistical method used to analyze differences between group means."&lt;SEP&gt;"Analysis of variance used to determine statistical significance."&lt;SEP&gt;"ANOVA (Analysis of Variance) is a statistical method used to compare means between groups in this study."&lt;SEP&gt;"Analysis of variance used to test differences between means of biometric parameters."&lt;SEP&gt;"ANOVA assesses significant differences among groups in terms of survival rates, weight changes, and microbial diversity."&lt;SEP&gt;"ANOVA is a statistical method used to evaluate differences in plastic consumption, turbidity assay, biofilm formation, and particle count analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"ANOVA assesses significant differences in PS and PU consumption rates, larval survival rates, and gut microbial diversities."&lt;SEP&gt;"ANOVA (Analysis of Variance) is a statistical technique used to compare the mean values of various parameters across different groups in the experiment."&lt;SEP&gt;"ANOVA is a statistical method used to evaluate differences in PE consumption and changes in molecular weight."&lt;SEP&gt;"ANOVA (Analysis of Variance) was performed to analyze the statistical significance of results."&lt;SEP&gt;"Analysis of variance is a statistical method used to assess significant differences in experimental data."&lt;SEP&gt;"Analysis of variance (ANOVA) was used to evaluate significant differences in survival indices and molecular weight values."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a38c714e7f1f701ec1149e25910e16e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6a80044bea074bdbcb68f489aa8af0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c095cc3175666d5093fe411f9a39cb66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e557113f1cfd2472fa9c51d1cdc3069a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a27dff473ed210517e6461ad3e5d783&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8f677b3b4d06e07d3a58446375133fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3380732c060363504db5f6e4b8610b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb1740bb657b0f90c48ee5e6d75945ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-512840a413df7ae3d881389c5cf1feb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb1c38c1c6dc6fea84d8f51b9f706cd2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b693d867918f89c9b28997fe94fc830&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c810740a381d4d9e829e28c01e62564&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4cdbea1d06006b95d57c8b628d9e3f8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6dce72fccb3df94ec407aba3d4df8eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f545e57b1a2b3da8601b4d23e1260c94</data>
    </node>
