    <node id="&quot;POLY(ETHYLENE TEREPHTHALATE)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A plastic polymer that is less degradable due to its high crystallinity, studied in relation to Ideonella sakaiensis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Poly(ethylene terephthalate) is a type of plastic polymer that can be degraded by specific enzymes and microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"PET is a synthetic polymer commonly used in plastics and targeted for degradation by specific enzymes and bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Poly(Ethylene Terephthalate), or PET, is a widely used thermoplastic polymer primarily utilized in bottles and fibers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Poly(ethylene terephthalate) (PET) is a thermoplastic polymer that can be degraded by specific bacteria."</data>
