    <node id="&quot;CYP6A2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CYP6A2 is a cytochrome P450 enzyme potentially involved in the metabolism of fatty acids."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dea2d94de229e98ea99b0d40b7b077ad</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CYP9F2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CYP9F2 is another cytochrome P450 enzyme whose expression increases in response to dietary changes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dea2d94de229e98ea99b0d40b7b077ad</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LINEAR BACKBONE OF LDPE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL FEATURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The linear backbone of LDPE is a structural characteristic that influences how plastics are broken down into shorter chains."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dea2d94de229e98ea99b0d40b7b077ad</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BENZENE RING SIDE GROUPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNCTIONAL GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Benzene ring side groups are chemical structures found in polystyrene, affecting its degradation process."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dea2d94de229e98ea99b0d40b7b077ad</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EPS-FED GROUP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DIET"</data>
      <data key="d1">"EPS-fed refers to a diet where mealworms are fed on expanded polystyrene, leading to specific changes in gene expression."&lt;SEP&gt;"The EPS-fed group refers to subjects consuming EPS (exopolysaccharides) as part of their diet."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dea2d94de229e98ea99b0d40b7b077ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73db2a18ccd822d0da3ef61e68d3a6f6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LDPE-FED GROUP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DIET"</data>
      <data key="d1">"LDPE-fed refers to a diet where mealworms are fed on low-density polyethylene, resulting in distinct metabolic and genetic responses."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dea2d94de229e98ea99b0d40b7b077ad</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENE FAMILIES RELATED TO SHORT-CHAIN FATTY ACID DEGRADATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENETIC CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"These gene families are involved in the metabolism of short-chain fatty acids, showing increased expression in certain conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dea2d94de229e98ea99b0d40b7b077ad</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARBON, METHANE, AND PROPANOATE METABOLISM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"This biological process involves the metabolism of carbon compounds, methane, and propanoates, often upregulated in specific dietary contexts."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dea2d94de229e98ea99b0d40b7b077ad</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BEESWAX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A long-chain hydrocarbon compound metabolized by Galleria mellonella, demonstrating microbiota-independent metabolic capabilities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Beeswax is a long-chain hydrocarbon metabolized by Galleria mellonella larvae, highlighting their metabolic capabilities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Beeswax is a natural polymer that Galleria Mellonella can metabolize independently of its microbiota."&lt;SEP&gt;"Beeswax is a natural product rich in hydrocarbon chains, used as a dietary component in some studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Beeswax is a substance that influences gene expression related to carboxylesterase and lipase families in organisms consuming it."&lt;SEP&gt;"Beeswax is a natural wax produced by honey bees, composed of long-chain hydrocarbons that can be metabolized by certain organisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Beeswax is a natural wax produced by honey bees, used in various applications and studied for its biodegradability."&lt;SEP&gt;"Beeswax is a natural substance produced by honeybees with various chemical compositions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Beeswax is a natural substance produced by honey bees, consisting of esters of long-chain alcohols and fatty acids, used for larval development and food storage."&lt;SEP&gt;"Beeswax is a natural wax produced by honey bees, metabolized independently of microbiota by Galleria mellonella."&lt;SEP&gt;"Beeswax is the diet provided to G. mellonella larvae prior to experimentation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Beeswax is a natural wax produced by honey bees, composed primarily of long-chain hydrocarbons."&lt;SEP&gt;"Beeswax is a natural wax produced by honey bees, which can be metabolized by certain organisms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ca3745cb01a4209e2eae28914dde3b52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d40b7debb6497167fa1aec874ebce45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab6b219720db5a6e3384c884c280984c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31f2ee9a779791fef2da810debc12720&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-648afbc8ee82935d4026f5915152491c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f15cc70e99a3287ced1a6cbb6c8d76a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e3ac1a351ece6e7f29ea15d8b1c721d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-032b3b0fe0366e6e76e86abf8c48d200&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dea2d94de229e98ea99b0d40b7b077ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a3e42eecd3967a9e53cfadc926363ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95142a3f585446bd848eeedadd1ab713&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b50c5a85182344022614ffe10dc9382&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbdeaa1a437ba819412de45788aa119c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HYDROCARBON CHAINS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hydrocarbon chains are long molecular structures found in various products like beeswax and plastics, serving as substrates for enzymatic activity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dea2d94de229e98ea99b0d40b7b077ad</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIPASE 1 AND 3 FAMILIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lipase 1 and 3 families are enzymes involved in breaking down lipids, showing overexpression in certain dietary conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dea2d94de229e98ea99b0d40b7b077ad</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIPASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An enzyme that catalyzes the hydrolysis of lipids into glycerol and free fatty acids."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzymes that hydrolyze lipids into fatty acids and glycerol, often involved in biodegradation processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipase is an enzyme encoded by the PueA gene in Pseudomonas chlororaphis, capable of breaking down ester bonds in lipids and polyesters."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipase is an enzyme produced by various microorganisms, including Rhizopus delemar, that catalyzes the hydrolysis of ester bonds in plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipase is an enzyme responsible for breaking down fats into fatty acids and glycerol, with certain families being overexpressed in larvae fed on beeswax."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipase facilitates the hydrolysis of lipids and participates in the generation of long-chain fatty acids from PS and lignin degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipase is an enzyme that catalyzes the hydrolysis of lipids, playing a role in breaking down complex molecules like PET."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipase is an enzyme that breaks down lipids into fatty acids and glycerol."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipase is an extracellular enzyme produced by Achromobacter lipolyticum, which catalyzes lipid hydrolysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-158317f8eba5f6198135df044d385935&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55bdcf1b4859e82ab15050837ab539dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2741fab96df80d452d2d4cc651730521&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3934e2c5488a209e54e10ba4c0335a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31f2ee9a779791fef2da810debc12720&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81610bdb5fdb95d9a333b42668532b9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67425e341a5b2c8102281581fa148554&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bb7b0638c9c59e134df0491b542efdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4c43611ebe237c15c5f9201a9f8dbee</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SHORT-CHAIN FATTY ACID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Short-chain fatty acids are metabolites produced from wax degradation and their degradation pathways are upregulated in gut tissues of G. mellonella larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-31f2ee9a779791fef2da810debc12720</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;METHANE METABOLISM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Methane metabolism involves biochemical reactions that produce or consume methane, which were upregulated in larvae fed on beeswax."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-31f2ee9a779791fef2da810debc12720</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROPANOATE METABOLISM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Propanoate metabolism includes biochemical processes for the production or consumption of propanoate, upregulated in larvae consuming beeswax."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-31f2ee9a779791fef2da810debc12720</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;N-ACETYLTRANSFERASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"N-acetyltransferase catalyzes the acetylation of aryl amines from acetyl-CoA, participating in isoniazid metabolism."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-31f2ee9a779791fef2da810debc12720</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ISONIAZID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DRUG"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Isoniazid is an antibiotic primarily used in the treatment of tuberculosis, undergoing metabolic reactions such as acetylation and hydrolysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-31f2ee9a779791fef2da810debc12720</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CYTOCHROME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROTEIN"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cytochrome proteins are involved in electron transport and oxidative phosphorylation, potentially linked to wax degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-31f2ee9a779791fef2da810debc12720</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FATTY ACIDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LIPID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fatty acids are bioactive molecules identified in the polar fraction of frass during metabolomics analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fatty acids are components of lipids stored in insects as an energy source during starvation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fatty acids are metabolic products derived from the digestion of plastics like PS, providing energy and carbon for mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fatty acids are organic compounds that may suppress the expression of carboxylesterase in mealworms, particularly unsaturated fatty acids."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fatty acids are organic compounds that serve as substrates in enzymatic reactions leading to α,ω-dicarboxylic acid formation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fatty acids are excreted more in Diets 2 and 3, likely due to biosynthesis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fatty acids are biochemical compounds found in living organisms, including insects, and can be methyl esters derived from modified methods."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fatty acids are essential nutrients examined in relation to larval microbiomes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fatty acids, including saturated, monounsaturated, and polyunsaturated forms, play critical roles in the energy storage and health of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fatty acids stored as triglycerides are an important energy source for insects during starvation, as observed by the depletion of lipids in mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Organic compounds essential for energy storage and cell membrane structure, involved in microbial metabolism."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fatty acids levels change during PS biodegradation, reflecting metabolic stress."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fatty acids are organic molecules found in beeswax and other natural substances, playing a role in the nutritional needs of larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fatty acids are components of fat that contribute to the nutritional value of insects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fatty acids are essential components of lipids, playing critical roles in energy storage and cell membrane structure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fatty acids are essential lipids whose content is evaluated to assess the nutritional value of edible insects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fatty acids are metabolites whose composition and concentration vary based on the diet provided to the mealworm larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fatty acids were analyzed to evaluate the nutritional content of Tenebrio molitor larvae under different feeding conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fatty acids are components of triglycerides and serve as primary energy sources during starvation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ee46611b24ea3848df979ded841f06b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab6b219720db5a6e3384c884c280984c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31f2ee9a779791fef2da810debc12720&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b0b175969d87b3be377f65b988d0a52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2281f98bcfd555a703fd86232dfa42fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0e30f29e9016acae216566f53e60cea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8a706f2bd66291a3ef925114ffd9300&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41635122b30ee45048cc885b38fff6ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ddf4b13293dd3d8d0887af10fc52c98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b74f16813537103549cdcb6770abaea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d01d291012bd548fc067e250ec39fba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b30daa90b5c91314e1d65e87f191166&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba22196a59b67cbf67af7d76a039af1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33180d5b7e1ebfedf8de59ba1a2a2d04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e25fe1af3bede4605e7b94d457c9634&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-531058c4540bd4e6a50d141db01d4d11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e4030ea35bee29093c1a8f19bc90774&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f71fddc259d51158d5c79f38bf41523f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ACETYLATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL REACTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Acetylation is a biochemical process where an acetyl group is transferred to a molecule, playing a role in isoniazid metabolism."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-31f2ee9a779791fef2da810debc12720</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEXATOMIC RINGS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL STRUCTURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hexatomic rings like pyridine and benzene are structural analogs of isoniazid and styrene, monomers of PS."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-31f2ee9a779791fef2da810debc12720</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PS (POLYSTYRENE)">
      <data key="d0">"MATERIAL"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PS or polystyrene is a plastic polymer that undergoes depolymerization and subsequent metabolic processes in mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-31f2ee9a779791fef2da810debc12720</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIPS (HIGH-IMPACT POLYSTYRENE)">
      <data key="d0">"MATERIAL"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HIPS is a type of polystyrene that mealworms can ingest, contributing minimally to their growth."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-31f2ee9a779791fef2da810debc12720</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EPS (EXPANDED POLYSTYRENE)">
      <data key="d0">"MATERIAL"</data>
      <data key="d1">"EPS is a lightweight form of polystyrene that mealworms can consume."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-31f2ee9a779791fef2da810debc12720</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LDPE (LOW-DENSITY POLYETHYLENE)">
      <data key="d0">"MATERIAL"</data>
      <data key="d1">"LDPE is a plastic material that mealworms can ingest but does not significantly contribute to their growth."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-31f2ee9a779791fef2da810debc12720</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LLDPE (LINEAR LOW-DENSITY POLYETHYLENE)">
      <data key="d0">"MATERIAL"</data>
      <data key="d1">"LLDPE is a plastic material that mealworms cannot effectively degrade."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-31f2ee9a779791fef2da810debc12720</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PP (POLYPROPYLENE)">
      <data key="d0">"MATERIAL"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PP is a plastic material that rigid forms are not degraded by mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-31f2ee9a779791fef2da810debc12720</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NAT (N-ACETYLTRANSFERASE)">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"NAT is an enzyme responsible for acetylating aryl amines, playing a role in isoniazid metabolism."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-31f2ee9a779791fef2da810debc12720</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CES2 (CARBOXYLESTERASE 2)">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CES2 is an enzyme that hydrolyzes carboxylic esters and exhibits amide-related activities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-31f2ee9a779791fef2da810debc12720</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GSTS (GLUTATHIONE S-TRANSFERASES)">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"GSTs are enzymes involved in detoxification processes, upregulated in mealworms fed on plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-31f2ee9a779791fef2da810debc12720</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OXYSTEROL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Oxysterols are oxidized derivatives of cholesterol that may act as inhibitors of carboxylesterase."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-31f2ee9a779791fef2da810debc12720</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DR. XI ZHOU&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dr. Xi Zhou provided technical support for the project and is associated with the Institute of Analysis, Guangdong Academy of Sciences."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4cdbea1d06006b95d57c8b628d9e3f8f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRACCOX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"BRACCOX, or peroxisomal acyl-CoA oxidase 3, is an enzyme involved in metabolic processes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4cdbea1d06006b95d57c8b628d9e3f8f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CES, or carboxylesterase, is an enzyme that hydrolyzes ester bonds."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4cdbea1d06006b95d57c8b628d9e3f8f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CPY, or cytochrome P450, is a family of enzymes involved in oxidation reactions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4cdbea1d06006b95d57c8b628d9e3f8f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CPY6A1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CPY6A1, or cytochrome P450 6A1, is a specific enzyme within the cytochrome P450 family."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4cdbea1d06006b95d57c8b628d9e3f8f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GSTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"GSTs, or glutathione S-transferases, are enzymes involved in detoxification processes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4cdbea1d06006b95d57c8b628d9e3f8f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KAT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"KAT, or 3-ketoacyl-CoA thiolase, is an enzyme involved in fatty acid metabolism."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4cdbea1d06006b95d57c8b628d9e3f8f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NAT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"NAT, or N-acetyltransferase, is an enzyme involved in various metabolic pathways."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4cdbea1d06006b95d57c8b628d9e3f8f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MCAD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"MCAD, or medium chain specific acyl-CoA, is an enzyme involved in fatty acid oxidation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4cdbea1d06006b95d57c8b628d9e3f8f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DEG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENETIC CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"DEG refers to differentially expressed genes, which are genes that show changes in expression levels under different conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4cdbea1d06006b95d57c8b628d9e3f8f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FDR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"STATISTICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"FDR, or false discovery rate, is a statistical method for controlling the expected proportion of incorrectly rejected null hypotheses."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4cdbea1d06006b95d57c8b628d9e3f8f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RT-PCR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A technique used to amplify RNA transcripts into cDNA, confirming the expression of specific genes such as nifH."&lt;SEP&gt;"RT-PCR (Reverse Transcription Polymerase Chain Reaction) is used to detect mRNA, indicating the expression of nifH genes."&lt;SEP&gt;"RT-PCR is a technique used to quantify mRNA expression levels."&lt;SEP&gt;"RT-PCR is used to quantify the expression levels of genes encoding degrading enzymes."&lt;SEP&gt;"RT-PCR, or real-time polymerase chain reaction, is a laboratory technique for detecting and quantifying mRNA levels."&lt;SEP&gt;"Real-time polymerase chain reaction, a technique used to validate the expression of differentially expressed genes (DEGs)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reverse Transcription Polymerase Chain Reaction (RT-PCR) combines reverse transcription of RNA into cDNA followed by amplification via PCR."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-158317f8eba5f6198135df044d385935&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac5b96e63e6f5e34fe841f690d9f78ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89c37eb3e3a5b6ab731f5dbe280aa054&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bf827d2b1d02488e17469a22da9e252&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e8cdca8afb1d7153fba5e3c11b1f669&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53ab7dd83bf51674598c6a5bdd146b90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4cdbea1d06006b95d57c8b628d9e3f8f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NCBI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"NCBI (National Center for Biotechnology Information) is a bioinformatics tool used for designing primers, aligning sequences, and conducting sequence analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"NCBI (National Center for Biotechnology Information) is a resource used to blast sequences against nucleotide databases in GenBank."&lt;SEP&gt;"NCBI (National Center for Biotechnology Information) provides access to databases and tools for molecular biology research."&lt;SEP&gt;"NCBI, or National Center for Biotechnology Information, provides access to a large collection of molecular biology databases."&lt;SEP&gt;"NCBI (National Center for Biotechnology Information) is where raw data on microbial diversity and sequences were submitted."&lt;SEP&gt;"NCBI (National Center for Biotechnology Information) is an organization where the nucleotide sequencing data of A. grisella was submitted."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d8b79a6f4c112b0b62ada6756140e3e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e8cdca8afb1d7153fba5e3c11b1f669&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af5eb6a8326b4977801e2f7694a2c750&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d71b4e70d7c620ee64c709aaeae634a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4cdbea1d06006b95d57c8b628d9e3f8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51daa29515cc5a431055291627bcb199</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"GO, or gene ontology, is a major bioinformatics initiative to unify the representation of gene and gene product attributes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4cdbea1d06006b95d57c8b628d9e3f8f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRINITY PLATFORM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Trinity Platform is a computational platform used for de novo transcript sequence reconstruction from RNA-seq data."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-47ee82f655853704e6653d8146973278</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EGGNOG 5.0&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"RESOURCE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"eggNOG 5.0 is an orthology resource providing hierarchical, functional, and phylogenetic annotations based on numerous organisms and viruses."</data>
