    <node id="&quot;YELLOW MEALWORMS (TENEBRIO MOLITOR)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Yellow Mealworms are larvae that can also consume plastics but show lower survival rates and plastic consumption rates compared to superworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Yellow mealworms demonstrate the ability to biodegrade polyether-polyurethane foam, impacting their gut microbiome composition."&lt;SEP&gt;"Yellow mealworms, or Tenebrio molitor, exhibit biodegradation capabilities for polystyrene and low-density polyethylene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-47ee82f655853704e6653d8146973278&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a8076792f39f6c801b538312a7b45fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a53d37e7ff6850fc55177f325e49861</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIPID HOMEOSTASIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lipid homeostasis refers to the balance of lipid synthesis, degradation, and storage within an organism."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipid homeostasis refers to the balance of lipids in the body, which is affected by PET consumption and linked to stress responses."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipid homeostasis refers to the regulation of lipid levels within an organism, which may play a role in polyethylene metabolism in Galleria mellonella larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-47ee82f655853704e6653d8146973278&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5f4bda412174e8b173f180d9b4311ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b19ac5bdc755bb8e9deb8e317ce365dd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CORE GUT MICROBIOME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The core gut microbiome of insects like Galleria mellonella can influence their ability to degrade plastics when supplemented with co-diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"The core gut microbiome refers to the essential microbial community within an organism's digestive system that contributes to various biological processes, including plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The core gut microbiome represents the essential set of microorganisms consistently present in an organism's digestive system."&lt;SEP&gt;"The core gut microbiome refers to the essential microorganisms consistently found in the digestive systems of specific species."&lt;SEP&gt;"The core gut microbiome represents the essential microorganisms present in the digestive system that contribute to specific biological functions, such as plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The core gut microbiome represents the essential microbial communities residing in the digestive tract, influencing health and metabolism."&lt;SEP&gt;"The core gut microbiome represents essential microorganisms involved in the metabolic processes of host organisms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-47ee82f655853704e6653d8146973278&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a8076792f39f6c801b538312a7b45fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79e833cbc3a0a6e2c80e1b69da50317e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bc3253e8d41785f994d1c6fcc2b6c47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b50c5a85182344022614ffe10dc9382&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03980ce7209ce3f1b1c62c6ed9961e27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a31a12c930b59b872c94dda484d0db4</data>
    </node>
