    <node id="&quot;METABOLISM&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-47ee82f655853704e6653d8146973278&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb16cd27b6682965375050748ee77862&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64a060d0c9650ae8bed2ca9b44eef10c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae2c294948460ef392ceeec82d5e81f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b50c5a85182344022614ffe10dc9382</data>
      <data key="d1">"Metabolism encompasses the biochemical processes within organisms, including the digestion and transformation of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"The hologenome concept highlights how both host and microbial genomes contribute to the metabolic capabilities of organisms like Galleria mellonella."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metabolism refers to the biochemical processes necessary for life, specifically generating substrates for cellular processes and shifting towards pyrimidine metabolism."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metabolism refers to the biochemical processes in mealworms necessary for maintaining life, affected by the type of food consumed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metabolism involves the chemical processes within living organisms that maintain life, including nutrient breakdown and energy production."</data>
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL FUNCTION"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KLEBSIELLA OXYTOCA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A bacterium found in the intestine of mealworms that digests polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"A bacterium isolated from Tenebrio molitor showing significant biodegradation of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Klebsiella oxytoca is a Gram-negative rod-shaped bacterium identified in the gut of mealworms, capable of degrading polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Klebsiella oxytoca is a bacterial strain examined for its biodegradable activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Klebsiella oxytoca is a bacterial strain identified and confirmed using PCR techniques."&lt;SEP&gt;"Klebsiella oxytoca is a bacterium involved in the degradation of plastic, specifically polystyrene, using it as a carbon source."&lt;SEP&gt;"Klebsiella oxytoca is a bacterium isolated from T. molitor's gut and identified through molecular techniques such as PCR with specific primers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Klebsiella oxytoca is a bacterium isolated from the gut of Tenebrio molitor mealworms, known for its potential role in polystyrene degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Klebsiella oxytoca strains were isolated from the guts of Tenebrio molitor and are capable of degrading polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Klebsiella oxytoca is a bacterium identified in the gut of mealworms, responsible for biodegrading plastic waste."&lt;SEP&gt;"Klebsiella oxytoca is a bacterium involved in the microbiome study associated with Tenebrio molitor."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d8b79a6f4c112b0b62ada6756140e3e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-678bd592bfdda3f6dd8f2a6659de7fde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0cdc0cc71ed5e76f044e4db50f81ad2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9fcb421212175a148a0a1858582cfb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-939f85d52d9301668deab282264e5fd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d4e1982efefa47339205e972562b51f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41635122b30ee45048cc885b38fff6ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-652bf0615ec39fba0cedd113ec87a78a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c341ee1e0a5f54e33ca3379aa9d01c62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88659f9848d30be72c37a99b551a9a0a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51daa29515cc5a431055291627bcb199</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALKB GENE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The AlkB gene is responsible for encoding enzymes involved in repairing alkylated DNA damage."&lt;SEP&gt;"The AlkB gene sequences from 14 different bacteria were used for phylogenetic analysis, indicating its importance in understanding evolutionary relationships."&lt;SEP&gt;"The alkB gene encodes for alkane-1-monoxygenase, an enzyme involved in the oxidation of inactive alkanes and potentially responsible for polystyrene degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The alkB gene is associated with bacterial adaptation to alkanes and is responsible for encoding an enzyme involved in the oxidation of alkanes."&lt;SEP&gt;"The alkB gene is associated with the enzyme Alkane-1-Monooxygenase and is being detected in Klebsiella oxytoca strains through PCR amplification."&lt;SEP&gt;"The alkB gene is responsible for plastic degradation and is found in bacterial isolates from mealworm guts."&lt;SEP&gt;"The alkB gene in Pseudomonas is identified as key in alkane biodegradation during polyethylene breakdown."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5b74e88d1f94354055e078b38af6a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8b79a6f4c112b0b62ada6756140e3e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0cdc0cc71ed5e76f044e4db50f81ad2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b4b45d826a6a7956015e680f5fb8ee6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d71b4e70d7c620ee64c709aaeae634a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51daa29515cc5a431055291627bcb199&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33649582d350bc1da7dbca1a65092127</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALKANE-1-MONOXYGENASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Alkane-1-monoxygenase is an enzyme encoded by the alkB gene, which plays a critical role in the biodegradation of polystyrene through the oxidation of alkanes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alkane-1-monoxygenase is an enzyme implicated in the degradation of hydrocarbons, including plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d8b79a6f4c112b0b62ada6756140e3e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0817d79fa27f2f5b078e09086250c6e0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;16S RIBOSOMAL RNA GENE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A genetic marker used for identifying bacterial species in the mealworms' gut."&lt;SEP&gt;"The 16S ribosomal RNA gene is a genetic marker used for bacterial identification through PCR amplification."&lt;SEP&gt;"The 16S ribosomal RNA gene is used as a marker for identifying bacterial species, specifically in this case, to differentiate among Klebsiella oxytoca strains."&lt;SEP&gt;"The 16S ribosomal RNA gene is used for bacterial identification and confirmation through PCR amplification."&lt;SEP&gt;"The 16S ribosomal RNA gene is a conserved genetic marker used for identifying and classifying bacterial species."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d8b79a6f4c112b0b62ada6756140e3e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d1301f6942d17092ef7b22ac40f19f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c341ee1e0a5f54e33ca3379aa9d01c62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-220952ca1d34f3ffef65c5d71e22015e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33649582d350bc1da7dbca1a65092127</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PCR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PCR (Polymerase Chain Reaction) is a technique used to amplify DNA sequences for further analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"PCR (Polymerase Chain Reaction) is a technique used to amplify DNA sequences, such as the 16S ribosomal RNA gene and the alkB gene."&lt;SEP&gt;"PCR (Polymerase Chain Reaction) is a technique used to amplify specific DNA sequences, crucial for identifying bacterial species."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polymerase Chain Reaction (PCR) is a laboratory technique used to amplify small segments of DNA, allowing researchers to produce millions of copies of a specific DNA sequence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polymerase Chain Reaction (PCR) is a molecular technique used to amplify specific DNA sequences for identification purposes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polymerase Chain Reaction (PCR) is a technique used to amplify specific DNA sequences. In this context, it is employed to identify bacterial strains based on their 16S ribosomal RNA gene sequences."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polymerase chain reaction (PCR) is a technique used to amplify specific DNA sequences."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polymerase chain reaction (PCR) is a technique used to amplify specific DNA segments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polymerase Chain Reaction (PCR) is a technique used to amplify specific regions of DNA for analysis, involving cycles of denaturation, annealing, and extension."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polymerase chain reaction (PCR) is used to amplify DNA sequences, specifically the 16S rRNA and nifH genes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5b74e88d1f94354055e078b38af6a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94bf67bf1b585ce1050569a2eb0000cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8b79a6f4c112b0b62ada6756140e3e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53ab7dd83bf51674598c6a5bdd146b90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e37da2fbe64f85c50c36da45006f4c23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c341ee1e0a5f54e33ca3379aa9d01c62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c83f95e0134b38f78f2624da01ab0f79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51daa29515cc5a431055291627bcb199&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-449dceb5649c6baa34ecc2218cd3e9e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33649582d350bc1da7dbca1a65092127</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SANGER SEQUENCING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sanger sequencing is a method used to determine the nucleotide sequence of DNA, employed here to sequence the amplified alkB gene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d8b79a6f4c112b0b62ada6756140e3e0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHYLOGENETIC TREE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A phylogenetic tree is constructed to represent evolutionary relationships among different species based on genetic sequences."&lt;SEP&gt;"A phylogenetic tree visually represents evolutionary relationships among organisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"A phylogenetic tree was constructed using the maximum likelihood method and Tamura-Nei model for phylogenetic analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"A phylogenetic tree represents evolutionary relationships among organisms or genes, constructed using sequence data like 16S rRNA."&lt;SEP&gt;"A phylogenetic tree represents evolutionary relationships among various biological species based on similarities and differences in their physical or genetic characteristics."&lt;SEP&gt;"A phylogenetic tree represents evolutionary relationships among identified bacterial strains based on genetic sequences."&lt;SEP&gt;"A phylogenetic tree represents evolutionary relationships among organisms based on genetic data."&lt;SEP&gt;"The phylogenetic tree represents evolutionary relationships among species, constructed using DNA sequences to classify A. grisella."&lt;SEP&gt;"A phylogenetic tree represents the evolutionary relationships among various biological species based on similarities and differences in their genetic characteristics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d8b79a6f4c112b0b62ada6756140e3e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aface14c9ee7dd5ccd25e7094ed5c1c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0cdc0cc71ed5e76f044e4db50f81ad2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d80979bb7e58b10bb558705b5d96fa99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01bf9080cbf55e62c0b26d0e054bd1fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e6fd56772ef66691cf6f1c613ba42e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-652bf0615ec39fba0cedd113ec87a78a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af5eb6a8326b4977801e2f7694a2c750&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d71b4e70d7c620ee64c709aaeae634a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SERRATIA MARCESCENS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A bacterial strain associated with hydrocarbon degradation and bioremediation, prevalent among identified isolates."&lt;SEP&gt;"Serratia marcescens is a bacterium found in the gut microbiome of T. molitor that enhances polystyrene degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Serratia marcescens is a bacterium isolated from the gut of Tenebrio molitor, known for its potential in plastic biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Serratia marcescens is a bacterial strain tested for its capacity to degrade plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"A bacterium isolated from Tenebrio molitor involved in various microbiome studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Serratia marcescens is a bacterium involved in the microbiome study associated with Tenebrio molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"A bacterium linked to PS biodegradation, also found in the gut flora of insect larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Serratia marcescens is a bacterium selected for evaluating polystyrene degradability."&lt;SEP&gt;"Serratia marcescens is one of the eight isolated species identified in this study that degrade polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a52fc2936b4d2a771dbc2d6a37eeb710&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8b79a6f4c112b0b62ada6756140e3e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07aae06c64778453da4bda48f5347de5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9fcb421212175a148a0a1858582cfb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-939f85d52d9301668deab282264e5fd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41635122b30ee45048cc885b38fff6ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cefffe48b3d2ec347f880c77300fc041&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eda80cb027c8107defa00011d491b002&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfd05eac1abc28ac416e6a56ccd6a9d6</data>
