      <data key="d0">"MEDIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A liquid medium used for incubating PS pieces with the bacterial strain YT2."&lt;SEP&gt;"LCFBM (liquid carbon-free basal medium) is used to enrich plastic-degrading gut bacteria by providing essential nutrients."&lt;SEP&gt;"LCFBM is the liquid culture medium used for culturing bacteria with PS pieces or micro powders as the sole carbon source."&lt;SEP&gt;"Liquid Carbon-Free Basal Medium (LCFBM) is a nutrient solution used for bacterial culture."&lt;SEP&gt;"LCFBM is a liquid carbon-free basal medium used as a carbon source for bacterial growth studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"LCFBM is a liquid culture medium used as a carbon source for bacterial growth and degradation studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"LCFBM is a liquid medium used for cultivating bacterial strains, especially for studies involving PE degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Liquid carbon-free basal medium used for culturing bacteria with PE as the sole carbon source."&lt;SEP&gt;"LCFBM is a liquid medium used for the enrichment of PS-degrading microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"LCFBM is the medium used for incubating PS samples with strain YT2, facilitating the degradation process."&lt;SEP&gt;"LCFBM is a carbon-free basal medium used for cultivating bacteria capable of degrading NPS."</data>
