    <node id="&quot;PHYLOGENETIC ANALYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Phylogenetic analysis determines evolutionary relationships among organisms based on genetic sequences."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phylogenetic analysis involves studying evolutionary relationships among organisms using genetic data."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phylogenetic analysis is a method used to infer evolutionary relationships among organisms based on genetic or morphological characteristics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phylogenetic analysis was performed using AlkB gene sequences to infer evolutionary relationships among bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"This is a method used to study evolutionary relationships among organisms by constructing phylogenetic trees based on genetic data."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phylogenetic analysis involves sequencing and comparing 16S rRNA genes to determine evolutionary relationships among bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phylogenetic analysis involves constructing a phylogenetic tree using the neighbor-joining method with bootstrap analysis of 1000 replicates, employing MEGA4 software."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bfa1d3c9710e10c5eb533d8d791c93e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b74e88d1f94354055e078b38af6a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af682f78e3e8970d7d70b027a8f79116&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70bab3579af07d0f99a5f948a90fe1e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d71b4e70d7c620ee64c709aaeae634a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51daa29515cc5a431055291627bcb199&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-57f3782f3c1c49764c4b911c60b37fed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEGAX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"SOFTWARE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"MEGAX is software used for constructing phylogenetic trees and performing molecular evolutionary analyses."&lt;SEP&gt;"MegaX is software used for conducting phylogenetic analyses, including inferring evolutionary relationships."&lt;SEP&gt;"MegaX is software used for constructing phylogenetic trees and analyzing evolutionary relationships."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4d71b4e70d7c620ee64c709aaeae634a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51daa29515cc5a431055291627bcb199&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aface14c9ee7dd5ccd25e7094ed5c1c7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MAXIMUM LIKELIHOOD METHOD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A statistical approach used in phylogenetic analysis to infer the most probable evolutionary tree given the observed genetic data."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Maximum Likelihood Method estimates parameters by maximizing the likelihood of observed data."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Maximum Likelihood Method is a statistical approach used to infer phylogenetic trees."&lt;SEP&gt;"The maximum likelihood method was used in phylogenetic analysis to infer evolutionary relationships based on sequence data."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4d71b4e70d7c620ee64c709aaeae634a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b74e88d1f94354055e078b38af6a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51daa29515cc5a431055291627bcb199</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TAMURA-NEI MODEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MODEL"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A model that accounts for different rates of nucleotide substitution and is commonly used in phylogenetic analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Tamura-Nei model accounts for differences in substitution rates between nucleotides."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Tamura-Nei model describes nucleotide substitution patterns and was applied during phylogenetic analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Tamura-Nei model is a method for estimating nucleotide substitution rates."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4d71b4e70d7c620ee64c709aaeae634a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b74e88d1f94354055e078b38af6a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51daa29515cc5a431055291627bcb199</data>
    </node>
