    <node id="&quot;AGAROSE GEL ELECTROPHORESIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A method used to separate DNA fragments based on size. It involves running DNA through a gel matrix under an electric field, where smaller fragments move faster than larger ones."&lt;SEP&gt;"Agarose gel electrophoresis is used to visualize the amplified DNA products from PCR reactions, enabling identification of bacterial strains."&lt;SEP&gt;"Agarose gel electrophoresis is a method used to separate and visualize DNA fragments based on size."&lt;SEP&gt;"Agarose gel electrophoresis is a technique used to separate DNA fragments based on size for confirming DNA isolation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5b74e88d1f94354055e078b38af6a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-568e2e90ce0d3bbb4e21079f4252f5de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-449dceb5649c6baa34ecc2218cd3e9e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33649582d350bc1da7dbca1a65092127</data>
    </node>
