      <data key="d2">chunk-0cdc0cc71ed5e76f044e4db50f81ad2f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIGESTIVE ACTIVITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Digestive activity of intestinal microorganisms aids in the degradation of plastic by insects like Tenebrio molitor."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0cdc0cc71ed5e76f044e4db50f81ad2f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GUT MICROORGANISMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gut Microorganisms found in mealworms play a crucial role in breaking down plastics such as polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut Microorganisms in mealworms play a crucial role in the biodegradation of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut Microorganisms play a crucial role in various biological processes, including digestion and immune response."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microorganisms are responsible for aiding in the digestion process of plastic consumed by Tenebrio molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microorganisms in Tenebrio molitor larvae play a crucial role in degrading plastics through enzymatic processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microorganisms include bacteria and other microbes residing in the digestive tract of organisms like mealworms, playing a key role in the breakdown of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microorganisms play a key role in the biodegradation of plastics within organisms like mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microorganisms in mealworms play a crucial role in the biodegradation of plastics like polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut Microorganisms within mealworms play a crucial role in the biodegradation of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut Microorganisms within mealworms and superworms play a critical role in breaking down plastics such as polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microorganisms refer to the bacteria and other microbes present in the digestive tract of organisms, playing a role in the biodegradation of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut Microorganisms in the digestive system of mealworms play a crucial role in the biodegradation of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbes present in the digestive systems of mealworms that contribute to the degradation of plastics such as polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut Microorganisms within mealworms are responsible for breaking down complex materials such as plastics through enzymatic processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbes residing in the digestive tract of mealworms, playing a critical role in the biodegradation of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microorganisms within mealworms play a crucial role in the biodegradation of plastics such as polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microorganisms are bacteria and other microbes residing in the digestive tract, playing roles in digestion and degradation processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microorganisms are bacteria and other microorganisms residing in the digestive tract, playing roles in biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microorganisms play a critical role in the biodegradation process within plastic-eating mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microorganisms play a crucial role in the biodegradation and mineralization of plastics like polystyrene within the digestive system of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microorganisms play a critical role in the biodegradation of polystyrene within mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eada60ee606520104bb515c4896d6b0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20a69982e6abe36c2a0d4a70b78720ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-550dde13ffd2abcf536dd87f7d4c1b40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b8cc3aa81b03290b589ccf0a1548ca0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0627e3f1b0fb440795f73c4fa33093c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0cdc0cc71ed5e76f044e4db50f81ad2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7232abef4870641de7945afeb6a4bf93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-908b8bfa7e446694958cf9bd0cfbc583&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38a07d29ecfa06f82d97e69f5cd2c801&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d97be338c51b4c4354e2d0f8de9c9dc8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cede90fd3b3eee0bd12d582eaa7d54c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24ba7d6b1b5275089cbabe56bc33b92e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33f35f87c2ff7792eb41bdd8debdb5f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db0003a7244c51697d0129eb84b8e28e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bce368b44455642f4b9a1dacc4cdf0f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5279ebea7d4d5e22eebe3106de3ba1c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc31a0931fceb1446bc6ec4d0c587f7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-276c82b9935756a3e668c788458ff922&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a3d3cf8ea423f7e0f637dddade1bbf1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c7bcc9530f9dc72038f774f6f084ab6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39598f698094d1663ca3438bc143bc90</data>
    </node>
