    <node id="&quot;PROTEIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Protein content is crucial for body functioning but is not accumulated for energetic purposes unless obtained endogenously."&lt;SEP&gt;"Protein is a crucial nutrient for T. molitor larvae, supporting their growth and development."&lt;SEP&gt;**Comprehensive Summary of PROTEIN in the Context of Mealworms and Nutrition:**

PROTEIN is a macromolecule composed of amino acids, derived from fixed nitrogen, and plays a critical role in the growth, maintenance, and repair of body tissues in living organisms, including mealworms (*Tenebrio molitor* larvae). As an essential macronutrient, PROTEIN supports physiological processes across species and is a fundamental building block for tissue formation in mealworms. It is also found in bran, which is crucial for the growth and development of *Tenebrio molitor* larvae.

In mealworms, the concentration of PROTEIN can be measured using methods such as the Bradford assay. While the protein content in mealworm tissues generally does not vary significantly depending on the type of food consumed, protein synthesis can decrease during periods of starvation. This highlights the dependency of protein synthesis on dietary fixed nitrogen, estimated at 8.6 to 23.0 μg per day per mealworm.

The nutritional value of mealworms as a source of PROTEIN is significant, making them valuable for both human consumption and animal feed. However, there is some variability in findings regarding the impact of diet on protein levels. For example, larvae fed unconventional diets, such as those containing polystyrene, may exhibit changes in protein content compared to those consuming conventional feeds. Some studies suggest an increase in protein content with unconventional diets, while others report decreases due to stress-induced impacts on protein synthesis and utilization. This inconsistency underscores the complex interplay between diet and physiological responses in mealworms.

Beyond its role as a nutrient, PROTEIN participates in biological processes like glycosylation, regulating functionality within biological systems. In experimental settings, protein content often serves as a normalization factor in analyses, such as fluorescence measurements assessing reactive oxygen species (ROS) levels, further emphasizing its importance in both nutritional and analytical contexts.

Overall, PROTEIN remains indispensable for supporting the health and nutritional quality of edible insects, including mealworms. Despite potential variations in protein synthesis influenced by specific diets, the consensus affirms the critical role of PROTEIN in sustaining the growth, development, and viability of these organisms.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6e415042ae4079ee5fe96c7105eb534c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e67971bdf45c447f2409fddb80e0d8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b12451ba2a22e6f74c543f982a0a7b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0d2f43eebe2309fba46c5335d76df56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-530244abdca5889849fcf86f017ebd77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40407fe311340b08da856202f38b459c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf697c73d05470fb4a143aa0e4700787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee46611b24ea3848df979ded841f06b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97444337eddb4e9e3d88bde93ce02aef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91831340731171413dc4c412a325e034&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84297b844ec01d2f58756b669806fd62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14f9f0280098bb86719394a4bd53e5bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56604c68c2f6221f63a4afa5d457e8ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41635122b30ee45048cc885b38fff6ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa10245aaff722ac7d69e73bed8afe74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0491f3e96c1d355b8431b9d74868f63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db672d5836dfe372ee7c47ee4dd6fbd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a97d5b092508f2e837932274d6b3282&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36b964b1825429cad2c7d13c1ea8827e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a38885f67ed46b97bb84086f575fd43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcf2bd0dbdce4d7299bfc35487eaf0f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5922f60fcd06ac6ffa27018026871346&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ee541583aebc7a78ac49285860e4da0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84f576487c8d473c1524eb1141730a12&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eaf641df5c55c7ff41895611514cdd22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c83f95e0134b38f78f2624da01ab0f79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4304c39ef3427872131caf77e7cdb438&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5279ebea7d4d5e22eebe3106de3ba1c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdc8398efba587929eebd0a0842f6e69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-302543e7a2fdb3596cc8a10e7072ec01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ead6f17ad517015b638608c5bfe6852&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2281f98bcfd555a703fd86232dfa42fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fbbfcf279533f78737706f5751ee5a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d01d291012bd548fc067e250ec39fba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6338d56b535220f260826703b0f7229&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b387da8298c55673284dca93ea82fc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d290a6a81802d3048c35d2a2fb1252c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0ec64a7c629b14bfb6652f1960a337c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d616d4c3c3199d53c1ae93ebcf3589d</data>
