      <data key="d2">chunk-81a3bc3c202af119c80775d5bf23d8b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e88a3caade44f7fbc493dfc1c3ca8f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb1c38c1c6dc6fea84d8f51b9f706cd2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPLEEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGAN"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An organ analyzed for weight changes to assess the effects of TMlp administration."&lt;SEP&gt;"The spleen is an organ examined for weight changes in the experiment."&lt;SEP&gt;"The spleen is an organ whose absolute and relative weights were measured in rats as part of the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"The spleen shows significant differences in both absolute and relative weights between experimental groups."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-81a3bc3c202af119c80775d5bf23d8b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e88a3caade44f7fbc493dfc1c3ca8f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c1e1694d44433fcf53dc8120c479ca4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb1c38c1c6dc6fea84d8f51b9f706cd2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;T-TEST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A statistical test used to compare the means of two groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"T-test is a statistical test used for comparing the means of two groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"A t-test was used to establish the significance of shifts in \(M_{w}\) and \(M_{n}\) values after PS ingestion by mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8d27c41781c64c2b407faecc4bc31466&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb1c38c1c6dc6fea84d8f51b9f706cd2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fb9111bd088e1990cde867c6d85cf28</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SIGNIFICANCE LEVEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Significance was determined at p&lt;0.05 compared with the control group."&lt;SEP&gt;"The threshold used to determine whether results are statistically significant, typically set at 0.05."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e88a3caade44f7fbc493dfc1c3ca8f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb1c38c1c6dc6fea84d8f51b9f706cd2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TOXICITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"HEALTH MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Harmful effects of degradation intermediates, such as chlorinated compounds, on organisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The potential harmful effects of substances on biological systems, assessed in this study."&lt;SEP&gt;"Toxicity encompasses the adverse effects of substances on living organisms, ranging from mild irritation to severe damage."&lt;SEP&gt;"Toxicity refers to the harmful effects that polystyrene might have on insect organisms and subsequently on human health."&lt;SEP&gt;"Toxicity refers to the degree to which a substance can harm living organisms, relevant during plastic biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Toxicity refers to the harmful effects of plastics like PE on the health and growth of yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Toxicity describes the harmful effects of micro- and nanoplastics on living organisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Toxicity refers to the harmful effects of substances, such as intermediate products of polymer degradation, on living organisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Toxicity measures the degree to which a substance can harm organisms, including the effects of microplastics and nanoplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Toxicity refers to harmful effects caused by substances, potentially affecting larval survival and growth in certain experimental groups."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a097963ab8ec0ad6b1d51685fc359027&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa3bd7c611ad935dba56fd3d7300cbc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f44f9d05edb3efaf7fdb8f0f1517549&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1536c14bdcd58ae9dabf3a49f6724cd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb1c38c1c6dc6fea84d8f51b9f706cd2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64a060d0c9650ae8bed2ca9b44eef10c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a31a12c930b59b872c94dda484d0db4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6cc0afd02f25b584d6e3a755fc7272b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65434948dabde813d99972f40a04d8de</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MOISTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Moisture contributes to the degradation of bioplastics by facilitating hydrolytic reactions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Water content present in TMlp, contributing minimally to its composition."&lt;SEP&gt;"Moisture is a physical property that affects the biodegradation rate of polystyrene in the environment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1c16f995987af72f86486559556052e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb1c38c1c6dc6fea84d8f51b9f706cd2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8518832c2d3e002c8acf71795e306144</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ND (NOT DETECTED)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MEASUREMENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Indicates that certain toxins or heavy metals were not detected in TMlp."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fb1c38c1c6dc6fea84d8f51b9f706cd2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;W/O EPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A control diet where Tenebrio molitor larvae are not fed expanded-polystyrene (EPS)."&lt;SEP&gt;"A product derived from Tenebrio molitor larvae powder without expanded-polystyrene feeding, used in experimental studies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e88a3caade44f7fbc493dfc1c3ca8f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81a3bc3c202af119c80775d5bf23d8b2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;W/ EPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A diet where Tenebrio molitor larvae are fed expanded-polystyrene (EPS), indicating an innovative solution to EPS waste management."&lt;SEP&gt;"A product derived from Tenebrio molitor larvae powder with expanded-polystyrene feeding, used in experimental studies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e88a3caade44f7fbc493dfc1c3ca8f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81a3bc3c202af119c80775d5bf23d8b2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;17Β-ESTRADIOL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"HORMONE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A hormone that plays a role in the regulation of reproductive and metabolic processes, tested for effects on MCF-7 cell viability."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e88a3caade44f7fbc493dfc1c3ca8f0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NEUTROPHILS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"IMMUNE RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of white blood cell involved in immune response, assessed through hematological examination."&lt;SEP&gt;"A type of white blood cell involved in immune response, measured in the experiment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Neutrophils are immune cells that show a tendency to increase in the W/ eps 10% group compared to the W/o eps 10% group."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e88a3caade44f7fbc493dfc1c3ca8f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c1e1694d44433fcf53dc8120c479ca4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81a3bc3c202af119c80775d5bf23d8b2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LYMPHOCYTES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"IMMUNE RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of white blood cell involved in immune response, assessed through hematological examination."&lt;SEP&gt;"A type of white blood cell involved in immune response, measured in the experiment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymphocytes are immune cells that tend to decrease in the W/ eps 10% group compared to the W/o eps 10% group."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e88a3caade44f7fbc493dfc1c3ca8f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c1e1694d44433fcf53dc8120c479ca4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81a3bc3c202af119c80775d5bf23d8b2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"AST (aspartate aminotransferase) is an enzyme found in various tissues, elevated levels can indicate liver damage."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aspartate aminotransferase (AST) is an enzyme found in the liver, heart, and muscles, used as a biomarker for liver function."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aspartate transaminase, a biochemical marker used to assess liver function."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e88a3caade44f7fbc493dfc1c3ca8f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e755eeac14110dcfdcfc32e51f30b89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8bf6d17dfbab29bcb302ae97679bc903</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"ALT (alanine aminotransferase) is an enzyme primarily found in the liver, increased levels suggest liver injury."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alanine aminotransferase (ALT) is an enzyme primarily found in the liver, serving as a key indicator of liver health."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alanine transaminase, a biochemical marker used to assess liver function."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e88a3caade44f7fbc493dfc1c3ca8f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e755eeac14110dcfdcfc32e51f30b89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8bf6d17dfbab29bcb302ae97679bc903</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"ALP (alkaline phosphatase) is an enzyme involved in phosphate metabolism, often associated with bone and liver health."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alkaline phosphatase (ALP) is an enzyme involved in various physiological processes, particularly in bone and liver health."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alkaline phosphatase, a biochemical marker used to assess liver function."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e88a3caade44f7fbc493dfc1c3ca8f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e755eeac14110dcfdcfc32e51f30b89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8bf6d17dfbab29bcb302ae97679bc903</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;T-BILI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"T-Bili (total bilirubin) is a breakdown product of heme metabolism, measured in milligrams per deciliter."&lt;SEP&gt;"Total bilirubin (T-Bili) is a breakdown product of hemoglobin, reflecting liver function and bile flow."&lt;SEP&gt;"Total bilirubin, a biochemical marker used to assess liver function."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e88a3caade44f7fbc493dfc1c3ca8f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e755eeac14110dcfdcfc32e51f30b89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8bf6d17dfbab29bcb302ae97679bc903</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AUTOPSY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Autopsy is the procedure performed to examine organ weights and other biological responses after test substance administration."&lt;SEP&gt;"Autopsy was performed on the rats after the completion of the administration test to measure organ weights."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e88a3caade44f7fbc493dfc1c3ca8f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c1e1694d44433fcf53dc8120c479ca4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ORGAN WEIGHTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Absolute and relative weights of various organs were measured in rats to assess the effects of different treatments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Organ weights provide insights into organ size and function, often used in toxicology and pathology studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Organ weights, both absolute and relative, are measured to evaluate potential toxicological effects."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e88a3caade44f7fbc493dfc1c3ca8f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e755eeac14110dcfdcfc32e51f30b89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c1e1694d44433fcf53dc8120c479ca4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SERUM BIOCHEMISTRY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Serum biochemistry involves analyzing chemical components in blood serum to assess health status and metabolic processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Serum components were analyzed through biochemical tests to evaluate liver function and other metabolic parameters."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e88a3caade44f7fbc493dfc1c3ca8f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfbd751517e11b1b4052961a01008cbc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STUDENT'S T TEST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"STATISTICAL METHOD"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Student's t test was used to determine statistical significance of differences between treatment groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"The student's t test was applied for statistical significance testing with Tukey's correction."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e88a3caade44f7fbc493dfc1c3ca8f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a27dff473ed210517e6461ad3e5d783</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONTROL GROUP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DIET"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Control group involves using wheat bran as a baseline feed to compare other dietary treatments."&lt;SEP&gt;"The control group consists of yellow mealworms fed with wheat bran, providing a baseline for comparison."&lt;SEP&gt;"The control group served as a baseline for comparison in the study of organ weights and serum components."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Control Group represents the standard feeding condition used as a baseline for comparison in the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"The control group represents a baseline for comparison, where larvae receive adequate nutrition and exhibit normal growth and reproduction."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e88a3caade44f7fbc493dfc1c3ca8f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eed90a978852274ead3771418cd60bed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a97d5b092508f2e837932274d6b3282&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2417ca11674320d88eecdf4cb66f9d6</data>
    </node>
