      <data key="d1">"A statistical test used to determine if there are significant differences between groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"Student's t-test is a statistical method used for comparing two groups in the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"Student's t-test is a statistical method used to compare means between two groups in biodegradation studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Student's t-test is a statistical method used to determine the significance of differences between groups in the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"Student's t-test was conducted to evaluate variations due to diet and species, with Tukey's correction applied."&lt;SEP&gt;"Student's t-test performs pairwise comparisons to evaluate differences between two groups, such as superworms and yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Student's t-test is a statistical test used for pairwise comparisons to assess differences between diets and species."&lt;SEP&gt;"Student's t-test was employed for pairwise comparisons of data."</data>
