    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MOISTURE CONTENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Moisture content impacts the survival and performance of mealworms during the biodepolymerization process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Moisture content was determined using a moisture analyzer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Moisture content was measured using the vacuum cryodesiccation method to assess the water composition of yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Moisture content is measured gravimetrically to identify differences due to diet."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ddb3edd44829125161ad624ea793ae71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b4ab01931acbc7aa9c77cd03531c57e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-196a7570e6cac531e94c1680c54f5491&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db672d5836dfe372ee7c47ee4dd6fbd3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARBOHYDRATES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Carbohydrate content was determined by difference after subtracting protein, fat, moisture, and ash."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbohydrates are essential energy sources found in bran, impacting mealworm growth and survival."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbohydrates are essential nutrients required for energy and growth, lacking in polystyrene but present in wheat flour."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbohydrates, including fiber, are components of the oatmeal diet that support mealworm larval development."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbohydrates are metabolites that were found to have increased relative abundance of DEGs in PS- and CS-fed groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbohydrates are nutrients whose total concentrations were determined using food safety testing standard GB/T 15,672-2009."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbohydrates are part of the larval biomass composition analyzed at the end of the test period."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbohydrates are nutrients that undergo thermal degradation alongside proteins, contributing to the observed transitions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbohydrates are a primary energy source for insects. The highest carbohydrate content was observed in mealworms fed PLA."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbohydrates are essential nutrients stored in mealworms, used alongside lipids for maintaining vital functions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The level of hydrolyzed carbohydrates in mealworms was determined using the Anthrone method."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbohydrates are nutrients present in the haemolymph of insects, playing a key role in sustaining the nervous system and other organs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5318125e74217718b470b7721d1d6365&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91831340731171413dc4c412a325e034&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3eb3742a8be739a1146cbf15e6b7ae5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eaf1f7b81bc271c665d7776cc3114a92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc88563632a3abf926bf4e4ac16973fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84558838faaf585c61e883356c52c0e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-728d6b0b96814c5c3c7b93042e9b9856&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b693d867918f89c9b28997fe94fc830&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0491f3e96c1d355b8431b9d74868f63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db672d5836dfe372ee7c47ee4dd6fbd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa33fb34ba06610c290cdfd8a5b4e916&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0ec64a7c629b14bfb6652f1960a337c</data>
    </node>
