      <data key="d2">chunk-6cbb8ccec16f4756fa7a1fb365886d9c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SULFORHODAMINE B (SRB)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sulforhodamine B is a protein-binding dye used to measure cellular protein content as an indicator of cell proliferation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6cbb8ccec16f4756fa7a1fb365886d9c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LACTATE DEHYDROGENASE (LDH)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lactate dehydrogenase is a cytosolic enzyme that catalyzes the conversion of lactate to pyruvate, serving as a marker for cytotoxicity when released into the medium due to membrane damage."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6cbb8ccec16f4756fa7a1fb365886d9c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TETRAZOLIUM SALT (INT)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The tetrazolium salt INT is reduced by NADH to form a red formazan product, which can be quantified to assess LDH activity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6cbb8ccec16f4756fa7a1fb365886d9c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FLUOSTAR OMEGA READER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"FLUOstar Omega Reader is a multimode microplate reader used to measure absorbance and fluorescence in various assays."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6cbb8ccec16f4756fa7a1fb365886d9c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANNEXIN V&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Annexin V is a protein that binds to phosphatidylserine exposed on the surface of apoptotic cells, used to detect apoptosis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6cbb8ccec16f4756fa7a1fb365886d9c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MUSE® CELL ANALYZER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Muse® Cell Analyzer is a flow cytometer used to analyze cell viability, apoptosis, and oxidative stress."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6cbb8ccec16f4756fa7a1fb365886d9c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PBS BUFFER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PBS buffer is used to rinse cells and maintain physiological conditions during the assays."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6cbb8ccec16f4756fa7a1fb365886d9c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRISMA® BASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Trisma® Base is used to dissolve the sulforhodamine B dye after staining fixed cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6cbb8ccec16f4756fa7a1fb365886d9c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PIERCE™ LDH CYTOTOXICITY ASSAY KIT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Pierce™ LDH Cytotoxicity Assay Kit is used to measure lactate dehydrogenase activity as a marker of cytotoxicity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6cbb8ccec16f4756fa7a1fb365886d9c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MUSE® ANNEXIN V &amp; DEAD CELL KIT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Muse® Annexin V &amp; Dead Cell Kit is used to detect cells in various stages of apoptosis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6cbb8ccec16f4756fa7a1fb365886d9c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MUSE® COUNT AND VIABILITY KIT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Muse® Count and Viability Kit is used to determine cell viability and total cell count."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6cbb8ccec16f4756fa7a1fb365886d9c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MUSE® OXIDATIVE STRESS KIT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A commercial kit used for measuring reactive oxygen species in cells, specifically superoxide radicals."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Muse® Oxidative Stress Kit is used to measure reactive oxygen species, specifically superoxide radicals, in cells undergoing oxidative stress."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6cbb8ccec16f4756fa7a1fb365886d9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fbbfcf279533f78737706f5751ee5a2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BALL HOMOGENIZER (MINILYS®, BERTIN TECHNOLOGIES)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The ball homogenizer is used to gently homogenize insect tissue for further analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6cbb8ccec16f4756fa7a1fb365886d9c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FLOW CYTOMETER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A flow cytometer is used to analyze stained cells for apoptosis, viability, and oxidative stress measurements."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6cbb8ccec16f4756fa7a1fb365886d9c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INSECT SPECIMENS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL SAMPLE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Insect specimens are used as biological samples to study oxidative stress parameters in the gastrointestinal tract."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6cbb8ccec16f4756fa7a1fb365886d9c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NADH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"NADH is a coenzyme involved in redox reactions, used here to reduce tetrazolium salts in the LDH assay."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6cbb8ccec16f4756fa7a1fb365886d9c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PYRUVATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A metabolite with high relative abundance in CB or unfed groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"An intermediate metabolite in cellular metabolism, enriched in CB or unfed larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pyruvate is a metabolic product formed from lactate by the action of lactate dehydrogenase."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6cbb8ccec16f4756fa7a1fb365886d9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64b3e57543d6b365fff3ef2b14ddb309</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUPEROXIDE RADICALS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Superoxide radicals are a type of reactive oxygen species involved in oxidative stress processes within cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Superoxide radicals are reactive oxygen species measured as indicators of oxidative stress in cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6cbb8ccec16f4756fa7a1fb365886d9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fbbfcf279533f78737706f5751ee5a2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MILLIPORE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"COMPANY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Millipore is a company that produces scientific equipment and reagents, including the Muse® Oxidative Stress Kit."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6fbbfcf279533f78737706f5751ee5a2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FLOW CYTOMETER MUSE® CELL ANALYZER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A device used for analyzing cell properties, such as the measurement of reactive oxygen species."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6fbbfcf279533f78737706f5751ee5a2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEALWORM (T. MOLITOR)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"INSECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mealworms are larvae of the darkling beetle, used in studies related to nutrient composition and digestion of unconventional materials like Styrofoam."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6fbbfcf279533f78737706f5751ee5a2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENERGY CONTENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Energy content measures the caloric value of food, which was lower in mealworms fed with Styrofoam."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6fbbfcf279533f78737706f5751ee5a2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FECULA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fecula is a byproduct of EPS biodegradation, analyzed via GPC, FTIR, TGA, and $^{1}$H-NMR for molecular weight determination."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fecula is a metabolic product generated during the thermal decomposition of Styrofoam, containing carbon compounds and showing different chemical compositions compared to the control."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fecula refers to the egested material containing residual Styrofoam fragments and intermediates."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fecula refers to the egested residues from mealworms after consuming Styrofoam, used to study changes in chemical and physical properties."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fecula refers to the excreted material from mealworms after consuming Styrofoam, containing depolymerized metabolites."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fecula refers to the excreted material from mealworms after consuming Styrofoam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fecula refers to the excreted waste material from mealworms after consuming Styrofoam, which is collected and analyzed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fecula refers to the waste material excreted by mealworms after consuming Styrofoam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fecula represents residues of Styrofoam egested through the gut of mealworms, containing degraded PS and other new components."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fecula refers to the excreted material from mealworms, containing degraded EPS, smaller polymer chains, and biological matter."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fecula refers to the waste material produced by mealworms after consuming EPS, which differs in composition from the original polystyrene feedstock."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-069f8447676509ffdd0028e9c05fb9ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15323ef47e29f2927f95274e49f4e5bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7fa795762aa89809d8221dc9dda92fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56c8b21b1eaba7633b49cea16714ddc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33a0a8b02ff930ea552c8902e4d0defd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81552b76a273b31cc2bd9ed21ed7a919&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21c07a838ff0a489c73c8319e5011134&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-260d8c268067de32e5ac98d66ab70a6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-086890e8567c60d8cfa7c03b0cc61f9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b33a3915745323f1bd29bd2febf60b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fbbfcf279533f78737706f5751ee5a2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GRAPHPAD PRISM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"SOFTWARE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"GraphPad Prism is software used for statistical analysis and graphing in scientific research."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6fbbfcf279533f78737706f5751ee5a2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENERGY NEEDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Energy needs refer to the caloric requirements of organisms, met through digestion of materials like polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"The energy requirements of mealworms that are met through the digestion of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Energy needs refer to the requirements of larvae for maintaining physiological functions and growth."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eed90a978852274ead3771418cd60bed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b27c93b39534612a0492f52ce1f3cd8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fbbfcf279533f78737706f5751ee5a2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOMASS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biomass is another product of EPS biodegradation by mealworm gut bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biomass refers to organic material derived from living organisms, including plastics processed by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biomass represents the total mass of living organisms, affected by dietary intake and metabolic processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biomass refers to the organic material produced during biodegradation, serving as an indicator of microbial activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"The total mass of living organisms in a given area or ecosystem, here referring to insect tissue analyzed for protein content."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biomass refers to the organic material derived from the assimilation of plastics like PS by mealworms, where about 0.5% of ingested PS carbon is incorporated."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biomass refers to the organic material derived from the assimilation of carbon from degraded products by microbes and the host."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biomass refers to the organic material produced by mealworms after consuming Styrofoam, reflecting their growth and metabolism."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biomass represents the small fraction of Styrofoam carbon incorporated into the mealworm's body."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biomass refers to the total mass of organisms in a given area or volume, used here to measure the growth of T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biomass represents the total mass of living organisms in a given system, here referring to yellow mealworm populations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biomass refers to the total mass of organisms in a given area or ecosystem, including components like fat, carbohydrate, and protein."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biomass refers to the weight gain of organisms during their growth phase, influenced by diet and environmental conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c095cc3175666d5093fe411f9a39cb66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5318125e74217718b470b7721d1d6365&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab6b219720db5a6e3384c884c280984c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33a0a8b02ff930ea552c8902e4d0defd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7fa795762aa89809d8221dc9dda92fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1d76ad321e1c68d5f139cdb94d5bf42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdb235a6eddd0a0e69be356e83362fc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fc215d3abb38f76b4ee0d22c4f1eb11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21c07a838ff0a489c73c8319e5011134&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b12468cce513394dbebb8b4ce27f62d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fbbfcf279533f78737706f5751ee5a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-640f0655e17fab473cca3b460c2795de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ac1b1db6ffab6f4cfea7a525785a2fc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYSTYRENE-EATING INSECTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Insects capable of digesting polystyrene, contributing to its breakdown and conversion into other forms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6fbbfcf279533f78737706f5751ee5a2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOCHEMICAL ASSAYS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biochemical assays are laboratory procedures used to quantify biological molecules or reactions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6fbbfcf279533f78737706f5751ee5a2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BASIC METABOLIC RATES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Basic metabolic rates describe the minimum energy expenditure required for maintaining life processes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6fbbfcf279533f78737706f5751ee5a2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SHAPIRO-WILK TEST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"STATISTICAL TEST"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Shapiro-Wilk test evaluates whether data follows a normal distribution, essential for choosing appropriate statistical methods."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6fbbfcf279533f78737706f5751ee5a2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TUKEY TEST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"STATISTICAL TEST"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Tukey test is used for comparing means across multiple groups while controlling for Type I errors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6fbbfcf279533f78737706f5751ee5a2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MANN-WHITNEY U TEST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"STATISTICAL TEST"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Mann-Whitney U test compares two independent samples when data does not follow a normal distribution."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6fbbfcf279533f78737706f5751ee5a2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KOLMOGOROV-SMIRNOV TEST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"STATISTICAL TEST"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Kolmogorov-Smirnov test assesses if two datasets come from the same continuous distribution."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6fbbfcf279533f78737706f5751ee5a2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LEVENE TEST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"STATISTICAL TEST"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Levene test checks for equality of variances among groups, important for ANOVA assumptions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6fbbfcf279533f78737706f5751ee5a2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BROWN-FORSYTH TEST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"STATISTICAL TEST"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Brown-Forsyth test is another method for testing equality of variances, often more robust than Levene's test."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6fbbfcf279533f78737706f5751ee5a2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ONE-WAY ANOVA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Analysis method used to evaluate differences in total content of proteins, sugars, and lipids in mealworms fed with different PS species."&lt;SEP&gt;"One-way ANOVA analyzes differences among group means based on a single factor."&lt;SEP&gt;"One-way ANOVA is a statistical method used to determine if there are significant differences between means of three or more independent groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"One-way ANOVA is a statistical method used for comparing more than two groups in the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"One-way ANOVA is a statistical method used for comparing means across multiple groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"One-way ANOVA is a statistical method used to determine if there are significant differences between groups, such as diet effects on gut microbiome diversity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8d27c41781c64c2b407faecc4bc31466&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-630e33352368a0c7f34d56ad45a38e56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e9eb740edf53e540b468122b302cb82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d39fc863538a777920c4eafb37bcf8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a11793261251544a542146bc9bf0c5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fbbfcf279533f78737706f5751ee5a2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TWO-WAY ANOVA WITH INTERACTIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"STATISTICAL TEST"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Two-way ANOVA examines the effects of two factors and their interaction on a dependent variable."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6fbbfcf279533f78737706f5751ee5a2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIKERT SCALE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"SURVEY TOOL"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A Likert scale measures attitudes or opinions using a range of agreement levels (e.g., strongly disagree to strongly agree)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6fbbfcf279533f78737706f5751ee5a2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEALWORM ADAPTATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mealworm adaptation refers to physiological changes in mealworms in response to unconventional diets like Styrofoam."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6fbbfcf279533f78737706f5751ee5a2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUPERWORM RESILIENCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Superworm resilience describes the ability of superworms to maintain stable nutrient composition despite feeding on Styrofoam."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6fbbfcf279533f78737706f5751ee5a2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;Z. MORIO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Z. morio harbors Aeromonas sp. TM1 in its intestines, contributing to polystyrene degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Z. morio is another species of insect studied for its ability to digest Styrofoam without apparent health effects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Z. morio refers to a genus of insects whose extracts have been tested for cytotoxicity and other biological effects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Zophobas morio is a genus of insects studied for its cytotoxic properties and health status when fed different diets, including polystyrene foam."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a097963ab8ec0ad6b1d51685fc359027&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea4f92fecc6ac55379b7db07587354ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eadba0dcfe8eff9c8040ec5f17e1adb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8f677b3b4d06e07d3a58446375133fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NR ASSAY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"NR (Neutral Red) assay is another method used to assess cytotoxicity by measuring the uptake of neutral red dye."&lt;SEP&gt;"NR Assay measures the number of viable cells based on the uptake of neutral red dye."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ea4f92fecc6ac55379b7db07587354ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8f677b3b4d06e07d3a58446375133fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SRB ASSAY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"SRB (Sulforhodamine B) assay measures the protein content of cells to evaluate cytotoxic effects."&lt;SEP&gt;"SRB Assay quantifies cellular protein content to determine cell proliferation or cytotoxicity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ea4f92fecc6ac55379b7db07587354ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8f677b3b4d06e07d3a58446375133fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LDH ASSAY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"LDH (Lactate Dehydrogenase) assay detects the release of LDH enzyme from damaged cells, indicating cytotoxicity."&lt;SEP&gt;"LDH Assay detects lactate dehydrogenase release from damaged cells, indicating cytotoxicity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ea4f92fecc6ac55379b7db07587354ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8f677b3b4d06e07d3a58446375133fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEP3B&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CELL LINE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hep3B is a human liver cancer cell line used in studies to evaluate cytotoxic effects of T. molitor larval extract."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ea4f92fecc6ac55379b7db07587354ba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SK-HEP-1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CELL LINE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"SK-HEP-1 is another human liver cancer cell line used in similar studies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ea4f92fecc6ac55379b7db07587354ba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;L929&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CELL LINE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"L929 is a normal murine fibroblast cell line used for testing cytotoxicity of medical devices."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ea4f92fecc6ac55379b7db07587354ba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CACO-2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CELL LINE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Caco-2 is a human colon cancer cell line sensitive to T. molitor larval extract."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ea4f92fecc6ac55379b7db07587354ba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEPG2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CELL LINE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HepG2 is a human liver cancer cell line affected by T. molitor larval extract."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ea4f92fecc6ac55379b7db07587354ba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HELA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CELL LINE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HeLa is a human cervical cancer cell line that shows sensitivity to T. molitor larval extract."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ea4f92fecc6ac55379b7db07587354ba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VERO CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CELL LINE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Vero cells are normal kidney epithelial cells extracted from an African green monkey, used to test Z. morio ethanol extract cytotoxicity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vero cells are normal kidney epithelial cells extracted from an African green monkey, used to test cytotoxicity of Z. morio extracts."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ea4f92fecc6ac55379b7db07587354ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8f677b3b4d06e07d3a58446375133fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LEE ET AL.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"RESEARCH STUDY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lee et al. conducted an in vitro study on the effects of T. molitor larval extract on various cell lines."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ea4f92fecc6ac55379b7db07587354ba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WU ET AL.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"RESEARCHER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Wu et al. conducted research that corroborated findings from Lee et al. regarding the cytotoxic effects of T. molitor extracts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wu et al. contributed significantly to understanding the degradation mechanisms of microplastics and strategies for reducing pollution."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ea4f92fecc6ac55379b7db07587354ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a3d3cf8ea423f7e0f637dddade1bbf1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HAN ET AL.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"RESEARCH STUDY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Han et al. studied the non-mutagenic and non-clastogenic effects of T. molitor larvae fed to rats over 28 days."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ea4f92fecc6ac55379b7db07587354ba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PESSINA ET AL.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"RESEARCH STUDY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pessina et al. demonstrated the beneficial effects of T. molitor extracts on spontaneously hypertensive rats."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ea4f92fecc6ac55379b7db07587354ba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;YUSOF ET AL.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"RESEARCH STUDY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Yusof et al. investigated the cytotoxicity of Z. morio ethanol extracts on Vero cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ea4f92fecc6ac55379b7db07587354ba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GLUTATHIONE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ANTIOXIDANT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Glutathione is an antioxidant that plays a role in cellular defense mechanisms, increased in red blood cells of hypertensive rats treated with T. molitor extracts."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ea4f92fecc6ac55379b7db07587354ba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GLUTATHIONE DISULPHIDE RATIO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The glutathione/glutathione disulphide ratio is a measure of oxidative stress and was improved in hypertensive rats treated with T. molitor extracts."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ea4f92fecc6ac55379b7db07587354ba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPONTANEOUSLY HYPERTENSIVE RATS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ANIMAL MODEL"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Spontaneously hypertensive rats were used as a model to study the effects of T. molitor extracts on cardiovascular health."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ea4f92fecc6ac55379b7db07587354ba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLOOD PRESSURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Blood pressure was significantly reduced in hypertensive rats treated with T. molitor extracts."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ea4f92fecc6ac55379b7db07587354ba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEART RATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Heart rate was decreased in hypertensive rats treated with T. molitor extracts."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ea4f92fecc6ac55379b7db07587354ba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CORONARY PERFUSION PRESSURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Coronary perfusion pressure was reduced in hypertensive rats treated with T. molitor extracts."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ea4f92fecc6ac55379b7db07587354ba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MCF-7 CELL LINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CELL LINE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"MCF-7 is a human breast cancer cell line used to evaluate the cytotoxic effects of Z. morio ethanolic extracts."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c8f677b3b4d06e07d3a58446375133fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYSTYRENE FOAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polystyrene Foam is a feed type that produced the lowest fatty acid content (80.3 g/kg dry matter) in mealworm larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene Foam is a form of polystyrene used as a substrate for mealworm digestion studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene foam is an alternative diet given to insects like Z. morio and T. molitor to study its effects on cytotoxicity and health."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene foam is used as feedstock for larvae in the incubation experiments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene foam is an expanded polystyrene insulation material, used as a test material for assessing plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene foam is a type of plastic used in experiments with insect larvae for biodegradation studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene foam is a type of plastic used in feeding experiments to study its effects on the gut microbiomes of larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene foam encompasses both EPS and XPS types, used in this study as potential feeds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene Foam refers to expanded or extruded polystyrene products such as Styrofoam, which degrade differently depending on density."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene Foam is a material with almost zero nutritional value, leading to high mortality and developmental issues in mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene foam (PS) is a plastic material with negligible nutritional value but contributes to lipid formation in mealworms after CO2 mineralization."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene foam serves as an unconventional feed source that demonstrates Tenebrio molitor's ability to biodegrade plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene foam was introduced as an experimental feed for its potential in biodegradation. However, it caused high larval mortality while increasing nitrogenous substances in both larvae and excrement."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-457d054c08a16428ed81526fc2ddce41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a660790845c6a68ed38b428a7756fc84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a8076792f39f6c801b538312a7b45fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89ff8edff56325c22cfed3871f4fbf48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8f677b3b4d06e07d3a58446375133fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-697bf99ecf19f99243f3b5a4ef5b334c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df045e015825dac8935c9c6d8a402cda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5b6629e8c030ab3162553d83aa6eca4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eed90a978852274ead3771418cd60bed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d01d291012bd548fc067e250ec39fba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10474cc69c90eb0c245c8f55d1ec2834&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5540fc6fe4d3ef0fd986ec36a589c77f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-531058c4540bd4e6a50d141db01d4d11</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IC50&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"IC50 is a measure of the effectiveness of a substance in inhibiting a specific biological or biochemical function, here used to compare the potency of Z. morio extracts."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c8f677b3b4d06e07d3a58446375133fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENDOTHELIAL CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CELL TYPE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Endothelial cells were used in the study to analyze the cytotoxic potential of insect homogenates."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c8f677b3b4d06e07d3a58446375133fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FIBROBLASTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CELL TYPE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fibroblasts are suggested as another cell type for future studies to ensure comprehensive evaluation of cytotoxicity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c8f677b3b4d06e07d3a58446375133fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EPITHELIAL CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CELL TYPE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Epithelial cells are mentioned as potential candidates for further studies to evaluate the cytotoxicity of insect extracts."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c8f677b3b4d06e07d3a58446375133fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ETHANOLIC EXTRACT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ethanolic extract refers to the extraction of active compounds from Z. morio using ethanol, tested for cytotoxicity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c8f677b3b4d06e07d3a58446375133fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ISOPROPANOLIC EXTRACT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Isopropanolic extract is another type of extract used in the study, showing higher cytotoxicity compared to ethanolic extracts on MCF-7 cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c8f677b3b4d06e07d3a58446375133fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FLOW CYTOMETRY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Flow cytometry is a technique used to analyze cell characteristics, such as viability, apoptosis, and ROS levels in insect gut cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c8f677b3b4d06e07d3a58446375133fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AFRICAN GREEN MONKEY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ANIMAL"</data>
      <data key="d1">"African green monkey is the source of Vero cells, which were used to test the cytotoxicity of Z. morio extracts."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c8f677b3b4d06e07d3a58446375133fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POST-HOC LSD TEST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"STATISTICAL METHOD"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Post-hoc LSD (Least Significant Difference) test is a follow-up statistical analysis used to determine significant differences among experimental groups."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c8f677b3b4d06e07d3a58446375133fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONSUMER ATTITUDES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Consumer attitudes refer to the perceptions and opinions of individuals regarding the consumption of insects fed on polystyrene foam."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c8f677b3b4d06e07d3a58446375133fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SCIENTIFIC RESEARCH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Scientific Research involves investigations to confirm the safety of insects fed on Styrofoam for human consumption."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a097963ab8ec0ad6b1d51685fc359027</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SAFETY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Safety is a key concern in evaluating whether insects fed on Styrofoam can be consumed by humans."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a097963ab8ec0ad6b1d51685fc359027</data>
    </node>
