    <node id="&quot;ACHROIA GRISEOLA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Achroia griseola, or the lesser wax moth, has been reported consuming polyethylene materials in certain regions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6264a99190316d0aeed63b5d6485999e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOLOGICAL PROCESS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biological processes encompass the mechanisms by which living organisms interact with their environment, such as biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biological processes encompass the various mechanisms and functions that occur within living organisms, potentially relevant to the study of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The biological process refers to the enzymatic and microbial activities involved in breaking down plastics like Styrofoam and polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"The biological process refers to the breakdown of plastics by mealworms, indicating their ability to metabolize polyethylene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ffb4e34985ec90215629dc19750c8bdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-988ef111808996ddbe6e483d6505ab45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35eed7e10fb1cc08baaecab1b1cffad0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6264a99190316d0aeed63b5d6485999e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ZOPHOBAS MORIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Zophobas moria, also known as superworms, are larvae investigated for their potential to produce antioxidant peptides."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6264a99190316d0aeed63b5d6485999e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANTIOXIDANT PEPTIDES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Antioxidant peptides derived from Zophobas moria have been investigated for their health benefits."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6264a99190316d0aeed63b5d6485999e</data>
    </node>
