      <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SULFORHODAMINE B&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-6cbb8ccec16f4756fa7a1fb365886d9c</data>
      <data key="d1">"Trisma® Base dissolves the sulforhodamine B dye bound to proteins in fixed cells for fluorescence measurement."</data>
      <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MASS LOSS&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-2a214d2b1c90aeb78e6e8562679d4963&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e45f9527e7b07e945435dae572dc387&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c651f9305c4265540ed7deeb891eae71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b42ef7860e1f056d47955d0d13a15cd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ada834fc8d4bea41c0ce1770d6f57e4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8ee8f544a1849c80a5a1524c4f2674c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2281f98bcfd555a703fd86232dfa42fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d47d39d364c5c66ef3fc32ef741ca63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc88563632a3abf926bf4e4ac16973fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5740f0973ff804cae61f6fc12f3e3753&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fbbfcf279533f78737706f5751ee5a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0491f3e96c1d355b8431b9d74868f63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54049db5a67a6464f459ccc427765140&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06a44b308af148551c5b7feef324d88b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6d515521d6d2b72e82154cc544d26cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eba752cb179633f5dd054ee7c9ee2cba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0ec64a7c629b14bfb6652f1960a337c</data>
      <data key="d1">"A measure of the reduction in mass of PP foam over time due to larval consumption."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mass loss in insects fed polystyrene indicates insufficient energy intake from this material."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mass loss refers to the reduction in weight of PS feedstock due to larval consumption."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mass loss represents the reduction in mass of microplastics after ingestion by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The mass loss of microplastics was monitored to determine the extent of degradation by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mass loss indicates the extent of PS mineralization to CO2 during microbial degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mass loss refers to the reduction in weight of LDPE substrates after exposure to larvae or homogenate, indicating potential degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mass loss refers to the reduction in weight of plastic waste after being digested by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mass loss refers to the reduction in weight of plastic films during microbial degradation experiments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mass loss is a measurable biological process observed for various polystyrene materials over time in the experiment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mass loss of studied materials is a parameter used to evaluate the effectiveness of polystyrene biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mass loss refers to the reduction in weight of polystyrene materials consumed by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mass loss is a biochemical measure indicating the extent of plastic degradation by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mass loss measurements were conducted to assess the efficiency of plastic degradation by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mass loss refers to the reduction in material weight after exposure to mealworms, indicating digestibility and degradation potential."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mass loss refers to the reduction in weight of both the mealworms and the plastic materials during the experiment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mass loss quantifies the reduction in PS chip weight due to larval feeding activity."</data>
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
    </node>
