    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"MPS (microplastic spheres) are small plastic particles studied for their effects on mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"MPS is a nutrient source fed to mealworms alone or in combination with bran to assess its impact on survival, growth, and pupation."&lt;SEP&gt;"MPS refers to microplastics, which are small plastic particles used in the study to examine their consumption and degradation by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Micro-PS (MPS) is a rigid plastic test material with a density of 1.114 g cm⁻³ and shore hardness of 25.6 HD. It was cleaned, eluted, and oven-dried before experiments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microplastics (MPs) are small plastic particles typically ranging from 1 to 5000 μm in size, known for their environmental persistence and potential toxicity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microplastics, smaller plastic particles generated during the biofragmentation process."&lt;SEP&gt;"MPs (microplastics) are small plastic particles that undergo biodegradation through oxidation and depolymerization."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-104d99248e84b2776ff5ca17c285a7bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98f748ef0b9e55c370617ad91bcf219c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-582f48080aab075de76c9c590558639f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1283355f048671359adcde7d3137af9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a522a615bbcac2e06f97f2e4e61975b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf697c73d05470fb4a143aa0e4700787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-640f0655e17fab473cca3b460c2795de</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;YOUNG LARVAL STAGE (YLS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LIFE STAGE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The YLS refers to one-month-old mealworms weighing approximately -3 mg ind⁻¹ used in the experiment."&lt;SEP&gt;"YLS represents the early developmental phase of mealworms, characterized by high vulnerability to microplastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1283355f048671359adcde7d3137af9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84558838faaf585c61e883356c52c0e0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MIDDLE LARVAL STAGE (MLS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LIFE STAGE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"MLS is an intermediate phase in the development of mealworms, showing increased resistance compared to YLS."&lt;SEP&gt;"The MLS refers to two-month-old mealworms weighing approximately -20 mg ind⁻¹ used in the experiment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1283355f048671359adcde7d3137af9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84558838faaf585c61e883356c52c0e0</data>
    </node>
