    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PREDATOR-PREY RELATIONSHIP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ECOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Predator-prey relationships describe interactions where one organism consumes another, influencing ecological dynamics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-640f0655e17fab473cca3b460c2795de</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TOXIN"</data>
      <data key="d1">"POPs (Persistent Organic Pollutants) are toxic chemicals that accumulate along with microplastics in the environment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-640f0655e17fab473cca3b460c2795de</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;YANG ET AL.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"RESEARCH STUDY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Yang et al. conducted studies on T. molitor larvae, observing biomass changes under different feeding conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Yang et al. conducted studies on the oxidation and biodegradation patterns of LDPE by different microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Yang et al. refers to the researchers who conducted previous studies on polymer depolymerization in T. molitor and T. obscurus larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;Yang et al. are a group of researchers who have extensively studied the biodegradation capabilities of Tenebrio molitor larvae, commonly known as mealworms, and their gut microorganisms in breaking down various types of plastics. Their research has focused on polystyrene (PS), expanded polystyrene (EPS), polyvinyl chloride (PVC), and low-density polyethylene (LDPE). They demonstrated that mealworms can digest plastics, assimilating carbon and energy from PS, and confirmed the mineralization of ingested PS into biomass. Additionally, they identified lignins in bran as part of the T. molitor larvae's diet.

The team conducted studies investigating the mechanisms of plastic biodegradation, including depolymerization patterns and the role of gut microbiota in the process. Yang et al. also explored the effects of antibiotic suppression on LDPE degradation and examined how Gentamicin sulfate impacts gut microbiota and its influence on polymer biodegradation pathways. Their findings revealed the survival of mealworms on EPS alone and highlighted the critical role of gut microbes in PS biodegradation.

Furthermore, Yang et al. contributed to understanding the chemical composition of Styrofoam used in related research and developed methods for estimating biodegradation rates based on EPS consumption data. Their work extends beyond mealworms, as they have also investigated the biodegradation of plastics by other larval species, such as superworms. Through multiple studies, Yang et al. provided valuable insights into the biodegradation and mineralization of plastics, advancing the field of plastic waste management through innovative biological approaches. Their prior research on mealworm gut microbiomes and plastic biodegradation has been widely referenced in subsequent studies.&lt;SEP&gt;"Yang et al. refers to a group of researchers who conducted studies on larval PS consumption and survival rates."&lt;SEP&gt;"Yang et al. represents studies conducted by researchers exploring PS metabolism and its effects on T. molitor larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-104d99248e84b2776ff5ca17c285a7bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3891caf14683493be3d8709ced467492&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-260d8c268067de32e5ac98d66ab70a6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16328c3c685f35501c3639525e997d2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1498160e7767dd16008724d09b2ac64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd90c8f9754a78aabdbd7053e1adf90b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26a193cc62c03cb6460b0434df42d8c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14f9f0280098bb86719394a4bd53e5bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4df787efdb36123e3f2a76b5402278ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5dc0ba5d8a1abfb746af0dedb7d575b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5740f0973ff804cae61f6fc12f3e3753&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b33a3915745323f1bd29bd2febf60b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba22196a59b67cbf67af7d76a039af1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-843d5746868067bce1a2f15dfc1571e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38e212e8bab88c4d7b6d63a157e27c00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a97d5b092508f2e837932274d6b3282&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-640f0655e17fab473cca3b460c2795de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f71fddc259d51158d5c79f38bf41523f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7f79551ab9793788cd662ab66bca5ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b08485bef3ee3db21e59e159ad4c3e20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b0b175969d87b3be377f65b988d0a52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc908e62eec4d1d05265c6e451cca84c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a8521d10cd6a04d8ba536be9f9dec8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5a94048d4a1499a73a50e74a59245e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a3d3cf8ea423f7e0f637dddade1bbf1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e97dc712df43805c553423ceb65cd6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09d03c0a2dce3f57876d209a83a2e82a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2d6bcd4d2cc81a978694e417e76747e</data>
    </node>
