    <node id="&quot;POLYETHYLENE TEREPHTHALATE (PET)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A common plastic polymer used as feedstock for degradation experiments."&lt;SEP&gt;"PET is a mass-produced fossil-based plastic polymer used in manufacturing materials like textile fibers and packaging, contributing to plastic pollution."&lt;SEP&gt;"PET is a synthetic polymer commonly used in plastics and textiles, which can be degraded by certain enzymes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene terephthalate (PET) is a common thermoplastic polymer resin that is part of the focus in plastic waste management studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene terephthalate is a plastic polymer tested for degradation by T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene terephthalate constitutes 6.9% of plastic usage and is associated with hazardous environmental effects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene terephthalate is a type of polyester used primarily in fibers and plastic bottles."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene terephthalate is a commonly used plastic polymer in packaging materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"PET is the most widely used polycondensate and is almost unsusceptible to biodegradation without engineered enzymes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene Terephthalate (PET) is a biodegradable polymer suggested for evaluation of physiological responses."&lt;SEP&gt;"PET is a type of plastic commonly used in packaging and textiles, known for its recyclability."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene terephthalate is a type of plastic that undergoes biodegradation by specific microorganisms or enzymes."&lt;SEP&gt;"PET is a type of plastic commonly studied for its interaction with insect larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene terephthalate is a common plastic polymer used in bottles and fibers."&lt;SEP&gt;"A type of plastic polymer known for its wide usage and potential to be degraded by certain microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene terephthalate is a common plastic used in bottles and fibers, subject to biodegradation studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene terephthalate is a widely used thermoplastic polymer resin commonly found in fibers, bottles, and food containers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-78f3828bbe45c2c38004a29d55dcbf40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25f3365d0b08e5e77183d813ce6a1049&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae2c294948460ef392ceeec82d5e81f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6aab9d327fcd7d10b5d4fbb22c03292a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-530244abdca5889849fcf86f017ebd77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff933f404b1e6da13d6c1319bc7432c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f44f9d05edb3efaf7fdb8f0f1517549&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22ae90a77be18cbac99e5441d47ce2d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fd138e047a780efd715a5ab4701b58c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd1ab39969c669dba42f162e8497c23f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1536c14bdcd58ae9dabf3a49f6724cd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f1aa99e321e9e3b94552e6c6f8e00f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d76783f53d38e8c7423dff747f0413d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b0664a95aeeb896dcab096b098c3b54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbdeaa1a437ba819412de45788aa119c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dafca19c0156f11127587dba3673503&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2cfbb4289b0cc4c8b69884f6d57c447</data>
    </node>
