    <node id="&quot;POLYDISPERSITY INDEX (PDI)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PDI is calculated as Mw/Mn and indicates the uniformity of polymer chain lengths."&lt;SEP&gt;"PDI measures the broadness of polymer distribution and is calculated as \(M_{\mathrm{w}} / M_{\mathrm{n}}\)."&lt;SEP&gt;"PDI measures the distribution of molecular mass in a given polymer sample."&lt;SEP&gt;"PDI measures the distribution of molecular mass in a given polymer sample."&lt;SEP&gt;"The polydispersity index measures the broadness of the polymer distribution, defined as \( PDI = M_n / M_w \)."&lt;SEP&gt;"PDI quantifies the distribution of molecular weights in a polymer sample, reflecting changes due to biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polydispersity Index is a measure used to quantify the distribution of molecular mass in a given polymer sample, calculated as PDI = Mw/Mn."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polydispersity index measures the distribution of molecular weights in a polymer sample, calculated as PDI = Mw/Mn."&lt;SEP&gt;"PDI measures the distribution of molecular weights in polymers, providing insights into biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polydispersity index measures the distribution of molecular weights in a polymer sample, reflecting uniformity after biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Polydispersity Index is a measure of the distribution of molecular mass in a polymer sample, calculated as PDI = Mw / Mv."&lt;SEP&gt;"PDI quantifies the distribution of molecular weights in a polymer sample."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polydispersity index measures the distribution of molecular weights in a polymer sample, with lower values indicating a narrower range of molecular sizes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polydispersity index quantifies the distribution of molecular weights in a polymer sample, indicating uniformity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d7f79551ab9793788cd662ab66bca5ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25f3365d0b08e5e77183d813ce6a1049&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdc8398efba587929eebd0a0842f6e69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-152e743d95b64fab136afadf0304d459&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e136b8a35c0d60811b9daf0cbd5729f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6afbb58ebe9108893daf7e65d59fac39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c39e41f4f36c9c6854fa71508c35a08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9af0d95fd5f52d02b9cb33387951963&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b04ae62930e9961f964284418f1848b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d76783f53d38e8c7423dff747f0413d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f75b58db5211fc7348ccca8206b9bbae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cbedc06292e5cf07fbca1958d8587e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31ad3152e855d5b8085e1e61af57515d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4265fd894f71345b4ef09c26e6adbda5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYURETHANE (PUR)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Another polymer included in studies related to plastic degradation by invertebrates."&lt;SEP&gt;"PUR is a polymer composed of organic units joined by carbamate links, commonly used in foams and coatings."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyurethane (PUR) is a polymer used in various applications and is among the plastics being investigated for biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyurethane is a plastic polymer tested for degradation by T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyurethane contributes to 7.4% of plastic usage and is among the hazardous plastics affecting the environment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyurethane is a polymer known for its elasticity and resilience, used in a variety of products including foams and coatings."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyurethane is a type of plastic polymer that undergoes changes in molecular weight during biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyurethane is a plastic polymer often used in various applications and is resistant to biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyurethane (PUR) is another persistent plastic recommended for further testing on its health risks."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyurethane is a polymer used in foam, coatings, and adhesives."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyurethane is a polymer that undergoes biodegradation processes in landfill microbial cultures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyurethane is a versatile polymer with potential for biodegradation research."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyurethane is a diverse class of polymers used in foams, coatings, adhesives, and elastomers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyurethane is another significant polymer impacting environmental health."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c2cfbb4289b0cc4c8b69884f6d57c447&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25f3365d0b08e5e77183d813ce6a1049&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a00d67f63d22d1959c8a565b6a86d22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2169963c4d6dae9b98da331d39eaa72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6aab9d327fcd7d10b5d4fbb22c03292a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-530244abdca5889849fcf86f017ebd77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f44f9d05edb3efaf7fdb8f0f1517549&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22ae90a77be18cbac99e5441d47ce2d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1536c14bdcd58ae9dabf3a49f6724cd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49ebafd73759fc2bf3d4a642ccad96e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d76783f53d38e8c7423dff747f0413d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b0664a95aeeb896dcab096b098c3b54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dafca19c0156f11127587dba3673503&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd1ab39969c669dba42f162e8497c23f</data>
    </node>
