      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Macroinvertebrates are small animals without a backbone, commonly used as indicators of ecosystem health due to their sensitivity to environmental changes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Macroinvertebrates refer to larger organisms without a backbone that contribute to the degradation of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Macroinvertebrates exhibit physiological responses to plastic exposure without degrading capabilities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Macroinvertebrates are small organisms that play a role in the biodegradation of plastics."</data>
