    <node id="&quot;SPCR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"SPCR refers to the specific consumption rate of polystyrene (PS) microplastics by mealworms, indicating how much PS is consumed per 100 larvae per day."&lt;SEP&gt;"SPCR stands for specific PS consumption rate, a measure of how much polystyrene is consumed by the larvae over time."&lt;SEP&gt;"SPCR, or specific polymer (PS) consumption rate, measures the mass of PS consumed by 100 larvae over a test period."&lt;SEP&gt;"Specific PET consumption rate, a metric used to quantify the amount of PET consumed by larvae per day."&lt;SEP&gt;"Specific LDPE consumption rate (SPCR) represents the amount of LDPE consumed per 100 larvae daily, with T. molitor having slightly higher rates than T. obscurus."&lt;SEP&gt;"SPCR stands for specific PS consumption rate, measuring how much PS MPs were consumed by the mealworms."</data>
