    <node id="&quot;VITAMINS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Essential organic compounds identified in the frass of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Essential organic compounds necessary for cell growth and metabolism, absent in the PET and agar diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vitamins are necessary nutrients for growth, not present in Styrofoam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vitamins are crucial nutrients absent in PET, affecting larval growth and development."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vitamins are essential nutrients synthesized by symbiotic bacteria to support the host's metabolic needs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vitamins are essential nutrients absent in plastics, impacting mealworm health and viability when consumed exclusively."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vitamins are micronutrients added to feed to enhance the overall development and health of larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vitamins are part of the nutritional profile of mealworms, enhancing their value as a food source."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vitamins are essential organic compounds produced by fungi, providing nutritional advantages under stringent conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vitamins are essential nutrients added to the diet to support larval health and development."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vitamins are nutrients added to the diet to enhance larval health and survival."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vitamins are supplements added to the larval diet in certain groups, aiming to enhance nutrition but still resulting in partial inhibition of growth and reproduction."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vitamins contribute to the health and development of T. molitor larvae, with their absence potentially affecting life cycle progression."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d9095195e9cf06b9887c03abde6284d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69679184959639a1ff81c7392cd5cef5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b387da8298c55673284dca93ea82fc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41b8c7f0b790b0289a7683fde0eca126&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1769c4becf46c99994cb7ced2bffda1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5740f0973ff804cae61f6fc12f3e3753&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d01d291012bd548fc067e250ec39fba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a97d5b092508f2e837932274d6b3282&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c5fc4d4324334254706d6d5f9312276&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-531058c4540bd4e6a50d141db01d4d11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d616d4c3c3199d53c1ae93ebcf3589d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f71fddc259d51158d5c79f38bf41523f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MINERALS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRITIONAL COMPONENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Inorganic nutrients crucial for cellular function, not adequately provided by PET or agar diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Minerals are essential nutrients absent in Styrofoam but needed for proper mealworm development."&lt;SEP&gt;"Minerals are vital nutrients not found in PET, influencing larval growth and development."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mineral content decreases in frass from Tenebrio molitor fed a polystyrene diet, attributed to increased cellular activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Minerals are necessary nutrients not provided by plastics, contributing to decreased mealworm viability during plastic consumption."&lt;SEP&gt;"Minerals are critical nutrients present in mealworms, contributing to their overall nutritional value."</data>
