    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AMINO ACIDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Amino Acids are organic compounds produced by fungi, contributing to their nutritional role in the gut microbiome."&lt;SEP&gt;"Amino acids are activated enzymatically, leading to amide bond formation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Amino acids are building blocks of proteins that are easily digestible and assimilated from yeast by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Amino acids are essential nutrients necessary for the survival and growth of mealworms, which are absent in PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Building blocks of proteins, essential for cell growth and repair, lacking in the PET and agar diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Amino acids are nutrients synthesized by symbiotic bacteria for the host under nutritional deficiency conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Amino acids are essential components provided by WB that are necessary for the growth and development of larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Amino acids are metabolites or residues observed at specific peaks in frass samples."</data>
