    <node id="&quot;AGAR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A gelatinous substance used as a solidifying agent in microbial media."&lt;SEP&gt;"Agar is a gelatinous substance used as a food source in experiments with T. molitor larvae, providing hydration and some nutrition."&lt;SEP&gt;"Agar is added to LB medium to solidify it for bacterial colony isolation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Agar is the solidifying agent in Blood Agar, providing a surface for microbial culture."&lt;SEP&gt;"Agar is a gelatinous substance used to solidify LB medium for bacterial culture."&lt;SEP&gt;"Agar is a gelatinous material derived from algae, used as a solidifying agent in microbiological culture media."&lt;SEP&gt;"Agar is a product used in the experiments as a control and mixed with PP polymers to feed larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Agar is used as an adhesive mixed with PE powders to facilitate ingestion by larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Agar is a gelling agent used in solid media formulations like CFBAM and LB medium to support bacterial colony formation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Agar is a gelatinous substance derived from algae, commonly used as a solidifying agent in microbial cultures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Agar is a solidifying agent used in the preparation of solid culture media like LB agar plates."&lt;SEP&gt;"Agar is a gelatinous substance derived from algae, used in the experiment to mix with PE polymers for feeding larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Agar is used as a nutrient medium mixed with PE MPs during the incubation process."&lt;SEP&gt;"A solidifying agent used in LB medium for bacterial culture."&lt;SEP&gt;"A solidifying agent used in the preparation of LB medium for culturing microorganisms."</data>
