    <node id="&quot;PUR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PUR (Polyurethane) is another hydrolyzable polymer with higher biodegradability compared to non-hydrolyzable plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"PUR (polyurethane) is another plastic material that may potentially be degraded by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"PUR refers to polyurethane, a plastic material that mealworms can consume."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyurethane (PUR) is a plastic material consumed by T. molitor larvae but at lower rates compared to PET."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyurethane, a plastic product degraded via gut-microbial-mediated mechanisms in T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyurethane (PUR) is a plastic material that some insects have demonstrated the ability to degrade."</data>
