      <data key="d1">"Proteins associated with bacterial flagella, enhancing adhesion and facilitating electron transport."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d5238515b2316265fb5cb6c6295c54e8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRICARBOXYLIC ACID CYCLE (TCA CYCLE)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A metabolic pathway where intermediates from PET degradation enter for energy production and mineralization."&lt;SEP&gt;"The tricarboxylic acid cycle is a central metabolic pathway involved in energy production and could be linked to the metabolism of PET degradation products."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c638e6375f0847be0d1116f4846e5e1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5238515b2316265fb5cb6c6295c54e8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNFED&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DIET"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Unfed refers to larvae not provided with any additional diet, serving as a baseline for comparison."&lt;SEP&gt;"Unfed refers to larvae that have not been fed any specific diet, serving as another control group."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eb14281b4a095b6c531146d40b5110a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5238515b2316265fb5cb6c6295c54e8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;4-HYDROXYPHENYLACETATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"4-Hydroxyphenylacetate is a metabolite involved in the degradation pathway of aromatic compounds."&lt;SEP&gt;"4-hydroxyphenylacetate is an intermediate compound generated during aerobic decomposition of PET."&lt;SEP&gt;"4-hydroxyphenylacetate is an intermediate product generated during aerobic decomposition of PET."&lt;SEP&gt;"A metabolite involved in PET degradation, processed by specific oxidases in the gut microbiome."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-38a07d29ecfa06f82d97e69f5cd2c801&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df5e2448d1e9703b511b85725469467e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5238515b2316265fb5cb6c6295c54e8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;3,4-DIHYDROXYPHENYLACETATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"3,4-dihydroxyphenylacetate is an intermediate metabolite formed during PET degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"A metabolite involved in PET degradation, processed by specific oxidases in the gut microbiome."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-df5e2448d1e9703b511b85725469467e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5238515b2316265fb5cb6c6295c54e8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;3-PHENYLPROPANOATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"3-phenylpropanoate is an intermediate compound produced during the degradation of PET."&lt;SEP&gt;"A metabolite involved in PET degradation, processed by specific oxidases in the gut microbiome."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-df5e2448d1e9703b511b85725469467e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5238515b2316265fb5cb6c6295c54e8</data>
    </node>
