      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MARKER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"This permease protein is another differential GO identified in the study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0efd7a9e4443dc5d3dfe588c7f7efc13</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIPID METABOLITES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lipid metabolites are significantly up-regulated in larvae fed PET, possibly due to oxidative stress defense or energy storage."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0efd7a9e4443dc5d3dfe588c7f7efc13</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GLYCEROPHOSPHOLIPID METABOLISM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Glycerophospholipid metabolism is a pathway affected by gut microbes during PET degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"This pathway maintains cell membrane properties and mitochondrial functions, being significantly enriched in the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"Glycerophospholipid metabolism is significantly upregulated in PET-fed samples, maintaining cell membrane properties and mitochondrial functions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Glycerophospholipid metabolism is linked to membrane integrity and active substance composition, observed in ultrahigh MW PS-fed mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0efd7a9e4443dc5d3dfe588c7f7efc13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b19ac5bdc755bb8e9deb8e317ce365dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df5e2448d1e9703b511b85725469467e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ee6535da22915c7094098e016b19d80</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ARGININE AND PROLINE METABOLISM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Arginine and proline metabolism helps maintain osmotic equilibrium and protect protein structures, being significantly perturbed in PS-M and PS-H-fed mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Critical for osmotic equilibrium and protein protection, this pathway may indicate stress response caused by microplastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0efd7a9e4443dc5d3dfe588c7f7efc13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ee6535da22915c7094098e016b19d80</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALPHA-LINOLENIC ACID METABOLISM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A plastic degradation-related pathway involving fatty acid metabolism, it was found to be enriched in the study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0efd7a9e4443dc5d3dfe588c7f7efc13</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ETHER LIPID METABOLISM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Another pathway linked to plastic degradation and fatty acid processes, showing enrichment in the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ether lipid metabolism is a pathway altered during PET degradation, influenced by gut microbes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ether lipid metabolism is significantly upregulated during PET degradation, supporting the production of intermediates from PET hydrolysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0efd7a9e4443dc5d3dfe588c7f7efc13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b19ac5bdc755bb8e9deb8e317ce365dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df5e2448d1e9703b511b85725469467e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AMINO SUGAR AND NUCLEOTIDE SUGAR METABOLISM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Amino Sugar and Nucleotide Sugar Metabolism involves the metabolism of these sugars."&lt;SEP&gt;"Amino Sugar and Nucleotide Sugar Metabolism involves the synthesis and breakdown of sugars involved in cell wall and glycoprotein formation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Amino sugar and nucleotide sugar metabolism involves the synthesis and degradation of amino sugars and nucleotide sugars, which are essential for cellular structures and functions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Key carbohydrate metabolism pathway significantly altered in the study, indicating biofragmentation effects."&lt;SEP&gt;"This metabolic pathway was enriched in bran-fed mealworms, reflecting carbohydrate and nucleotide processing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9424d3ce58d3ff2e0adc795d24fe84f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d290a6a81802d3048c35d2a2fb1252c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5f4bda412174e8b173f180d9b4311ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0efd7a9e4443dc5d3dfe588c7f7efc13</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GALLERIA MELLONELLA LARVAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"INSECT LARVAE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Galleria mellonella larvae are another species of insect larvae capable of degrading plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Galleria mellonella larvae are insects whose gut contains A. flavus PEDX3, a strain capable of degrading polyethylene (PE)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Galleria mellonella larvae compensate for nutrient deficiency by enhancing lipid metabolic pathways when fed plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Galleria mellonella larvae are organisms studied for their ability to degrade polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Galleria mellonella larvae are plastic-degrading insect larvae suggested for further research."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d2169963c4d6dae9b98da331d39eaa72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0efd7a9e4443dc5d3dfe588c7f7efc13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47e7fe379fcd6b17740bc4d953cd3b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d33654bada6ddaf4917586dd5fd41e9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17052974ec1c317689bf07f0684f130f</data>
    </node>
