    <node id="&quot;GLUTATHIONE METABOLISM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A pathway involved in stress responses caused by microplastics, potentially active in this study."&lt;SEP&gt;"Glutathione metabolism is a key pathway involved in detoxifying reactive oxygen species and maintaining redox balance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Glutathione metabolism is upregulated as part of the stress response to plastic exposure in BSF larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0efd7a9e4443dc5d3dfe588c7f7efc13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae2c294948460ef392ceeec82d5e81f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-939800f545beed77f5a7d1c026c250fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICROBIOTA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Microbiota refers to communities of microorganisms capable of degrading certain types of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbiota refers to the community of microorganisms that reside in the insect gut, playing a crucial role in PET biodegradation and metabolism."&lt;SEP&gt;"The whole microbiota refers to the bacterial communities living in the digestive tract of T. molitor, which interact with the environment and play a role in PS biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbiota refers to the community of microorganisms inhabiting a specific environment, such as the gut of Tenebrio molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbiota refers to the community of microorganisms residing in the digestive tract of Tenebrio molitor larvae, contributing to polystyrene degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbiota refers to the community of microorganisms residing in the gut of insects, contributing to their ability to degrade plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbiota refers to the community of microorganisms inhabiting a particular environment or organism."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6e415042ae4079ee5fe96c7105eb534c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dd9a0647afad70038c8052c24eb5a67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8518832c2d3e002c8acf71795e306144&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a54f7d9e0a43fb94e2fc35f93656fc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-032b3b0fe0366e6e76e86abf8c48d200&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df5e2448d1e9703b511b85725469467e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b50c5a85182344022614ffe10dc9382</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIODEGRADATION PROCESS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biodegradation refers to the breakdown of organic materials by living organisms, such as mealworms consuming plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"The biodegradation process involves the breakdown of PET by microbial enzymes and host mechanisms, leading to metabolic products."&lt;SEP&gt;"The biological process through which plastics like PVC and polyethylene are broken down into simpler compounds by microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The biodegradation process refers to the mechanism through which mealworms break down polystyrene polymers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f15cc70e99a3287ced1a6cbb6c8d76a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df24ea37743c236d369911024fc20bfc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df5e2448d1e9703b511b85725469467e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70eb294c60e73338ed59a2eddf057c1e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIPID METABOLISM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lipid metabolism encompasses pathways such as ether lipid metabolism and glycerophospholipid metabolism, influenced by gut microbes during PET degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The biochemical processes involved in the synthesis and breakdown of lipids within an organism."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipid metabolism encompasses the processes involved in the synthesis and degradation of lipids within organisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipid metabolism involves the synthesis and degradation of lipids, crucial for energy storage and membrane structure."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d5f4bda412174e8b173f180d9b4311ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b715dc0bf578795b387fe1255d07f22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df5e2448d1e9703b511b85725469467e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d616d4c3c3199d53c1ae93ebcf3589d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXTRACELLULAR PET HYDROLYSES AND OXIDASES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"These enzymes secreted by microbes and the host initiate the PET degradation process."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-df5e2448d1e9703b511b85725469467e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AEROBIC BACTERIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROBE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Aerobic bacteria participate in the oxidation and depolymerization of PET during the biodegradation process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacteria that require oxygen to survive and contribute to the biodegradation of PET."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2b715dc0bf578795b387fe1255d07f22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df5e2448d1e9703b511b85725469467e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FACULTATIVE ANAEROBIC BACTERIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROBE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Facultative anaerobic bacteria contribute to hydrolysis, fermentation, and mineralization during PET degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-df5e2448d1e9703b511b85725469467e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHEMOTAXIS PROTEINS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROTEIN"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chemotaxis proteins enable gut microorganisms to seek carbon sources during PET degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Proteins that play a role in the movement of cells towards chemicals or stimuli, aiding in plastic degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2b715dc0bf578795b387fe1255d07f22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df5e2448d1e9703b511b85725469467e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRANSPORT PROTEINS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROTEIN"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Proteins responsible for transporting substances across cell membranes, contributing to the degradation process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Transport proteins facilitate the movement of PET degradation intermediates across cellular membranes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2b715dc0bf578795b387fe1255d07f22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df5e2448d1e9703b511b85725469467e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FLAGELLA FORMATION-RELATED PROTEINS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROTEIN"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Flagella formation-related proteins aid in the motility of gut microorganisms for efficient carbon source acquisition."&lt;SEP&gt;"Proteins involved in the formation of flagella, which help in bacterial motility and interaction with plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2b715dc0bf578795b387fe1255d07f22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df5e2448d1e9703b511b85725469467e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TCA CYCLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The TCA cycle (tricarboxylic acid cycle) is central to energy production through the oxidation of acetyl-CoA."&lt;SEP&gt;"The TCA cycle is a metabolic pathway involved in the breakdown of PET intermediates into usable energy."&lt;SEP&gt;"The TCA cycle is a metabolic pathway where intermediates from styrene decomposition enter for further processing."&lt;SEP&gt;"The TCA cycle, also known as the Krebs cycle, is a central metabolic pathway involved in energy production."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Tricarboxylic acid cycle (TCA cycle) is a central metabolic pathway involved in energy production within cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"The TCA cycle, also known as the Krebs cycle, is a central metabolic pathway for generating energy through the oxidation of acetyl-CoA."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-158317f8eba5f6198135df044d385935&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3c4d027474e8769f550ce290c9391ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1679027e80b766e0469f7323db15b497&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a708f09b97ac93da05bd1d20bdfe174&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df5e2448d1e9703b511b85725469467e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FORMIC ACID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A weak acid used in both phases A and B of the UHPLC mobile phase."&lt;SEP&gt;"An organic acid used as an additive in the mobile phase for LC-MS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Formic acid is an intermediate product formed during facultative anaerobic/anaerobic decomposition of PET."&lt;SEP&gt;"Formic acid is used in LC-MS grade applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Used in both phases A and B of the UHPLC mobile phase."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-92b1e432ea4bee0f332d7303188e6de7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b4ab01931acbc7aa9c77cd03531c57e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df5e2448d1e9703b511b85725469467e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e69c793c3b67aed7a68bf864c2c7a309</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NITROGEN FIXING MICROBES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROBE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nitrogen fixing microbes convert dissolved N2 to ammonium as an N source to mitigate nitrogen deficiency."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-df5e2448d1e9703b511b85725469467e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PET POLYMER DEGRADING ENZYMES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Enzymes involved in the degradation of PET polymer, including hydrolases, oxidases, decarboxylase, depolymerase, oxidoreductase, and dehydrogenase."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2b715dc0bf578795b387fe1255d07f22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ASSIMILATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Assimilation involves the integration of absorbed nutrients into the biological system of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Assimilation refers to the incorporation of carbon from degraded products into biomass."&lt;SEP&gt;"The incorporation of nutrients or substrates into the metabolic pathways of organisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Assimilation is the biological process by which the bacterium incorporates breakdown products of poly(ethylene terephthalate) into its own metabolism."&lt;SEP&gt;"Assimilation is the process by which energy is absorbed from food and stored as reserves within the organism."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2b715dc0bf578795b387fe1255d07f22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eee7e44e4c15567a057d7d295d240211&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21c07a838ff0a489c73c8319e5011134&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb16cd27b6682965375050748ee77862&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d7f6907ee7ce47b00537b1458fcc029</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FACULTATIVE BACTERIA&quot;">
