    <node id="&quot;SYNTHETIC POLYMERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Synthetic Polymers are man-made polymers that can be broken down through enzymatic degradation, highlighting the versatility of enzymatic activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Synthetic Polymers are man-made polymers with various industrial applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Synthetic polymers are man-made materials that form the basis of many plastic products."&lt;SEP&gt;"Synthetic polymers are man-made materials with a wide range of applications, including plastics and textiles."&lt;SEP&gt;"Synthetic polymers are materials fed to mealworms to observe their digestion and chemical transformation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Synthetic polymers include materials like polystyrene and polyethylene, used experimentally as part of mealworm diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Synthetic polymers are man-made materials composed of long-chain molecules, widely used in manufacturing and contributing to plastic waste."&lt;SEP&gt;"Synthetic Polymers are materials like polystyrene targeted for degradation by gut microbes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Synthetic polymers are man-made materials that can be degraded by certain microorganisms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ee46611b24ea3848df979ded841f06b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78f3828bbe45c2c38004a29d55dcbf40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71372e333b39cee7eea0c53f89bec5c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40407fe311340b08da856202f38b459c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-512840a413df7ae3d881389c5cf1feb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56af57b5211422531c03b0cbcfded1b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59453e4c878e72ac6985a08043cdf126&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c31fc195067eeb8acb7f98417bd6744&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a81144d30653377d6d90e26c4497eb0</data>
    </node>
