    <node id="&quot;YANG, BRANDON, ET AL.&quot;\">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Researchers who have contributed to studies on the biodegradation of plastics by T. molitor larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c2cfbb4289b0cc4c8b69884f6d57c447</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENTAMICIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ANTIBIOTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">Gentamicin is an antibiotic extensively studied for its effects on gut microbial communities, particularly in the larvae of Tenebrio molitor (commonly known as mealworms or superworms) and Zophobas atratus. It plays a critical role in investigating the degradation processes of various plastics, including polystyrene (PS), polypropylene (PP), and low-density polyethylene (LDPE).

In studies involving Tenebrio obscurus, Gentamicin was used to suppress gut bacteria in larvae, which significantly inhibits their ability to degrade polystyrene. The antibiotic acts as an inhibitor, affecting the depolymerization of PS by reducing bacterial counts in the larval gut. This highlights the essential role that gut bacteria play in the biodegradation process. While Gentamicin inhibits the depolymerization of PS, it does not appear to have the same effect on LDPE. Research has confirmed that LDPE biodegradation in Tenebrio larvae is independent of gut microbes, suggesting that digestive enzymes rather than microbial activity are responsible for this process.

Gentamicin has also been utilized in suppression tests to examine its effects on gut microbes and the biodegradation of PP in larvae of both T. molitor and Z. atratus. In these experiments, the antibiotic suppresses gut bacteria, leading to a loss of plastic-depolymerizing ability in the larvae. Techniques such as inhibition halo tests have been employed to assess the impact of Gentamicin on mealworm gut bacteria, demonstrating its ability to depress bacterial populations and inhibit bacterial growth.

Additionally, Gentamicin can inhibit the growth of specific bacteria, such as Exiguobacterium sp. YT2, which are involved in the degradation of extracellular polymeric substances (EPS). As a result, the antibiotic decreases the effectiveness of gut bacteria in depolymerizing EPS, further confirming the importance of microbial activity in plastic degradation.

Overall, Gentamicin's effects on gut flora have provided valuable insights into the mechanisms underlying plastic depolymerization by larvae. By suppressing gut microbes, the antibiotic allows researchers to study the role of microflora in the degradation of plastics, emphasizing the interdependence between gut bacteria and the larval ability to break down polymers. These findings underscore the complex interactions between larvae, their gut microbiota, and the biodegradation of different types of plastics.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e340b8704554cdc28486ac37e78ab0fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-effe1e87d51e126ff4ec5cf9e49d6524&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b12451ba2a22e6f74c543f982a0a7b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89c37eb3e3a5b6ab731f5dbe280aa054&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-260d8c268067de32e5ac98d66ab70a6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85c9587b55f24a8ae5ba6b478dbb98e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b95a108327e39d37d20bdd99db541164&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4443da1fe36ec7133cd5add18d1957a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cbedc06292e5cf07fbca1958d8587e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-207d77d551e893eda6578be68ca3d0db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4265fd894f71345b4ef09c26e6adbda5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d5a9fbe4803ded646c6a5e4d23ca93a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89a76f613b36454134940f78fba1c0f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10004ab6a85cecf4effb74c306df57cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4df787efdb36123e3f2a76b5402278ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5dc0ba5d8a1abfb746af0dedb7d575b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-843d5746868067bce1a2f15dfc1571e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68c274a59cd5db4cd675bca51f11adb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb14281b4a095b6c531146d40b5110a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ab754d1dc0a02ee3f869d2b082a710e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c42631c88da011b836666dae04cfa11a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-069f8447676509ffdd0028e9c05fb9ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7f79551ab9793788cd662ab66bca5ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8b7b5a840af17cee78d71347e532d51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04683827a8d88bc2fa28ae73ccc0714f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-697bf99ecf19f99243f3b5a4ef5b334c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70735757eafccc0f762f21f5d3ac8556&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d3b3c7bbc61318a9728caff13ac5b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5613b129e38cb777855c04f228fe7e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3c4d027474e8769f550ce290c9391ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cb5478046e8b80ff49694ccdb8f92fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06ba9ca61fb4f42582bbf7bd00ff0005&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8ee8f544a1849c80a5a1524c4f2674c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e05bc34fccfca5e177064daf8346866&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfe58fb1bbaa5c35e9c6c837d0b1050f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d39fc863538a777920c4eafb37bcf8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9aa972c0f1c2838103f61cd8ae101a8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2cfbb4289b0cc4c8b69884f6d57c447</data>
