    <node id="&quot;MOLECULAR WEIGHTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Molecular Weights refer to the mass of molecules in a sample, which can change due to degradation processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Molecular weights describe the size of molecules, which can change during degradation processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Molecular weights of polymers influence their resistance to biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Molecular weights refer to the size of polymer chains, analyzed here using HT-GPC."&lt;SEP&gt;"Molecular weights (Mw, Mp, Ms) are critical measures used to assess the extent of polymer degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Molecular weights are used to quantify changes in polymer size during biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Molecular weights describe the size of polymer chains, which change during depolymerization."</data>
