      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Acinetobacterium sp. is another bacterial species with potential for degrading plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4c39e41f4f36c9c6854fa71508c35a08</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RESIDUAL POLYMER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Residual polymer refers to the non-degraded and partially degraded polymer found in larval frass after plastic consumption."&lt;SEP&gt;"Residual polymer refers to the remaining polymer after biodegradation, often recovered from frass via solvent extraction."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4c39e41f4f36c9c6854fa71508c35a08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2d6bcd4d2cc81a978694e417e76747e</data>
