    <node id="&quot;NUMBER AVERAGE MOLECULAR WEIGHT (MN)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The number average molecular weight provides information about the lowest molecular weight fraction in polymers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4c39e41f4f36c9c6854fa71508c35a08</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WEIGHT AVERAGE MOLECULAR WEIGHT (MW)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The weight average molecular weight represents the central portion of the molecular weight distribution curve."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4c39e41f4f36c9c6854fa71508c35a08</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SIZE AVERAGE MOLECULAR WEIGHT (MZ)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The size average molecular weight indicates the highest molecular weight portion in polymers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4c39e41f4f36c9c6854fa71508c35a08</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VISCOSITY AVERAGE MOLECULAR WEIGHT (MV)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The viscosity average molecular weight reflects the viscosity of the polymer sample based on empirical equations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4c39e41f4f36c9c6854fa71508c35a08</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SODIUM DODECYL SULFATE (SDS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"SDS cleans the plastic surface prior to analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sodium Dodecyl Sulfate (SDS) is a detergent commonly used for cleaning and pretreatment of polymer samples to remove biofilm and organics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sodium dodecyl sulfate is used in pretreatment processes to remove biofilm from residual plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sodium dodecyl sulfate is a detergent used to remove biofilms from PS film surfaces for analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sodium dodecyl sulfate is a detergent used to remove biofilm from surfaces."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sodium Dodecyl Sulfate is a detergent used to wash PE film for accurate weight measurement."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5af82472112cbc9e76b1fd1ac6e8c54e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70735757eafccc0f762f21f5d3ac8556&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c39e41f4f36c9c6854fa71508c35a08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e6fd56772ef66691cf6f1c613ba42e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f1aa99e321e9e3b94552e6c6f8e00f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b12468cce513394dbebb8b4ce27f62d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STARCH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A carbohydrate component found in low-density PE (LDPE) used in experiments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Starch is a carbohydrate present in the barley bran, serving as an energy source for the larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Starch is another co-diet component that may lead to significant misinterpretation of TGA results."&lt;SEP&gt;"Starch is a carbohydrate component present in barley bran at 22% concentration."&lt;SEP&gt;"Starch is a carbohydrate component in feed that affects the overall development time of larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Starch is a beneficial nutrient identified as influencing the growth and development of T. molitor larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b4ab01931acbc7aa9c77cd03531c57e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84f576487c8d473c1524eb1141730a12&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b12468cce513394dbebb8b4ce27f62d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a8521d10cd6a04d8ba536be9f9dec8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a97d5b092508f2e837932274d6b3282&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-531058c4540bd4e6a50d141db01d4d11</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROTON NUCLEAR MAGNETIC RESONANCE (\({ }^{1} \MATHRM{H} \MATHRM{NMR}\))&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"\({ }^{1} \mathrm{H} \mathrm{NMR}\) is a spectroscopic technique used to study chemical modifications in polymers after biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0b12468cce513394dbebb8b4ce27f62d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIFFERENTIAL SCANNING CALORIMETRIC (DSC) ANALYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"DSC analysis evaluates thermal properties of materials and detects shifts in glass transition temperatures as indicators of biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0b12468cce513394dbebb8b4ce27f62d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICROSCOPIC OBSERVATIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Microscopic observations are used to visualize microbial colonization and biofilm formation on plastic polymer surfaces."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0b12468cce513394dbebb8b4ce27f62d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIVE/DEAD BACLIGHT BACTERIAL VIABILITY KIT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The LIVE/DEAD BacLight Bacterial Viability Kit is a tool used to stain and assess bacterial viability."&lt;SEP&gt;"This kit is used to stain and differentiate live and dead bacterial cells during microscopic observations."</data>
