    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SCANNING ELECTRON MICROSCOPY (SEM)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"SEM is a process used to analyze the surface alterations of PS films after microbial exposure."&lt;SEP&gt;"SEM is a technique used for direct observation of microbial colonization and structural changes on polymer surfaces."&lt;SEP&gt;"SEM is employed to directly observe microbial colonization and structural changes like cracks and holes on polymer surfaces."&lt;SEP&gt;"SEM is a technique used to visualize the surface morphology of materials at high magnifications, revealing pits and cracks on the HDPE film after bacterial treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Scanning Electron Microscopy is a technique used to observe changes in polystyrene surfaces caused by bacterial activity, such as cracks and holes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Scanning Electron Microscopy is a technique used to visualize microscopic structures, revealing changes in polystyrene caused by microbial activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"SEM observed micro-morphological images of raw CS, PS feedstocks, and frass of PS-, CS-fed larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"SEM is a technique used to examine the surface structure and characterization of nanoplastics before and after treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"SEM is a technique used to investigate the physical changes in degraded PS films."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6c808bc1867233246c6ad41186de9452&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dd9a0647afad70038c8052c24eb5a67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-262d7fa1c8f2581943a41cf4897fa253&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20395efa1299dc8b777774e765ad1159&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a54f7d9e0a43fb94e2fc35f93656fc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3196d2d200ebf060e966a565b5eb26de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b12468cce513394dbebb8b4ce27f62d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02761f0aee6116a25ce05444f6ce8242</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WATER CONTACT ANGLE (WCA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A measure of hydrophobicity determined using a contact angle measuring device."&lt;SEP&gt;"WCA measures hydrophobicity changes on polymer surfaces, serving as an indicator of biodegradation activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"WCA measures the wettability of a surface, which can change during plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Water Contact Angle measures the hydrophobicity of a surface, indicating changes in the properties of PS film due to microbial activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Water contact angle is a measure of hydrophobicity of the PS film surface after microbial treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"WCA is a method used to measure surface properties of degraded PS films."&lt;SEP&gt;"WCA measures the hydrophobicity of a polymer surface, providing insights into surface properties post-biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"WCA measures the hydrophobicity or hydrophilicity of surfaces, including PE powder and frass samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Water contact angle measures the hydrophobicity or hydrophilicity of surfaces like PP foam and frass samples."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6c808bc1867233246c6ad41186de9452&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68041096d198a27b4ed526281746b7f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24ba7d6b1b5275089cbabe56bc33b92e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06ba9ca61fb4f42582bbf7bd00ff0005&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6afbb58ebe9108893daf7e65d59fac39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70735757eafccc0f762f21f5d3ac8556&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b12468cce513394dbebb8b4ce27f62d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f75b58db5211fc7348ccca8206b9bbae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4265fd894f71345b4ef09c26e6adbda5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ISOTOPIC LABELING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Isotopic labeling uses labeled isotopes (e.g., 14C, 13C) to track biodegradation and mineralization of plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0b12468cce513394dbebb8b4ce27f62d</data>
    </node>
