    <node id="&quot;WCA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"WCA (Water Contact Angle) measures the hydrophobicity of surfaces, indicating changes in the surface properties of plastics after ingestion by Tenebrio species."&lt;SEP&gt;"WCA (Water Contact Angle) measures the wettability of a surface, indicating changes in the hydrophobicity of PS films after microbial treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"WCA (water contact angle) analysis measures the hydrophobicity or hydrophilicity of plastic surfaces after microbial interaction."&lt;SEP&gt;"Water contact angle measurements assess surface properties during microbial degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"WCA (water contact angle) analysis confirms oxidation and biodegradation of PP in both insect larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Water contact angle (WCA) is used to quantify surface hydrophobicity, with lower values indicating reduced hydrophobicity."</data>
