      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL COMPOUND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A chemical component used in microbial media preparation."&lt;SEP&gt;"KH2PO4 is a potassium phosphate salt used in the preparation of the inorganic salt medium."&lt;SEP&gt;"Another form of potassium phosphate, acting as a buffer in CFBM."&lt;SEP&gt;"KH2PO4 is a chemical compound included in the mineral salt medium to support bacterial growth."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5f1aa99e321e9e3b94552e6c6f8e00f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c808bc1867233246c6ad41186de9452&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3235cc6102d988875f1dda974a56038&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70bab3579af07d0f99a5f948a90fe1e1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;K2HPO4&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL COMPOUND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A chemical component used in microbial media preparation."&lt;SEP&gt;"K2HPO4 (Potassium phosphate) is a chemical compound included in the inorganic salt medium to support microbial growth."&lt;SEP&gt;"K2HPO4 is a potassium phosphate salt used in the preparation of the inorganic salt medium."&lt;SEP&gt;"Potassium phosphate is a buffer component in CFBM."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5f1aa99e321e9e3b94552e6c6f8e00f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3235cc6102d988875f1dda974a56038&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70bab3579af07d0f99a5f948a90fe1e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b42ef7860e1f056d47955d0d13a15cd8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MGSO4&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL REACTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A chemical component used in microbial media preparation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5f1aa99e321e9e3b94552e6c6f8e00f3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NH4NO3&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL COMPOUND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A chemical component used in microbial media preparation."&lt;SEP&gt;"NH4NO3 is ammonium nitrate, a nitrogen source used in the preparation of the inorganic salt medium."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ammonium nitrate supplies nitrogen in CFBM."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5f1aa99e321e9e3b94552e6c6f8e00f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3235cc6102d988875f1dda974a56038&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70bab3579af07d0f99a5f948a90fe1e1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FESO4·7H2O&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL COMPOUND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A chemical component used in microbial media preparation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ferrous sulfate heptahydrate provides iron ions in CFBM."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5f1aa99e321e9e3b94552e6c6f8e00f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3235cc6102d988875f1dda974a56038</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ZNSO4&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL COMPOUND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A chemical component used in microbial media preparation."&lt;SEP&gt;"ZnSO4 is zinc sulfate, a micronutrient added to the mineral salt medium."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5f1aa99e321e9e3b94552e6c6f8e00f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c808bc1867233246c6ad41186de9452</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MNSO4·H2O&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL COMPOUND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A chemical component used in microbial media preparation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Manganese sulfate monohydrate provides manganese ions in CFBM."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5f1aa99e321e9e3b94552e6c6f8e00f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3235cc6102d988875f1dda974a56038</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BACTERIOLOGICAL TRYPTONE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A component of the LB medium used for microbial cultivation."&lt;SEP&gt;"A nutrient-rich substance used in microbial media preparation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacteriological tryptone is a rich nutrient source in the LB and NB media, supporting bacterial proliferation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5f1aa99e321e9e3b94552e6c6f8e00f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6f28f1c36076d1f249dbc4cd67b16f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10004ab6a85cecf4effb74c306df57cf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;YEAST EXTRACT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL COMPONENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A complex organic nutrient in FMM medium providing vitamins, amino acids, and other growth factors."&lt;SEP&gt;"A nutrient-rich substance used in microbial media preparation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Yeast extract is a nutrient-rich substance used in the preparation of LB medium."&lt;SEP&gt;"Yeast extract is included in the LB medium to provide vitamins and other nutrients for bacterial growth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Yeast extract supplies vitamins, minerals, and other nutrients essential for microbial growth."&lt;SEP&gt;"A nutrient added to LB medium to support bacterial culture."&lt;SEP&gt;"A nutrient-rich component added to the LB medium for microbial growth."&lt;SEP&gt;"A nutrient-rich substance used in the preparation of TYE medium."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d3235cc6102d988875f1dda974a56038&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-050a4c71685bf71165985a79f528ed58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3099f2d6fd3abc2f73550f579999b13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a32ea55d79e87933e26b4165db47b1fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10004ab6a85cecf4effb74c306df57cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f1aa99e321e9e3b94552e6c6f8e00f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70bab3579af07d0f99a5f948a90fe1e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6f28f1c36076d1f249dbc4cd67b16f1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PS MPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PS MPs (polystyrene microplastics) are plastic particles that induce oxidative stress in organisms such as larvae and earthworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS microplastics (MPs) are small particles of polystyrene used as a carbon source for bacterial cultures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene microplastics are used as feedstock in the diet for larvae, mixed with bran and jelly powder."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene Microplastics (PS MPs) are tiny plastic particles derived from polystyrene, known for their potential environmental impact."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS MPs refer to polystyrene microplastics with varying molecular weights used in the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS MPs refers to polystyrene microplastics, which were used as a carbon and energy source in the experiment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene microplastics (PS MPs) are polymers that undergo depolymerization during biodegradation by mealworms, resulting in significant reductions in molecular weight parameters such as \(M_{w}\), \(M_{n}\), and \(M_{d}\)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c29fa50fac7d523f43c540627750c823&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcf2bd0dbdce4d7299bfc35487eaf0f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e98fb757cb68ae45626058d9c3a15cb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9af0d95fd5f52d02b9cb33387951963&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67028993c2650049216602d03fb3f786&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5540fc6fe4d3ef0fd986ec36a589c77f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92ea4ca7a83af5c086ae157fb801b326</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JELLY POWDER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Jelly powder is used as an adhesive to mix polystyrene microplastics (PS MPs) with wheat bran in larval diets."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5540fc6fe4d3ef0fd986ec36a589c77f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANNIBAL RATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A measure of the extent to which larvae consume dead bodies of other larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cannibal rate assesses the extent of cannibalism among larvae during the incubation period."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cannibal rate refers to the tendency of larvae to consume each other under certain dietary conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8ee8f544a1849c80a5a1524c4f2674c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5540fc6fe4d3ef0fd986ec36a589c77f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4265fd894f71345b4ef09c26e6adbda5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PUPATION RATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pupation rate evaluates the proportion of larvae that successfully transition to the pupal stage."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pupation rate measures the proportion of larvae that transform into pupae under different dietary conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5540fc6fe4d3ef0fd986ec36a589c77f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e97dc712df43805c553423ceb65cd6b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DEIONIZED WATER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Boiled deionized water is used to dissolve jelly powder for mixing with PS MPs and bran."&lt;SEP&gt;"Deionized water is purified water used as a solvent in preparing various media and solutions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Deionized water is used in washing procedures to ensure purity of PE film samples."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5af82472112cbc9e76b1fd1ac6e8c54e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5540fc6fe4d3ef0fd986ec36a589c77f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70bab3579af07d0f99a5f948a90fe1e1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GLASS BEAKER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A glass beaker is used to prepare the mixture of PS MPs, bran, and jelly powder."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5540fc6fe4d3ef0fd986ec36a589c77f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALUMINUM PAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An aluminum pan is utilized for air-drying the larval diet mixture before feeding."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5540fc6fe4d3ef0fd986ec36a589c77f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMPRESSED AIR FLUSHING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Compressed air flushing is used to cleanse larvae before transferring them to clean containers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5540fc6fe4d3ef0fd986ec36a589c77f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PP CONTAINER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polypropylene (PP) containers are used to hold larvae temporarily for frass collection."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5540fc6fe4d3ef0fd986ec36a589c77f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ABSOLUTE ETHANOL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Absolute ethanol (\(&gt;99.5\%\)) is used to kill larvae prior to DNA extraction for gut microbiome analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ethanol used for sterilization and cleaning of PE particles."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5540fc6fe4d3ef0fd986ec36a589c77f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c6dfb08bb454e8ff642e7975ba7af10</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ETHANOL PRESERVATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ethanol preservation maintains larval samples at \(-80^{\circ} \mathrm{C}\) before DNA extraction."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5540fc6fe4d3ef0fd986ec36a589c77f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TGA ANALYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"TGA analysis (thermogravimetric analysis) evaluates the thermal stability and degradation characteristics of PP foam and frass samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"TGA analysis demonstrates thermal decomposition stages of PS and frass, indicating significant reduction of PS components in the frass."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thermogravimetric analysis (TGA) is employed to study the thermal stability of frass components."&lt;SEP&gt;"TGA analysis demonstrates thermal degradation stages and weight loss patterns of polymers after being metabolized by mealworms, indicating chemical composition changes."&lt;SEP&gt;"TGA analysis is a technique used to study thermal stability and degradation of materials, applied here to analyze PS and PE samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"TGA analysis evaluates thermal properties of PU foam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thermogravimetric analysis used to study weight loss and structural modifications in PU and PU-virgin."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-edd352a71a8bc6e66ece9484f8b59118&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2c62bcfb28547d6b2336f142d27a326&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3d2baf02fdfbafa95ded13de61aaaa1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5540fc6fe4d3ef0fd986ec36a589c77f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb14281b4a095b6c531146d40b5110a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ed721221326657b60aadb09faeeac92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4265fd894f71345b4ef09c26e6adbda5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\( ^{1} \MATHRM{H} \) NMR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL REACTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Proton nuclear magnetic resonance (\( ^{1} \mathrm{H} \) NMR) is used to analyze the molecular structure of frass constituents."&lt;SEP&gt;"Proton nuclear magnetic resonance (\( ^{1} \mathrm{H} \) NMR) is used to characterize the structure of residual PET polymers after degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5540fc6fe4d3ef0fd986ec36a589c77f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c426315f0f412528b9c6fb2a82dff2c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MASS BALANCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mass balance analysis assesses the fate of ingested plastics, providing evidence for mineralization through unaccounted gas losses."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mass balance calculations determine the amount of residual PS in frass to evaluate biodegradation efficiency."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mass balance refers to the principle of tracking material inputs and outputs during biodegradation studies, ensuring accurate quantification of polymer consumption and waste production."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mass balance is the principle of accounting for all material inputs and outputs in an experiment, ensuring accurate measurements."&lt;SEP&gt;"The accounting of all material inputs and outputs in an experiment, crucial for validating degradation claims."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mass balance involves analyzing input and output materials to assess digestion efficiency and waste excretion."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mass balance involves measuring various components like added WC or PE, frass weight, extractable fraction, and accumulated biomass."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mass balance represents the quantitative accounting of material inputs and outputs in a system, such as PE degradation by waxworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mass balance refers to the method of tracking the weight of ingested plastic versus recovered residues and changes in insect weight to assess degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mass balance involves tracking the mass of ingested plastics, egested frass, and residual polymer content."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mass balance refers to the monitoring of plastic removal and digestion efficiency based on the mass of frass and residual plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0cba3b06dd82e87d3b582bc21c475868&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b08485bef3ee3db21e59e159ad4c3e20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e05bc34fccfca5e177064daf8346866&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-681ece0a8beca8b22f3c6aa11a564f63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c84ac252cb9ce906354bda2ad1113aba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-490fdb90ad8a65d35f3c2cd42a8c4c8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f2303f3680e9313daac77bb7e27e7da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5540fc6fe4d3ef0fd986ec36a589c77f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05b7bf66b11c66f02e73a07fb823b8fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c7abab621f928edec1e33d1fe2afd4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b25215becbc007a60f24b86a2d6aaf26</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INCUBATORS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Incubators are devices used to maintain controlled temperature and humidity conditions for breeding mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Incubators maintain controlled temperature and humidity conditions for larval growth experiments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5540fc6fe4d3ef0fd986ec36a589c77f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e96b716e9400e9e77e099de5cca7c548</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TEMPERATURE CONTROL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Temperature control ensures optimal conditions for larval development during experiments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Temperature control involves maintaining a temperature of \(27 \pm 1^{\circ} \mathrm{C}\) during the experiment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5540fc6fe4d3ef0fd986ec36a589c77f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3d2baf02fdfbafa95ded13de61aaaa1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HUMIDITY CONTROL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Humidity control involves maintaining relative humidity at \(80 \pm 3\%\)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Humidity control maintains appropriate moisture levels in incubators for larval experiments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maintaining constant humidity ensures accurate weight measurements during the experiment, avoiding water-related errors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5540fc6fe4d3ef0fd986ec36a589c77f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05b7bf66b11c66f02e73a07fb823b8fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3d2baf02fdfbafa95ded13de61aaaa1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANNIBAL RATE (CR)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cannibal Rate represents the percentage of larvae that have disappeared due to cannibalism, calculated as CR = (N - N_c - N_d) / N × 100%, where N is the initial number of larvae, N_c is the number of live larvae, and N_d is the number of dead larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cannibal rate indicates the percentage of larvae engaging in cannibalism under starvation or other conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c7abab621f928edec1e33d1fe2afd4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92ea4ca7a83af5c086ae157fb801b326</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PUPATION RATE (PR)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LIFE STAGE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pupation Rate measures the percentage of larvae that have transformed into pupae, calculated using PR = N_p / N × 100%, where N_p is the accumulated number of pupae and N is the initial number of larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c7abab621f928edec1e33d1fe2afd4c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DCM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL SOLVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dichloromethane (DCM) is utilized for extracting specific polymers like PLA, LDPE, and PP from the frass residue."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c7abab621f928edec1e33d1fe2afd4c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1,2 DCB&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL SOLVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"1,2 Dichlorobenzene (1,2 DCB) is employed for extracting low-density polyethylene (LDPE) and polypropylene (PP) residues from the frass."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c7abab621f928edec1e33d1fe2afd4c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WATER SOLUBLE FRACTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The water-soluble fraction includes soluble salts and dissolved organic products extracted from the frass using deionized water."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c7abab621f928edec1e33d1fe2afd4c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THF EXTRACTABLE FRACTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"THF extractable fraction measures the PS residue in frass during the degradation process."&lt;SEP&gt;"THF-extractable fraction specifically targets residual polystyrene (PS) in the frass sample, facilitating polymer characterization via techniques like GPC."&lt;SEP&gt;"The THF extractable fraction measures the extent of PS digestion in the frass of Tenebrio molitor larvae over time."&lt;SEP&gt;"The THF extractable fraction refers to the portion of PS in frass that can be extracted using tetrahydrofuran."&lt;SEP&gt;"THF extractable fraction refers to the residual PS found in mealworm frass after ingestion."&lt;SEP&gt;"THF extractable fraction refers to the portion of PVC or frass that dissolves in tetrahydrofuran, used to quantify polymer residues."&lt;SEP&gt;"The THF (tetrahydrofuran) extractable fraction measures the amount of PVC degraded in the mealworm gut."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fb00229bf45a3bd9b8a17e10a1c93d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31b36e69e51416db099951b925beff9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89344d5b5d9debdca45ab8c7c963a585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0c513c586aa89e48e9570525bfc5366&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54049db5a67a6464f459ccc427765140&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c7abab621f928edec1e33d1fe2afd4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92ea4ca7a83af5c086ae157fb801b326</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ULTRASONIC TREATMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ultrasonic treatment is applied to frass samples to enhance water extraction efficiency, improving subsequent filtration and analysis steps."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c7abab621f928edec1e33d1fe2afd4c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VACUUM DRYING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Vacuum drying is utilized to remove moisture from frass samples after various extraction steps, enabling precise weight measurements."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c7abab621f928edec1e33d1fe2afd4c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TEFLON COATED SEPTUM COVER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Teflon-coated septum covers are used to seal glass vials containing extracted fractions, preserving samples for further analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c7abab621f928edec1e33d1fe2afd4c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLY(ETHER SULFONE) (PES) MEMBRANE FILTER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PES membrane filters are used to filter water solutions during frass processing, ensuring separation of soluble components."&lt;SEP&gt;"Poly(ether sulfone) (PES) membrane filter is used to filter THF solutions during the extraction process."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8bb63b06976c3a8e6f2cea85c1ecf518&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c7abab621f928edec1e33d1fe2afd4c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PS REMOVAL EFFICIENCY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PS removal efficiency quantifies the percentage of PS removed from the feedstock by the larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-54049db5a67a6464f459ccc427765140</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NMR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL REACTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"NMR (Nuclear Magnetic Resonance) provides detailed chemical structure information about the plastic residues."&lt;SEP&gt;"NMR (Nuclear Magnetic Resonance) spectroscopy provides detailed information about molecular structure, dynamics, and chemical environment in polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"NMR, or nuclear magnetic resonance, analyzes changes in the end groups of egested polymer at ambient temperature."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nuclear magnetic resonance (NMR) is used to analyze the degradation of PVC by yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"NMR analysis reveals chemical modifications consistent with degradation and partial oxidation of polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nuclear Magnetic Resonance (NMR) spectroscopy identifies chemical modifications in the residual polymer, revealing new peaks associated with alkene bonds and oxygen incorporation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dad389953d78e790a40a9267c5b591c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b7c2ef16f6809388c0c1a87c26bd5c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bd3778dedc6a0463017df9f8d6396eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54049db5a67a6464f459ccc427765140&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05b7bf66b11c66f02e73a07fb823b8fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87427955fe47fc204be31f4d99036055</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KBR PELLET&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
