      <data key="d0">"SOLVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A solvent used for dissolving samples, with a deuterated form allowing for NMR analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chloroform-D is a deuterated solvent used in $^{1}$H NMR analysis to dissolve frass samples for characterization of polymer end products."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chloroform-D is a deuterated solvent with 99.8% purity, used for extracting dried residues for NMR analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chloroform-d is a deuterated solvent used for NMR experiments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chloroform-D is a solvent used for extracting residual PE from frass samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chloroform-D is a solvent used in nuclear magnetic resonance spectroscopy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chloroform-D is a deuterated solvent utilized in NMR spectroscopy to dissolve samples for analysis."</data>
