      <data key="d2">chunk-92ea4ca7a83af5c086ae157fb801b326</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LDPE, PVC, PLA, PET, PP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"These are additional plastics, besides PS, that T. molitor larvae can ingest and digest."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-92ea4ca7a83af5c086ae157fb801b326</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TEMPERATURE (25°C)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Temperature is a critical condition for larval activity and PS degradation experiments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-92ea4ca7a83af5c086ae157fb801b326</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SHAKING (120-180 RPM)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Shaking ensures proper mixing and aeration of cultures during incubation at 25°C."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-92ea4ca7a83af5c086ae157fb801b326</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICROSCOPE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LABORATORY EQUIPMENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A microscope is used to observe morphotypes of bacteria grown in PS-containing media."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-92ea4ca7a83af5c086ae157fb801b326</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLATE STREAKING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Plate streaking is a technique used to obtain pure bacterial cultures on agar plates."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-92ea4ca7a83af5c086ae157fb801b326</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PS FOAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PS Foam (Polystyrene Foam) is a type of plastic consumed by superworms and yellow mealworms, with notable changes in chemical structure after ingestion."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS Foam (Polystyrene Foam) is another type of plastic mentioned as part of the larvae's diet."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS foam (polystyrene foam) is a commercially available material used as feed for mealworms in experiments."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS foam is a type of plastic consumed by mealworms, providing them with energy and carbon for survival."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS foam is one form of polystyrene ingested by T. molitor larvae in experiments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene foam is a type of plastic used in the experiments to evaluate degradation efficiency by mealworms and superworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS Foam is a type of polystyrene used as feed for mealworms, impacting their growth, development, and reproduction."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene foam provided as part of the diet for beetles and juveniles to support their lifecycle."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS foam, or polystyrene foam, is a type of plastic studied for its degradation by insect larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS foam is a type of microplastic used in the experiment, showing higher consumption by larvae compared to PE film."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS Foam refers to polystyrene foam, a type of non-hydrolyzable plastic that undergoes biodegradation through depolymerization by the larvae of T. obscurus."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bdc8398efba587929eebd0a0842f6e69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705bf68703e5d236b2ffabb7ecb3de5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0638e0fe93dc27e678672a164e6088c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b0b175969d87b3be377f65b988d0a52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0014171c7ef07a60c6be3b57e791688c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd3cec3addc1bee202783dff1583ba54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0caad5c42a4b470a8c41ac3fb68c1f64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e96b716e9400e9e77e099de5cca7c548&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cbedc06292e5cf07fbca1958d8587e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d290a6a81802d3048c35d2a2fb1252c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92ea4ca7a83af5c086ae157fb801b326</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MWD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"MWD (molecular weight distribution) indicates the range of molecular weights present in PS residues, shifting to lower values during degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Molecular weight distribution, indicating the range of molecular weights within a polymer sample."&lt;SEP&gt;"Molecular Weight Distribution (MWD) measures the range of molecular weights present in a polymer sample."&lt;SEP&gt;"MWD (molecular weight distribution) refers to the range of molecular weights present in a polymer sample, which shifted towards lower values after LDPE digestion by larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-89344d5b5d9debdca45ab8c7c963a585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-639bb2429f20c4fe3994c4a0d15f3295&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e24cc3865ed97850c3f25795ff514e8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fb9111bd088e1990cde867c6d85cf28</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\(M_{\MATHRM{N}}\)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Number-average molecular weight (\(M_{\mathrm{n}}\)) reflects the average chain length of polymers, showing reduction after digestion by larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"\(M_{\mathrm{n}}\) represents the number-average molecular weight of PS, which decreases significantly during biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b95a108327e39d37d20bdd99db541164&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89344d5b5d9debdca45ab8c7c963a585</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\(M_{\MATHRM{W}}\)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Weight-average molecular weight (\(M_{\mathrm{w}}\)) indicates the weighted average of polymer chains, significantly reduced after digestion."&lt;SEP&gt;"\(M_{\mathrm{w}}\) represents the weight-average molecular weight of PS, also decreasing significantly during biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b95a108327e39d37d20bdd99db541164&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89344d5b5d9debdca45ab8c7c963a585</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RING-BENDING VIBRATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ring-bending vibration corresponds to specific peaks in FTIR spectra, indicating the presence of PS benzene rings."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ring-bending vibration is a characteristic of PS that shows high intensity in the feedstock but weakens in frass samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ring-bending vibration is a characteristic peak in FTIR spectra indicating changes in PS structure during degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ring-bending vibration refers to a specific type of molecular vibration observed in FTIR spectra, indicative of structural changes in PS."</data>
