    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENTAMYCIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ANTIBIOTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An antibiotic that disrupts the ability of mealworms to degrade PS, implicating gut bacteria in this process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gentamycin is a bactericidal antibiotic that inhibits the depolymerization of polystyrene in mealworms, indicating the involvement of gut bacteria in the process."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c343b12adf5bbce5bf80b96909fe66d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f6621e8191c2fc4d28a63e80e5d467e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOLOGICAL DEGRADATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biological degradation encompasses the enzymatic and microbial processes that lead to the breakdown of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biological degradation involves breaking down complex substances like plastics into simpler forms through biological mechanisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biological degradation involves the enzymatic breakdown of complex polymers like polystyrene into simpler compounds for energy or assimilation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biological degradation refers to the breakdown of materials by living organisms, such as the microbial degradation of plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c343b12adf5bbce5bf80b96909fe66d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a31a12c930b59b872c94dda484d0db4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a54f7d9e0a43fb94e2fc35f93656fc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8624d79db8ed1c4488f890a1d0c085a5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIPIDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fatty molecules that incorporate carbon from degraded PS in mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipids are biochemical compounds synthesized by mealworms from the carbon derived from polystyrene degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipids are a group of molecules that include fats and oils. The total lipid content in mealworms decreased significantly depending on the diet."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipids are organic compounds that serve as energy storage molecules and are extracted from sewage sludge and scum for biodiesel production."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipids are organic compounds used as precursors for biodiesel production and are not derived from PE consumption by larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipids are organic molecules found on polyethylene surfaces that may interfere with FTIR analysis results."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipids from mealworms are considered for conversion into biodiesel, with associated greenhouse gas emissions estimated."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipids are biochemical compounds that incorporate $^{13}$C-labeled PS during the biodegradation process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipids are metabolites that were found to have increased relative abundance of DEGs in PS- and CS-fed groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipids are biochemical macromolecules analyzed in the mealworms' organisms to assess the efficiency and benefits of polystyrene biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipids are fats or fat-like substances that store energy and play structural roles in organisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipids are essential nutrients stored in mealworms, used for maintaining vital functions during starvation or while processing plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Total lipids in mealworms were quantified using the Sulfo-Phospho-Vanillin Assay (SPVA)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipids are a class of nutrients serving as an energy reserve in insects."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f7fa795762aa89809d8221dc9dda92fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b08485bef3ee3db21e59e159ad4c3e20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16700b183fc641abfa74ad7fbb0917fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91831340731171413dc4c412a325e034&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eaf1f7b81bc271c665d7776cc3114a92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc88563632a3abf926bf4e4ac16973fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a11793261251544a542146bc9bf0c5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eed90a978852274ead3771418cd60bed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c343b12adf5bbce5bf80b96909fe66d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06a44b308af148551c5b7feef324d88b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6d515521d6d2b72e82154cc544d26cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0ec64a7c629b14bfb6652f1960a337c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8624d79db8ed1c4488f890a1d0c085a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f6621e8191c2fc4d28a63e80e5d467e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;13C-LABELED PS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL REACTION PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"13C-labeled PS is a version of polystyrene enriched with carbon-13 isotopes, used to track carbon flow during decomposition."&lt;SEP&gt;"13C-labeled polystyrene is used in isotopic studies to track the mineralization and incorporation of carbon from polystyrene into lipids."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS labeled with Carbon-13 isotopes used in experiments to trace carbon assimilation in mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c343b12adf5bbce5bf80b96909fe66d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b0b175969d87b3be377f65b988d0a52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33a0a8b02ff930ea552c8902e4d0defd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OXIDATIVE TRANSFORMATIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Oxidative transformations refer to chemical changes induced by oxygen, observed in the functional groups of polystyrene residues after biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c343b12adf5bbce5bf80b96909fe66d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\({ }^{13} \MATHRM{C}\)-LABELED PS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"This refers to polystyrene labeled with carbon-13 isotopes, used in studies to trace its degradation and incorporation into lipids."&lt;SEP&gt;"\({ }^{13} \mathrm{C}\)-labeled PS is a carbon-isotope labeled polystyrene used for tracking degradation processes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-70735757eafccc0f762f21f5d3ac8556&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f6621e8191c2fc4d28a63e80e5d467e</data>
