    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXIGUOBACTERIUM SP.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A specific bacterial strain isolated from mealworms capable of degrading PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exiguobacterium sp. is a bacterium isolated from the digestive tract of Tenebrio molitor larvae that demonstrates the ability to degrade polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exiguobacterium sp. is a bacterial species found in the gut microbiota of insects involved in plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exiguobacterium sp. is a bacterium capable of creating biofilms and degrading polystyrene in the gut of Tenebrio molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exiguobacterium sp. is a bacterium previously identified for its ability to degrade polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2a54f7d9e0a43fb94e2fc35f93656fc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53d382cbd1392dbcf9530428c2eb8584&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cefffe48b3d2ec347f880c77300fc041&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56af57b5211422531c03b0cbcfded1b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f6621e8191c2fc4d28a63e80e5d467e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PS DEGRADATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PS degradation involves the enzymatic breakdown of polystyrene into simpler compounds."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS degradation refers to the breakdown of polystyrene by microbial processes, potentially enhanced by secreted factors from the gut microbiome."&lt;SEP&gt;"The process by which mealworms consume and break down polystyrene into simpler compounds."&lt;SEP&gt;"The degradation of polystyrene, another type of plastic, previously studied in T. obscurus versus T. molitor larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-668212da3bf356132cadb63df6ce09b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22d348f5320f96e129128362b6e0407c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d616d4c3c3199d53c1ae93ebcf3589d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f6621e8191c2fc4d28a63e80e5d467e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GEL PERMEATION CHROMATOGRAPHY (GPC)">
      <data key="d0">CHEMICAL REACTION</data>
      <data key="d1">"A technique employed to measure changes in the molecular weight of PS during its degradation process."&lt;SEP&gt;"A technique used to assess changes in molecular weight of PS during degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gel Permeation Chromatography (GPC) is a technique used to analyze the molecular weight distribution of polymers, revealing differences between Styrofoam and its degradation products in frass."&lt;SEP&gt;GPC is a technique used to quantify molecular weights of residual polymers in the frass samples, indicating depolymerization of plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-be41a05c5e519995f6622e2258511b70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-838d20fb5f3709d303402ea916d8172f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f6621e8191c2fc4d28a63e80e5d467e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOURIER TRANSFORM INFRARED (FTIR) SPECTROSCOPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A method used to identify chemical modifications resulting from PS digestion."&lt;SEP&gt;"A spectroscopic method used to identify chemical modifications in PS residues after digestion by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTIR complements TG analysis by identifying functional groups present in the samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTIR spectroscopy identifies functional groups of PE-MPs before and after digestion."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTIR characterizes chemical modifications in polymer structures and monitors oxidized functional groups in residual PE polymers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-81552b76a273b31cc2bd9ed21ed7a919&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6afbb58ebe9108893daf7e65d59fac39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa33fb34ba06610c290cdfd8a5b4e916&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f6621e8191c2fc4d28a63e80e5d467e</data>
    </node>
