    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENERGY RECOVERY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Energy recovery involves extracting energy from waste materials, often through incineration or other methods."&lt;SEP&gt;"Energy recovery involves extracting energy from waste materials, often through incineration, to reduce landfill usage and generate power."&lt;SEP&gt;"Energy recovery refers to the process by which mealworms derive energy from ingested plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Energy recovery refers to obtaining energy from waste materials, often through incineration."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a11793261251544a542146bc9bf0c5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b0b175969d87b3be377f65b988d0a52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c42631c88da011b836666dae04cfa11a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8624d79db8ed1c4488f890a1d0c085a5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRANDON ET AL.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"RESEARCHER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A research study referenced for comparison, highlighting differences in experimental conditions and results."&lt;SEP&gt;"A research study that reported community shifts in T. molitor fed PE, PS, and bran."&lt;SEP&gt;"A research team that documented the consumption of PE by mealworms, contributing to understanding their plastic-eating behavior."&lt;SEP&gt;"Brandon et al. represents another set of research studies focusing on plastic degradation mechanisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"A study claiming full mass balance during the degradation of PE and PS mixtures by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Researchers who studied the degradation efficiency of plastics by yellow mealworms, providing foundational data for subsequent studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Researchers who documented the biodegradation of PE by T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Brandon et al. studied the carbon mass balance and confirmed the effectiveness of gut bacteria in EPS biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Authors who conducted previous studies on mealworm plastic biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Brandon et al. conducted studies on the biodegradation of plastics by T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Brandon et al. explored the biodegradation of PP polymers by insect larvae, confirming alkene bond formation in frass extracts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Brandon et al. studied the effects of PS diet on T. molitor larvae, including insufficient food supply and toxic effects."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2a214d2b1c90aeb78e6e8562679d4963&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-104d99248e84b2776ff5ca17c285a7bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b08485bef3ee3db21e59e159ad4c3e20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd90c8f9754a78aabdbd7053e1adf90b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b0b175969d87b3be377f65b988d0a52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-260d8c268067de32e5ac98d66ab70a6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4df787efdb36123e3f2a76b5402278ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5dc0ba5d8a1abfb746af0dedb7d575b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a8521d10cd6a04d8ba536be9f9dec8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16328c3c685f35501c3639525e997d2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2d6bcd4d2cc81a978694e417e76747e</data>
    </node>
