    <node id="&quot;ERWINIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Erwinia is a bacterial genus found in the mealworm gut microbiome, indicating variability in bacterial communities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Erwinia is a genus of bacteria that becomes more prevalent in the gut microbiota of mealworms fed PS diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Erwinia is a genus of Gram-negative bacteria, with one species isolated from the adult gut of T. molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Erwinia is another genus of bacteria isolated from the guts of T. molitor larvae, contributing to the microbiota composition."&lt;SEP&gt;"Erwinia is a genus of bacteria closely related to Mixta."</data>
