    <node id="&quot;MOLECULAR WEIGHT DISTRIBUTION (MWD)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"MWD describes the distribution of molecular weights in a polymer sample. Shifts in MWD indicate changes in polymer structure during biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"MWD describes the range of molecular weights present in a polymer sample, indicating structural changes during degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"MWD indicates changes in molecular weights of PS residues, reflecting degradation progress."&lt;SEP&gt;"MWD measures the distribution of molecular weights in a polymer sample, providing insights into PS degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"MWD reflects the distribution of molecular weights in PS feedstock and frass samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Molecular weight distribution characterizes the range of molecular sizes in a polymer sample."&lt;SEP&gt;"Molecular weight distribution describes the range of molecular weights present in a polymer sample, influencing its degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"MWD measures the range of molecular weights within a polymer sample, providing insights into the effects of biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Molecular Weight Distribution (MWD) is a key factor influencing the biodegradability of polymers, including number-averaged (Mn), weight-average (Mw), and size-averaged weight (Mz)."&lt;SEP&gt;"MWD measures the range of molecular weights present in a polymer sample, used here to assess PS degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Molecular Weight Distribution quantifies changes in the size of PS molecules after degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"MWD measures the range of molecular weights in a polymer sample, used in characterizing depolymerization."&lt;SEP&gt;"Molecular Weight Distribution measures the range of molecular weights in LDPE feedstocks and frass, indicating the extent of depolymerization."&lt;SEP&gt;"MWD describes the range of molecular weights present in a polymer sample, influencing its physical and chemical properties."&lt;SEP&gt;"MWD describes the range of molecular weights present in the polymer sample."&lt;SEP&gt;"Molecular weight distribution describes the range of molecular weights within a polymer sample, influencing material properties."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1e45f9527e7b07e945435dae572dc387&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c29fa50fac7d523f43c540627750c823&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cbedc06292e5cf07fbca1958d8587e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0638e0fe93dc27e678672a164e6088c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04683827a8d88bc2fa28ae73ccc0714f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc6b858a4eb57553f5b1ae041e1c7160&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d3b3c7bbc61318a9728caff13ac5b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1679027e80b766e0469f7323db15b497&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9af0d95fd5f52d02b9cb33387951963&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b95a108327e39d37d20bdd99db541164&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67028993c2650049216602d03fb3f786&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b7c2ef16f6809388c0c1a87c26bd5c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc7f923e7edaa7bcfa79c0f7a9896e00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d76783f53d38e8c7423dff747f0413d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1006283f24aba2aa605f9e719f36cf9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f75b58db5211fc7348ccca8206b9bbae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LACTOBACILLACEAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FAMILY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A bacterial family associated with lactic acid production and inositol metabolism."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lactobacillaceae is a bacterial family present in the gut microbiota of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lactobacillaceae is a family of beneficial bacteria enriched in the digestive tract of animals consuming T. molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lactobacillaceae is a bacterial family predominantly found in the bran-fed control group of yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lactobacillaceae is a bacterial family negatively affected by polymer additives."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lactobacillaceae is a family of bacteria whose abundance in the gut microbiota of Tenebrio molitor larvae decreases due to microplastic ingestion."</data>
