    <node id="&quot;EXIGUOBACTERIUM SP. YT2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A bacterial strain isolated from the guts of T. molitor larvae capable of degrading PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"A bacterium isolated from Tenebrio molitor showing high biodegradation capability."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exiguobacterium sp. YT2 is a PS-degrading bacterium isolated from mealworm guts, belonging to Phylum Firmicutes and Class Bacilli."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exiguobacterium sp. YT2 is a bacterium capable of degrading EPS and was first identified in previous studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exiguobacterium sp. YT2 is a bacterium previously identified as an EPS-degrading organism."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exiguobacterium sp. YT2 is a bacterium isolated from the mealworm gut microbiome that degrades polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exiguobacterium sp. YT2 is a PS-degrading strain isolated from mealworms' gut, achieving up to 7.4 ± 0.4% PS degradation after 60 days."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exiguobacterium sp. YT2 is a bacterial strain isolated from yellow mealworm intestines that degrades polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exiguobacterium sp. YT2 is a bacterial strain isolated for its ability to degrade polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c3c4d027474e8769f550ce290c9391ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a52fc2936b4d2a771dbc2d6a37eeb710&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07aae06c64778453da4bda48f5347de5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-939f85d52d9301668deab282264e5fd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0c513c586aa89e48e9570525bfc5366&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dfcb17715cb4e5148b33061c1b6cbf1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e5407936cdb4f49bd5363f782dab563&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dafca19c0156f11127587dba3673503</data>
