    <node id="&quot;ENZYMATIC DEPOLYMERIZATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Enzymatic Depolymerization refers to the process of breaking down polymers into smaller molecules through enzymatic activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzymatic depolymerization is the breakdown of polymers into smaller units using enzymes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzymatic depolymerization refers to the breakdown of plastics like PS by enzymes secreted by microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzymatic depolymerization is the process by which enzymes break down long chains of PS molecules into lower molecular weight substances."</data>
