    <node id="&quot;BIOOXIDATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biooxidation is a biological process where organic materials are oxidized by living organisms, such as in the case of Ecolyte PS polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biooxidation refers to the biological degradation process involving microorganisms breaking down organic materials such as plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"The biological oxidation of substances, such as polymers, leading to their breakdown."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biooxidation refers to the biological oxidation of organic materials, often resulting in their breakdown into simpler compounds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biooxidation is the process by which microorganisms oxidize organic compounds, contributing to the biodegradation of polymers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eada60ee606520104bb515c4896d6b0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a72a9944bcd114b6a3be55ad9b596c77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b27c93b39534612a0492f52ce1f3cd8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a21a8e638d3972014f836efe8aa62e3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf8041a3cdcd6091f6c96b8b67229df2</data>
