      <data key="d1">"FTIR Analysis detects oxygen incorporation in PS during its passage through the mealworm gut, confirming chemical changes."&lt;SEP&gt;"The integration of oxygen into molecular structures, critical for rapid plastic biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oxygen incorporation refers to the addition of oxygen functional groups during the biodegradation process, observed through 1H NMR analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Incorporation of oxygen into the polymer structure is detected through FTIR and NMR analyses, suggesting plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The process by which oxygen atoms are introduced into the LDPE structure during biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
    </node>
