      <data key="d2">chunk-2ee6535da22915c7094098e016b19d80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c84ac252cb9ce906354bda2ad1113aba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2efbc0287662aa64684e4db6a131c3de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89a76f613b36454134940f78fba1c0f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0c513c586aa89e48e9570525bfc5366</data>
      <data key="d1">"Clostridia are hypothesized to play a role in PS depolymerization under anaerobic conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS depolymerization refers to the breakdown of polystyrene into smaller molecules, involving both host enzymes and gut microbiota."&lt;SEP&gt;"Depolymerization of polystyrene (PS) shows similarities to PP depolymerization in terms of gut microbe-dependence."&lt;SEP&gt;"The breakdown of polystyrene (PS) polymers, which is affected by gut microbes and antibiotic treatments."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS depolymerization is the process by which mealworms break down polystyrene polymers into smaller components."</data>
