    <node id="&quot;LIFE CYCLE&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-69679184959639a1ff81c7392cd5cef5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab6b219720db5a6e3384c884c280984c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91831340731171413dc4c412a325e034&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eecad183fc5700f3d7e0a266e293de1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a3d3cf8ea423f7e0f637dddade1bbf1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ff228c7711f94fb27152b187b1fa3eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d1301f6942d17092ef7b22ac40f19f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a7768b61a3d166f2cd01d4e87ac88cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9bd8cf0d5102bbca724e0773be0eeae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81b6237c84f002117fbfe7575d9cdd6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39598f698094d1663ca3438bc143bc90</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Life Cycle of an organism includes all stages from birth to death."&lt;SEP&gt;"The life cycle of an organism encompasses all stages from birth to death; in this case, it relates to the yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The life cycle of plastic-eating waxworms can be influenced by their ability to degrade plastics, affecting their growth and reproduction."&lt;SEP&gt;"The life cycle refers to the series of changes that an organism undergoes from its initial form through reproduction."&lt;SEP&gt;"The life cycle of yellow mealworms involves stages like egg, larva, pupa, and adult beetle."&lt;SEP&gt;"The developmental stages of T. molitor larvae, influenced by dietary nutrients and their ability to complete growth and metamorphosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"The life cycle encompasses the developmental stages of lesser waxworms, including larva, pupa, and adult moth."&lt;SEP&gt;"The life cycle includes stages such as larvae, pupae, moth, and egg, with the lesser waxworm completing all stages even when fed on polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"The life cycle refers to the stages of development from larvae to pupae and eventually moths, which was successfully completed only in worms fed with PE-WC."&lt;SEP&gt;"The life cycle encompasses the stages of development an organism undergoes, which can be affected by external factors like plastic consumption."&lt;SEP&gt;"The life cycle refers to the stages of development an organism goes through, impacted by nutrient availability."</data>
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DEGRADATION COMPOUNDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Degradation compounds include monomers and oligomers formed during the biodegradation process of polystyrene by mealworm larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4f26c2702cadbaabe34c0d0e5cd2ec9f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;H2O&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Water facilitates better hydration and enhances PS consumption in certain diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Water significantly improves the biodegradation of polystyrene monomer and oligomer residues."&lt;SEP&gt;"Water, a dietary component influencing gut microflora composition in T. molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Water, crucial for oxygen availability and overall metabolic activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Water, essential for supporting microbial growth and facilitating both aerobic and anaerobic degradation processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Water is another byproduct of the biodegradation process of plastics into simpler molecules."&lt;SEP&gt;"Water is a chemical compound involved in metabolic processes and may be lost during PE degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Water is a chemical compound used in the sterilization process with a syringe filter."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6e415042ae4079ee5fe96c7105eb534c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c095cc3175666d5093fe411f9a39cb66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3815960770483b9c0a1579ca8442e3a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b25215becbc007a60f24b86a2d6aaf26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9aa972c0f1c2838103f61cd8ae101a8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9578db0f9ed0398705827be5d4ee450&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f26c2702cadbaabe34c0d0e5cd2ec9f</data>
    </node>
