      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A bacterial species identified in the gut microbiome of T. molitor when fed with PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrospira defluvii is a bacterium found in the gut microbiome of T. molitor larvae, potentially aiding in plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrospira defluvii is a bacterial species identified in some studies as abundant in mealworms fed on polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrospira defluvii is an OTU significantly associated with the PS-fed gut microbiome."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8c28d5d503e85e3e6ad15cee35d50e98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2122660fcfebecf752000198a16f222&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f7eff62476fb3de27969b584ac3e605&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14f9f0280098bb86719394a4bd53e5bb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROPIONIBACTERIUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A bacterial genus observed in the gut microbiome of T. molitor when fed with PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Propionibacterium is a genus of bacteria present in the gut microbiome of T. molitor larvae, contributing to plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Propionibacterium is a bacterial genus identified in some studies as dominant in the mealworm gut microbiome."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2122660fcfebecf752000198a16f222&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f7eff62476fb3de27969b584ac3e605&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14f9f0280098bb86719394a4bd53e5bb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;Α-MANNOSIDASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"α-Mannosidase is an enzyme involved in the breakdown of plastics within the gut microbiome of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"α-mannosidase hydrolyzes α-mannosidic linkages, potentially aiding in metabolic processes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2ddf4b13293dd3d8d0887af10fc52c98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f7eff62476fb3de27969b584ac3e605</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;Α-FUCOSIDASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"α-Fucosidase is an enzyme contributing to the degradation of plastics by the gut microbiome of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"α-fucosidase catalyzes the breakdown of fucose-containing compounds."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2ddf4b13293dd3d8d0887af10fc52c98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f7eff62476fb3de27969b584ac3e605</data>
