      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A bacterial genus observed in both Diet 3 and previous studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Clostridium is a bacterial genus known for its potential involvement in styrene degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Clostridium is an anaerobic bacterium stimulated by undigested nutrients in Diet 3."&lt;SEP&gt;"Clostridium is a bacterial genus found in the mealworm gut microbiome, contributing to microbial diversity."&lt;SEP&gt;"A genus of Gram-positive bacteria known for its involvement in fermentation processes and potentially contributing to nitrogen fixation in the gut flora of Tenebrio larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Clostridium is found in T. obscurus larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Clostridium is a genus of anaerobic bacteria found in the posterior gut of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"A bacterial genus with differential abundance between bran and ethylene diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Clostridium is a genus of bacteria identified in the gut microbiota of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Clostridium is a genus of anaerobic bacteria found in the hindgut of mealworms, contributing to the degradation of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Clostridium is a bacterial genus often found in the gut microbiota of mealworms and some species are capable of nitrogen fixation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Clostridium is a genus of bacteria found to participate in nitrogen fixation processes."</data>
