      <data key="d2">chunk-de9904e6f38706256e15c7957f8f0527</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1A-TETRALIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL COMPOUND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A chemical compound identified as a degradation product in the context of styrene oligomers."&lt;SEP&gt;"A tetrahydronaphthalene derivative identified in the insect frass."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2122660fcfebecf752000198a16f222&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de9904e6f38706256e15c7957f8f0527</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1E-TETRALIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL COMPOUND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A tetrahydronaphthalene derivative identified in the insect frass."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-de9904e6f38706256e15c7957f8f0527</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GREGARIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gregaria is a bacterial genus whose presence may be facilitated by water."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-de9904e6f38706256e15c7957f8f0527</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WEISELLA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A bacterial genus linked to Diet 2 conditions in the gut microbiome of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Weisella is a genus of bacteria that may benefit from the presence of water."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2122660fcfebecf752000198a16f222&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de9904e6f38706256e15c7957f8f0527</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIET 1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DIET"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A diet with a bran-to-PS ratio of 4:1 used in the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diet 1 has a bran:PS ratio of 4:1 and shows higher PS residues and lower biodegradation yields."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diet 1 follows previous studies, ensuring comparable results while adjusting feed amounts to prevent larval starvation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diet 1 consists of a bran-to-PS ratio of 4:1 without water, leading to moderate PS degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diet 1 consists of a bran:PS ratio of 4:1 without added water, resulting in higher excretion of PS oligomers and significant depolymerization."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diet 1 consists of bran and PS at a ratio of 4:1 w/w."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diet 1 contains a bran:PS ratio of 4:1 and shows higher moisture content compared to other diets."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6e415042ae4079ee5fe96c7105eb534c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c4244cae75095bda7fb526c3d0c9d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3eb3742a8be739a1146cbf15e6b7ae5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b4ab01931acbc7aa9c77cd03531c57e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de9904e6f38706256e15c7957f8f0527&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6338d56b535220f260826703b0f7229&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-395b01f15fd97b70e2368941120e9a37</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIET 2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DIET"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A diet with a bran-to-PS ratio of 20:1 supplemented with water."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diet 2 contains a high bran:PS ratio (20:1) and water, supporting better hydration and higher PS consumption."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diet 2 incorporates water and an increased bran:PS ratio (20:1) to test its effect on PS degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diet 2 consists of a bran-to-PS ratio of 20:1 with water, resulting in the highest extent of PS degradation among all diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diet 2 consists of a bran:PS ratio of 20:1 with added water (\(\mathrm{H}_{2} \mathrm{O}\)), leading to a lower excretion of PS oligomers compared to other diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diet 2 consists of bran and PS at a ratio of 20:1 w/w with hydration."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diet 2 includes additional water and exhibits the lowest nitrogen frass content and protein content."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6e415042ae4079ee5fe96c7105eb534c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c4244cae75095bda7fb526c3d0c9d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3eb3742a8be739a1146cbf15e6b7ae5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b4ab01931acbc7aa9c77cd03531c57e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de9904e6f38706256e15c7957f8f0527&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6338d56b535220f260826703b0f7229&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-395b01f15fd97b70e2368941120e9a37</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIET 3&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DIET"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A diet with a bran-to-PS ratio of 20:1 without additional water."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diet 3 contains a bran:PS ratio of 20:1 without water, leading to increased protein content and reduced survival rates."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diet 3 uses the same bran:PS ratio (20:1) without water, investigating larval preference for PS consumption."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diet 3 consists of a bran-to-PS ratio of 20:1 without water, showing less PS degradation compared to Diet 2."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diet 3 consists of a bran:PS ratio of 20:1 without added water, showing similar effects as Diet 1 in terms of PS depolymerization."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diet 3 consists of bran and PS at a ratio of 20:1 w/w without hydration."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diet 3 shows the highest statistically significant value for average larval weight."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6e415042ae4079ee5fe96c7105eb534c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c4244cae75095bda7fb526c3d0c9d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3eb3742a8be739a1146cbf15e6b7ae5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b4ab01931acbc7aa9c77cd03531c57e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de9904e6f38706256e15c7957f8f0527&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6338d56b535220f260826703b0f7229&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-395b01f15fd97b70e2368941120e9a37</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SACCHAROMYCETACEAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FAMILY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Saccharomycetaceae is a family of yeasts that includes Candida species."&lt;SEP&gt;"Saccharomycetaceae is a fungal family found predominantly in outer-fed group."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a91a3c11281861b559c31c3107c72e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de9904e6f38706256e15c7957f8f0527</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PS MONOMERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL COMPOUND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polystyrene monomers analyzed in the insect biomass."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-de9904e6f38706256e15c7957f8f0527</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PS OLIGOMERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PS oligomers are intermediate breakdown products of polystyrene observed in insect frass."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene oligomers identified in the insect biomass."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS oligomers are small molecular fragments resulting from the breakdown of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS oligomers are smaller polymer units resulting from the degradation of PS, identified through NMR analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6e415042ae4079ee5fe96c7105eb534c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3eb3742a8be739a1146cbf15e6b7ae5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de9904e6f38706256e15c7957f8f0527&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e25fe1af3bede4605e7b94d457c9634</data>
    </node>
