      <data key="d2">chunk-f2122660fcfebecf752000198a16f222</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LACTOBACILLUS LACTIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A bacterial species positively correlated with Diet 2 conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2122660fcfebecf752000198a16f222</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GREGARINA POLY-MORPHA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PARASITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A protozoan parasite associated with Diet 2 conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2122660fcfebecf752000198a16f222</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PS POLYMER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PS polymer belongs to amorphous plastics and is more susceptible to depolymerization compared to PE polymers in the mealworm gut."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene polymer analyzed for degradation in mealworm frass samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene, a polymer whose degradation products are studied in relation to gut microbiota."&lt;SEP&gt;"The PS polymer undergoes significant biodegradation in the intestines of insects, showing a reduction in molecular weights and an increase in polydispersity index (PDI), indicating broad depolymerization."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-92b1e432ea4bee0f332d7303188e6de7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-beb3c133fa4d5851f0feff55507c6874&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1536c14bdcd58ae9dabf3a49f6724cd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2122660fcfebecf752000198a16f222</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IRGAFOS 168&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A chemical additive whose degradation product is 2,4-di-tert butyl phenol."&lt;SEP&gt;"Irgafos 168 (tris(2,4-di-tert-butylphenyl) phosphate) is an antioxidant additive commonly used in food contact materials."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-57edc76f6646a41c4845d94baa519950&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2122660fcfebecf752000198a16f222</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STREPTOCOCCUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A bacterial genus present in the gut microbiome of T. molitor when fed with PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Streptococcus is a bacterial genus identified in the mealworm gut microbiome, playing a role in microbial community composition."&lt;SEP&gt;"Streptococcus exhibited high abundance in PS- and CS-fed larvae, associated with lignocellulose or plastic degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eaf1f7b81bc271c665d7776cc3114a92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2122660fcfebecf752000198a16f222&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14f9f0280098bb86719394a4bd53e5bb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HAEMOPHILUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A bacterial genus identified in the gut microbiome of T. molitor when fed with PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Haemophilus is a bacterial genus found in the mealworm gut microbiome, contributing to microbial diversity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2122660fcfebecf752000198a16f222&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14f9f0280098bb86719394a4bd53e5bb</data>
