    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RELATIVE HUMIDITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Humidity is controlled at 55 ± 5% in the climate-controlled room to ensure consistent experimental conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Relative humidity was maintained at 60 ± 5% during the experiment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Humidity levels were controlled in specific experiments to assess their impact on LDPE degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Relative humidity is maintained at 100% to optimize conditions for microbial activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"The experiment maintained a relative humidity of +45% during the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"Relative humidity is the measure of moisture content in the air, maintained during incubation of plates."&lt;SEP&gt;"Relative humidity represents the moisture content in the air during the experiment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Relative humidity measures the amount of moisture in the air and is controlled in experiments to optimize mealworm growth and PS degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Relative humidity impacts the rearing environment and affects the growth and survival of mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2a214d2b1c90aeb78e6e8562679d4963&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d7e47d05442ff6cd0cf042db9974f2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16700b183fc641abfa74ad7fbb0917fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53dd546535ef4247004faab1fa475889&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70735757eafccc0f762f21f5d3ac8556&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84f576487c8d473c1524eb1141730a12&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d575c206eb616c4c970fd48fe3349247&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d01d291012bd548fc067e250ec39fba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5710c6b3eb755779f706360ec72260e</data>
    </node>
