    </node>
    <node id="&quot;YAKPSL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENETIC CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"YAKPsl is a specific retrotransposon identified in the variegated cutworm Peridroma saucia, potentially influencing genomic stability."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c038f908eb10a4a5715fb9cff3e05527</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LONG-CHAIN FATTY ACIDS&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-e155a60beeedb5736450fdc1ffa4699e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e8cdca8afb1d7153fba5e3c11b1f669&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f26c2702cadbaabe34c0d0e5cd2ec9f</data>
      <data key="d1">"Long-chain fatty acids are products of the β-oxidation process, derived from the breakdown of complex substrates."&lt;SEP&gt;"Long-chain fatty acids such as undecanoic acid, oleic acid, and hexadecanoic acid are detected in the frass or intestinal samples of PS-fed larvae during degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The presence of long-chain fatty acids correlates with the metabolic stress experienced by insects when fed polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
