      <data key="d1">"Polystyrene Degradation is the process by which mealworms metabolize and break down PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene degradation is the process by which microorganisms break down polystyrene into simpler compounds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene degradation refers to the breakdown of polystyrene into smaller components through thermal or chemical processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Enterobacteriaceae family, specifically Erwinia olea, was more abundant in T. molitor fed with PS, suggesting its potential role in polystyrene degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene degradation refers to the microbial processes involved in breaking down polystyrene plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene degradation involves the breakdown of polystyrene by microorganisms, such as bacteria and fungi."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene degradation involves the breakdown of polystyrene by microorganisms through mechanisms such as cell adhesion, growth, and decomposition."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene degradation involves the chemical breakdown of polystyrene polymers into smaller molecules."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene degradation is the process by which polystyrene is broken down into smaller compounds, often through microbial or enzymatic action."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene degradation refers to the breakdown of polystyrene, possibly occurring in mealworm guts."</data>
