    <node id="&quot;BIOREMEDIATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bioremediation involves using living organisms to degrade environmental pollutants, such as plastics, into less toxic forms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The process of using living organisms, such as worms, to clean up environmental pollutants like plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bioremediation is the use of microorganisms or their enzymes to remove or neutralize pollutants from the environment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bioremediation refers to the process of using biological agents, such as microorganisms or enzymes, to degrade environmental pollutants, specifically plastic waste in this context."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bioremediation is the use of biological agents, such as microorganisms, to remove or neutralize pollutants from contaminated environments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bioremediation involves using microorganisms, such as bacteria, to degrade environmental pollutants like nanoplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bioremediation is the use of microorganisms to remove or neutralize pollutants."&lt;SEP&gt;"The use of biological agents like microbes to clean up polluted environments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bioremediation involves using living organisms to reduce or remove pollutants, including microplastics, from the environment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b08485bef3ee3db21e59e159ad4c3e20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8518832c2d3e002c8acf71795e306144&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a889b716cac361e6e04405777075076&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbf098ec253f99187f3c98d5d0589f7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fd138e047a780efd715a5ab4701b58c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32e10966ec80ea585746639b6be7e04e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d642e5476221b3ea202c68d7e6070b96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcc545cfe4d6e8e04c3698a149d4101a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59dab99372af01b60a073d8eac17870f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BREVIBACILLUS BORSTELENSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Brevibacillus borstelensis is a bacterium associated with soil that contributes to the biodegradation of plastic waste."&lt;SEP&gt;"Brevibacillus borstelensis is a bacterium capable of producing enzymes that break down plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Brevibacillus borstelensis is a thermophilic bacterium capable of degrading polyethylene, contributing to the biodegradation of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Brevibacillus borstelensis is a bacterium capable of degrading polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Brevibacillus borstelensis is a thermophilic bacterium that can degrade polyethylene, according to research findings."&lt;SEP&gt;"Brevibacillus borstelensis is a thermophilic bacterium involved in the biodegradation of polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Brevibacillus borstelensis is a thermophilic bacterium capable of degrading polyethylene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ca3745cb01a4209e2eae28914dde3b52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8518832c2d3e002c8acf71795e306144&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecf2c478d08c7bc8e491f630aa289881&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-648afbc8ee82935d4026f5915152491c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bb7b0638c9c59e134df0491b542efdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bd104d06a1ede06701ecfa96bccc2c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5251cc2ed910c3785b2c7242b7cbc11e</data>
