    <node id="&quot;PYROLYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pyrolysis is a chemical reaction where plastics decompose under high temperatures in anaerobic conditions, producing biofuel."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pyrolysis is a thermal decomposition process used to convert plastic waste into fuel or other valuable products."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pyrolysis is a thermal decomposition process occurring at elevated temperatures in the absence of oxygen, applied to convert materials like plastics into bio-oil."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pyrolysis is a thermal decomposition process where organic materials break down into combustible gases and biochar."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pyrolysis is a thermal decomposition process used to mitigate microplastics in sewage sludge by altering their chemical structure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pyrolysis is a thermal decomposition process used to mitigate microplastics in waste materials."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-069f8447676509ffdd0028e9c05fb9ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e3058d086d89f1ce9baa29cbc29bb48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8518832c2d3e002c8acf71795e306144&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfbd751517e11b1b4052961a01008cbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bb7b0638c9c59e134df0491b542efdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d642e5476221b3ea202c68d7e6070b96</data>
