    <node id="&quot;POLYMER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polymer is a scientific journal focused on the study of polymers, including their synthesis, properties, and applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polymers are large molecules composed of repeating structural units, such as PS, PVC, and LDPE."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polymers are materials with specific chemical bonds that influence the biodegradation process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polymers are large molecules made up of repeating structural units, often used in plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polymer, specifically poly(ethylene terephthalate), serves as a substrate for bacterial degradation and assimilation."</data>
