      <data key="d1">"Pseudomonas stutzeri is a bacterial species that contributes to NPS degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas stutzeri is a bacterium involved in the biodegradation of plastic waste."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas stutzeri is a bacterium known for its ability to efficiently degrade high-molecular-weight polyethylene glycols."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas stutzeri is another bacterial strain identified for its potential in degrading polystyrene nanoplastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5251cc2ed910c3785b2c7242b7cbc11e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbf098ec253f99187f3c98d5d0589f7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55bdcf1b4859e82ab15050837ab539dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bb7b0638c9c59e134df0491b542efdf</data>
