      <data key="d1">"A species of beetle studied for its benzoquinone production and associated genetic mechanisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tribolium confusum is a beetle species known for its ability to breach certain types of packaging films."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tribolium confusum is a beetle species that can penetrate certain types of packaging films."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tribolium confusum is a beetle whose larvae contribute to the degradation of plastics like PE and PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tribolium confusum, or confused flour beetle larvae, have been studied for their potential to biodegrade plastic waste."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tribolium confusum, also called the confused flour beetle, is an insect whose adults can damage packaging films."</data>
