      <data key="d1">"Another polyurethane material (PU2) distinguished by high levels of chlorine (Cl) and phosphorus (P)."&lt;SEP&gt;"PU2 (polyurethane 2) is another variant of polyurethane plastic tested in the experiment."&lt;SEP&gt;"PU2 (polyurethane foam 2) is another type of plastic foam with a greater number of edges initially. Post-digestion, these edges are significantly smoothed."&lt;SEP&gt;"PU2 is a type of rigid polyurethane (commercial insulation foam) utilized by mealworms with 59.0% efficiency."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-065b846c5f5f23f64023995cdb21c3db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4b03ca32b0efbf0ca6a3c8761c0d03d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fc215d3abb38f76b4ee0d22c4f1eb11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78cd8d4684fa9e0519635dba9f124a08</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MASS REDUCTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mass reduction measures the extent to which a polymer's mass decreases during biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mass reduction refers to the decrease in weight of PET polymers during biodegradation by Tenebrio molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mass reduction refers to the decrease in weight of plastics due to their consumption and degradation by mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-78cd8d4684fa9e0519635dba9f124a08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-411368ddb6a73777c1dd4c683bd389c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1679027e80b766e0469f7323db15b497</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MORPHOLOGICAL PARAMETERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Morphological parameters include measurements like mass and length of mealworm larvae, reflecting changes induced by plastic consumption."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-78cd8d4684fa9e0519635dba9f124a08</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;P&lt;0.05&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"STATISTICAL SIGNIFICANCE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"P&lt;0.05 indicates statistically significant differences in biochemical measures between experimental and control groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"p&lt;0.05 indicates the threshold for statistical significance, marking whether observed differences are likely not due to chance."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3d47d39d364c5c66ef3fc32ef741ca63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78cd8d4684fa9e0519635dba9f124a08</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;N=3&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EXPERIMENTAL DESIGN"</data>
      <data key="d1">"n=3 specifies the number of biological replications performed to ensure reliability of the experimental results."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-78cd8d4684fa9e0519635dba9f124a08</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CUMULATIVE LOSS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cumulative loss refers to the progressive reduction in plastic mass over time as mealworms consume them."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-78cd8d4684fa9e0519635dba9f124a08</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INITIAL MASS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Initial mass denotes the starting weight of plastics at the beginning of the experiment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-78cd8d4684fa9e0519635dba9f124a08</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FINAL MASS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Final mass indicates the remaining weight of plastics after being consumed by mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-78cd8d4684fa9e0519635dba9f124a08</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UTILIZATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Utilization measures the percentage of plastic consumed and processed by mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-78cd8d4684fa9e0519635dba9f124a08</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PERCENTAGE LOSS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Percentage loss quantifies the extent of plastic degradation expressed as a percentage of the initial mass."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-78cd8d4684fa9e0519635dba9f124a08</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LENGTH OF 1 LARVAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The length of one larva measured in centimeters, with variations observed across different plastic types."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-065b846c5f5f23f64023995cdb21c3db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MASS OF 1 ADULT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The mass of one adult measured in grams, showing differences between various plastic types."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-065b846c5f5f23f64023995cdb21c3db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LENGTH OF 1 ADULT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The length of one adult measured in centimeters, indicating significant variations depending on the plastic type."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-065b846c5f5f23f64023995cdb21c3db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ELEMENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Br is bromine, an element found in non-trace amounts in PS samples, often added as flame retardants."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bromine is an element found in high concentration in PS."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-065b846c5f5f23f64023995cdb21c3db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-119b3f144b4ec234392cca17031bd7a9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ca is calcium, present in plastics like PU1, serving as a filler and reinforcement agent."&lt;SEP&gt;"Calcium is present in substantial quantities in PU1 and PE."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ca represents calcium content in the chemical composition of frass."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-110013d54a5fd492446b1fe049a60fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-065b846c5f5f23f64023995cdb21c3db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-119b3f144b4ec234392cca17031bd7a9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Al is aluminum, present in PU1, possibly due to the use of Al-based fillers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aluminum is detected in PU1 and PE."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aluminum is present in trace amounts in PS and PE, with higher concentrations in PU1."&lt;SEP&gt;"Al represents aluminum content in the chemical composition of frass."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-110013d54a5fd492446b1fe049a60fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-065b846c5f5f23f64023995cdb21c3db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-119b3f144b4ec234392cca17031bd7a9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ELEMENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Silicon is identified in PU1."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-065b846c5f5f23f64023995cdb21c3db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ELEMENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chlorine is abundant in PU2 and present in smaller amounts in other plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cl is chlorine, found in PU1 and PU2, potentially linked to green pigments or antimicrobial agents."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-065b846c5f5f23f64023995cdb21c3db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-119b3f144b4ec234392cca17031bd7a9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;P&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ELEMENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"P is phosphorus, found in higher concentrations in PU2, likely due to the use of chlorinated alkyl phosphates as flame retardants."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phosphorus is notably found in PU2."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-065b846c5f5f23f64023995cdb21c3db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-119b3f144b4ec234392cca17031bd7a9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HF&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ELEMENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hafnium is detected in trace amounts in both PS and PE."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hf is hafnium, an exotic element found in trace amounts in PS and PE samples, possibly from contamination during production."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-065b846c5f5f23f64023995cdb21c3db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-119b3f144b4ec234392cca17031bd7a9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ELEMENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Barium was not detected in any of the investigated plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-065b846c5f5f23f64023995cdb21c3db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chromium is found in trace amounts across PS, PU1, and PE, with slightly higher levels in PU1."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cr represents chromium content in the chemical composition of frass."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-110013d54a5fd492446b1fe049a60fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-065b846c5f5f23f64023995cdb21c3db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CU&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Copper is detected in all investigated plastics except PU2, with the highest concentration in PU1."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cu represents copper content in the chemical composition of frass."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-110013d54a5fd492446b1fe049a60fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-065b846c5f5f23f64023995cdb21c3db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fe represents iron content in the chemical composition of frass."&lt;SEP&gt;"Iron is present in trace amounts in PS, PU1, and PE, with minimal presence in PU2."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-110013d54a5fd492446b1fe049a60fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-065b846c5f5f23f64023995cdb21c3db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;K&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"K represents potassium content in the chemical composition of frass."&lt;SEP&gt;"Potassium is identified in PS, PU2, and PE, with varying concentrations across these materials."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-110013d54a5fd492446b1fe049a60fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-065b846c5f5f23f64023995cdb21c3db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ni represents nickel content in the chemical composition of frass."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nickel is only found in trace amounts in PU1."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-110013d54a5fd492446b1fe049a60fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-065b846c5f5f23f64023995cdb21c3db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;S&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ELEMENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sulfur is present in PS and PU1, with lower levels in PE."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-065b846c5f5f23f64023995cdb21c3db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CORN FLOUR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRITIONAL COMPONENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A dietary component provided to larvae as part of their codiet along with gentamicin sulfate."&lt;SEP&gt;"Corn Flour is the normal diet for T. obscurus larvae, offering necessary nutrients and carbon for growth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Corn flour is a dietary component used in feeding T. obscurus larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Corn flour is a nutritional supplement provided as a codiet to enhance PS consumption and larval growth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Corn flour is another dietary supplement that improves the PS utilization rate of T. obscurus mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Corn flour is used as a dietary component for mealworms in experimental groups to compare with polystyrene-fed groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"Corn flour is mentioned as the preferred food source for T. obscurus larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Corn flour is another dietary supplement used in the study to assess its impact on polystyrene degradation by larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e340b8704554cdc28486ac37e78ab0fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d5a9fbe4803ded646c6a5e4d23ca93a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8bb63b06976c3a8e6f2cea85c1ecf518&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-568e2e90ce0d3bbb4e21079f4252f5de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df147b253e29abfa812d060407051e45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85c9587b55f24a8ae5ba6b478dbb98e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa33fb34ba06610c290cdfd8a5b4e916&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4b03ca32b0efbf0ca6a3c8761c0d03d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MITOCHONDRIAL DNA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENETIC CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mitochondrial DNA in T. molitor was studied for epigenetic modifications caused by PU as a sole source of feed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mitochondrial DNA is investigated for epigenetic modifications in T. molitor caused by PU consumption."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f4b03ca32b0efbf0ca6a3c8761c0d03d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fc215d3abb38f76b4ee0d22c4f1eb11</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PU&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PU (Polyurethane) is a product utilized by mealworms in the study, with different types such as PU1 (kitchen sponge) and PU2 (commercial insulation foam), each having distinct chemical compositions and properties."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyurethane foam used in the experiment, subjected to degradation by microorganisms and enzymes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyurethane is a plastic type included in the study, with focus on its ingestion and degradation by larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"PU (Polyurethane) is a type of plastic degraded by unclassified Enterobacteriaceae."&lt;SEP&gt;"PU (Polyurethane) is a type of plastic consumed by yellow mealworms, showing significant changes in Mn, Mw, and Mz during biodegradation via broad depolymerization."&lt;SEP&gt;"PU (polyurethane) is a foam plastic fed to yellow mealworms in one of the experimental groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"PU likely refers to Polyurethane, a versatile product used in foams, coatings, and adhesives."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d2c62bcfb28547d6b2336f142d27a326&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7043eb8aa4221f396a5c65fb6493bd41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fc215d3abb38f76b4ee0d22c4f1eb11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d0e4cb4324bc684ebb2ca6136c04ad0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0014171c7ef07a60c6be3b57e791688c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a91a3c11281861b559c31c3107c72e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-444b8acd02a76616457012e1ac0db23b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALIPHATIC ALCOXY-GROUPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNCTIONAL GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Aliphatic alcoxy-groups are functional groups present in PU1, contributing to its softness."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4fc215d3abb38f76b4ee0d22c4f1eb11</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AROMATIC ALKOXY-GROUPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNCTIONAL GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Aromatic alkoxy-groups are functional groups present in PU2, contributing to its rigidity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4fc215d3abb38f76b4ee0d22c4f1eb11</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYOLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A chemical component of polyester plastics containing C=O bonds, contributing to the enrichment of fungal colonies in the gut."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyols are compounds used in the formulation of both soft and rigid foams, differing in molecular weight."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3e34d58a20a707b35e8fcd5658ba2924&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fc215d3abb38f76b4ee0d22c4f1eb11</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIISOCYANATES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Diisocyanates are compounds used in the formulation of soft foams."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4fc215d3abb38f76b4ee0d22c4f1eb11</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRISOCYANATES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Trisocyanates are compounds used in the formulation of rigid foams."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4fc215d3abb38f76b4ee0d22c4f1eb11</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICROBIOMES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Microbiomes inhabiting the intestines of mealworm larvae influence the degree of plastic utilization."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4fc215d3abb38f76b4ee0d22c4f1eb11</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPECIFIC CONSUMPTION RATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Specific consumption rate measures the amount of plastic consumed per day per larva, varying based on the type of plastic and supplemental feeds."&lt;SEP&gt;"The specific consumption rate measures how much polymer Tenebrio molitor larvae consume per unit time."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eb14281b4a095b6c531146d40b5110a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fc215d3abb38f76b4ee0d22c4f1eb11</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VIDEO S1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"OBSERVATIONAL DATA"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Video S1 provides visual evidence of the experimental setup, highlighting the early appearance of pupae during the study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4fc215d3abb38f76b4ee0d22c4f1eb11</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TABLE 4&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DATA REPRESENTATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Table 4 summarizes the specific consumption rates of various plastics by mealworms, comparing results from this study with those reported in the literature."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4fc215d3abb38f76b4ee0d22c4f1eb11</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PUPAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pupae are a developmental stage of insects that emerge quickly during the experiment, impacting the biodegradation process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pupae represent a life stage of mealworms where they stop actively consuming plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pupae refer to the developmental stage of superworms after they stop consuming Styrofoam and before emerging as adult beetles."&lt;SEP&gt;"The intermediate stage in insect development, significant for metamorphosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pupae refer to the developmental stage of T. molitor where weight significantly influences fecundity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pupae represent the transitional stage between larvae and imago in the mealworm's life cycle."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pupae represent the stage between larvae and adult insects, further reared separately to the adult stage."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1ead6f17ad517015b638608c5bfe6852&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98d7ae4d155085781614411da5564816&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd3cec3addc1bee202783dff1583ba54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eed90a978852274ead3771418cd60bed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a54e547b0e77432a65a8a9804c44c5d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be41a05c5e519995f6622e2258511b70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32f340b7166025be3c56178a94ae480d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENETIC DIFFERENCES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENETIC CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Genetic differences among mealworm populations can significantly impact their plastic consumption rates."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a54e547b0e77432a65a8a9804c44c5d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXPANDED PS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A variant of Polystyrene, expanded PS, was tested and showed different effects on the weight of mealworm larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a54e547b0e77432a65a8a9804c44c5d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MASS CHANGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mass change in mealworm larvae is a key indicator used to evaluate the effect of diet, including plastics, on their growth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mass change in mealworms reflects their growth or decline depending on the type of plastic consumed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mass change reflects fluctuations in mealworm weight due to plastic consumption and digestion."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mass change reflects the alteration in mealworm weight due to plastic consumption or lack of proper nutrition."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ff201df58dec460c49cd31920c29f11a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a54e547b0e77432a65a8a9804c44c5d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53f87a406d4812c07e783e6cbfc09606&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b387da8298c55673284dca93ea82fc9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;58 DAYS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LIFE STAGE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The duration of the experiment (58 days) provides a standardized timeframe for measuring plastic consumption and larval development."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a54e547b0e77432a65a8a9804c44c5d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1 KG OF EACH WASTE PLASTIC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"This represents the target amount of plastic waste intended to be consumed by mealworms within the experimental period."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a54e547b0e77432a65a8a9804c44c5d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;K, CL, P, S, CA, ZN, FE, CU&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MINERAL COMPONENTS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"These elements represent the major mineral components found in mealworm larvae after the experiment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-119b3f144b4ec234392cca17031bd7a9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;P. AERUGINOSA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"P. aeruginosa is a bacterium isolated from the gut of Zophobas mor, contributing to the biodegradation of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"P. aeruginosa is a bacterium isolated from the gut of Zophobas morio insect that contributes to the biodegradation of plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-119b3f144b4ec234392cca17031bd7a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98d7ae4d155085781614411da5564816</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEXABROMOCYCLODODECANE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL COMPOUND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hexabromocyclododecane is a brominated flame retardant commonly added to polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-119b3f144b4ec234392cca17031bd7a9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CACO₃&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL COMPOUND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CaCO₃, or calcium carbonate, is used as a filler in plastics like PU1 to enhance strength."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-119b3f144b4ec234392cca17031bd7a9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WOLLASTONITE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MINERAL"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Wollastonite (CaSiO₃) is a silicate mineral sometimes added to plastics for reinforcement and improved flame retardancy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-119b3f144b4ec234392cca17031bd7a9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHLORINATED/BROMINATED PHTHALOCYANINE COMPOUNDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL COMPOUND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"These compounds are pigments added to plastics, contributing to coloration and potentially affecting biodegradability."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-119b3f144b4ec234392cca17031bd7a9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRICLOSAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Triclosan is a compound whose toxicity is potentiated by microplastics in marine environments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Triclosan is an antimicrobial agent sometimes added to plastics, impacting microbial activity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-119b3f144b4ec234392cca17031bd7a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5cbd81fc528c18f42514a2a74d4921e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHLORINATED ALKYL PHOSPHATES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL COMPOUND"</data>
