    <node id="&quot;OXYGEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Controlled oxygen levels were maintained in certain experiments to observe their effect on LDPE degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oxygen concentration is maintained at atmospheric levels to support microbial activity in the fermenter."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oxygen content increases during the biodegradation process, indicating oxidative changes in plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oxygen is a chemical element essential for the degradation of EPS through oxidation processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oxygen is a chemical element whose presence increased on the surface of polystyrene after incubation with strain YT2."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oxygen is a critical factor in determining the conditions under which bacteria degrade plastics, influencing aerobic and anaerobic processes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eafea2357c59ac6712f4d9ab41ac5d14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a214d2b1c90aeb78e6e8562679d4963&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3c4d027474e8769f550ce290c9391ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16700b183fc641abfa74ad7fbb0917fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06ba9ca61fb4f42582bbf7bd00ff0005&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98d7ae4d155085781614411da5564816</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADULT INSECTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LIFE STAGE"</data>
