    <node id="&quot;PSEUDOMONAS AERUGINOSA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A bacterium capable of degrading crude oil and producing rhamnolipids that accelerate hydrocarbon degradation. Found in the gut microbiome of PS-degrading mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"A bacterium that produces rhamnolipid biosurfactants, which enhance the bioavailability of hydrocarbons for bioremediation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas aeruginosa is a bacterium capable of degrading various types of plastics, isolated from superworm gut extracts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas aeruginosa is a bacterial strain isolated for its biodegradable ability."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas aeruginosa is a bacterial species capable of breaking down polystyrene (PS) and previously isolated from the gut of mealworm larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas aeruginosa is a bacterial species known for its enzymatic activities and ability to degrade NPS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas aeruginosa is a bacterium involved in the microbiome study associated with Tenebrio molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas aeruginosa is a soil bacterium capable of degrading plastic waste including PS foam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas aeruginosa is a bacterium capable of degrading polyethylene."</data>
