    <node id="&quot;DRAGON FRUIT CACTI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PLANT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dragon fruit cacti (Hylocereus undatus) are hardy plants used as an indicator species in this study. Superworm frass supports superior growth compared to mealworm frass."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dragon fruit cacti (Hylocereus undatus) are plants used in this study to test the efficacy of worm frass as a growth-supporting fertilizer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dragon fruit cacti are plants used in the study to evaluate the effectiveness of superworm and mealworm frass on growth."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-44565f26e7290c5eb0f26935608a5f16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-078b6698be699eb7105b7cffadf709af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32e10966ec80ea585746639b6be7e04e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUCROSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"COMPOUND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sucrose is a common sugar that can be metabolized by various bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sucrose is a disaccharide sugar that serves as an energy source for microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sucrose is a food additive used in the study to increase polystyrene consumption rates by worms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sucrose is a nutrient that significantly increased PS consumption in mealworms and had a notable effect on superworms' PS consumption."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sucrose is a sugar additive that enhances the consumption of polystyrene by both mealworms and superworms significantly."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sucrose is used as a carbon source in the Carbon-Free Basal Agar media for comparison in the acid production assay."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sucrose is a disaccharide that BIT-26T cannot utilize for acid production."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sucrose is mixed with ammonium sulfate to form a powdered working standard for calibration."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-55bdcf1b4859e82ab15050837ab539dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d043948723ae25a365e297c98300be3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44565f26e7290c5eb0f26935608a5f16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32e10966ec80ea585746639b6be7e04e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01bf9080cbf55e62c0b26d0e054bd1fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e37da2fbe64f85c50c36da45006f4c23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12ceb4368e146509caa737d9534ce3c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-014b72d0a2657cbc89c4dee5f2b32bba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHOSPHORUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Phosphorus is a mineral critical for energy transfer and metabolic processes in waxworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phosphorus is an essential mineral found in yellow mealworm larvae that contributes to their nutritional value."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phosphorus is an essential nutrient absent in Styrofoam but necessary for mealworm growth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phosphorus is an essential nutrient found in worm frass, supporting plant development."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phosphorus is part of the NPK fertilizer components and is present in worm frass."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phosphorus plays a key role in energy metabolism and structural components in organisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phosphorus is an essential nutrient lacking in PP but provided by WB for larval development."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2359b10600f30376fe077f5e942cc999&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab6b219720db5a6e3384c884c280984c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd3092744be0c66dad5833977dedd913&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32e10966ec80ea585746639b6be7e04e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1769c4becf46c99994cb7ced2bffda1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b25215becbc007a60f24b86a2d6aaf26</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POTASSIUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A cation determined and quantified using commercial standards."&lt;SEP&gt;"Potassium is a cation measured in frass from Tenebrio molitor, involved in biochemical processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Potassium is an essential nutrient found in worm frass, aiding in plant health."&lt;SEP&gt;"Potassium is part of the NPK fertilizer components and is present in worm frass."&lt;SEP&gt;"Potassium is a mineral necessary for the physiological functions of waxworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Potassium is a vital nutrient that supports physiological functions in lesser waxworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Potassium is another essential nutrient provided by WB, missing in PP."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-92b1e432ea4bee0f332d7303188e6de7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab6b219720db5a6e3384c884c280984c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd3092744be0c66dad5833977dedd913&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5922f60fcd06ac6ffa27018026871346&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32e10966ec80ea585746639b6be7e04e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b25215becbc007a60f24b86a2d6aaf26</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMMENSAL GUT BACTERIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Commensal gut bacteria in mealworms play a role in enabling the metabolism and mineralization of polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-32e10966ec80ea585746639b6be7e04e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ZERO-WASTE CIRCULAR ECONOMY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ECOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A system designed to minimize waste and make the most of resources, aiming for sustainable practices."&lt;SEP&gt;"A zero-waste circular economy aims to minimize waste and make the most of resources, where worms degrade plastic and their frass supports plant growth."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-44565f26e7290c5eb0f26935608a5f16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32e10966ec80ea585746639b6be7e04e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NPK FERTILIZERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"NPK fertilizers are traditional fertilizers containing nitrogen, phosphorus, and potassium, which can be substituted by worm frass."&lt;SEP&gt;"NPK fertilizers provide essential nutrients like nitrogen, phosphorus, and potassium to crops."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b79a227bc8e127f6b71fd2edb0e650a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32e10966ec80ea585746639b6be7e04e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLACK SOLDIER FLY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Black Soldier Fly (BSF) is a type of insect larva used in the study to evaluate the impact of plastic exposure on insect metabolism."&lt;SEP&gt;"Black soldier flies are insects whose frass has been shown to support plant growth, similar to mealworm and superworm frass."&lt;SEP&gt;"Black soldier fly is an insect whose frass (excrement) can be used as organic fertilizer for crops like maize."&lt;SEP&gt;"The black soldier fly (Hermetia illucens) has unique head morphology and mouthparts adapted for specific functions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-394b3365ffb36d05dca2ef06bf74e462&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d40b7debb6497167fa1aec874ebce45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b79a227bc8e127f6b71fd2edb0e650a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32e10966ec80ea585746639b6be7e04e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MAIZE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PLANT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Maize is a crop that benefits from nitrogen supplied through black soldier fly frass fertilizer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maize is a crop that has been demonstrated to grow using black soldier fly frass as fertilizer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b79a227bc8e127f6b71fd2edb0e650a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32e10966ec80ea585746639b6be7e04e</data>
