    </node>
    <node id="&quot;XRD SPECTRA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"XRD spectra analysis shows the structural changes in polymers before and after being metabolized by mealworms, indicating transformations in their crystalline structures."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7ed721221326657b60aadb09faeeac92</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARBONYL GROUP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNCTIONAL GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Carbonyl groups appear in the frass collected from mealworms from Tai'an and Shenzhen, indicating oxidation of hydrocarbon chains."&lt;SEP&gt;"Functional group identified through chemical shifts in NMR spectra, associated with carbon-oxygen double bonds."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3ab754d1dc0a02ee3f869d2b082a710e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ed721221326657b60aadb09faeeac92</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;C=O STRETCHING VIBRATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL BOND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A chemical reaction involving the stretching of C=O bonds, indicating the presence of carbonyl groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"C=O stretching vibration bands appear in the frass collected from mealworms, indicating the formation of carbonyl groups."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4e50d86c5a0ab8e4188ede9ae519d241&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ed721221326657b60aadb09faeeac92</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;C–O STRETCHING VIBRATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL BOND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A chemical reaction involving the stretching of C–O bonds, indicating the presence of ether or ester groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"C–O stretching vibration bands appear in the frass, signifying the presence of carbonyl groups and structural changes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4e50d86c5a0ab8e4188ede9ae519d241&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ed721221326657b60aadb09faeeac92</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;O–H STRETCHING VIBRATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL BOND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A chemical reaction involving the stretching of O–H bonds, indicating the presence of hydroxyl groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"O–H stretching vibration bands are observed in the frass from Guangzhou mealworms fed with PVC, indicating water formation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4e50d86c5a0ab8e4188ede9ae519d241&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ed721221326657b60aadb09faeeac92</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CH₂ SHEAR VIBRATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL BOND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A chemical reaction involving the shear vibration of CH₂ bonds, indicating specific molecular configurations."&lt;SEP&gt;"CH₂ shear vibration bands disappear in the frass from Guangzhou mealworms, suggesting molecular structure changes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4e50d86c5a0ab8e4188ede9ae519d241&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ed721221326657b60aadb09faeeac92</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CH₂ PLANE SWING VIBRATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL BOND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CH₂ plane swing vibration bands disappear in the frass, further supporting molecular structure changes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7ed721221326657b60aadb09faeeac92</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CH₂ AND CH STRETCHING VIBRATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL REACTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A chemical reaction involving the stretching of CH₂ and CH bonds, indicating the presence of alkane or alkene groups."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4e50d86c5a0ab8e4188ede9ae519d241</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;C–CL STRETCHING VIBRATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL REACTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A chemical reaction involving the stretching of C–Cl bonds, indicating the presence of chlorinated compounds."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4e50d86c5a0ab8e4188ede9ae519d241</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DECHLORINATION&quot;">
