    <node id="&quot;METAGENOMIC ANALYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Metagenomic analysis involves studying genetic material recovered directly from environmental samples to understand microbial diversity and function."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metagenomic analysis involves studying genetic material recovered directly from environmental samples, providing insights into microbial communities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metagenomic analysis is a technique used to study genetic material recovered directly from environmental samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metagenomic analysis involves studying genetic material recovered directly from environmental samples, providing insights into microbial communities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7734a37a076c4f934de059042daf10cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-648afbc8ee82935d4026f5915152491c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3667703f7416ebab666e65b375dd8582&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc6c2706bd609f920aa61d5ef2310db6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-827853316f7304c444884dc82f757802</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STYRENE DEGRADATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Styrene degradation involves microbial processes that break down styrene into simpler compounds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Styrene degradation is a biological process involved in xenobiotic bio-degradation, enriched in both PS- and CS-fed groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"Styrene degradation is a biological process involving the breakdown of styrene by microorganisms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7734a37a076c4f934de059042daf10cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eaf1f7b81bc271c665d7776cc3114a92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4af956dbe737dee68ab6b9834fe2fcc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HOMEOSTASIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Homeostasis describes the stable internal environment maintained by organisms despite external changes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Homeostasis refers to the maintenance of internal stability and balance within an organism."&lt;SEP&gt;"Homeostasis refers to the stable state maintained by organisms or systems, crucial for symbiotic relationships."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maintenance of stable internal conditions in mealworms, influenced by PS biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7734a37a076c4f934de059042daf10cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0d2f43eebe2309fba46c5335d76df56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77a9d70651c9f13362e4c1e3ce10eab0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f71fddc259d51158d5c79f38bf41523f</data>
    </node>
