    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYSTYRENE DIGESTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polystyrene digestion involves the enzymatic and microbial processes that break down polystyrene within the digestive system of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene digestion refers to the enzymatic breakdown of polystyrene by Tenebrio molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"The breakdown of polystyrene by gut microbiota, involving both aerobic and anaerobic processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene digestion refers to the enzymatic breakdown of polystyrene by microorganisms within insect larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene digestion is the process by which organisms like mealworms break down polystyrene into simpler compounds."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dc31a0931fceb1446bc6ec4d0c587f7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc744f6fa5a9ea876a0423d37eedfc87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-550dde13ffd2abcf536dd87f7d4c1b40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5ea4395a1eb1886507c72cdf33db169&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84297b844ec01d2f58756b669806fd62</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENVIRONMENTAL CHANGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ECOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Environmental change encompasses alterations in environmental conditions that can influence ecosystems and organisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environmental change refers to alterations in the natural environment, which can influence the composition and function of gut microbiota in organisms like mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environmental change refers to alterations in natural environments, affecting ecosystems and their inhabitants."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environmental change encompasses variations in environmental conditions that can affect ecosystems and the organisms within them."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bc744f6fa5a9ea876a0423d37eedfc87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eaf641df5c55c7ff41895611514cdd22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-827853316f7304c444884dc82f757802&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf7769e197cb664b8d9e41a4c93eec50</data>
    </node>
