      <data key="d0">"ECOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Soil invertebrates are organisms living in soil ecosystems, some of which have been shown to use plastics as food sources."&lt;SEP&gt;"Soil invertebrates contribute to the breakdown of organic matter in soil ecosystems."&lt;SEP&gt;"Soil invertebrates include earthworms, isopods, millipedes, slugs, and snails tested for their ability to degrade polystyrene."</data>
