      <data key="d2">chunk-c42631c88da011b836666dae04cfa11a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SIZE-AVERAGE MOLECULAR WEIGHT (M&lt;SUB&gt;Z&lt;/SUB&gt;)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Size-average molecular weight measures the average mass of molecules based on their size distribution and decreases during biodegradation processes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c42631c88da011b836666dae04cfa11a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOURIER TRANSFORM INFRARED SPECTROSCOPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A technique used to analyze chemical changes in polyethylene films, indicating oxidation during microbial degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fourier transform infrared spectroscopy is a technique used to confirm the formation of new oxygen-containing functional groups in the frass produced by Tenebrio molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fourier transform infrared spectroscopy (FT-IR) is a technique used to obtain an infrared spectrum of absorption or emission of a solid, liquid, or gas."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fourier transform infrared spectroscopy (FTIR) is a technique used to analyze changes in functional groups of materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTIR is a technique used to obtain an infrared spectrum of absorption or emission of a solid, liquid, or gas."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-aa3bd7c611ad935dba56fd3d7300cbc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f79f3fee16e3f983c9f04a66e4d50760&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3aaf626f7d7f62d0cee4a0e5efafeb69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-567c36cf69b624a7ec0d891d3bd15163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c42631c88da011b836666dae04cfa11a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THERMOGRAVIMETRIC ANALYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Thermogravimetric analysis (TGA) measures weight changes in materials as a function of temperature."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thermogravimetric analysis is a method used to study changes in physical properties and chemical modifications in the frass produced by Tenebrio molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thermogravimetric analysis (TGA) studies weight changes in materials as a function of temperature."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f79f3fee16e3f983c9f04a66e4d50760&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3aaf626f7d7f62d0cee4a0e5efafeb69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c42631c88da011b836666dae04cfa11a</data>
    </node>
