      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Low-Density Polyethylene (PE-1) is a specific type of LDPE with a weight-average molecular weight of 130.6 kDa that undergoes broad depolymerization during biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c42631c88da011b836666dae04cfa11a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOW-DENSITY POLYETHYLENE (PE-2)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Low-Density Polyethylene (PE-2) is another specific type of LDPE with a weight-average molecular weight of 288.7 kDa that undergoes limited extent depolymerization during biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c42631c88da011b836666dae04cfa11a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHYSICAL PROPERTY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL FEATURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Physical property refers to any measurable property of an object or system that can be observed without changing the substance's composition, such as changes in texture or structure observed during biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c42631c88da011b836666dae04cfa11a</data>
    </node>
