    <node id="&quot;CONTACT ANGLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Contact angle is a measure of hydrophobicity used in contact angle analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Contact angle is a measure of surface wetting ability, used to quantify the hydrophobicity of substances."&lt;SEP&gt;"Contact angle measures the wettability of a material's surface, indicating hydrophilic or hydrophobic characteristics."&lt;SEP&gt;"The contact angle measures the degree of hydrophilicity or hydrophobicity of a surface, indicating microbial colonization potential."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-361c5d4ba2e879627f4eb7fc4011ee3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-668212da3bf356132cadb63df6ce09b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-902ed6a67c601276c5dbf43c35dd824f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41635122b30ee45048cc885b38fff6ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PS FILM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PS film is a form of polystyrene used as a substrate for microbial degradation studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS film is a substrate used in contact angle analysis to test hydrophobicity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene film used as a substrate for microbial degradation experiments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene film used as a substrate for microbial biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS film is a material that undergoes degradation by the bacterial strains WJ2020 and WJ2025, leading to changes in its physical and chemical properties."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS film refers to the polystyrene film used in experiments to determine degradation ability of bacterial strains."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS film is a material used in experiments to study the oxidation and degradation effects of bacterial strains."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS film is a polymer film used as a carbon source for bacterial growth and biodegradation studies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-939f85d52d9301668deab282264e5fd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e6fd56772ef66691cf6f1c613ba42e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe29ef34ad1e5ab11c4ec7f5270fa94d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-668212da3bf356132cadb63df6ce09b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-345c72af5aa26d5c4e06d7df5d8a1c85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eba752cb179633f5dd054ee7c9ee2cba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f91980be083a0bf5b52d43a640e9d787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eda80cb027c8107defa00011d491b002</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICROBIAL RESPIRATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Microbial respiration refers to the metabolic process where microorganisms use organic substrates, such as plastics, for energy production."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbial respiration refers to the process by which gut microbiota produce CO2 as a result of metabolic activity, measured here in the context of PS degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a8b07ee5dc7a7af59a93d03311efe60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-902ed6a67c601276c5dbf43c35dd824f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUPERNATANT FRACTIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Supernatant fractions are metabolites secreted by mealworms, specifically analyzed for their molecular weight and hydrophobicity properties."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-902ed6a67c601276c5dbf43c35dd824f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EMULSIFYING AGENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An emulsifying agent is a compound secreted by T. molitor that helps mix immiscible substances like water and oil, enhancing PS degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"An emulsifying agent is a compound secreted by the mealworm or its gut microbiome that aids in the breakdown of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"An emulsifying agent is a substance that facilitates the mixing of immiscible liquids, such as water and oil, enhancing the bioavailability of hydrophobic substrates."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a8b07ee5dc7a7af59a93d03311efe60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eba752cb179633f5dd054ee7c9ee2cba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-902ed6a67c601276c5dbf43c35dd824f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STATISTICAL SIGNIFICANCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Statistical significance indicates whether observed differences or relationships are likely not due to chance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Statistical significance was used to analyze differences in the total content of proteins, sugars, and lipids among mealworms fed with various PS species."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a11793261251544a542146bc9bf0c5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-902ed6a67c601276c5dbf43c35dd824f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANTIBIOTIC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ANTIBIOTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A mixture of five antibiotics was used to suppress gut microbes in T. molitor larvae to study the role of host enzymes in PET depolymerization."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibiotics are substances used to inhibit or kill bacteria, applied here to study their effects on larval gut microbiota and plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibiotics are substances used to suppress gut microbiota in experiments to study their role in polystyrene degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibiotics are used to suppress gut microbiota, demonstrating their role in polystyrene degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibiotics were used in some experimental conditions to assess their impact on emulsifying agent production and PS degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibiotics are substances used to treat infections by killing or inhibiting the growth of microorganisms, here affecting larval gut microbiota."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibiotics are substances used to suppress microbial growth, affecting the biodegradation process differently depending on the polymer type."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibiotics are used to suppress gut microbes, demonstrating the host's ability to degrade PET independently."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e155a60beeedb5736450fdc1ffa4699e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69679184959639a1ff81c7392cd5cef5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79c11bccb4ef9bd152bdae9b5c2c5c8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c84ac252cb9ce906354bda2ad1113aba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-411368ddb6a73777c1dd4c683bd389c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-497648a1cf8e41fac896250ae1eebbb1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-902ed6a67c601276c5dbf43c35dd824f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4304c39ef3427872131caf77e7cdb438</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TWEEN-80&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"SURFACTANT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tween-80 is a known surfactant used as a reference for comparing the emulsification activity of mealworm-produced agents."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-902ed6a67c601276c5dbf43c35dd824f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLASTIC FILM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Plastic film is used as a substrate in experiments to evaluate the hydrophobicity and emulsification activity of supernatant fractions."</data>
