    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOAVAILABILITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bioavailability describes how easily a substance can be accessed and utilized by living organisms, impacting the efficiency of biodegradation processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bioavailability describes the extent to which a substance can be absorbed or utilized by organisms, here referring to the accessibility of PS for microbial degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bioavailability describes the extent to which a substance, such as polystyrene, can be absorbed and utilized by living organisms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9bc3253e8d41785f994d1c6fcc2b6c47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c16f995987af72f86486559556052e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-902ed6a67c601276c5dbf43c35dd824f</data>
    </node>
