    <node id="&quot;NON-HYDROLYZABLE PLASTICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Non-Hydrolyzable Plastics are a category of plastics resistant to hydrolysis, making them difficult to degrade."&lt;SEP&gt;"Non-hydrolyzable plastics refer to a class of synthetic materials resistant to chemical breakdown, requiring alternative degradation methods."&lt;SEP&gt;"Non-hydrolyzable plastics are a focus of interdisciplinary research regarding bio-oxidation processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Non-hydrolyzable plastics like PE, PS, and LDPE are resistant to degradation but can be processed by certain insect larvae."</data>
