      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A Bacterial Consortium is a group of bacteria working together to achieve specific functions, such as degrading plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"A bacterial consortium refers to a community of bacteria working together, offering an alternative solution for overcoming challenges in PE degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Bacterial Consortium refers to a group of bacteria working together, isolated from soil for the degradation of polyurethane."&lt;SEP&gt;"A bacterial consortium enriched from the gut of Tenebrio molitor larvae is responsible for degrading polyvinyl chloride."</data>
