      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Greater wax moth larvae (Galleria Mellonella) are known for their ability to degrade polyethylene and other plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Greater wax moth larvae are insects whose homogenate is tested for LDPE degradation capability."&lt;SEP&gt;"Greater wax moth larvae (Galleria mellonella) have demonstrated potential in degrading polyethylene and polystyrene through their gut microbiome."&lt;SEP&gt;"Greater wax moth larvae refer to Galleria mellonella, an insect whose intestinal microbiota includes PS-degrading bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Greater wax moth larvae (Galleria mellonella) demonstrate the ability to fully digest polystyrene microplastics without reliance on gut microbiota."</data>
