      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Serratia is a genus of bacteria able to degrade bioplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Serratia is enriched in the gut of PS-fed larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Serratia is strongly associated with polyethylene diets in greater wax moth larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Serratia is a genus of bacteria identified in the core gut microbiome of greater wax moths."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-188daf7716cd1d683a79562bf4d6ab90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-323c02b97d9365a25761a155d358b17a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81f09d7c1a5d91a7a0b4766ca0e47f56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e5407936cdb4f49bd5363f782dab563</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLY-CAPROLACTONE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Poly-caprolactone (PCL) is a biodegradable plastic degraded by microorganisms in soil, water, and compost."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-188daf7716cd1d683a79562bf4d6ab90</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RHYZOPERTHA DOMINICA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rhyzopertha dominica is a species of beetle associated with infesting stored grains and packaging materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rhyzopertha dominica, commonly known as the lesser grain borer, is an insect capable of consuming plastic materials."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3351564dbd6a0ee6a8b97f6687378ffc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-188daf7716cd1d683a79562bf4d6ab90</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PSP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PSP (Polystyrene used for packaging purposes) is more favorable and frequently attacked by mealworms compared to raw polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"PSp is a type of plastic material studied for its susceptibility to larval biting and chewing."&lt;SEP&gt;"PSp represents food package polystyrene, demonstrating notable mass loss during the experiment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-188daf7716cd1d683a79562bf4d6ab90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d47d39d364c5c66ef3fc32ef741ca63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41635122b30ee45048cc885b38fff6ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GPPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"GPPS (General Purpose Polystyrene) is a type of polystyrene used in many products."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-188daf7716cd1d683a79562bf4d6ab90</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NGS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"NGS (Next-Generation Sequencing) is a technique used to analyze the gut microbiome diversity in Tenebrio molitor larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-188daf7716cd1d683a79562bf4d6ab90</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOPLASTIC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bioplastics are environmentally friendly plastics that degrade naturally into water and CO2."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-188daf7716cd1d683a79562bf4d6ab90</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TOXIC COMPOUNDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TOXIN"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Toxic Compounds are harmful substances produced during the degradation of PU Foam, contributing to metabolic stress in mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Toxic compounds in polystyrene have an impact on human health problems and ecosystem changes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-188daf7716cd1d683a79562bf4d6ab90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2338bb97657d74ab5d8a444849037692</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BACTERIOME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The bacteriome is a large symbiotic organ formed by aggregating microorganisms, which plays a critical role in insect digestion."&lt;SEP&gt;"The bacteriome is a large symbiotic organ where microorganisms aggregate in the guts, body cavities, or cells of insects."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-96c2e7d253d2108b0ed94be7f2dc7466&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-188daf7716cd1d683a79562bf4d6ab90</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PBSA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PBSA (Bionolle 3020MD) is a bioplastic polymer used in experiments to assess bacterial degradation abilities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-96c2e7d253d2108b0ed94be7f2dc7466</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PCL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PCL is a bioplastic polymer that was identified as degradable by certain bacterial strains."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-96c2e7d253d2108b0ed94be7f2dc7466</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIGESTIVE PROCESS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The digestive process involves microorganisms breaking down food materials, providing essential nutrients and aiding in detoxification within the host insects."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-96c2e7d253d2108b0ed94be7f2dc7466</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIPID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lipids are a significant energy reserve in insects. The highest lipid content was found in control mealworms fed oatmeal."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipids are extracted from the dried mealworm bodies using chloroform for biochemical analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipids are organic molecules studied in the context of changes in T. molitor bodies based on feeding type."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipids are organic molecules that include fats and fat-like substances. In this study, the total lipid content in mealworms decreased significantly when fed polystyrene materials, indicating starvation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Total lipid content in mealworm homogenates was analyzed using chloroform: methanol and vanillin reagent."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipids are organic compounds that serve as energy sources and structural components in living organisms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-56c8b21b1eaba7633b49cea16714ddc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40407fe311340b08da856202f38b459c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14f9f0280098bb86719394a4bd53e5bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0491f3e96c1d355b8431b9d74868f63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96c2e7d253d2108b0ed94be7f2dc7466&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36b964b1825429cad2c7d13c1ea8827e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FEEDING TYPE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Feeding type refers to the diet provided to mealworms during experiments, which includes various types of polystyrene and controls."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-96c2e7d253d2108b0ed94be7f2dc7466</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STARVATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Starvation is a biological process where organisms experience a lack of available energy, leading to physiological responses such as decreased growth and survival."&lt;SEP&gt;"Starvation is a biological process where organisms experience insufficient food intake, leading to physiological adaptations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Starvation is a biological process where organisms utilize stored fat reserves to survive periods without food."&lt;SEP&gt;"Starvation is a physiological state where organisms experience reduced nutrient intake, affecting their metabolic processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Starvation refers to the condition where mealworms are deprived of food to assess changes in their gut microbiome."&lt;SEP&gt;"Starvation refers to the condition where mealworms were not fed any food, serving as a comparison group for nutrient analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Starvation refers to the condition where organisms lack sufficient food, leading to changes in nutrient levels."&lt;SEP&gt;"Starvation refers to the condition where organisms lack sufficient nutrients. It significantly impacts lipid, carbohydrate, and protein levels in mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Starvation refers to a period without food, potentially reducing fat content in larvae as noted in some studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Starvation represents a condition where mealworms were not fed any food."&lt;SEP&gt;"Starvation refers to the physiological condition where mealworms lack sufficient food, leading to changes in nutrient utilization and energy reserves."&lt;SEP&gt;"Starvation is a condition where organisms utilize stored proteins and fats as energy sources."&lt;SEP&gt;"Starvation refers to a diet condition where larvae are deprived of sufficient nutrients, leading to decreased scaled reserve density and affecting somatic maintenance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Starvation refers to conditions where larvae receive no food, affecting their growth and survival."&lt;SEP&gt;"Starvation refers to the state where an organism lacks sufficient food, affecting its energy reserves."&lt;SEP&gt;"Starvation represents a feeding condition where larvae receive no food, leading to reduced survival rates."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3891caf14683493be3d8709ced467492&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91831340731171413dc4c412a325e034&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eee7e44e4c15567a057d7d295d240211&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc88563632a3abf926bf4e4ac16973fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14f9f0280098bb86719394a4bd53e5bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41635122b30ee45048cc885b38fff6ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9af0d95fd5f52d02b9cb33387951963&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a11793261251544a542146bc9bf0c5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5740f0973ff804cae61f6fc12f3e3753&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96c2e7d253d2108b0ed94be7f2dc7466&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0491f3e96c1d355b8431b9d74868f63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a97d5b092508f2e837932274d6b3282&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a170da66288c73388872b8a43fa51e33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f71fddc259d51158d5c79f38bf41523f</data>
    </node>
