    <node id="&quot;PROTEINS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Proteins are biochemical macromolecules analyzed in the mealworms' organisms to evaluate the effectiveness of polystyrene biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Proteins are essential nutrients required for growth, which are lacking in Styrofoam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Proteins are macromolecules essential for various biological functions, and their levels were analyzed in mealworms fed with different PS species."&lt;SEP&gt;"Proteins can also interfere with FTIR analysis, leading to potential misinterpretation of results."&lt;SEP&gt;"Proteins are macromolecules essential for growth and development, absent in polystyrene but present in wheat flour."&lt;SEP&gt;"Proteins are essential nutrients, positively correlated with the PS diet in PCA analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Proteins are essential growth nutrients lacking in PET but present in whole bran, impacting larval weight gain."&lt;SEP&gt;"Proteins are macromolecules found in yeast that support the growth and development of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Proteins are macromolecules that degrade over a broad range of temperatures, contributing to the thermal transitions observed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Proteins are essential nutrients that positively influence larval growth when included in the feed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Proteins are macromolecules present in the body biomass digested by starvation mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5318125e74217718b470b7721d1d6365&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69679184959639a1ff81c7392cd5cef5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b08485bef3ee3db21e59e159ad4c3e20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ee6535da22915c7094098e016b19d80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3eb3742a8be739a1146cbf15e6b7ae5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0e30f29e9016acae216566f53e60cea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a11793261251544a542146bc9bf0c5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1769c4becf46c99994cb7ced2bffda1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06a44b308af148551c5b7feef324d88b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32f340b7166025be3c56178a94ae480d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-531058c4540bd4e6a50d141db01d4d11</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUGARS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sugars are biochemical components analyzed in the mealworms' organisms to determine the impact of polystyrene digestion on their metabolism."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sugars are metabolites that play a critical role in sustaining organs, especially the nervous system. Their levels were significantly different in mealworms fed various polystyrene materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sugars represent carbohydrates that serve as an energy source. Their content was measured in mealworms under different feeding conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06a44b308af148551c5b7feef324d88b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2281f98bcfd555a703fd86232dfa42fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a11793261251544a542146bc9bf0c5dd</data>
    </node>
