      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mealworms are insect larvae used in experiments to test the degradability of plastics and their nutritional effects."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a11793261251544a542146bc9bf0c5dd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MASS CHANGES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mass changes refer to the weight fluctuations observed in mealworms over time, influenced by the type of food consumed."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a11793261251544a542146bc9bf0c5dd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WETTING ANGLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The wetting angle measures the wettability of a solid by a liquid, which was assessed for different types of polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a11793261251544a542146bc9bf0c5dd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MELT FLOW RATIO (MFR)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"MFR characterizes differences in the molecular structure of materials and was evaluated for various polystyrene types."&lt;SEP&gt;"MFR is a measure characterizing polystyrene materials, used to assess their properties."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06a44b308af148551c5b7feef324d88b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a11793261251544a542146bc9bf0c5dd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GLOSS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gloss indicates the surface shine or luster of materials, and it was measured for different polystyrene types."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gloss refers to the surface shininess of materials, influencing their susceptibility to larval biting."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gloss is a measure used to characterize the surface properties of polystyrene materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gloss refers to the surface reflectivity of materials, measured alongside hardness for PS and PSr."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06a44b308af148551c5b7feef324d88b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d47d39d364c5c66ef3fc32ef741ca63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a11793261251544a542146bc9bf0c5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41635122b30ee45048cc885b38fff6ea</data>
    </node>
