      <data key="d2">chunk-a11793261251544a542146bc9bf0c5dd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIODEGRADABLE ACTIVITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biodegradable activity refers to the ability of microorganisms to break down plastic materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodegradable activity refers to the ability of microorganisms to break down plastics into simpler substances."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3891caf14683493be3d8709ced467492&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41635122b30ee45048cc885b38fff6ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PSR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROGRAM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PSR is an internal program of the University of Siena supporting the research."&lt;SEP&gt;"PSr is a plastic material characterized by higher hardness and lower susceptibility to larval biting."&lt;SEP&gt;"PSr is a recycled variant of polystyrene, exhibiting particular hardness, gloss, and significant mass loss during the experiment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3d47d39d364c5c66ef3fc32ef741ca63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59453e4c878e72ac6985a08043cdf126&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41635122b30ee45048cc885b38fff6ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MFR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"MFR (Melt Flow Rate) indicates the flow rate of a polymer when melted, affecting the ease of chewing and biting."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-41635122b30ee45048cc885b38fff6ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRIGLYCERIDE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LIPID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Triglyceride is a form of stored fat that serves as an important energy source in insects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Triglycerides are the primary form of stored energy in insects, which are broken down during starvation to release fatty acids for energy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Triglycerides are the main constituents of animal fats and vegetable oils, playing a role in gut lipid metabolism."&lt;SEP&gt;"Triglycerides are a form of stored energy in insects, broken down into fatty acids during starvation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Triglyceride is a type of lipid that serves as an energy reserve in insects and its level correlates with the duration of the starvation period."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2281f98bcfd555a703fd86232dfa42fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc88563632a3abf926bf4e4ac16973fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14f9f0280098bb86719394a4bd53e5bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41635122b30ee45048cc885b38fff6ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95142a3f585446bd848eeedadd1ab713</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FATTY ACID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fatty acid is a nutrient measured in live larvae after experiments, showing variation across diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fatty acids are a key component of lipids and serve as an energy source during malnutrition. The oxidation of fatty acids stored as triglycerides is crucial for insects during starvation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fatty acids are metabolites involved in energy reserves and biological processes during PET degradation in T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fatty acids are components of lipids that may be affected by exposure to plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fatty acids are crucial components of mealworm nutrition, identified in previous studies analyzing mealworm gut contents."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a38885f67ed46b97bb84086f575fd43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41b8c7f0b790b0289a7683fde0eca126&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14f9f0280098bb86719394a4bd53e5bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b387da8298c55673284dca93ea82fc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a24fcfbc571e8620a1fc59b215b42e56</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TREHALOSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Trehalose is a disaccharide that serves as an energy source and stress protectant in organisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Trehalose is the main carbohydrate found in insect bodies and plays a crucial role in maintaining organ function, especially in the nervous system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Trehalose is a metabolite involved in biosynthesis processes that help organisms respond to abiotic stresses."&lt;SEP&gt;"Trehalose is a metabolite synthesized in response to abiotic stresses."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1d40b7debb6497167fa1aec874ebce45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a81144d30653377d6d90e26c4497eb0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14f9f0280098bb86719394a4bd53e5bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-915331bc1ae85fe139629eaebc4042cd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GLUCONEOGENESIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gluconeogenesis is a metabolic pathway that results in the generation of glucose from non-carbohydrate precursors, such as amino acids."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gluconeogenesis is the metabolic pathway that results in the generation of glucose from non-carbohydrate precursors like proteins."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-14f9f0280098bb86719394a4bd53e5bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0491f3e96c1d355b8431b9d74868f63</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PAENIBACILLUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Paenibacillus is a bacterial genus detected in the mealworm gut microbiome, contributing to its microbial diversity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Paenibacillus is a genus of bacteria found in landfill sediments that can decompose micro-sized polyethylene efficiently."&lt;SEP&gt;"Paenibacillus is another genus of bacteria found dominantly in landfill sediments, capable of efficiently decomposing micro-sized PE."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7367fc6115c08ae427a6e9e91eaa1de3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6eb7955dc484d5f656e1be7b406abb3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14f9f0280098bb86719394a4bd53e5bb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LACTOBACILLUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A genus of beneficial bacteria significantly associated with the PE + bran diet compared to other diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lactobacillus is a bacterial genus identified in the mealworm gut microbiome, contributing to its microbial diversity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lactobacillus is a dominant genus in the guts of yellow mealworms, indicating its importance in the gut microbial ecosystem."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lactobacillus is a genus of bacteria significantly associated with the PE + bran diet in the gut microbiome of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lactobacillus is significantly associated with the PE + bran diet, contributing to gut health."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lactobacillus is a genus of bacteria present in the gut of mealworms."</data>
