    </node>
    <node id="&quot;-\MATHRM{C}=\MATHRM{O}&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNCTIONAL GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A new functional group appearing in degraded PVC, indicating an oxidative process during breakdown."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9424d3ce58d3ff2e0adc795d24fe84f4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HYDROXYL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNCTIONAL GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hydroxyl groups appear in the degraded PVC, signifying chemical modifications via an oxidative process."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9424d3ce58d3ff2e0adc795d24fe84f4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;-\MATHRM{C}-\MATHRM{CL}&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL BOND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The reduction in C-Cl stretching indicates a decrease in chlorine content during PVC degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9424d3ce58d3ff2e0adc795d24fe84f4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ESCHERICHIA-SHIGELLA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Escherichia-Shigella genus increased in abundance in the PVC-fed mealworm gut microbiota compared to bran-fed controls."&lt;SEP&gt;"Escherichia-Shigella is a genus of bacteria present in the core gut microbiome of yellow mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9424d3ce58d3ff2e0adc795d24fe84f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e5407936cdb4f49bd5363f782dab563</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PELOMONAS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pelomonas genus exhibited the most significant increase in PVC-fed mealworms, suggesting a role in plastic degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9424d3ce58d3ff2e0adc795d24fe84f4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CITRATE CYCLE (TCA CYCLE)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The citrate cycle was significantly enriched in the PVC group, suggesting metabolic adaptation to plastic degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9424d3ce58d3ff2e0adc795d24fe84f4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OXIDATIVE PHOSPHORYLATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Oxidative phosphorylation is a metabolic pathway that generates energy through the production of ATP."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oxidative phosphorylation pathways were upregulated in PVC-fed mealworms, reflecting energy production for plastic breakdown."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9424d3ce58d3ff2e0adc795d24fe84f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc6c2706bd609f920aa61d5ef2310db6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PENTOSE PHOSPHATE PATHWAY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The pentose phosphate pathway involves L-arabinose as an intermediate, contributing to central metabolism during intensive digestion."&lt;SEP&gt;"The pentose phosphate pathway was enriched in bran-fed mealworms, indicating its role in carbohydrate metabolism."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9424d3ce58d3ff2e0adc795d24fe84f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a38885f67ed46b97bb84086f575fd43</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARBON FIXATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Carbon fixation pathways were associated with bran-fed mealworms, highlighting photosynthetic organism processes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9424d3ce58d3ff2e0adc795d24fe84f4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GLYCOLYSIS/GLUCONEOGENESIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Glycolysis and gluconeogenesis pathways were enriched in bran-fed mealworms, showing energy production mechanisms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9424d3ce58d3ff2e0adc795d24fe84f4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CYSTEINE AND METHIONINE METABOLISM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cysteine and Methionine Metabolism involve the synthesis and degradation of these sulfur-containing amino acids."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cysteine and Methionine Metabolism involves the metabolism of these amino acids."&lt;SEP&gt;"This metabolic pathway was enriched in bran-fed mealworms, emphasizing sulfur-containing amino acid processing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9424d3ce58d3ff2e0adc795d24fe84f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d290a6a81802d3048c35d2a2fb1252c4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VALINE METABOLISM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Valine metabolism was significantly enriched in PVC-fed mealworms, suggesting adaptation to plastic degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9424d3ce58d3ff2e0adc795d24fe84f4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENTEROBACTERIALES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORDER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An order partly characteristic of PE-oxo diets, related to gut microbiome changes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacteriales has an average abundance of 4.5%, highly abundant in PE-based groups but lower in the PS group."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacteriales is an order of Gram-negative bacteria often associated with human and animal intestines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacteriales is an order of bacteria involved in pesticide degradation and metabolism of aromatic compounds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacteriales order was enriched in PVC-fed mealworms, implicating it in plastic-related microbial functions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacteriales is the bacterial order under which Mixta tenebrionis is classified."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacteriales is an order of gram-negative bacteria that includes nitrogen-fixing genera like Klebsiella, Mixta, Kluyvera, and Citrobacter."&lt;SEP&gt;"The taxonomic order to which the genus Klebsiella belongs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-146789a250a0dbaae0d8438de692e191&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bf827d2b1d02488e17469a22da9e252&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9424d3ce58d3ff2e0adc795d24fe84f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0e30f29e9016acae216566f53e60cea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa10245aaff722ac7d69e73bed8afe74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc6c2706bd609f920aa61d5ef2310db6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a4712059883b356b4aea23cb7ef1514&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84297b844ec01d2f58756b669806fd62</data>
    </node>
