    <node id="&quot;LACCASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An enzyme capable of degrading lignin and potentially involved in plastic degradation, such as PS and CS."&lt;SEP&gt;"An enzyme that catalyzes the oxidation of phenols and other substrates, contributing to the biodegradation of PP polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Laccase is a copper-binding enzyme produced by Rhodococcus ruber, playing a role in the biodegradation of polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Laccase is an enzyme reported to have low activity on polyethylene plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"An enzyme that oxidizes phenols and similar molecules, often using molecular oxygen."&lt;SEP&gt;"Laccase is an enzyme involved in lignin degradation and exhibits activity related to the PS- and CS-degrading abilities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Laccase is an enzyme secreted by fungi to catalyze the oxidative breakdown of lignin."&lt;SEP&gt;"Laccase is an oxidoreductase enzyme capable of degrading lignin, playing a role in lignocellulosic feedstock processing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Laccase is an oxidative enzyme that decomposes aromatic compounds and polymers like PET."&lt;SEP&gt;"Laccase is an enzyme with oxidative capabilities, effective in degrading synthetic textile dyes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0f2fd4b2e978e6745e0dde602114a826&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-158317f8eba5f6198135df044d385935&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac5b96e63e6f5e34fe841f690d9f78ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-181e2c8b4d78916fefcf87c119f11d02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5f4bda412174e8b173f180d9b4311ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53d382cbd1392dbcf9530428c2eb8584&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfa5755e6c9a5eeae3f595d901dff422&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa9972450967f344c19cb747d7ce649e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c4652e08c4ac6887914d0deebe761b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4c43611ebe237c15c5f9201a9f8dbee</data>
