    <node id="&quot;BOMBELLI ET AL.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"RESEARCH REFERENCE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A research study that reported LDPE degradation using homogenate paste from greater wax moth larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"A study that explored the biodegradation of polyethylene by larvae and identified ethylene glycol as a potential metabolite."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bombelli et al. reported the accelerated biodegradation of polyethylene by Galleria mellonella larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bombelli et al. contributed to the understanding of functional group formation during polymer degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bombelli et al. contributed research findings related to LDPE biodegradation by various larvae species."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2a214d2b1c90aeb78e6e8562679d4963&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b08485bef3ee3db21e59e159ad4c3e20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd90c8f9754a78aabdbd7053e1adf90b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff933f404b1e6da13d6c1319bc7432c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5a94048d4a1499a73a50e74a59245e6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WEBER ET AL.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"RESEARCH STUDY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A research study suggesting that observed mass losses in LDPE degradation experiments could be due to mechanical wear rather than actual chemical degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"This study questioned the results of Bombelli et al., raising concerns about methodological issues such as FTIR analysis and mass loss interpretation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Weber et al. questioned some findings of Bombelli et al. regarding polyethylene degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ff933f404b1e6da13d6c1319bc7432c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a214d2b1c90aeb78e6e8562679d4963&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b08485bef3ee3db21e59e159ad4c3e20</data>
    </node>
