      <data key="d2">chunk-16700b183fc641abfa74ad7fbb0917fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GLOBAL WARMING POTENTIAL (GWP)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENVIRONMENTAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"GWP estimates the cradle-to-gate emissions related to natural gas and electricity consumption."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-16700b183fc641abfa74ad7fbb0917fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIODIESEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biodiesel is a renewable fuel derived from biological sources, such as the grease from yellow mealworm beetles."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodiesel is a renewable fuel derived from lipids, with potential to offset fossil diesel."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodiesel is a renewable fuel derived from vegetable oils or animal fats, often used as a substitute for conventional diesel."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodiesel is a renewable fuel produced from lipids in sewage sludge, scum, and mealworm remains, used as an alternative to low S diesel."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e6d515521d6d2b72e82154cc544d26cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b74f16813537103549cdcb6770abaea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16700b183fc641abfa74ad7fbb0917fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-463ac9dfa68274d35700c61208f4ea85</data>
    </node>
