      <data key="d2">chunk-e6d515521d6d2b72e82154cc544d26cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GREATER WAX MOTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Common name for Gmel larvae, involved in PS metabolism studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Greater Wax Moth is another species whose gut microbes contribute to the biodegradation of PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Greater wax moth is a species of larvae that demonstrates increased community diversity in its gut microbiome after being fed polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Greater wax moth is a species of larvae with moderate PS consumption and survival rates. Its weight change is less pronounced compared to superworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Greater wax moth is the larval form of Galleria mellonella, demonstrating moderate efficiency in degrading polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Greater Wax Moth is a microorganism whose larvae have been observed to interact with and potentially degrade low-density polyethylene (LDPE)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The greater wax moth is an insect whose larvae were used in experiments to test their ability to degrade LDPE."&lt;SEP&gt;"The greater wax moth is the species of mealworms used in experiments to digest plastic waste."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-99f8bb992751f8875d9449507e9c46ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a214d2b1c90aeb78e6e8562679d4963&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a52fc2936b4d2a771dbc2d6a37eeb710&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-681ece0a8beca8b22f3c6aa11a564f63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f91ffc7c76e8e0a1757d91f7cf62f568&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e5407936cdb4f49bd5363f782dab563&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6d515521d6d2b72e82154cc544d26cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-013f364e92a266c0e922cb0582f7a997</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MONTE CARLO SIMULATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Monte Carlo simulation is a statistical method used to estimate variability in energy, GWP, and cost metrics for treating mixed plastic waste."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e6d515521d6d2b72e82154cc544d26cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THERMAL ENERGY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENERGY SOURCE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Thermal energy is used in the treatment process for rearing mealworms and processing plastic waste alongside electricity."</data>
