    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARBON MASS BALANCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A method using \(^{13}\)C-labeled carbon to estimate the proportion of EPS removed but not ingested."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon mass balance estimates carbon flow through mealworms using CO2 trapping systems."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon mass balance experiments measure the conversion of ingested Styrofoam into CO2 and frass over various incubation periods."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon mass balance is a method used to estimate the conversion efficiencies of ingested Styrofoam into carbon dioxide and frass residues."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon mass balance is a method used to estimate the degradation of EPS by mealworms based on carbon content."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon mass balance is a method used to track the fate of carbon atoms from consumed EPS into biomass, carbon dioxide, and fecula."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon mass balance refers to the method used to quantify carbon flow and storage within an organism."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b8b7b5a840af17cee78d71347e532d51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81552b76a273b31cc2bd9ed21ed7a919&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-260d8c268067de32e5ac98d66ab70a6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c11c77665793ac79aecfb19a89dd1f52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-497648a1cf8e41fac896250ae1eebbb1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b33a3915745323f1bd29bd2febf60b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f71fddc259d51158d5c79f38bf41523f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BACL2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL COMPOUND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"BaCl2 (barium chloride) reacts with NaOH-collected CO2 to form BaCO3 for measurement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Barium chloride reacts with trapped CO2 to form BaCO3 for isotopic analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-81552b76a273b31cc2bd9ed21ed7a919&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8b7b5a840af17cee78d71347e532d51</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BACO3&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"BaCO3 (barium carbonate) is a precipitate formed during the respirometry test, used to quantify trapped CO2."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b8b7b5a840af17cee78d71347e532d51</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TG CURVES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Thermogravimetric (TG) curves represent weight loss as a function of temperature during thermal decomposition."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b8b7b5a840af17cee78d71347e532d51</data>
    </node>
