      <data key="d1">"The elemental analyzer measures the carbon content of Styrofoam and frass, contributing to the carbon mass balance analysis."</data>
      <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STYROFOAM CONVERSION&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-b8b7b5a840af17cee78d71347e532d51</data>
      <data key="d1">"The study provides detailed procedures for estimating the conversion of ingested Styrofoam into CO2 and frass."</data>
      <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHEMICAL AND PHYSICAL CHARACTERISATION&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-8cede90fd3b3eee0bd12d582eaa7d54c</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chemical and physical characterisation helps understand changes in polystyrene during degradation."</data>
      <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BACILLUS SP. PELW2042&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bacillus sp. PELW2042 is a strain of bacteria isolated from the gut contents of Tenebrio molitor larvae, capable of degrading high-density polyethylene (HDPE)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-02761f0aee6116a25ce05444f6ce8242</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOURIER TRANSFORM-INFRARED SPECTROSCOPY (FT-IR)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"FT-IR is a spectroscopic technique that detects functional groups by measuring molecular vibrations, identifying carbonyl groups and other oxygen-containing groups on HDPE after degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-02761f0aee6116a25ce05444f6ce8242</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARBONYL GROUPS (-C=O)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNCTIONAL GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Carbonyl groups are functional groups identified on the degraded HDPE surface, indicating oxidation processes during biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbonyl groups are oxygen-containing functional groups formed during the biodegradation of HDPE, indicating initial hydroxylation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6675480dfd01dcb533166d01b8e5482e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02761f0aee6116a25ce05444f6ce8242</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OXYGEN-CONTAINING FUNCTIONAL GROUPS (-C-O)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNCTIONAL GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"These groups are newly formed on the HDPE surface after biodegradation, suggesting chemical modification of the polymer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-02761f0aee6116a25ce05444f6ce8242</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;16SDNA SEQUENCE ANALYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"16sDNA sequence analysis is a method used to identify bacterial species based on their ribosomal RNA gene sequences."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-02761f0aee6116a25ce05444f6ce8242</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PSEUDOMONAS BACTERIOPHAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pseudomonas bacteriophage refers to a group of bacteria isolated from the Dandora landfill, capable of degrading low-density polyethylene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-02761f0aee6116a25ce05444f6ce8242</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WEIGHT LOSS OF HDPE FILM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The weight loss of HDPE film quantifies the extent of biodegradation by Bacillus sp. PELW2042."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-02761f0aee6116a25ce05444f6ce8242</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RELATIVE CRYSTALLINITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Relative crystallinity refers to the degree of order in the polymer structure, which decreases during biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-02761f0aee6116a25ce05444f6ce8242</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;YELLOW MEALWORM LARVAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Yellow mealworm larvae (Tenebrio molitor) are insects whose gut microbiota has been shown to play a crucial role in the biodegradation of plastics like polyethylene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b42ef7860e1f056d47955d0d13a15cd8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SURFACE PHYSICOCHEMICAL PROPERTIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Surface physicochemical properties describe changes in the physical and chemical nature of plastic surfaces due to microbial activity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b42ef7860e1f056d47955d0d13a15cd8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STERILIZATION METHOD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sterilization method involves treating HDPE film with ethanol, sterile water, and UV light to ensure experimental cleanliness."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b42ef7860e1f056d47955d0d13a15cd8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INORGANIC SALT MEDIUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Inorganic Salt Medium is prepared using various salts dissolved in deionized water, serving as a culture medium for bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Inorganic salt medium provides essential nutrients for culturing microorganisms involved in plastic degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-70bab3579af07d0f99a5f948a90fe1e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b42ef7860e1f056d47955d0d13a15cd8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SALINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Saline solution is prepared by dissolving NaCl in deionized water and is utilized for creating bacterial suspensions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Saline solution was utilized during the cleaning process of larvae before dissection."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-70bab3579af07d0f99a5f948a90fe1e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6dce72fccb3df94ec407aba3d4df8eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIODEGRADATION ASSAYS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A process used to characterize the degradation of PS by bacterial strain YT2."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodegradation assays measure the ability of bacteria to break down HDPE through weight loss and contact angle changes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-70bab3579af07d0f99a5f948a90fe1e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68041096d198a27b4ed526281746b7f3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GRAM STAIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gram staining determines bacterial cell wall properties, classifying bacteria as Gram-positive or Gram-negative."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-70bab3579af07d0f99a5f948a90fe1e1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MGSO4-7H2O&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL COMPOUND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"MgSO4-7H2O is magnesium sulfate heptahydrate, a salt used in the preparation of the inorganic salt medium."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-70bab3579af07d0f99a5f948a90fe1e1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FESO4-7H2O&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL COMPOUND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"FeSO4-7H2O is iron(II) sulfate heptahydrate, an iron source used in the preparation of the inorganic salt medium."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-70bab3579af07d0f99a5f948a90fe1e1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ZNSO4-7H2O&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL COMPOUND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"ZnSO4-7H2O is zinc sulfate heptahydrate, a zinc source used in the preparation of the inorganic salt medium."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-70bab3579af07d0f99a5f948a90fe1e1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MNSO4-H2O&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL COMPOUND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"MnSO4-H2O is manganese(II) sulfate monohydrate, a manganese source used in the preparation of the inorganic salt medium."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-70bab3579af07d0f99a5f948a90fe1e1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRYPTONE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL COMPONENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A component of LB medium that provides nutrients for bacterial growth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tryptone is a nutrient-rich component of LB broth, providing peptides and amino acids for bacterial growth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tryptone is a nutrient-rich substance derived from casein, used in the preparation of LB medium."&lt;SEP&gt;"A nutrient-rich substance used in the preparation of TYE medium."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a32ea55d79e87933e26b4165db47b1fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3235cc6102d988875f1dda974a56038&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70bab3579af07d0f99a5f948a90fe1e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3099f2d6fd3abc2f73550f579999b13</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIGH-PRESSURE STEAM STERILIZATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"High-pressure steam sterilization is a process used to sterilize media, buffers, and solutions at \(121^\circ \mathrm{C}, 103.4 \mathrm{kPa}, 20 \mathrm{~min}\)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-70bab3579af07d0f99a5f948a90fe1e1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VORTEX MIXER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A vortex mixer is a laboratory device used to mix samples vigorously, such as intestinal suspensions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vortex mixing ensures homogenization of gut suspensions from larvae during sample preparation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vortex mixing is employed to homogenize gut suspensions from larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Device used to detach bacteria from PS films after incubation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d3235cc6102d988875f1dda974a56038&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-050a4c71685bf71165985a79f528ed58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70bab3579af07d0f99a5f948a90fe1e1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MSM AGAR PLATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"MSM agar plate is a minimal salts medium agar plate used for culturing PE-degrading bacteria."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-70bab3579af07d0f99a5f948a90fe1e1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONTROL GROUPS&quot;">
