      <data key="d1">"Control groups are experimental setups without bacterial inoculation or HDPE film, used to validate experimental results."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-70bab3579af07d0f99a5f948a90fe1e1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONTACT ANGLE CHANGES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Contact angle changes are a metric used in biodegradation assays to assess surface alterations on HDPE."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-70bab3579af07d0f99a5f948a90fe1e1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPSS 20.0&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"SOFTWARE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"SPSS 20.0 is statistical software used for analyzing data from biodegradation assays."&lt;SEP&gt;"Statistical software used for performing ANOVA and Student's t-tests on experimental data."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-70bab3579af07d0f99a5f948a90fe1e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6dce72fccb3df94ec407aba3d4df8eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEGA 6 SOFTWARE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"SOFTWARE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"MEGA 6 software is used for constructing phylogenetic trees based on 16S rRNA gene sequences."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-70bab3579af07d0f99a5f948a90fe1e1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OPTIMAL GROWTH TEMPERATURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Optimal growth temperature refers to the temperature at which bacteria grow best, identified as \(35^\circ \mathrm{C}\) for strain PELW2042."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-70bab3579af07d0f99a5f948a90fe1e1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PELW2042&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PELW2042 is a Gram-positive bacterium isolated from mealworms with the ability to degrade HDPE. It forms biofilms on the surface of HDPE films, leading to visible cracks, cavities, and pits."&lt;SEP&gt;"PELW2042 is a microbial strain capable of degrading HDPE, as evidenced by weight loss, molecular weight decrease, and changes in chemical structure."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-361c5d4ba2e879627f4eb7fc4011ee3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6675480dfd01dcb533166d01b8e5482e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CALMODULIN (CAM)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROTEIN"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Calmodulin is a calcium-binding protein used in gene sequence analysis to identify strain PELW2042 as Bacillus sp."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-361c5d4ba2e879627f4eb7fc4011ee3b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SURFACTANT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Surfactant secreted by PELW2042 may contribute to the biodegradation of HDPE."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6675480dfd01dcb533166d01b8e5482e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ETHER GROUPS (-C-O-C-)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNCTIONAL GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ether groups are oxygen-containing functional groups identified during the biodegradation process of HDPE."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6675480dfd01dcb533166d01b8e5482e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALKB&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"AlkB is an enzyme cloned into recombinant cells to facilitate the biodegradation of polyethylene by a soil bacterium."&lt;SEP&gt;"AlkB is an enzyme involved in the hydroxylation of polyethylene, contributing to its biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9528beb2e85a7fb89449a9233eb979bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6675480dfd01dcb533166d01b8e5482e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;P450&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"P450 is an enzyme family involved in the hydroxylation of polyethylene, contributing to its biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6675480dfd01dcb533166d01b8e5482e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HYDROXYLASES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hydroxylases are enzymes involved in the depolymerization of PET in the midgut of T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hydroxylases perform the initial hydroxylation of polyethylene at the terminal carbon, initiating the degradation process."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6675480dfd01dcb533166d01b8e5482e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b19ac5bdc755bb8e9deb8e317ce365dd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRIMARY ALCOHOL DEHYDROGENASE (ADH)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Adh converts hydroxylated polyethylene into ketones, further advancing the degradation process."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6675480dfd01dcb533166d01b8e5482e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MOLECULAR WEIGHT DECREASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Molecular weight decrease reflects the depolymerization of HDPE chains during biodegradation by PELW2042."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6675480dfd01dcb533166d01b8e5482e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MELTING POINT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Melting point is a thermal property of HDPE that changes during biodegradation, reflecting molecular alterations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6675480dfd01dcb533166d01b8e5482e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GPC DATA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"GPC data provides insights into the molecular weight distribution of HDPE, indicating depolymerization during biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6675480dfd01dcb533166d01b8e5482e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OXIDATION LEVEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Oxidation level increases during HDPE biodegradation, contributing to its degradation and weight loss."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6675480dfd01dcb533166d01b8e5482e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LONG CHAIN STRUCTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL FEATURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The long chain structure of HDPE is broken down during biodegradation, leading to lower molecular weight fragments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6675480dfd01dcb533166d01b8e5482e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AMORPHOUS PART&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL FEATURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The amorphous part of HDPE is attacked by microorganisms during biodegradation, causing structural and chemical changes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6675480dfd01dcb533166d01b8e5482e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PE-DEGRADING MICROORGANISMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PE-degrading microorganisms are bacteria capable of breaking down polyethylene, isolated from environments like soil, waste treatment plants, and seawater."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8eca628f2d85c664191a5205194ec475</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STRAIN PELW2042&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Strain PELW2042 is a specific strain of Bacillus sp. isolated from the gut of mealworms, showing high efficiency in degrading HDPE."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8eca628f2d85c664191a5205194ec475</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SYNERGISTIC EFFECT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Synergistic effect refers to the combined action of insect larvae and their gut microbiome, enhancing the biodegradation of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"The synergistic effect describes the combined action of host digestive functions and gut microbiota in facilitating plastic degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8eca628f2d85c664191a5205194ec475&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31b2c5f608adabba1cc6986356e96598</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WEIGHT LOSS RATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Weight loss rate refers to the reduction in mass of polyethylene during its degradation process."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8eca628f2d85c664191a5205194ec475</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SURFACE MORPHOLOGY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL FEATURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Surface morphology refers to the physical characteristics of a sample's surface after enzymatic treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Surface morphology refers to the physical structure and texture of the surface of polyethylene, altered during degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8eca628f2d85c664191a5205194ec475&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e8cdca8afb1d7153fba5e3c11b1f669</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HYDROPHOBICITY REDUCTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hydrophobicity reduction is the decrease in water-repellent properties of polyethylene during degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8eca628f2d85c664191a5205194ec475</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CRYSTALLINITY REDUCTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Crystallinity reduction refers to the decrease in the ordered structure of polyethylene during degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8eca628f2d85c664191a5205194ec475</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EMULSIFIERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Emulsifiers are substances secreted by insect larvae that facilitate the biodegradation of plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8eca628f2d85c664191a5205194ec475</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AQUATIC ENVIRONMENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ECOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Aquatic environments encompass water bodies such as oceans, lakes, and rivers where microplastics and nanoplastics impact ecological health."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7ffec9fc63ae323ee0c22c612bb89755</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONTAMINANT TRANSPORT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Contaminant transport involves the movement of harmful substances, often facilitated by microplastics, through different environmental compartments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7ffec9fc63ae323ee0c22c612bb89755</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOOD SECURITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Food security is the availability and accessibility of sufficient, safe, and nutritious food, which is threatened by microplastic pollution."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7ffec9fc63ae323ee0c22c612bb89755</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SYNTHETIC FIBERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Synthetic fibers are man-made fibers, some of which degrade into microplastics and contribute to environmental pollution."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7ffec9fc63ae323ee0c22c612bb89755</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ATMOSPHERIC FALLOUT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Atmospheric fallout refers to the deposition of airborne particles, including synthetic fibers and microplastics, onto surfaces."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7ffec9fc63ae323ee0c22c612bb89755</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHINESE COASTAL AND MARGINAL SEAS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Chinese coastal and marginal seas are regions where microplastic pollution has been extensively studied and documented."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7ffec9fc63ae323ee0c22c612bb89755</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CASPIAN SEA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Caspian Sea is a large inland body of water where microplastic distribution, abundance, and composition have been investigated."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7ffec9fc63ae323ee0c22c612bb89755</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COASTAL LAGOONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Coastal lagoons are shallow bodies of water separated from larger bodies, serving as sites for microplastic studies globally."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7ffec9fc63ae323ee0c22c612bb89755</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOURCE-PATHWAY-RECEPTOR MODEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPTUAL FRAMEWORK"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A conceptual framework used to describe the movement of microplastics through the environment, identifying sources, pathways, and receptors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7ffec9fc63ae323ee0c22c612bb89755</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLATEAU CULTIVATED LAND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Plateau cultivated land refers to agricultural areas on elevated plateaus where microplastic abundance and distribution have been studied."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7ffec9fc63ae323ee0c22c612bb89755</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GULF OF VENICE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Gulf of Venice is a protected area where microplastic contamination levels have been assessed."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7ffec9fc63ae323ee0c22c612bb89755</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RAWAL LAKE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rawal Lake is a freshwater reservoir in Pakistan where microplastic pollution evidence has been reported."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7ffec9fc63ae323ee0c22c612bb89755</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOIL-GROUNDWATER ENVIRONMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ECOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The soil-groundwater environment represents interconnected systems where microplastics can age, migrate, and co-transport contaminants."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7ffec9fc63ae323ee0c22c612bb89755</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MARINE FOOD WEB&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The marine food web describes feeding relationships among organisms in marine ecosystems, impacted by trophic transfer of microplastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7ffec9fc63ae323ee0c22c612bb89755</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AGGREGATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Aggregation refers to the process by which microplastics and nanoplastics clump together in aquatic environments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7ffec9fc63ae323ee0c22c612bb89755</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DEPOSITION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Deposition involves the settling of microplastics from water or air onto surfaces such as sediments or soil."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7ffec9fc63ae323ee0c22c612bb89755</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENHANCED CONTAMINANT TRANSPORT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Enhanced contaminant transport describes how microplastics facilitate the movement of pollutants through ecosystems."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7ffec9fc63ae323ee0c22c612bb89755</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOST AT SEA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPTUAL FRAMEWORK"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lost at Sea is a term used to describe the unaccounted-for plastic waste that ends up in marine environments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7ffec9fc63ae323ee0c22c612bb89755</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TEXTILE FIBERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Textile fibers include materials like synthetic fibers that degrade into microplastics and contribute to environmental contamination."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7ffec9fc63ae323ee0c22c612bb89755</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INDOOR AND OUTDOOR ENVIRONMENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Indoor and outdoor environments are areas where microplastics and synthetic fibers can be found due to atmospheric fallout."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7ffec9fc63ae323ee0c22c612bb89755</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICROPLASTICS DISTRIBUTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Microplastics distribution refers to the spread and allocation of microplastics across different environmental compartments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7ffec9fc63ae323ee0c22c612bb89755</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ABUNDANCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Abundance indicates the quantity or prevalence of microplastics in specific locations such as sediments or organisms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7ffec9fc63ae323ee0c22c612bb89755</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMPOSITION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Composition describes the makeup or chemical structure of microplastics found in various environmental samples."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7ffec9fc63ae323ee0c22c612bb89755</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SEDIMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRITIONAL COMPONENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sediment refers to solid particles that settle at the bottom of water bodies, often containing microplastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7ffec9fc63ae323ee0c22c612bb89755</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BENTHIC ORGANISMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Benthic organisms are creatures living on or near the seabed, potentially interacting with microplastics in sediments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7ffec9fc63ae323ee0c22c612bb89755</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GLOBAL COASTAL LAGOONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Global coastal lagoons represent diverse ecosystems worldwide where microplastic pollution has been systematically reviewed."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7ffec9fc63ae323ee0c22c612bb89755</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AGING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Aging refers to the changes that occur in microplastics over time, affecting their properties and behavior in the environment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7ffec9fc63ae323ee0c22c612bb89755</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MIGRATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Migration describes the movement of microplastics through soil and groundwater systems."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7ffec9fc63ae323ee0c22c612bb89755</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CO-TRANSPORT OF CONTAMINANTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Co-transport of contaminants involves the simultaneous movement of microplastics and other pollutants through environmental media."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7ffec9fc63ae323ee0c22c612bb89755</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TROPHIC TRANSFER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Trophic transfer refers to the movement of microplastics and associated contaminants up the food chain."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7ffec9fc63ae323ee0c22c612bb89755</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GREATER WAXMOTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The greater waxmoth is an insect whose larvae have been found to contribute to the biodegradation and mineralization of LDPE films."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1a53fba6106c000acc0dac3484d37a4c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RHODOCOCCUS SP.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rhodococcus is a genus of bacteria known for its ability to degrade various types of plastics, including polypropylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rhodococcus sp. is a bacterial species identified in the gut microbiota of T. molitor larvae that aids in the degradation of polystyrene and corn straw."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rhodococcus sp. is a bacterial genus involved in the microbiome study associated with Tenebrio molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rhodococcus sp. is a genus of Gram-positive bacteria capable of degrading various hydrocarbons and polymers like polypropylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rhodococcus sp. is a genus of actinobacteria capable of degrading various hydrocarbons and polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rhodococcus sp. refers to bacteria from the Rhodococcus genus involved in styrene degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b9fcb421212175a148a0a1858582cfb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53d382cbd1392dbcf9530428c2eb8584&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cefffe48b3d2ec347f880c77300fc041&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a53fba6106c000acc0dac3484d37a4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-827853316f7304c444884dc82f757802&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3fe22bd6c91507d8d1e60d24886e0eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STENOTROPHOMONAS SP.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stenotrophomonas is a genus of bacteria capable of degrading untreated LDPE when isolated from waste dumpsites."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stenotrophomonas sp. is a bacterium involved in the formation of tunnels, cracks, and cellular aggregates on PS sheets, contributing to plastic degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c4804d2c00d1d5fff2b89eaf6da26da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a53fba6106c000acc0dac3484d37a4c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ACHROMOBACTER SP.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Achromobacter is a genus of bacteria that has shown potential in the biodegradation of untreated LDPE."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1a53fba6106c000acc0dac3484d37a4c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRICHODERMA HARZIANUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNGUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Trichoderma harzianum is a fungus that contributes to the degradation of polyethylene through enzymatic processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Trichoderma harzianum is a fungus that contributes to the degradation of polyethylene, as evidenced by SEM, FTIR, and NMR analyses."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1a53fba6106c000acc0dac3484d37a4c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MANGROVE SEDIMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ECOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mangrove sediment is a type of soil found in mangrove ecosystems, hosting diverse microbial communities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mangrove sediment provides a habitat rich in microorganisms that contribute to the degradation of polypropylene microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mangrove sediment serves as a habitat for microorganisms capable of degrading plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1a53fba6106c000acc0dac3484d37a4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-827853316f7304c444884dc82f757802&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3fe22bd6c91507d8d1e60d24886e0eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DRILLING FLUID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Drilling fluid is a substance used in drilling operations and can harbor microorganisms involved in LDPE degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1a53fba6106c000acc0dac3484d37a4c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXTRACELLULAR MATRIX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The extracellular matrix produced by bacterial biofilms plays a role in the biocorrosion of polyethylene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1a53fba6106c000acc0dac3484d37a4c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;P450-DRIVEN SYNTHETIC BACTERIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"P450-driven synthetic bacteria are engineered bacteria designed to degrade plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1a53fba6106c000acc0dac3484d37a4c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MARINE BACTERIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bacteria isolated from pelagic waters of the Arabian Sea involved in the biodegradation of low-density polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Marine bacteria isolated from pelagic waters contribute to the biodegradation of low-density polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Marine bacteria are microorganisms found in oceanic environments, some of which can degrade plastics like low-density polyethylene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ecf2c478d08c7bc8e491f630aa289881&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a53fba6106c000acc0dac3484d37a4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30b68116bde3b0e31c29adbd05cadaaa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SYNTHETIC BACTERIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Synthetic bacteria are genetically engineered microorganisms designed to perform specific functions, such as plastic degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1a53fba6106c000acc0dac3484d37a4c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICROCOCCUS LUTEUS STRAIN CGR112&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A bacterial strain isolated from cow dung with efficient biofilm-forming ability and potential to degrade high-density polyethylene (HDPE)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-30b68116bde3b0e31c29adbd05cadaaa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TENEBRIO MOLITOR (MEALWORM LARVAE)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Insect larvae whose gut microbiome contains microorganisms capable of enhancing the bioavailability and biodegradation of polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-30b68116bde3b0e31c29adbd05cadaaa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COW DUNG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A natural waste product from cows that serves as a source for isolating microorganisms with biodegradation potential."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-30b68116bde3b0e31c29adbd05cadaaa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENRICHMENT CULTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A technique used to enhance the growth of specific microorganisms by providing favorable conditions, as applied to the gut microbiome of Tenebrio molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"The enrichment culture involves inoculating gut cell suspension into a flask containing polystyrene emulsion and LCFBM."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enrichment Culture enhances microbial activity for biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enrichment cultures are established using gut and frass samples from early and late instar larvae to isolate PS-degrading bacteria."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fdb13eda4d3cf5385a0a8284c7e213b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85fe36521680f0d09a603eab04706561&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94bf67bf1b585ce1050569a2eb0000cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30b68116bde3b0e31c29adbd05cadaaa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ARABIAN SEA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A body of water where marine bacteria capable of degrading LDPE were isolated."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Arabian Sea is a body of water where marine bacteria have been isolated and studied for their potential to degrade low-density polyethylene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ecf2c478d08c7bc8e491f630aa289881&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30b68116bde3b0e31c29adbd05cadaaa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LANDFILL SOIL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ECOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Soil found in landfills, serving as a habitat for microorganisms like Aspergillus clavatus strain JASK1."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-30b68116bde3b0e31c29adbd05cadaaa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOFILM-FORMING ABILITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL FUNCTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The capacity of certain microorganisms, such as Micrococcus luteus strain CGR112, to form biofilms on surfaces."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-30b68116bde3b0e31c29adbd05cadaaa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIGH-DENSITY POLYETHYLENE (HDPE) DEGRADATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The biological breakdown of HDPE into simpler compounds by microbial action."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-30b68116bde3b0e31c29adbd05cadaaa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYSTYRENE BIOAVAILABILITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The degree to which polystyrene is accessible and can be metabolized by microorganisms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-30b68116bde3b0e31c29adbd05cadaaa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TENEBRIO MOLITOR GUT MICROBIOME-DERIVED ENRICHMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An enriched microbial culture derived from the gut microbiome of Tenebrio molitor larvae, specifically tailored for polystyrene degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-30b68116bde3b0e31c29adbd05cadaaa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PREDICTED GROWTH&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-7ffec9fc63ae323ee0c22c612bb89755</data>
      <data key="d1">"The predicted growth in plastic waste exacerbates plastic pollution, leading to increased microplastic contamination."</data>
      <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHROMOBACTERIUM VIOLACEUM&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-1a53fba6106c000acc0dac3484d37a4c</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chromobacterium violaceum biofilms enhance polyethylene biocorrosion through the formation of extracellular matrices, aiding in material breakdown."</data>
      <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WASTE DUMPSITE&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-1a53fba6106c000acc0dac3484d37a4c</data>
      <data key="d1">"Waste dumpsites are locations where Stenotrophomonas sp. can be isolated for studies on LDPE degradation."</data>
      <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOLID-STATE $^{13}$C CROSS-POLARIZATION/MAGIC ANGLE SPINNING NUCLEAR MAGNETIC RESONANCE (CP/MAS NMR)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CP/MAS NMR spectroscopy is employed to confirm the cleavage/depolymerization of long-chain PS molecules."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f7fa795762aa89809d8221dc9dda92fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THERMOGRAVIMETRIC FOURIER TRANSFORM INFRARED (TG-FTIR)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"TG-FTIR spectroscopy substantiates the chemical changes in PS molecules during degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f7fa795762aa89809d8221dc9dda92fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GLOBAL PLASTIC CONSUMPTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ECOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Global plastic consumption refers to the large-scale production and use of synthetic plastics like polystyrene, contributing to environmental pollution."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f7fa795762aa89809d8221dc9dda92fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MUNICIPAL SOLID WASTE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"WASTE MANAGEMENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Municipal solid waste includes discarded materials from urban areas, where polystyrene often ends up in landfills."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f7fa795762aa89809d8221dc9dda92fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MIXED MICROBIAL CONSORTIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mixed microbial consortia consist of various microorganisms isolated from soil, sewage sludge, or manure for biodegradation studies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f7fa795762aa89809d8221dc9dda92fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EGG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LIFE STAGE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The egg stage is one of the four life stages of mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-086890e8567c60d8cfa7c03b0cc61f9a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LARVA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The larva refers to the immature form of an insect, specifically the lesser waxworm in this context, identified through morphology and validated using monographs."&lt;SEP&gt;"The larval stage is the feeding stage of mealworms, during which they consume Styrofoam."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5af82472112cbc9e76b1fd1ac6e8c54e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-086890e8567c60d8cfa7c03b0cc61f9a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADULT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LIFE STAGE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Adult represents the mature life stage of insects, where structural changes in jaws may prevent ingestion of certain materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"The adult stage is the final stage in the life cycle of mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c4804d2c00d1d5fff2b89eaf6da26da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-086890e8567c60d8cfa7c03b0cc61f9a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OATS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Oats (Quaker Oats) used as bedding material and food source for mealworms and beetles in the habitats."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oats are part of the conventional diet used to rear mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oats were used as bedding material in experiments to study their effect on EPS consumption rates."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oats are used as part of the mealworm diet in control and experimental groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oats represent a dietary component mixed with EPS to observe its impact on mealworm larval behavior and EPS consumption."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oats serve as the control diet for mealworms in the experiment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d3235cc6102d988875f1dda974a56038&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e557113f1cfd2472fa9c51d1cdc3069a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1d76ad321e1c68d5f139cdb94d5bf42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c11c77665793ac79aecfb19a89dd1f52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-086890e8567c60d8cfa7c03b0cc61f9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed48dc66abf9c27721101b1adac15e7a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GRAIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Grain is included in the conventional diet for mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-086890e8567c60d8cfa7c03b0cc61f9a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POTATO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Potato is a food source provided to mealworms along with grains."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-086890e8567c60d8cfa7c03b0cc61f9a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CABBAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cabbage is a vegetable used in the conventional diet for mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-086890e8567c60d8cfa7c03b0cc61f9a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARROTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Carrots are a food source provided to mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carrots are used as a dietary supplement alongside polystyrene for mealworms in one of the experimental groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carrots are a potential supplemental nutrient that could be used to enhance mealworm consumption rates."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3b2f11b2dff6f9e39c409f2bbd26c9d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-568e2e90ce0d3bbb4e21079f4252f5de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-086890e8567c60d8cfa7c03b0cc61f9a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;APPLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Apple is a fruit included in the conventional diet for mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-086890e8567c60d8cfa7c03b0cc61f9a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOLID-STATE 13C CP/MAS NMR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"This nuclear magnetic resonance technique analyzes chemical structures within samples at specific operational parameters."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-81552b76a273b31cc2bd9ed21ed7a919</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CO2 TRAPPERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CO2 trappers remove CO2 from air using NaOH solutions during carbon balance experiments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-81552b76a273b31cc2bd9ed21ed7a919</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;13C-CARBON ISOTOPE TRACER EXPERIMENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"These experiments trace carbon metabolism using isotopically labeled polystyrene and bran."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-81552b76a273b31cc2bd9ed21ed7a919</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ISOTOPE RATIO MASS SPECTROMETRY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"This technique analyzes isotopic composition of carbon atoms in samples."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-81552b76a273b31cc2bd9ed21ed7a919</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AGAR JELLY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Agar jelly serves as a medium to mix and deliver labeled PS and bran to mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-81552b76a273b31cc2bd9ed21ed7a919</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;Α 13C-LABELED PS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL COMPOUND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"This is a specific isotopically labeled form of polystyrene used in tracer experiments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-81552b76a273b31cc2bd9ed21ed7a919</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;Β 13C-LABELED PS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL COMPOUND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Another isotopically labeled form of polystyrene utilized in tracer experiments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-81552b76a273b31cc2bd9ed21ed7a919</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NAOH SOLUTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL COMPOUND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sodium hydroxide solution traps CO2 during carbon balance measurements."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-81552b76a273b31cc2bd9ed21ed7a919</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHLOROFORM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chloroform (CHCl3) is a solvent used in extracting lipophilic compounds from biological samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chloroform (CHCl3) is a solvent utilized in extraction procedures during metabolomics studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chloroform extracts lipids from lyophilized mealworm bodies for further analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chloroform is a solvent used in the Soxhlet extractor to extract lipids from lyophilized mealworm bodies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chloroform is a solvent used in the separation of organic and aqueous layers during the NPS extraction process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chloroform was used in the extraction process to separate nanoplastics from other materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chloroform is a solvent used to dissolve polystyrene film."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e557113f1cfd2472fa9c51d1cdc3069a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56c8b21b1eaba7633b49cea16714ddc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-262d7fa1c8f2581943a41cf4897fa253&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c4244cae75095bda7fb526c3d0c9d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81552b76a273b31cc2bd9ed21ed7a919&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9578db0f9ed0398705827be5d4ee450&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e25fe1af3bede4605e7b94d457c9634</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LYOPHILIZATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lyophilization dries mealworms while preserving their structure for subsequent analyses."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lyophilization is the process of freeze-drying the mealworm bodies to facilitate lipid extraction."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lyophilization is a process used to preserve materials by freezing and reducing atmospheric pressure to remove water through sublimation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-81552b76a273b31cc2bd9ed21ed7a919&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56c8b21b1eaba7633b49cea16714ddc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b693d867918f89c9b28997fe94fc830</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GUT TISSUE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ANATOMICAL STRUCTURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gut tissue may contain fecula and is removed during sample preparation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-81552b76a273b31cc2bd9ed21ed7a919</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIPID EXTRACTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lipid extraction isolates lipids from mealworm bodies using chloroform."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-81552b76a273b31cc2bd9ed21ed7a919</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;13C-LABELED PRODUCTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"These are metabolized compounds labeled with carbon-13 isotopes for tracking metabolic processes in mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-56c8b21b1eaba7633b49cea16714ddc1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FATTY ACIDS (FAS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fatty acids are separated by gas chromatography from the lipid-chloroform solution for further analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fatty acids serve as biomarkers in this study, indicating the assimilation of carbon from labeled PS into mealworm biomass."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1769c4becf46c99994cb7ced2bffda1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56c8b21b1eaba7633b49cea16714ddc1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GAS CHROMATOGRAPHY (GC)">
      <data key="d0">CHEMICAL REACTION</data>
      <data key="d1">Gas chromatography is used to separate fatty acids into individual components for analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-56c8b21b1eaba7633b49cea16714ddc1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMBUSTION-ISOTOPE RATIO MASS SPECTROMETRY (GC-C-IRMS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"INSTRUMENT</data>
      <data key="d1">This technique is used to analyze the composition and isotopic ratios of fatty acids derived from mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-56c8b21b1eaba7633b49cea16714ddc1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEOH/NAOH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A mixture of methanol and sodium hydroxide used to resuspend dried samples for further processing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-56c8b21b1eaba7633b49cea16714ddc1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;METHYLATED DERIVATIVES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Methylated derivatives are produced during the chemical transformation of fatty acids for analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-56c8b21b1eaba7633b49cea16714ddc1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BORON TRIFLUORIDE (BF₃)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Boron trifluoride is used as a catalyst in the methylation process of fatty acids."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-56c8b21b1eaba7633b49cea16714ddc1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SATURATED NACL AQUEOUS SOLUTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A saturated saltwater solution added to separate phases during the extraction of methylated fatty acids."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-56c8b21b1eaba7633b49cea16714ddc1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BEIJING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Beijing is a city in China where studies related to T. molitor larvae's biodegradation capabilities were conducted."&lt;SEP&gt;"Beijing is one of the locations where mealworms were sourced for the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"Beijing is the location of Mei5 Biotechnology."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e37da2fbe64f85c50c36da45006f4c23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56c8b21b1eaba7633b49cea16714ddc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc908e62eec4d1d05265c6e451cca84c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;QINHUANGDAO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Qinhuangdao is another location where mealworms were sourced for the study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-56c8b21b1eaba7633b49cea16714ddc1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HAM LAKE, MN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ham Lake, Minnesota, is a location in the U.S. where mealworms were sourced for the study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-56c8b21b1eaba7633b49cea16714ddc1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRIBOLIUM MOLITOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"SPECIES"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tribolium molitor, also known as mealworms, are the primary subjects of the study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-56c8b21b1eaba7633b49cea16714ddc1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THF (TETRAHYDROFURAN)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"SOLVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"THF is an organic solvent used to extract residual PS from frass samples for analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tetrahydrofuran is used as a solvent to extract degraded polystyrene products from fecula."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-490fdb90ad8a65d35f3c2cd42a8c4c8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56c8b21b1eaba7633b49cea16714ddc1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TG/DTG ANALYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"TG/DTG analysis involves thermal decomposition of samples to study weight loss and evolved gaseous compounds during pyrolysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-15323ef47e29f2927f95274e49f4e5bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NMR SPECTROSCOPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"NMR spectroscopy is used to identify the native composition of solid substrates without separation of components."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-15323ef47e29f2927f95274e49f4e5bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALIPHATIC HYDROCARBONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Aliphatic hydrocarbons are metabolites derived from PS metabolism and found in faeces."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aliphatic hydrocarbons are newly detected resonance signals in the fecula spectrum, indicating their presence after digestion."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aliphatic hydrocarbons are organic compounds degraded by Achromobacter species, including both straight and branched-chain hydrocarbons."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-15323ef47e29f2927f95274e49f4e5bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26138366e1d9310732edc569ba338bfe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f71fddc259d51158d5c79f38bf41523f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INSECT CUTICLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL FEATURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Insect cuticle is a biological structure containing chitin, identified through NMR analysis in the fecula spectrum."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-15323ef47e29f2927f95274e49f4e5bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WEIGHT LOSS STAGES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Weight loss stages refer to distinct phases of thermal decomposition observed in TG/DTG profiles."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-15323ef47e29f2927f95274e49f4e5bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NMR SPECTRA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"NMR spectra offer insights into the molecular structures and native compositions of evolved gaseous compounds."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-33a0a8b02ff930ea552c8902e4d0defd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARBON BALANCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Analysis confirming the majority of ingested LDPE is converted into CO2 through oxidation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon balance is an estimate used to track the loss of Styrofoam carbon during degradation trials."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon balance refers to the accounting of carbon inputs and outputs during the decomposition process, helping quantify recovery rates."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon balance refers to the accounting of carbon during the digestion of polystyrene by mealworms, showing mineralization and incorporation into biomass."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-21c07a838ff0a489c73c8319e5011134&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4443da1fe36ec7133cd5add18d1957a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33a0a8b02ff930ea552c8902e4d0defd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89a76f613b36454134940f78fba1c0f6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INCUBATION TIME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Incubation time refers to the duration for which bacterial cultures are allowed to grow under controlled conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Incubation time represents the duration over which mealworms are exposed to Styrofoam, influencing decomposition and metabolic outcomes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bfa1d3c9710e10c5eb533d8d791c93e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33a0a8b02ff930ea552c8902e4d0defd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot; ELEMENTAL ANALYZER &quot;">
      <data key="d0">"INSTRUMENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An elemental analyzer is a device used to measure the carbon content in various materials such as Styrofoam, biomass, and fecula."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-33a0a8b02ff930ea552c8902e4d0defd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEALWORM BIOMASS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mealworm biomass measures the growth or change in weight of mealworms after consuming Styrofoam."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-33a0a8b02ff930ea552c8902e4d0defd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARBON PROPORTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Carbon proportion quantifies the percentage of ingested Styrofoam recovered as CO₂, biomass, or fecula residues."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-33a0a8b02ff930ea552c8902e4d0defd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;13C SIGNATURES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"13C signatures provide isotopic evidence for the origin of CO₂ produced by mealworms fed on 13C-labeled PS."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-33a0a8b02ff930ea552c8902e4d0defd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARBON DIOXIDE (CO₂)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Carbon dioxide is a product of the mineralization of ingested Styrofoam, serving as an energy source for mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1769c4becf46c99994cb7ced2bffda1d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;¹³C-LABELED PS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"¹³C-labeled PS is a form of polystyrene used in the study to trace carbon assimilation in mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1769c4becf46c99994cb7ced2bffda1d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;Δ¹³C VALUE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The δ¹³C value measures the ratio of carbon isotopes and indicates the extent of carbon assimilation from labeled PS into mealworm biomass."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1769c4becf46c99994cb7ced2bffda1d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GC-C-IRMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"GC-C-irMS is a technique used to analyze the δ¹³C values in individual fatty acids of mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1769c4becf46c99994cb7ced2bffda1d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENDOGENOUS METABOLISM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Endogenous metabolism refers to the internal metabolic processes used by starving mealworms as an energy source."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1769c4becf46c99994cb7ced2bffda1d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SYNTHETIC LIGNIN HYDROCARBONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Synthetic lignin hydrocarbons are compounds studied in termites, analogous to the degradation of PS in mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1769c4becf46c99994cb7ced2bffda1d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;¹⁴C-LABELED LIGNIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"¹⁴C-labeled lignin was used in a termite study, showing limited assimilation into termite bodies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1769c4becf46c99994cb7ced2bffda1d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TERMITE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Termites, like mealworms, can degrade complex organic materials such as lignin, with limited assimilation into their bodies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1769c4becf46c99994cb7ced2bffda1d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GUT TRACT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL FEATURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The gut tract of mealworms serves as an efficient bioreactor for the degradation and mineralization of PS."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1769c4becf46c99994cb7ced2bffda1d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;13C STABLE CARBON ISOTOPE TRACER EXPERIMENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"These experiments help in understanding the fate of carbon atoms from ingested Styrofoam."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-21c07a838ff0a489c73c8319e5011134</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TGA-FTIR THERMOGRAMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Thermogravimetric analysis coupled with Fourier-transform infrared spectroscopy provides insights into the degradation process."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-21c07a838ff0a489c73c8319e5011134</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYM. SCI.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polym. Sci. refers to the scientific study of polymers, including their synthesis, properties, and degradation processes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0462cccaa75cf13e553e16026939880b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOAMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Foams are lightweight, porous materials often used for cushioning, insulation, or packaging."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0462cccaa75cf13e553e16026939880b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHOTODEGRADED POLYMERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Photodegraded polymers are materials that have undergone degradation due to exposure to light, studied for their biodegradability."&lt;SEP&gt;"Photodegraded polymers are plastics that have undergone degradation due to exposure to light, making them more susceptible to biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Photodegraded polymers are plastics that have undergone degradation due to exposure to sunlight, making them more susceptible to microbial attack."&lt;SEP&gt;"Photodegraded polymers are polymers that have undergone degradation due to exposure to light, leading to changes in their chemical structure."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bf8041a3cdcd6091f6c96b8b67229df2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eada60ee606520104bb515c4896d6b0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c02a8ea5e75c58dcb9cfbbcd64f37d82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0462cccaa75cf13e553e16026939880b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PENETRATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Penetration refers to the ability of insects or other organisms to physically breach packaging materials."</data>
