      <data key="d0">"LIPID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cholesterol is a lipid detected in the larvae tissue, with higher levels observed in diets with increased bran:PS ratios."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cholesterol is a sterol lipid identified in the frass, playing roles in cell membrane structure and function."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cholesterol levels are higher in diets with increased bran:PS ratios (Diets 2 and 3)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cholesterol levels are higher in larvae fed with increased bran:PS ratios (Diets 2 and 3)."</data>
