    <node id="&quot;PCA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PCA (Principal Component Analysis) is a statistical method used to visualize and interpret variations in gut microbial communities across different dietary conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"PCA (Principal Component Analysis) is a statistical technique used to identify correlations between features and diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Principal Component Analysis (PCA) is a statistical method used to analyze and interpret complex data sets, reducing dimensionality while preserving variance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Principal Component Analysis (PCA) is a statistical method used to identify patterns in data and reduce dimensionality."&lt;SEP&gt;"Principal Component Analysis is a statistical method used to analyze and visualize complex data sets, such as those obtained from GC-TOF-MS analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Principal Component Analysis (PCA) is a statistical method used to reduce data dimensionality and identify patterns."&lt;SEP&gt;"Principal components analysis used to examine correlations between experimental variants and studied variables."&lt;SEP&gt;"Principal Component Analysis, a statistical method used to analyze microbial community data."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-57edc76f6646a41c4845d94baa519950&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-512840a413df7ae3d881389c5cf1feb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6f28f1c36076d1f249dbc4cd67b16f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e356bad5f8c2dd9188b38c0d9462b9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a4712059883b356b4aea23cb7ef1514&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7df3b1ec42b9ac5c08513c3b568a399&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d616d4c3c3199d53c1ae93ebcf3589d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e663286500e382f6d296e2b683bf542</data>
    </node>
