      <data key="d1">"A bacterial genus significantly different in abundance across multiple diet comparisons."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stenotrophomonas is a genus of Gram-negative bacteria, three species of which were isolated from the larval gut of T. molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stenotrophomonas is a genus of bacteria isolated from T. molitor, showing significant morphological and biochemical characteristics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stenotrophomonas is a genus of bacteria known for its ability to degrade polymers such as polypropylene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5318125e74217718b470b7721d1d6365&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc908e62eec4d1d05265c6e451cca84c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2665d67f816d2da20a065d708c370210&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64e35cb810117768309e5f4db5d7e6b8</data>
    </node>
