      <data key="d2">chunk-2665d67f816d2da20a065d708c370210</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CATALASE-POSITIVE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Catalase-positive bacteria produce the enzyme catalase, which breaks down hydrogen peroxide."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2665d67f816d2da20a065d708c370210</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VP-POSITIVE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"VP-positive (Voges-Proskauer test) bacteria produce acetoin, reflecting their fermentation capabilities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2665d67f816d2da20a065d708c370210</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CITRATE-POSITIVE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Citrate-positive bacteria can utilize citrate as a carbon source."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2665d67f816d2da20a065d708c370210</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OXIDASE-POSITIVE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Oxidase-positive bacteria produce cytochrome c oxidase, an enzyme involved in cellular respiration."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2665d67f816d2da20a065d708c370210</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MOTILITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL FEATURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Motility refers to the ability of bacteria to move actively, often through flagellar action."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2665d67f816d2da20a065d708c370210</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MINERAL MEDIUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A medium prepared at pH 6.8 containing various salts such as KH₂PO₄, K₂HPO₄, NH₄NO₃, NaCl, MgSO₄·7H₂O, FeSO₄·7H₂O, ZnSO₄·7H₂O, and MnSO₄·7H₂O dissolved in 1 L of distilled water."&lt;SEP&gt;"A solid medium used for observing efficient degradation of polystyrene by microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mineral Medium is used for culturing microorganisms under conditions where polystyrene is the only carbon source."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mineral Medium serves as the growth medium for bacteria during degradation studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mineral medium is a nutrient-poor environment used to study bacterial growth on specific substrates like PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mineral medium is used as a nutrient source for bacterial growth and polystyrene degradation experiments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mineral medium was used for culturing symbiotic bacteria isolated from mealworm guts."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-07a91e5cf8b623163be09e14d1f4978e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c1bb645805a7158e2e18e95313565f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d4e1982efefa47339205e972562b51f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a32ea55d79e87933e26b4165db47b1fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10f59d5d10f08e8107f36bff5a4c93ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9578db0f9ed0398705827be5d4ee450&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2665d67f816d2da20a065d708c370210</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PS SHEET&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PS sheet refers to polystyrene sheets used as substrates for studying microbial degradation processes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c4804d2c00d1d5fff2b89eaf6da26da</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOFILM GENERATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biofilm generation is a biological process where microorganisms form a structured community on a surface, initiating the degradation of materials like polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c4804d2c00d1d5fff2b89eaf6da26da</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MATERIAL DETERIORATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Material deterioration describes the breakdown of polystyrene due to the enzymatic activity of microorganisms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c4804d2c00d1d5fff2b89eaf6da26da</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CITRIC ACID CYCLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The citric acid cycle is a metabolic pathway involved in the oxidation of styrene to phenylacetate, common among various microorganisms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c4804d2c00d1d5fff2b89eaf6da26da</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHENYLACETATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Phenylacetate is a metabolic product formed from the oxidation of styrene, indicating a key step in the degradation of polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c4804d2c00d1d5fff2b89eaf6da26da</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SEM-ASSISTED WORKS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"SEM-assisted works refer to studies utilizing scanning electron microscopy techniques to document bacterial-driven transformations of plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c4804d2c00d1d5fff2b89eaf6da26da</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANNIBALISTIC BEHAVIORS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BEHAVIORAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cannibalistic behaviors are exhibited by T. molitor larvae when feeding solely on polystyrene for extended periods, highlighting nutritional deficiencies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c4804d2c00d1d5fff2b89eaf6da26da</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BODY SIZE REDUCTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Body size reduction occurs in T. molitor larvae due to insufficient nutrition when fed only polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c4804d2c00d1d5fff2b89eaf6da26da</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INTESTINAL FLORA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Intestinal flora refers to the microbial community in the gut of yellow mealworms, which changes significantly after ingesting different types of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Intestinal flora represents the community of microorganisms residing in the digestive tract, playing a role in the degradation of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"The intestinal flora of yellow mealworms plays a crucial role in the degradation of plastics, as bacterial strains isolated from this flora effectively break down plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c4804d2c00d1d5fff2b89eaf6da26da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a8521d10cd6a04d8ba536be9f9dec8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdb235a6eddd0a0e69be356e83362fc7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JAW CHANGES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Jaw changes describe the structural modifications occurring during the transition from larval to adult stages in T. molitor, affecting their ability to ingest certain materials."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c4804d2c00d1d5fff2b89eaf6da26da</data>
    </node>
