    <node id="&quot;TENEBRIO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A genus encompassing T. molitor and T. obscurus, both capable of LDPE degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"A genus of beetles, specifically T. obscurus and T. molitor, whose larvae were studied for their ability to degrade plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio is a genus comprising species like *T. molitor* and *T. obscurus*, whose larvae were studied for gut microbial community shifts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio is a genus mentioned in the keywords, likely associated with T. molitor, and relevant to the study of bacteria in the digestive tract."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio is a genus of beetles, commonly known as darkling beetles, which includes species like T. molitor and T. obscurus."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio is a genus of beetles, including species like T. molitor and T. obscurus, which have demonstrated the ability to degrade plastics such as PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio refers to larvae species studied for their gut microbiome's potential in plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio is a genus that includes T. molitor and T. obscurus, both of which exhibit plastic-degrading capabilities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d9095195e9cf06b9887c03abde6284d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f23046f647dab4d4caebd663db9aecde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d908d878ed4e7fc36f3af71a5be7f2ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89a76f613b36454134940f78fba1c0f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e276f74ca596eed69175a31dab0bf51b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b30daa90b5c91314e1d65e87f191166&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cbedc06292e5cf07fbca1958d8587e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88706f91768bcf0eaa7a49ef2d4b771f</data>
