      <data key="d1">"Conditions that negatively impact insect survival and development."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1ead6f17ad517015b638608c5bfe6852</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PALMITOLEIC ACID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FATTY ACID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A monounsaturated fatty acid found in higher proportions in OAT-fed larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1ead6f17ad517015b638608c5bfe6852</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MYRISTOLEIC ACID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FATTY ACID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A rare fatty acid with lower fractions observed in the OAT variant."&lt;SEP&gt;"Myristoleic acid is a monounsaturated fatty acid identified in mealworm fatty acid compositions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ee46611b24ea3848df979ded841f06b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ead6f17ad517015b638608c5bfe6852</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;L-ARABINOSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A nutrient positively correlated with the lignocellulose diet and the first ordination axis."&lt;SEP&gt;"A pentose sugar uniquely taken up by PE and PS groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"L-arabinose is a pentose sugar involved in various metabolic pathways."&lt;SEP&gt;"L-arabinose is an intermediate in the pentose phosphate pathway, utilized differently across diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"L-arabinose is one of the substrates from which acids are produced by Mixta tenebrionis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a38885f67ed46b97bb84086f575fd43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-146789a250a0dbaae0d8438de692e191&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f65bf081bdd3c6718fa0310993bfc0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a4712059883b356b4aea23cb7ef1514&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84297b844ec01d2f58756b669806fd62</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRYPTOPHAN DEAMINASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tryptophan deaminase is an enzyme involved in amino acid metabolism in mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tryptophan deaminase is an enzyme involved in tryptophan metabolism, showing differential activity across diets."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ee46611b24ea3848df979ded841f06b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a38885f67ed46b97bb84086f575fd43</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AMYGDALIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A glycoside metabolized by PE and PS groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"Amygdalin is a compound whose utilization varies depending on the diet."&lt;SEP&gt;"Amygdalin is a glycoside compound that could be metabolized by mealworm gut bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Amygdalin is a glycoside compound that may be metabolized by some bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Amygdalin is a glycoside that BIT-26T cannot utilize for acid production."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ee46611b24ea3848df979ded841f06b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a38885f67ed46b97bb84086f575fd43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d043948723ae25a365e297c98300be3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84297b844ec01d2f58756b669806fd62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-014b72d0a2657cbc89c4dee5f2b32bba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHENYLACTIC ACID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Phenylactic acid is a metabolite with differential utilization depending on the diet."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a38885f67ed46b97bb84086f575fd43</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRISODIUM CITRATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A metabolite negatively correlated with the lignocellulose diet and the first ordination axis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Trisodium citrate is a metabolite utilized differently across various diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Trisodium citrate is a salt form of citric acid, often used in biochemical reactions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Trisodium citrate is a salt form of citric acid, possibly utilized in mealworm energy metabolism."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ee46611b24ea3848df979ded841f06b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a38885f67ed46b97bb84086f575fd43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f65bf081bdd3c6718fa0310993bfc0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a4712059883b356b4aea23cb7ef1514</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UREASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An enzyme catalyzing the hydrolysis of urea, associated with PE-oxo and PS diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Urease is an enzyme involved in urea hydrolysis, showing variable activity levels across diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Urease is an enzyme that catalyzes the hydrolysis of urea into ammonia and carbon dioxide, contributing to nitrogen metabolism in mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Urease is an enzyme that catalyzes the hydrolysis of urea into ammonia and carbon dioxide."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ee46611b24ea3848df979ded841f06b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a38885f67ed46b97bb84086f575fd43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84297b844ec01d2f58756b669806fd62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-014b72d0a2657cbc89c4dee5f2b32bba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;D-MELIBIOSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A nutrient negatively correlated with the lignocellulose diet and the first ordination axis."&lt;SEP&gt;"D-melibiose is a disaccharide composed of galactose and glucose."&lt;SEP&gt;"D-melibiose is a disaccharide that is strongly utilized in the OAT variant."&lt;SEP&gt;"D-melibiose is a disaccharide that may be utilized by mealworm gut microorganisms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ee46611b24ea3848df979ded841f06b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a38885f67ed46b97bb84086f575fd43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f65bf081bdd3c6718fa0310993bfc0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a4712059883b356b4aea23cb7ef1514</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INOSITOL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Inositol is a compound with high utilization capacity in the PS variant."&lt;SEP&gt;"Inositol is a cyclic sugar alcohol involved in cell signaling and structural roles."&lt;SEP&gt;"Inositol is a cyclic sugar alcohol that plays a role in mealworm cellular functions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ee46611b24ea3848df979ded841f06b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a38885f67ed46b97bb84086f575fd43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a4712059883b356b4aea23cb7ef1514</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DECANOIC ACID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FATTY ACID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A metabolite negatively correlated with the lignocellulose diet and the first ordination axis."&lt;SEP&gt;"A saturated fatty acid consumed by microbiota in the PE-oxo diet."&lt;SEP&gt;"Decanoic acid is a fatty acid highly utilized in the PE-oxo variant."&lt;SEP&gt;"Decanoic acid is a medium-chain saturated fatty acid present in mealworm lipid content."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ee46611b24ea3848df979ded841f06b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a38885f67ed46b97bb84086f575fd43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f65bf081bdd3c6718fa0310993bfc0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84297b844ec01d2f58756b669806fd62</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ACETOIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A product of fermentation produced by microbiota in CEL variant diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Acetoin is a product with high production potential in the CEL variant."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a38885f67ed46b97bb84086f575fd43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84297b844ec01d2f58756b669806fd62</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADIPIC ACID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A metabolite positively correlated with the lignocellulose diet and the first ordination axis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Adipic acid is a compound utilized by larvae in the CEL variant."&lt;SEP&gt;"Adipic acid is a dicarboxylic acid that may be involved in mealworm metabolic processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"An organic compound consumed by microbiota in CEL variant diets."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ee46611b24ea3848df979ded841f06b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a38885f67ed46b97bb84086f575fd43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f65bf081bdd3c6718fa0310993bfc0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84297b844ec01d2f58756b669806fd62</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;D-SORBITOL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A sugar alcohol utilized by microbiota in the PE-oxo diet."&lt;SEP&gt;"D-sorbitol is a metabolite with differential utilization across various diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"D-sorbitol is a sugar alcohol potentially involved in mealworm energy metabolism."&lt;SEP&gt;"D-sorbitol is a sugar alcohol used as a carbohydrate source by some microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"d-Sorbitol is a sugar alcohol that can be metabolized by certain bacteria."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ee46611b24ea3848df979ded841f06b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a38885f67ed46b97bb84086f575fd43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a4712059883b356b4aea23cb7ef1514&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84297b844ec01d2f58756b669806fd62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-014b72d0a2657cbc89c4dee5f2b32bba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UREASE ACTIVITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL FUNCTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Urease activity varies across different diets, indicating diet-specific effects on enzyme functionality."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a38885f67ed46b97bb84086f575fd43</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DECANOIC ACID UTILIZATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Decanoic acid utilization is prominent in the PE-oxo variant, reflecting specific metabolic adaptations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a38885f67ed46b97bb84086f575fd43</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CORE TRAITS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Core traits refer to biochemical parameters that remain constant across treatments, identified as 15 out of 31 traits in this study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a38885f67ed46b97bb84086f575fd43</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIFFERENTIATION TRAITS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Differentiation traits are biochemical parameters that vary depending on the diet and activity levels, forming 7 distinct branches."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a38885f67ed46b97bb84086f575fd43</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRAY-CURTIS DISSIMILARITIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bray-Curtis dissimilarities quantify differences between groups, showing the greatest variation for biometrics, gene numbers, and microbiome composition."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a38885f67ed46b97bb84086f575fd43</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EUCLIDEAN CLUSTERING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Euclidean clustering is a method used to group diets based on overall results, revealing high dissimilarity (approx. 100) among the diets."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a38885f67ed46b97bb84086f575fd43</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POTASSIUM GLUCONATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Potassium gluconate is a salt used in mealworm nutrient analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Potassium gluconate is utilized differently across diets, with low or no utilization observed in the CEL variant."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ee46611b24ea3848df979ded841f06b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a38885f67ed46b97bb84086f575fd43</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIGESTIVE SYSTEM CAPACITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Digestive system capacity varies significantly across diets, with CEL showing the most distinct profile."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a38885f67ed46b97bb84086f575fd43</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CENTRAL METABOLISM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Central Metabolism refers to the pathways that produce precursor metabolites, reducing power, and metabolic energy necessary for cellular function."&lt;SEP&gt;"The core metabolic pathways essential for cellular energy production and biosynthesis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-84297b844ec01d2f58756b669806fd62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0e30f29e9016acae216566f53e60cea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CLOSTRIDIALES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORDER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An order characteristic of OAT and PE-reg diets, linked to anaerobic metabolism."&lt;SEP&gt;"Clostridiales is an order of Gram-positive bacteria often associated with anaerobic environments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Clostridiales is an order of bacteria with an average abundance of 14.5%, higher in the OAT diet."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-84297b844ec01d2f58756b669806fd62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a4712059883b356b4aea23cb7ef1514&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0e30f29e9016acae216566f53e60cea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LACTOBACILLALES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORDER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An order associated with PE-oxo and PS diets, involved in lactate fermentation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lactobacillales is an order of Gram-positive bacteria commonly found in fermented foods and the gut."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lactobacillales is an order of bacteria with an average of 10.5%, more prolific in PE-oxo, PE-reg, and PS groups."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-84297b844ec01d2f58756b669806fd62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a4712059883b356b4aea23cb7ef1514&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0e30f29e9016acae216566f53e60cea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SELENOMONADALES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORDER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An order uniquely increased in CEL-fed groups, indicating distinct microbial compositions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Selenomonadales has a mean abundance of 3.0%, with the highest levels in the CEL group."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-84297b844ec01d2f58756b669806fd62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0e30f29e9016acae216566f53e60cea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RHODOBACTERALES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORDER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An order characteristic of the PE-oxo diet, indicating specific metabolic activities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rhodobacterales has a mean abundance of 3.9%, with the highest levels in OAT and PE-oxo groups."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-84297b844ec01d2f58756b669806fd62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0e30f29e9016acae216566f53e60cea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NITROSIRIPLAS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORDER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nitrosiriplas is an order with an average abundance of 1.5%, highest in the PS variant."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f0e30f29e9016acae216566f53e60cea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLANCTOMYCETALES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORDER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An order characteristic of PS diets, involved in unique metabolic pathways."&lt;SEP&gt;"An order of bacteria positively correlated with the PS diet and the second ordination axis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Planctomycetales is an order with an average abundance of 9.9%, highest in the PS variant."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-84297b844ec01d2f58756b669806fd62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f65bf081bdd3c6718fa0310993bfc0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0e30f29e9016acae216566f53e60cea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CORIOBACTERIALES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORDER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Coriobacteriales has an average abundance of 1.8%, lower in the PS group."&lt;SEP&gt;"Coriobacteriales is a bacterial order associated with lipid metabolism in mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ee46611b24ea3848df979ded841f06b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0e30f29e9016acae216566f53e60cea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPHINGOBACTERIALES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORDER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sphingobacteriales has a low abundance with a mean of 1.3%, not varying by diet."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sphingobacteriales is another bacterial order identified in mealworm guts, aiding in polymer digestion."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sphingobacteriales is another bacterial order identified in mealworm guts, contributing to the digestion of synthetic polymers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ee46611b24ea3848df979ded841f06b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0e30f29e9016acae216566f53e60cea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AMOA GENE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A gene responsible for nitrogen metabolism, positively correlated with the PS diet and protein levels in larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"The amoA gene is responsible for nitrogen metabolism, positively correlated with the PS diet in PCA analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6f65bf081bdd3c6718fa0310993bfc0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0e30f29e9016acae216566f53e60cea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CLOSTRIDIUM BACTERIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of bacteria present in the digestive system of larvae, negatively correlated with the PS diet and the first ordination axis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Clostridium bacteria are negatively correlated with the PS diet in PCA analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6f65bf081bdd3c6718fa0310993bfc0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0e30f29e9016acae216566f53e60cea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OAT DIET&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DIET"</data>
