    <node id="&quot;NIFH GENE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A gene encoding enzymes involved in nitrogenase activity, crucial for nitrogen fixation."&lt;SEP&gt;"A gene negatively correlated with the lignocellulose diet and the first ordination axis."&lt;SEP&gt;"The nifH gene encodes a subunit of nitrogenase, an enzyme involved in the biological nitrogen fixation process."&lt;SEP&gt;"The nifH gene encodes dinitrogen reductase, an enzyme essential for nitrogen fixation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The nifH gene is associated with nitrogenase enzymes and is detected using PCR amplification."&lt;SEP&gt;"The nifH gene is responsible for encoding the nitrogenase enzyme complex necessary for nitrogen fixation."&lt;SEP&gt;"nifH Gene encodes a protein essential for nitrogenase activity, enabling nitrogen fixation in certain bacteria."</data>
