      <data key="d2">chunk-566afea8a2a89bd188f68d0afa1bb173</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARBON CHAINS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Carbon chains are structural components of polypropylene that hinder its degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-566afea8a2a89bd188f68d0afa1bb173</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PP (POLYPROPYLENE)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PP is a type of plastic polymer associated with Spiroplasma dominance and specific microbial communities."&lt;SEP&gt;"PP is a type of plastic that exhibits high resistance to degradation and is studied for its biodegradation by larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"PP is a type of plastic that significantly alters the gut bacterial community when consumed, leading to an increase in specific bacterial families and genera."&lt;SEP&gt;"PP refers to polypropylene, a type of plastic that was fed to the larvae for studying its biodegradation process."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a3f07da33b55bf8a25fe06beee23e90e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-476e13b69587aa4e81395e2fd00a9d5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31b2c5f608adabba1cc6986356e96598&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4265fd894f71345b4ef09c26e6adbda5</data>
    </node>
