    <node id="&quot;MEALWORM GUT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ECOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Mealworm Gut is the digestive system of Tenebrio molitor larvae, where polystyrene undergoes biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The digestive system of mealworms involved in enzymatic activity and microbial community adaptation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The mealworm gut refers to the digestive system of mealworms where plastics undergo biodegradation with the help of gut microbes."&lt;SEP&gt;"The mealworm gut is an ecological niche where microorganisms like Strain LG3 reside and contribute to the degradation of polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-457d054c08a16428ed81526fc2ddce41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38e212e8bab88c4d7b6d63a157e27c00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2c62bcfb28547d6b2336f142d27a326&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d80979bb7e58b10bb558705b5d96fa99</data>
    </node>
