      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Growth inhibition describes the reduced ability of larvae to grow and develop properly due to exposure to certain types of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Growth inhibition occurs when mealworms experience reduced weight gain due to poor nutrition from excessive plastic ingestion."&lt;SEP&gt;"Growth inhibition refers to the slowing or cessation of growth due to inadequate nutrition or toxic exposure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Growth inhibition refers to the reduced growth of larvae due to microplastic consumption."</data>
