      <data key="d1">"CFUs (Colony-Forming Units) are measures of viable bacterial or fungal numbers, indicating microbial activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"CFUs refer to colony-forming units, a measure of viable bacterial cells in the gut microbiota."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colony Forming Units (CFUs) are used to quantify microbial populations in samples from T. molitor larvae guts."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1d39fc863538a777920c4eafb37bcf8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c84ac252cb9ce906354bda2ad1113aba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a88f3ed3eec20cee61421cc094dde89f</data>
    </node>
