      <data key="d2">chunk-c84ac252cb9ce906354bda2ad1113aba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RT-QPCR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"RT-qPCR is a technique used to quantify the copy number of specific DNA sequences, assessing microbial abundance."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c84ac252cb9ce906354bda2ad1113aba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PVC FOAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PVC foam is another type of plastic material studied for its effects on mealworm weight and survival."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c84ac252cb9ce906354bda2ad1113aba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SYNERGETIC ROLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Synergetic role refers to the combined action of host enzymes and gut microbiota in breaking down plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c84ac252cb9ce906354bda2ad1113aba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LDPE PLASTIC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"LDPE (Low-Density Polyethylene) is a type of plastic that differs from PS in terms of microbial degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c84ac252cb9ce906354bda2ad1113aba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HOST ENZYMES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Host enzymes are proteins produced by the mealworms that contribute to the depolymerization of plastics like PS."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e155a60beeedb5736450fdc1ffa4699e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;C=O&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNCTIONAL GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"C=O represents a functional group identified in the FTIR spectra, indicating depolymerization processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"C=O represents the carbonyl functional group detected in FTIR spectra of frass from PS-fed larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"The C=O stretching vibration is observed at 1643 cm\(^{-1}\), indicating carbonyl group involvement."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9859524b7a6851b786570d2a704e34f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e155a60beeedb5736450fdc1ffa4699e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-013f364e92a266c0e922cb0582f7a997</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;C-O&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNCTIONAL GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"C-O indicates the carbon-oxygen single bond found in FTIR spectra analysis of frass from both PS- and CS-fed larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"C-O represents a chemical bond detected in the FTIR spectra analysis, indicating oxidation processes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e155a60beeedb5736450fdc1ffa4699e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-013f364e92a266c0e922cb0582f7a997</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;R-OH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNCTIONAL GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"R-OH represents hydroxyl groups identified in FTIR spectra of frass from PS-fed larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"R-OH signifies hydroxyl groups detected in the FTIR spectra, suggesting oxidation and depolymerization processes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e155a60beeedb5736450fdc1ffa4699e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-013f364e92a266c0e922cb0582f7a997</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EDS MAPPING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"EDS mapping identifies elements like carbon, oxygen, and nitrogen in the frass of PS- and CS-fed larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e155a60beeedb5736450fdc1ffa4699e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GC–MS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"GC–MS (gas chromatography–mass spectrometry) is used to profile degradation intermediates of PS and CS in larval gut and frass samples."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e155a60beeedb5736450fdc1ffa4699e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LC–MS/MS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"LC–MS/MS (liquid chromatography–tandem mass spectrometry) is employed for comparative metabolomic analysis to characterize differential metabolites in larval gut samples."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e155a60beeedb5736450fdc1ffa4699e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LARVAL GUT MICROBIOTA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Larval gut microbiota refers to the microorganisms present in the digestive system of mealworm larvae, contributing to plastic degradation processes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e155a60beeedb5736450fdc1ffa4699e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BENZENE, 1,3-DIMETHYL-(C8H10)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Benzene, 1,3-dimethyl-(C8H10) is a compound whose relative abundance decreases in the frass or intestinal samples of PS-fed larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e155a60beeedb5736450fdc1ffa4699e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CYCLOHEXENE (C6H12)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cyclohexene (C6H12) is a compound observed in the larval gut and frass samples, with decreased abundance in PS-fed larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e155a60beeedb5736450fdc1ffa4699e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHTHALIC ACID (C26H42O4)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
