      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Unclassified Enterobacteriaceae is a common genus across all test groups, contributing to the gut bacterial community."&lt;SEP&gt;"Unclassified Enterobacteriaceae is a group within Enterobacteriaceae family, strongly associated with plastics degradation in superworms Z. atratus larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Unclassified Enterobacteriaceae shows higher abundance in PS-fed larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Unidentified members of the Enterobacteriaceae family are prevalent gut-associated microbes in yellow mealworms and dark mealworms, playing a role in gut microbial composition."&lt;SEP&gt;"Unclassified Enterobacteriaceae was dominant in PU-fed groups, showing strong association with PU degradation and other plastic degradation processes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a3f07da33b55bf8a25fe06beee23e90e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-476e13b69587aa4e81395e2fd00a9d5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df045e015825dac8935c9c6d8a402cda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a91a3c11281861b559c31c3107c72e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81f09d7c1a5d91a7a0b4766ca0e47f56</data>
