    <node id="&quot;CRYSTALLINITY DEGREE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A measure of the crystalline regions in a polymer, impacting its susceptibility to microbial degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Crystallinity degree of PE contributes to changes in gut microbiome structure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Crystallinity degree affects the biodegradability of polyethylene, where higher crystallinity negatively impacts depolymerization."&lt;SEP&gt;"Crystallinity degree describes the structural organization of polymers, affecting their degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Crystallinity degree is a parameter that influences the biodegradation of PE polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Crystallinity degree measures the level of crystalline structure in polymers, influencing their stability and susceptibility to degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-326a8dda1cdd196236b9c836192c76f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e24cc3865ed97850c3f25795ff514e8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3380732c060363504db5f6e4b8610b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f75b58db5211fc7348ccca8206b9bbae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-988ef111808996ddbe6e483d6505ab45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e1faf524e6fabeb512a07b13f37e51e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1H NMR ANALYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL REACTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"1H NMR analysis is used to study the incorporation of oxygen and breakdown of long-chain PE polymers in the frass samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nuclear magnetic resonance analysis used to study structural modifications in PET after biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e24cc3865ed97850c3f25795ff514e8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98d4ea946a931acf7e5a8292c30ea4c7</data>
    </node>
