      <data key="d1">"1H NMR Spectra is used to analyze residual PET from frass, revealing new singlets related to oxidation and indicating modifications in the PET molecular structure."&lt;SEP&gt;"1H NMR spectra are utilized to examine residual PE polymers from the frass of larvae consuming LLDPE, LDPE, and HDPE."&lt;SEP&gt;"1H NMR Spectra provide insights into molecular structure changes in PS residues, detecting carbonyl and hydroxyl groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"1H NMR spectra detect specific hydrogen-containing groups, revealing transformations in PS structure during biodegradation."</data>
