      <data key="d1">"Root sepsis is a condition caused by infection, often associated with Sebaellida termitidis in certain animals."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1fd138e047a780efd715a5ab4701b58c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANAEROBIC DEGRADING BACTERIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Anaerobic degrading bacteria are microorganisms capable of breaking down organic polymers under oxygen-free conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1fd138e047a780efd715a5ab4701b58c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PANTOEA SP.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pantoea sp. is a bacterium known for its ability to increase amino acid contents in plant tissues, facilitating ammonium excretion and nitrogenase activity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-81610bdb5fdb95d9a333b42668532b9f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SERINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"AMINO ACID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Serine is an amino acid that plays a role in biological processes such as protein synthesis and metabolic pathways."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-81610bdb5fdb95d9a333b42668532b9f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALANINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"AMINO ACID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Alanine is an amino acid involved in energy production and the regulation of blood sugar levels."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alanine is an amino acid whose metabolic pathway was altered due to plastic exposure."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-81610bdb5fdb95d9a333b42668532b9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-939800f545beed77f5a7d1c026c250fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GLUTAMINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"AMINO ACID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Glutamine is an essential amino acid crucial for protein synthesis and cellular energy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-81610bdb5fdb95d9a333b42668532b9f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ASPARAGINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"AMINO ACID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Asparagine is an amino acid involved in the metabolism of proteins and the regulation of gene expression."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-81610bdb5fdb95d9a333b42668532b9f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANDIDA ANTARCTICA (CALB)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNGUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Candida antarctica (CALB) produces lipase enzymes that can act synergistically with other enzymes for PET hydrolysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-81610bdb5fdb95d9a333b42668532b9f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HUMICOLA INSOLENS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNGUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Humicola insolens produces cutinase enzymes that work synergistically with lipases for the breakdown of PET plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-81610bdb5fdb95d9a333b42668532b9f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THERMOBIFIDA FUSCA KWS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Thermobifida fusca KWS produces carboxylesterase enzymes capable of hydrolyzing cyclic poly(ethylene terephthalate) trimers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-81610bdb5fdb95d9a333b42668532b9f</data>
    </node>
