      <data key="d1">"GPC (gel permeation chromatography) analyses indicate limited depolymerization patterns during PP biodegradation by T. molitor and Z. atratus larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"GPC confirms that PET depolymerization continues even under antibiotic suppression, indicating host-independent degradation."</data>
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOLOGICAL PROCESSES&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-d290a6a81802d3048c35d2a2fb1252c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2961e2aad708e7b78a585260097b4d2e</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biological processes describe the mechanisms by which microorganisms degrade nanopolystyrene, altering its physical properties."&lt;SEP&gt;"Transmembrane transporter activity plays a key role in various biological processes such as nutrient uptake and waste removal."</data>
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENERGY PRODUCTION&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-d290a6a81802d3048c35d2a2fb1252c4</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pyruvate metabolism is vital for energy production, linking glycolysis to the citrate cycle and other metabolic pathways."</data>
      <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENE REGULATION&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-d290a6a81802d3048c35d2a2fb1252c4</data>
      <data key="d1">"Purine metabolism influences gene regulation and DNA synthesis, highlighting its importance in cellular processes."</data>
      <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
    </node>
