      <data key="d2">chunk-d290a6a81802d3048c35d2a2fb1252c4</data>
      <data key="d1">"Glycolysis and gluconeogenesis maintain energy balance by regulating glucose levels in cells and tissues."</data>
      <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NEURAL SIGNALING&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-d290a6a81802d3048c35d2a2fb1252c4</data>
      <data key="d1">"Neuroactive ligand-receptor interaction is crucial for neural signaling, enabling communication between neurons and target cells."</data>
      <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CELL WALL SYNTHESIS&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-d290a6a81802d3048c35d2a2fb1252c4</data>
      <data key="d1">"Amino sugar and nucleotide sugar metabolism are essential for cell wall synthesis and glycoprotein formation in organisms."</data>
      <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AMINO ACID&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-81610bdb5fdb95d9a333b42668532b9f</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pantoea sp. increases the content of amino acids like serine, alanine, glutamine, and asparagine in plant tissues, enhancing ammonium excretion and nitrogenase activity."</data>
      <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PET HYDROLYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-81610bdb5fdb95d9a333b42668532b9f</data>
      <data key="d1">"Candida antarctica (CALB) produces lipase enzymes that act synergistically with cutinase for the hydrolysis of PET plastics."</data>
      <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICROPLASTICS DEGRADATION&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-81610bdb5fdb95d9a333b42668532b9f</data>
      <data key="d1">"The metagenomic approach helps identify microorganisms potentially involved in the degradation of microplastics."</data>
      <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BENZOQUINONE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A compound whose production in Tribolium confusum has been genetically analyzed for its ecological and biochemical roles."&lt;SEP&gt;"Benzoquinone is a compound measured in the biomass composition of larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Benzoquinone is a compound whose concentration increases in larvae fed with polyethylene, suggesting metabolic changes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-276c82b9935756a3e668c788458ff922&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-acbe3a2cb3a17985d07d15bed638bd90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98d4ea946a931acf7e5a8292c30ea4c7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INTESTINAL TISSUE DAMAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Intestinal tissue damage is an adverse effect observed in larvae fed with polyethylene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-acbe3a2cb3a17985d07d15bed638bd90</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RATTUS NORVEGICUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANISM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rattus norvegicus (brown rat) is used as a model organism for evaluating acute oral toxicity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rattus norvegicus, commonly known as brown rats, is used in ecotoxicological studies to evaluate the effects of polyethylene degradation products."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-acbe3a2cb3a17985d07d15bed638bd90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b693d867918f89c9b28997fe94fc830</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ECOTOXICOLOGICAL SIMULATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An ecotoxicological simulation is a process used to study the potential toxic effects of substances on ecosystems and organisms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-acbe3a2cb3a17985d07d15bed638bd90</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;T.E.S.T.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"T.E.S.T. is a specific ecotoxicological simulation method used to confirm the ecotoxicity of polyethylene degradation products."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-acbe3a2cb3a17985d07d15bed638bd90</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHYSICAL AND CHEMICAL PROPERTIES (PCPS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Physical and chemical properties refer to the characteristics of polyethylene that influence its degradability and interaction with organisms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-acbe3a2cb3a17985d07d15bed638bd90</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRANCHING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Branching describes the structure of polyethylene chains, influencing its physical properties and suitability for various applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Branching refers to the structural complexity of polymers, affecting their biodegradation potential."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-30a7209d626a6319ba5600bea7f27299&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-acbe3a2cb3a17985d07d15bed638bd90</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WEIGHT CHANGES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Weight Changes refer to the alterations in the body weight of larvae after consuming different types of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Weight changes in larvae fed with polyethylene indicate the impact of the material on their growth and metabolism."&lt;SEP&gt;"Weight changes reflect alterations in larval weights due to diet and development stages."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a38c714e7f1f701ec1149e25910e16e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-acbe3a2cb3a17985d07d15bed638bd90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b21eb0db725b38c3e0b5c01526ce90b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPODOPTERA FRUGIPERDA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"INSECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Spodoptera frugiperda (fall armyworm) has demonstrated the potential to biodegrade PE."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ffb4e34985ec90215629dc19750c8bdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THERMAL OR PHOTO-OXIDATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL REACTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Thermal or photo-oxidation processes are prerequisites for the biodegradation of PE in natural environments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ffb4e34985ec90215629dc19750c8bdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PS STYROFOAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polystyrene (PS) styrofoam is a type of plastic that can be biodegraded by certain insects."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ffb4e34985ec90215629dc19750c8bdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARBON ATOMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Carbon atoms are fundamental building blocks in organic molecules, forming strong chemical bonds with other atoms to create complex structures such as polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon atoms are structural components of polymers and influence the properties and degradability of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon atoms form the backbone of polyethylene polymers and play a crucial role in determining their physical properties."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ffb4e34985ec90215629dc19750c8bdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-326a8dda1cdd196236b9c836192c76f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab6b219720db5a6e3384c884c280984c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mice are utilized in research to examine inflammatory responses caused by microplastic exposure."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d8c6850a83a1c6efd4f1a3a37a0a8181</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLASTIC DEGRADATION INTERMEDIATES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"These intermediates are formed during the degradation of plastics by insect larvae and may influence larval physiology."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d8c6850a83a1c6efd4f1a3a37a0a8181</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AQUATIC AND TERRESTRIAL ORGANISMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ECOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"These organisms could be affected by toxic substances excreted in the frass of plastic-degrading larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d8c6850a83a1c6efd4f1a3a37a0a8181</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FENTON SYSTEM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Fenton system is employed to extract PE-MPs from frass material after grinding."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-aa33fb34ba06610c290cdfd8a5b4e916</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OLIVE OIL-BASED EXTRACTION METHOD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An olive oil-based extraction method complements the Fenton system for extracting PE-MPs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-aa33fb34ba06610c290cdfd8a5b4e916</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARBONYL INDEX (CI)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CI evaluates oxidation levels of PE-MPs through carbonyl peak intensity."&lt;SEP&gt;"CI measures the degree of aging in polymers, correlating positively with microbial community growth."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-582f48080aab075de76c9c590558639f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa33fb34ba06610c290cdfd8a5b4e916</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROTON NUCLEAR MAGNETIC RESONANCE (NMR)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"NMR spectrometry analyzes proton nuclear magnetic resonance properties of PE-MPs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-aa33fb34ba06610c290cdfd8a5b4e916</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PYROLYSIS-GAS CHROMATOGRAPHY/MASS SPECTROMETRY (PY-GC/MS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Py-GC/MS involves pyrolyzing PE-MPs and analyzing their components via gas chromatography and mass spectrometry."&lt;SEP&gt;"Py-GC/MS studies differences in chemical composition between original PE samples and residual PE polymers in frass."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6afbb58ebe9108893daf7e65d59fac39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa33fb34ba06610c290cdfd8a5b4e916</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CRUDE FATS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Crude fats are lipids with their total concentrations determined according to GB 5009.6–2016."&lt;SEP&gt;"Crude fats are measured as part of the larval biomass nutrient concentration."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9b693d867918f89c9b28997fe94fc830&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa33fb34ba06610c290cdfd8a5b4e916</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CRUDE PROTEINS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Crude proteins are assessed in the larval biomass composition analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Crude proteins are proteins whose total concentrations were determined based on GB/T 6433-2006."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9b693d867918f89c9b28997fe94fc830&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa33fb34ba06610c290cdfd8a5b4e916</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TENEBRIO LARVAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tenebrio larvae are model organisms used to study oxidative stress induced by PE microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio larvae, including T. obscurus and T. molitor, are central to the biodegradation experiments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a24fcfbc571e8620a1fc59b215b42e56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa33fb34ba06610c290cdfd8a5b4e916</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PE-MPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PE-MPs (Polyethylene Microplastics) are the microplastic particles derived from HDPE, LLDPE, and LDPE."&lt;SEP&gt;"PE-MPs (polyethylene microplastics) are analyzed for their impact on larval metabolism and oxidative stress."&lt;SEP&gt;"PE-MPs refers to polyethylene microplastics that are consumed and biodegraded by the larvae of T. molitor and T. obscurus."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene microplastics (PE-MPs) are metabolites that induce oxidative stress and ecotoxicity in T. obscurus and T. molitor larvae when ingested."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene microplastics (PE-MPs) serve as a carbon-rich oligotrophic substance, providing an energy and carbon source for Tenebrio larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-90367ecb21e0f14b2e548acf307a2628&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b693d867918f89c9b28997fe94fc830&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa33fb34ba06610c290cdfd8a5b4e916&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd4d84d6de496440fcabc6616d1c96ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ac1b1db6ffab6f4cfea7a525785a2fc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ARTIFICIAL CLIMATE CHAMBER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EQUIPMENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An artificial climate chamber is used to maintain controlled environmental conditions during experiments."&lt;SEP&gt;"The artificial climate chamber maintains controlled conditions for larval incubation."&lt;SEP&gt;"An artificial climate chamber maintained at 25.0 ± 0.5 °C with 65 ± 5% humidity, used to incubate larvae during the experiment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8ee8f544a1849c80a5a1524c4f2674c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30a7209d626a6319ba5600bea7f27299&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa33fb34ba06610c290cdfd8a5b4e916</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NICOLET IS50 FTIR SPECTROMETER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
