      <data key="d2">chunk-9b693d867918f89c9b28997fe94fc830</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPECR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"SPECR represents specific polymer consumption rates, indicating how much PE polymer is consumed per day by the larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bd4d84d6de496440fcabc6616d1c96ff</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AWCRS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"AWCRs denote average weight change rates, reflecting changes in larval weight over the test period."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bd4d84d6de496440fcabc6616d1c96ff</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NIA MAGNA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TOXIN"</data>
      <data key="d1">"nia magna is a substance with potential developmental toxicity, as indicated by its LC50 value."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bd4d84d6de496440fcabc6616d1c96ff</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ORIGIN (V. 2022B)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"SOFTWARE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Origin (v. 2022b) is the software used for statistical analysis in this study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bd4d84d6de496440fcabc6616d1c96ff</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;C-O-C GROUPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNCTIONAL GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"C-O-C groups are oxidative functional groups detected through FTIR analysis during the biodegradation process."&lt;SEP&gt;"C-O-C groups represent ether functional groups identified through FTIR analysis, indicating oxidative changes in the plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1b21eb0db725b38c3e0b5c01526ce90b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd4d84d6de496440fcabc6616d1c96ff</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARBOXYLIC ACIDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Carboxylic acids are organic compounds containing a carboxyl functional group (-COOH), detected in the plastics through FTIR analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carboxylic acids are oxidative functional groups formed during the biodegradation of PE polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carboxylic acids are organic compounds present in the mealworm fecula, likely resulting from biodegradation processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carboxylic acids are organic compounds released from PVC, contributing to the mass reduction in mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ff201df58dec460c49cd31920c29f11a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-069f8447676509ffdd0028e9c05fb9ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b21eb0db725b38c3e0b5c01526ce90b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd4d84d6de496440fcabc6616d1c96ff</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KETONES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TOXIN"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ketones are organic compounds with a carbonyl group (C=O) bonded to two hydrocarbon groups, identified in the plastics through FTIR analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ketones are oxidative functional groups identified during the biodegradation process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ketones are toxic compounds that can cause serious health hazards."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1b21eb0db725b38c3e0b5c01526ce90b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bd104d06a1ede06701ecfa96bccc2c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd4d84d6de496440fcabc6616d1c96ff</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALDEHYDES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNCTIONAL GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Aldehydes are organic compounds containing a formyl group (-CHO), detected in the plastics through FTIR analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1b21eb0db725b38c3e0b5c01526ce90b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LACTONES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNCTIONAL GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lactones are cyclic esters formed by the intramolecular esterification of hydroxycarboxylic acids, identified in the plastics through FTIR analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1b21eb0db725b38c3e0b5c01526ce90b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPECIFIC PE CONSUMPTION RATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Specific PE consumption rate quantifies the amount of polyethylene consumed per 100 larvae over a 21-day period."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1b21eb0db725b38c3e0b5c01526ce90b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RESIDUAL PE IN FRASS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Residual PE in frass represents the percentage of undigested polyethylene remaining in the waste excreted by the larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1b21eb0db725b38c3e0b5c01526ce90b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CI (Carbonyl Index) measures the degree of oxidation in the residual polymers, reflecting the extent of chemical modification."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1b21eb0db725b38c3e0b5c01526ce90b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARBONYL INDEX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Carbonyl Index (CI) is a measure of oxidation levels in plastics during aging and degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbonyl Index measures the degree of oxidation in plastics, reflecting the extent of chemical modification during biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The carbonyl index measures oxidation levels in residual PE polymers found in the frass of larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"The carbonyl index measures the degree of oxidation in nanoplastics, with higher values indicating greater degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbonyl index measures the degree of oxidation in PE, indicating its biodegradation progress."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbonyl index quantifies oxidative degradation of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"The carbonyl index measures the degree of oxidation on the surface of microplastics, indicating degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bdc8398efba587929eebd0a0842f6e69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98d4ea946a931acf7e5a8292c30ea4c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbf098ec253f99187f3c98d5d0589f7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39596f0742e3d89f278017df88b8065b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b21eb0db725b38c3e0b5c01526ce90b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3fe22bd6c91507d8d1e60d24886e0eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b25215becbc007a60f24b86a2d6aaf26</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VIRGIN LLDPE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Virgin LLDPE represents the initial state of Linear Low-Density Polyethylene before undergoing biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1b21eb0db725b38c3e0b5c01526ce90b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VIRGIN HDPE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Virgin HDPE represents the initial state of High-Density Polyethylene before being subjected to biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1b21eb0db725b38c3e0b5c01526ce90b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AMINOIC GROUPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNCTIONAL GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Aminoic groups are one of the oxygen-containing functional groups identified in the biodegradation process."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-98d4ea946a931acf7e5a8292c30ea4c7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALDEHYDE GROUPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNCTIONAL GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Aldehyde groups are part of the oxygen-containing functional groups incorporated into the PE polymers during biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-98d4ea946a931acf7e5a8292c30ea4c7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;METHYL GROUPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNCTIONAL GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Methyl groups are identified as part of the chemical changes occurring in PE polymers during biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-98d4ea946a931acf7e5a8292c30ea4c7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNSATURATED ALLYLIC GROUPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNCTIONAL GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Unsaturated allylic groups are observed in the biodegradation process, indicating specific chemical transformations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-98d4ea946a931acf7e5a8292c30ea4c7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PENG ET AL., 2019&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"STUDY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A previous study by Peng et al. (2019) explored the ability of T. molitor and T. obscurus to oxidize PS."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-98d4ea946a931acf7e5a8292c30ea4c7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DING ET AL., 2023&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"STUDY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A study by Ding et al. (2023) highlighted the nutritional composition differences between T. molitor and T. obscurus."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-98d4ea946a931acf7e5a8292c30ea4c7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PENG ET AL., 2023A&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"STUDY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Another recent study by Peng et al. (2023a) further examined the Cys content differences between T. molitor and T. obscurus."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-98d4ea946a931acf7e5a8292c30ea4c7</data>
    </node>
