    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICROBIAL COMMUNITY ASSEMBLY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Microbial community assembly describes the formation and structuring of microbial populations in the larval gut environment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbial community assembly refers to the stochastic process by which diverse microbial populations form within the mealworm gut microbiome."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-896c5c0e4d1805ded38b335876a02f78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f23046f647dab4d4caebd663db9aecde</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ΒNTI/RCBRAY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"βNTI/RCbray measures beta-null turnover and community structure, helping assess differences among microbial communities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f23046f647dab4d4caebd663db9aecde</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WATER CONTACT ANGLES (WCA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Water contact angles measure surface properties, potentially influenced by microbial interactions with materials."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f23046f647dab4d4caebd663db9aecde</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SIMPSON DIVERSITY INDEX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Simpson Diversity Index quantifies biodiversity by accounting for richness and evenness of species in a community."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f23046f647dab4d4caebd663db9aecde</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEIP EVENNESS INDEX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Heip Evenness Index evaluates the evenness of species distribution within a community, providing insights into ecological balance."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f23046f647dab4d4caebd663db9aecde</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LEVINS OTU ABUNDANCE MATRIX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Levins OTU abundance matrix assesses niche breadth, indicating how OTUs interact with their environment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f23046f647dab4d4caebd663db9aecde</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;Β DIVERSITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"β Diversity measures differences in microbial community composition between samples, reflecting environmental influences."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f23046f647dab4d4caebd663db9aecde</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PARTIAL LEAST SQUARES PATH MODELING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Partial Least Squares Path Modeling is a statistical method used to analyze complex relationships among variables, such as gut microbiota and molecular weight changes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f23046f647dab4d4caebd663db9aecde</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BACTEROIDOTA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bacteroidota are a phylum of bacteria observed in the gut microbiomes of mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6ac1b1db6ffab6f4cfea7a525785a2fc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PERMANOVA ANALYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PERMANOVA (Permutational Multivariate Analysis of Variance) is a statistical method used to analyze differences in multivariate datasets, often applied to ecological studies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6ac1b1db6ffab6f4cfea7a525785a2fc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRAY-CURTIS DISSIMILARITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bray-Curtis dissimilarity is a statistical measure used to quantify the compositional difference between two samples."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6ac1b1db6ffab6f4cfea7a525785a2fc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NICHE WIDTH&quot;">
