    <node id="&quot;BLACK SOLDIER FLY (BSF)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"INSECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"BSF larvae are cosmopolitan and applied to upcycle many organic substrates, lacking well-developed mandibles and focusing degradation potential on enzymes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Black Soldier Fly larvae were used in the study and exhibited specific metabolic responses when exposed to plastics like PET, indicating unique biochemical pathways such as elevated pyrimidine metabolism and downregulated Vitamin B6 metabolism."&lt;SEP&gt;"Black soldier flies (BSF) are insect larvae used as a model for studying plastic degradation and metabolic interactions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6ce341034979daadf1f9dc7037397d1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c8dab62f56f2bfabf08bfe99049386a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae2c294948460ef392ceeec82d5e81f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEALWORM (MW)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"INSECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"MW is the most investigated larval model in plastic biodegradation and has been proposed as a model in micro- and nanoplastic toxicity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworm larvae were metabolically more active on PLA and expanded foam plastics during the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms (MW) are insect larvae that show altered metabolic pathways when exposed to plastic substrates."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6ce341034979daadf1f9dc7037397d1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c8dab62f56f2bfabf08bfe99049386a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae2c294948460ef392ceeec82d5e81f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WAX MOTH (WM)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"INSECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Wax Moth larvae showed metabolic activity on PLA and expanded foam plastics and exhibited an elevation in Vitamin B6 metabolism."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wax moths (WM) are insect larvae that exhibit metabolic responses to plastic exposure similar to mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6ce341034979daadf1f9dc7037397d1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae2c294948460ef392ceeec82d5e81f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VITAMIN B6 METABOLISM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The metabolic pathway involving Vitamin B6 was downregulated in BSF across all plastics but elevated in WM, suggesting gut-symbiont interactions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6ce341034979daadf1f9dc7037397d1b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PYRIMIDINE METABOLISM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pyrimidine metabolism involves the synthesis and degradation of pyrimidines, essential components of nucleic acids."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pyrimidine metabolism was upregulated as a result of oxidative stress caused by plastic exposure."&lt;SEP&gt;"This metabolic pathway was elevated in BSF larvae when reared on PET."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pyrimidine metabolism is essential for RNA and DNA synthesis, membrane lipid biosynthesis, and protein glycosylation, significantly perturbed only in ultrahigh MW PS-fed mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6ce341034979daadf1f9dc7037397d1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae2c294948460ef392ceeec82d5e81f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-939800f545beed77f5a7d1c026c250fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ee6535da22915c7094098e016b19d80</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CENTRAL CARBON METABOLISM (CCM)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CCM metabolites were analyzed via LC-QqQ-MS, providing insights into the biochemical impacts of plastic exposure on insects."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6ce341034979daadf1f9dc7037397d1b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LC-QQQ-MS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Liquid chromatography triple quadrupole mass spectrometry was used to analyze CCM metabolites in the insect models."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6ce341034979daadf1f9dc7037397d1b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROTEIN PRODUCTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Insects are used to produce valuable protein products from organic waste streams, which may be affected by plastic contamination."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6ce341034979daadf1f9dc7037397d1b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXPANDED POLYETHYLENE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PLASTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A variant of polyethylene that increased metabolic activity in MW and WM larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6ce341034979daadf1f9dc7037397d1b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WASTE MANAGEMENT SYSTEMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENVIRONMENTAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Systems utilizing insects to process organic waste, where plastic contamination can negatively impact efficiency."&lt;SEP&gt;"Waste management systems face challenges due to the rapid increase in plastic production and low recycling rates."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6ce341034979daadf1f9dc7037397d1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bd3778dedc6a0463017df9f8d6396eb</data>
