    <node id="&quot;SIMCA 17.01&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"SOFTWARE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"SIMCA 17.01 is a multivariate data analysis software used for analyzing metabolic data."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-394b3365ffb36d05dca2ef06bf74e462</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXPANDED FOAM POLYETHYLENE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Expanded foam polyethylene (Exp PE) is a type of plastic tested in the study for its effects on insect metabolism."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-394b3365ffb36d05dca2ef06bf74e462</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AGILENT INFINITY FLEX II UHPLC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Agilent Infinity Flex II UHPLC is a piece of equipment used for measuring CCM metabolites."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-394b3365ffb36d05dca2ef06bf74e462</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AGILENT 6470 TRIPLE QUADRUPOLE MASS SPECTROMETER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Agilent 6470 Triple Quadrupole Mass Spectrometer (QqQ-MS) is a device used for analyzing CCM metabolites."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-394b3365ffb36d05dca2ef06bf74e462</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CAPTIVA EMR CARTRIDGES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Captiva EMR cartridges are used to remove the lipid fraction during metabolite extraction."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-394b3365ffb36d05dca2ef06bf74e462</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MILLIQ WATER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"MilliQ water is high-purity water used in various steps of the metabolite extraction process."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-394b3365ffb36d05dca2ef06bf74e462</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;METHANOL:ETHANOL MIXTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL REACTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Methanol:ethanol mixture is used as a solvent in the metabolite extraction procedure."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-394b3365ffb36d05dca2ef06bf74e462</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CAMBRIDGE ISOTOPE LABORATORIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An organization providing high-purity chloroform-D for $^{1}$H NMR analysis of polystyrene residues."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cambridge Isotope Laboratories, Inc. is the supplier of Succinic Acid \({ }^{13} \mathrm{C}_{2}\)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-394b3365ffb36d05dca2ef06bf74e462&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53dd546535ef4247004faab1fa475889</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MERCK&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Merck is a supplier of analytical-grade chemicals used in the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"Merck is the supplier of LiChrosolv® methanol:ethanol mixture used in the study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-394b3365ffb36d05dca2ef06bf74e462&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed48dc66abf9c27721101b1adac15e7a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EPPENDORF&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Eppendorf is the manufacturer of the Centrifuge 5430R used in the metabolite extraction process."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-394b3365ffb36d05dca2ef06bf74e462</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BSF&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Black Soldier Fly larvae are used in experiments to study the metabolic effects of plastic exposure. They exhibited specific metabolic changes when exposed to different plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-939800f545beed77f5a7d1c026c250fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"WM larvae had reduced mean larval weights due to supplementation and showed a significant effect of supplementation on survival rates."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-939800f545beed77f5a7d1c026c250fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VITAMIN B6&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"VITAMIN"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Vitamin B6 metabolism was downregulated in all plastic treatments compared to control groups, affecting various downstream pathways."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-939800f545beed77f5a7d1c026c250fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PYRIDOXINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"VITAMIN"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pyridoxine is a form of Vitamin B6 and its depletion indicates potential disruption in fatty acid synthesis and other biochemical processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pyridoxine supplementation enhances the activity of recombinant glutamate decarboxylase."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1d40b7debb6497167fa1aec874ebce45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-939800f545beed77f5a7d1c026c250fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ASPARTATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"AMINO ACID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Aspartate is an amino acid involved in altered metabolic pathways due to plastic exposure."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-939800f545beed77f5a7d1c026c250fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GLUTAMATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"AMINO ACID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Glutamate is an amino acid whose metabolic pathway was affected by plastic exposure."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-939800f545beed77f5a7d1c026c250fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ARGININE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"AMINO ACID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Arginine is an amino acid with altered expression in metabolic pathways after plastic exposure."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-939800f545beed77f5a7d1c026c250fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROLINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"AMINO ACID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Proline is an amino acid whose metabolic pathway was impacted by plastic exposure."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-939800f545beed77f5a7d1c026c250fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;4-AMINOBUTANOATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"4-aminobutanoate is involved in butanoate metabolism which was altered by plastic exposure."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-939800f545beed77f5a7d1c026c250fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;Γ-AMINOBUTYRATE (GABA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"GABA levels were elevated, suggesting potential Vitamin B6 and Ala-Asp-Glu metabolic pathways pooling via GABA intermediates."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-939800f545beed77f5a7d1c026c250fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;N-ACETYL GALACTOSAMINE (NACGAL)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"NAcGal is a precursor metabolised by microbial enzymes to form glycosphospholipids required for microbial adhesion."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-939800f545beed77f5a7d1c026c250fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;URIDINE 5-DIPHOSPHATE (UDP)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"UDP is a precursor metabolised by microbial enzymes to form glycosphospholipids and is involved in antigenic signalling."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-939800f545beed77f5a7d1c026c250fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRANS-TRANS-MUCONIC ACID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Elevated levels suggest plastic degradation activity in the insect gut."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-939800f545beed77f5a7d1c026c250fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;4-AMINOBENZOIC ACID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"This metabolite's elevation suggests plastic degradation activity in the insect gut."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-939800f545beed77f5a7d1c026c250fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HOMOCYSTEINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Homocysteine, a glutathione metabolism intermediate, was elevated indicating oxidative stress caused by plastic exposure."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-939800f545beed77f5a7d1c026c250fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BUTANOATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Butanoate metabolism was altered in the presence of plastics, specifically via 4-aminobutanoate."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-939800f545beed77f5a7d1c026c250fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GLYCOSPHOSPHOLIPIDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LIPID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Glycosphospholipids are lipids formed from precursors like N-acetyl galactosamine and uridine 5-diphosphate, playing a role in microbial adhesion."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-939800f545beed77f5a7d1c026c250fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICROBIAL UDP-GALACTOPYRANOSE MUTASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An enzyme that metabolizes precursors to form glycosphospholipids required for microbial adhesion and antigenic signaling."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-939800f545beed77f5a7d1c026c250fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NUCLEOTIDE SUGARS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nucleotide sugars are intermediates in metabolic pathways, with precursors such as N-acetyl galactosamine and uridine 5-diphosphate."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-939800f545beed77f5a7d1c026c250fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MARINE MICROBIOTA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Marine microbiota encompasses microorganisms found in marine environments, impacted by plastic-induced oxidative stress."&lt;SEP&gt;"Marine microbiota showed similar perturbed nucleotide metabolism and oxidative stress responses due to plastic exposure."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ae2c294948460ef392ceeec82d5e81f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-939800f545beed77f5a7d1c026c250fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ZEBRAFISH MICROBIOTA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Zebrafish microbiota also exhibited oxidative stress and metabolic changes due to plastic exposure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Zebrafish microbiota represents gut microorganisms in zebrafish, affected by plastic exposure."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ae2c294948460ef392ceeec82d5e81f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-939800f545beed77f5a7d1c026c250fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DOWNSTREAM PATHWAYS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Downstream pathways involve numerous biochemical reactions affected by the depletion of Vitamin B6 co-factors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-939800f545beed77f5a7d1c026c250fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANTIGENIC SIGNALLING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"IMMUNE RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Antigenic signalling in insects involves glycosphospholipids formed by microbial enzymes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-939800f545beed77f5a7d1c026c250fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NUCLEOTIDE METABOLISM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nucleotide metabolism includes the synthesis and degradation of nucleotides, crucial for DNA and RNA formation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ae2c294948460ef392ceeec82d5e81f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLASTIC TOXICITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TOXIN"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Plastic toxicity refers to the harmful effects of plastics on biological systems, including oxidative stress and metabolic alterations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ae2c294948460ef392ceeec82d5e81f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOMARKERS OF OXIDATIVE STRESS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MARKER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biomarkers of oxidative stress are measurable indicators reflecting the level of oxidative damage in cells or tissues."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ae2c294948460ef392ceeec82d5e81f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STARCH AND SUCROSE METABOLISM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Starch and sucrose metabolism involve the breakdown and utilization of carbohydrates for energy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Starch and sucrose metabolism is significantly perturbed in medium and ultrahigh MW PS polymer-fed mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ae2c294948460ef392ceeec82d5e81f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ee6535da22915c7094098e016b19d80</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PENTOSE PHOSPHATE PATHWAY (PPP)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The pentose phosphate pathway generates NADPH and ribose-5-phosphate, important for biosynthetic processes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ae2c294948460ef392ceeec82d5e81f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AMINO SUGAR AND NUCLEOTIDE SUGAR PATHWAY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"This pathway is involved in the synthesis of amino sugars and nucleotide sugars, essential for cell wall and glycoprotein formation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ae2c294948460ef392ceeec82d5e81f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GUANINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Guanine is a purine base found in DNA and RNA, observed to be downregulated in mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ae2c294948460ef392ceeec82d5e81f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;L-DIHYDROOROTIC ACID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"L-dihydroorotic acid is an intermediate in pyrimidine biosynthesis, also downregulated in mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ae2c294948460ef392ceeec82d5e81f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;Β-NICOTINAMIDE ADENINE NUCLEOTIDE (Β-NAD)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"COFACTOR"</data>
      <data key="d1">"β-NAD is a coenzyme involved in redox reactions, elevated in mealworms via purine metabolism."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ae2c294948460ef392ceeec82d5e81f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FLAVIN ADENINE NUCLEOTIDE (FAD)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"COFACTOR"</data>
      <data key="d1">"FAD is a cofactor participating in various enzymatic reactions, increased in mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ae2c294948460ef392ceeec82d5e81f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;N-ACETYL GLUCOSAMINE (NACGLU)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"N-acetyl glucosamine is an amino sugar involved in cell wall and glycoprotein synthesis, elevated in mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ae2c294948460ef392ceeec82d5e81f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GLUCOSAMINE 6-PHOSPHATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Glucosamine 6-phosphate is an intermediate in amino sugar metabolism, increased in mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ae2c294948460ef392ceeec82d5e81f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXPANDED POLYSTYRENE (EXP PE)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PLASTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Expanded polystyrene is a foam-based plastic tested for its interaction with insect models."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ae2c294948460ef392ceeec82d5e81f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BSF LARVAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"BSF larvae are insects that interact metabolically with plastics, showing positive interactions with PET and negative/neutral interactions with expanded PE plastic."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c6ced866009d759592c16009bc619b4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXP PE PLASTIC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PLASTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Expanded PE plastic has a negative or neutral interaction with BSF larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c6ced866009d759592c16009bc619b4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MW AND WM MODEL INSECTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"These model insects perform well in terms of CCM outputs when interacting with PLA and foam-based plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c6ced866009d759592c16009bc619b4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CCM OUTPUTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CCM outputs refer to the central carbon metabolism outputs, which indicate the performance of insects on various plastic substrates."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c6ced866009d759592c16009bc619b4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIPIDOMICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lipidomics is a process used to study the impact of polybrominated diphenyl ether-47 on breast cancer mice."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipidomics is an analytical approach used to study lipids, providing insights into how plastics are assimilated into insect biomass."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipidomics is the study of cellular lipids on a large scale, used here to analyze changes in Tenebrio molitor during polystyrene degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipidomics studies the presence of cellular and membrane lipids linked to biochemical pathways."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c6ced866009d759592c16009bc619b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8e18d03240e025c60621d616f1de85b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5922f60fcd06ac6ffa27018026871346&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ddf4b13293dd3d8d0887af10fc52c98</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICROBIOME COMPOSITIONAL ANALYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Microbiome compositional analysis studies the gut microbiome's composition, aiding in understanding the interaction between insects and plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c6ced866009d759592c16009bc619b4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLASTIC DEGRADATION ASSESSMENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Plastic degradation assessments evaluate the extent to which plastics are broken down by insects."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c6ced866009d759592c16009bc619b4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INSECT BIOMASS VARIANCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Insect biomass variance refers to the variation in weight distribution among larvae within treatments, posing a limitation to the study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c6ced866009d759592c16009bc619b4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;METABOLOMICS STANDARD INITIATIVE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"STANDARD"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Metabolomics Standard Initiative provides guidelines for minimum reporting standards in biological samples."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c6ced866009d759592c16009bc619b4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GUT MICROBIOME INTERACTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gut microbiome interaction describes the relationship between the insect's gut microbiome and plastic substrates."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c6ced866009d759592c16009bc619b4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MOLASSES SUPPLEMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Molasses supplement is added to plastic substrates and potentially enhances the metabolic interaction of insects with plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c6ced866009d759592c16009bc619b4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PFAS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TOXIN"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PFAS are persistent organic pollutants studied for their bioaccumulation effects in organisms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c6ced866009d759592c16009bc619b4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WILD-CAUGHT FRESHWATER TURTLES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ANIMAL"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Wild-caught freshwater turtles were used in studies examining the bioaccumulation of PFAS mixtures."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c6ced866009d759592c16009bc619b4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OMIC-BASED ECOSSURVEILLANCE TECHNIQUES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNIQUE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Omic-based ecossurveillance techniques involve using omics approaches (e.g., metabolomics) to monitor environmental health."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c6ced866009d759592c16009bc619b4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CSIRO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CSIRO is an organization involved in the research and analysis of insect biotransformation and plastic degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c6ced866009d759592c16009bc619b4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AGRICULTURAL SOILS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL FEATURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Agricultural soils are the top layer of land used for farming, impacted by microplastics leading to ecological and health concerns."&lt;SEP&gt;"Agricultural soils can accumulate plastic residues through compost application."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4c7bcc9530f9dc72038f774f6f084ab6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d40b7debb6497167fa1aec874ebce45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KYNURENINES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Kynurenines are metabolites that exhibit toxic and neurobehavioral effects in adult mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1d40b7debb6497167fa1aec874ebce45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYETHYLENE MICROPLASTICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polyethylene microplastics cause molecular to individual-level adverse effects in zebrafish."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1d40b7debb6497167fa1aec874ebce45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HYPHAL Β-GLUCAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hyphal β-glucan is concealed from the immune system by Aspergillus galactosaminogalactan."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1d40b7debb6497167fa1aec874ebce45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GREENSHELL™ MUSSELS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
