      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL FEATURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Areas on agar plates where PS degradation is evident, indicating the presence of active bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Clear zones indicate areas where NPS-degrading bacteria have emulsified or degraded the polymer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fdb13eda4d3cf5385a0a8284c7e213b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3235cc6102d988875f1dda974a56038</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EMULSIFICATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Emulsification is the process by which NPS-degrading bacteria disperse NPS particles into smaller droplets."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d3235cc6102d988875f1dda974a56038</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CFU (COLONY-FORMING UNITS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A measure used to estimate the number of viable bacteria in a sample."&lt;SEP&gt;"CFU is a unit used to quantify the number of viable bacterial cells capable of forming colonies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d3235cc6102d988875f1dda974a56038&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77817419b966e501f1106866cbea7350</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXPERIMENTAL GROUPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Experimental groups include PS-1, PS-2, PS-3, PS-4, PS-5, and PS-6, each representing different molecular weights of polystyrene microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Experimental groups refer to the different mealworm diets tested in the study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d3235cc6102d988875f1dda974a56038&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e136b8a35c0d60811b9daf0cbd5729f5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POSITIVE CONTROL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A positive control ensures that the experimental setup works as intended by producing a known effect."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d3235cc6102d988875f1dda974a56038</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LONG-TERM INCUBATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Long-term incubation involves maintaining cultures over extended periods to observe changes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d3235cc6102d988875f1dda974a56038</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HOMOGENIZED GUT SUSPENSION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"This suspension contains gut contents from mealworms, prepared for microbial isolation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d3235cc6102d988875f1dda974a56038</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BACTERIAL CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bacterial cells are the microorganisms of interest, whose growth and viability are measured using plate count assays."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01bf9080cbf55e62c0b26d0e054bd1fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLATE COUNT ASSAY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The plate count assay is a method used to determine the number of viable bacterial cells in a sample."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01bf9080cbf55e62c0b26d0e054bd1fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ACID PRODUCTION ASSAY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The acid production assay detects the degradation of Nano-polystyrene by measuring the amount of acid produced."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01bf9080cbf55e62c0b26d0e054bd1fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BROMOCRESOL PURPLE (BCP)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bromocresol purple is an indicator used to detect acidity changes during the degradation of Nano-polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01bf9080cbf55e62c0b26d0e054bd1fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOFILM ACTIVITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biofilm activity refers to the formation of bacterial biofilms on surfaces, influenced by the presence of Nano-polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01bf9080cbf55e62c0b26d0e054bd1fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYSTYRENE 96-WELL MICROTITER PLATES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polystyrene 96-well microtiter plates are used for culturing bacteria and measuring biofilm formation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01bf9080cbf55e62c0b26d0e054bd1fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CRYSTAL VIOLET (CV)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Crystal violet is a stain used to quantify bacterial biomass in biofilm assays."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01bf9080cbf55e62c0b26d0e054bd1fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WEIGHT LOSS OF PS FILM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The weight loss of polystyrene film indicates the extent of microbial degradation over time."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01bf9080cbf55e62c0b26d0e054bd1fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENOMIC DNA EXTRACTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Genomic DNA extraction is a procedure to isolate DNA from plastic-degrading bacterial strains for identification."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01bf9080cbf55e62c0b26d0e054bd1fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;16S RDNA REGION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENETIC CONCEPT"</data>
