      <data key="d2">chunk-01bf9080cbf55e62c0b26d0e054bd1fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PSEUDOMONAS AERUGINOSA M2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A bacterium isolated from Tenebrio molitor capable of biodegrading polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas aeruginosa M2 is a bacterial strain capable of degrading NPS, as indicated by weight loss of PS film."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas aeruginosa M2 is a strain identified as capable of degrading Nano-polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas aeruginosa M2 is one of the bacterial strains isolated from mealworms capable of degrading polystyrene nanoplastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3196d2d200ebf060e966a565b5eb26de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbf098ec253f99187f3c98d5d0589f7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-939f85d52d9301668deab282264e5fd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01bf9080cbf55e62c0b26d0e054bd1fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PSEUDOMONAS STUTZERI M3&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pseudomonas stutzeri M3 is a bacterial strain with potential for NPS degradation, contributing to surface alterations of PS films."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas stutzeri M3 is a strain identified as capable of degrading Nano-polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3196d2d200ebf060e966a565b5eb26de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01bf9080cbf55e62c0b26d0e054bd1fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PSEUDOMONAS M7&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pseudomonas M7 is a strain identified as capable of degrading Nano-polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01bf9080cbf55e62c0b26d0e054bd1fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PSEUDOMONAS AERUGINOSA M8&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pseudomonas aeruginosa M8 is a bacterial strain capable of contributing to the breakdown of polystyrene nanoplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas aeruginosa M8 is a bacterial strain isolated from the intestines of yellow mealworms, contributing to biodegradation studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas aeruginosa M8 is a bacterial strain participating in the biodegradation of NPS, affecting the physical properties of PS films."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas aeruginosa M8 is a strain identified as capable of degrading Nano-polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3196d2d200ebf060e966a565b5eb26de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbf098ec253f99187f3c98d5d0589f7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26138366e1d9310732edc569ba338bfe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01bf9080cbf55e62c0b26d0e054bd1fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ACHROMOBACTER XYLOSIDANS M9&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Achromobacter xylosidans M9 is a bacterial strain identified for its ability to degrade nanoplastics, showing significant reduction in nanoplastic particle counts and size."&lt;SEP&gt;"Achromobacter xylosidans M9 is a strain identified as capable of degrading Nano-polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3196d2d200ebf060e966a565b5eb26de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01bf9080cbf55e62c0b26d0e054bd1fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENZYMATIC ACTIVITY SCREENING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Enzymatic activity screening evaluates the ability of bacterial isolates to produce enzymes like cellulases, esterases, lipases, proteases, and laccases."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01bf9080cbf55e62c0b26d0e054bd1fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHOSPHATE BUFFER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A 20 mM phosphate buffer of pH 6.8 is used to dissolve Nano-polystyrene emulsion for the turbidity assay."&lt;SEP&gt;"A phosphate buffer at pH 7.4 was used during homogenization to maintain optimal conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e0ec64a7c629b14bfb6652f1960a337c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01bf9080cbf55e62c0b26d0e054bd1fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ABSORBANCE MEASUREMENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Absorbance measurements at 650 nm are taken to assess the reduction in turbidity during the turbidity assay."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01bf9080cbf55e62c0b26d0e054bd1fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;95% ETHANOL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"95% ethanol is used for extracting crystal violet stain from bacterial biofilms and for surface sterilization of PS film."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01bf9080cbf55e62c0b26d0e054bd1fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARBOXYMETHYL CELLULOSE (CMC)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"SUBSTRATE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CMC is a substrate used to test the activity of cellulase enzymes in the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carboxymethyl cellulose is used as a substrate to test cellulase activity in enzymatic activity screening."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-262d7fa1c8f2581943a41cf4897fa253&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01bf9080cbf55e62c0b26d0e054bd1fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TWEEN 20&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"SUBSTRATE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tween 20 is a substrate used to test the activity of esterase enzymes in the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tween 20 is used as a substrate to test esterase activity in enzymatic activity screening."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-262d7fa1c8f2581943a41cf4897fa253&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01bf9080cbf55e62c0b26d0e054bd1fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TWEEN 80&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"SUBSTRATE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tween 80 is a substrate used to test the activity of lipase enzymes in the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tween 80 is used as a substrate to test lipase activity in enzymatic activity screening."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-262d7fa1c8f2581943a41cf4897fa253&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01bf9080cbf55e62c0b26d0e054bd1fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CASEIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"SUBSTRATE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Casein is a substrate used to test the activity of protease enzymes in the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"Casein is used as a substrate to test protease activity in enzymatic activity screening."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-262d7fa1c8f2581943a41cf4897fa253&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01bf9080cbf55e62c0b26d0e054bd1fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GUAIACOL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"SUBSTRATE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Guaiacol is a substrate used to test the activity of laccase enzymes in the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"Guaiacol is used as a substrate to test laccase activity in enzymatic activity screening."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-262d7fa1c8f2581943a41cf4897fa253&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01bf9080cbf55e62c0b26d0e054bd1fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ELECTROPHORESIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Electrophoresis is a laboratory process used to separate DNA, RNA, or proteins based on size and charge, typically conducted using agarose gels in TAE buffer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Electrophoresis is used to separate and purify amplified DNA products during genomic DNA extraction."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-53ab7dd83bf51674598c6a5bdd146b90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01bf9080cbf55e62c0b26d0e054bd1fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PCR AMPLIFICATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A molecular biology technique used to amplify specific DNA sequences, such as the nifH gene, for analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"PCR amplification is used to amplify the 16S rDNA region during genomic DNA extraction."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polymerase Chain Reaction technique used to amplify specific regions of the 16S rRNA gene for microbial community analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85c9587b55f24a8ae5ba6b478dbb98e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77817419b966e501f1106866cbea7350&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01bf9080cbf55e62c0b26d0e054bd1fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLAST TOOL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The BLAST tool is used to analyze obtained sequences against existing sequences in the NCBI database for bacterial identification."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01bf9080cbf55e62c0b26d0e054bd1fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEGA 11 SOFTWARE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"MEGA 11 software is used to construct a phylogenetic tree based on bacterial sequence analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01bf9080cbf55e62c0b26d0e054bd1fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ACTIVITY INDEX (AI)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Activity Index measures the diameter of the yellow zone minus colony diameter in the acid production assay."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01bf9080cbf55e62c0b26d0e054bd1fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CELLULASES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cellulases are enzymes produced by Achromobacter species, aiding in the decomposition of cellulose."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cellulases are enzymes that break down cellulose into smaller molecules, such as glucose. They were tested using carboxymethyl cellulose (CMC) as a substrate in the study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-26138366e1d9310732edc569ba338bfe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-262d7fa1c8f2581943a41cf4897fa253</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ISOPROPANOL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Component of solvent B in UHPLC mobile phase."&lt;SEP&gt;"Isopropanol is a chemical solvent used in LC-MS grade applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Isopropanol is a solvent used in combination with chloroform for layer separation during the NPS extraction process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Isopropanol was used in combination with chloroform for the separation of nanoplastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e557113f1cfd2472fa9c51d1cdc3069a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92b1e432ea4bee0f332d7303188e6de7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b4ab01931acbc7aa9c77cd03531c57e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-262d7fa1c8f2581943a41cf4897fa253</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KIM ET AL. (2005)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Kim et al. (2005) developed a method for screening cellulase enzyme activity using carboxymethyl cellulose agar media."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-262d7fa1c8f2581943a41cf4897fa253</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KUMAR ET AL. (2012)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Kumar et al. (2012) provided a method for screening esterase and lipase enzyme activities using Tween 80 and Tween 20 media."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-262d7fa1c8f2581943a41cf4897fa253</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VIJAYARAGHAVAN AND VINCENT (2013)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
