      <data key="d2">chunk-262d7fa1c8f2581943a41cf4897fa253</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;M9&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"M9 is a Gram-negative bacterial strain isolated from yellow mealworms, showing significant growth and producing dark orange, sticky colonies on LCFBM."&lt;SEP&gt;"M9 is a bacterial isolate identified as Achromobacter xylosoxidans, exhibiting high NPS degradation capability and producing esterase, laccase, catalase, oxidase, and cellulase."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e557113f1cfd2472fa9c51d1cdc3069a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55bdcf1b4859e82ab15050837ab539dc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GCMS&quot;">
