    <node id="&quot;ACHROMOBACTER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A bacterial genus significantly affected by the bran diet."&lt;SEP&gt;"Achromobacter is a bacterial genus capable of degrading xenobiotics, including pyrene and other pollutants."&lt;SEP&gt;"Achromobacter is a bacterial genus known for its ability to degrade hydrocarbons and other pollutants."&lt;SEP&gt;"Achromobacter is a genus of bacteria known for its robust enzymatic activity and efficacy in xenobiotic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Achromobacter is a genus of bacteria known for its wide array of enzymes and adaptability in degrading various environmental pollutants."&lt;SEP&gt;"Achromobacter is a genus of bacteria that includes strains capable of degrading polystyrene nanoplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Achromobacter is another bacterial genus identified among the gut isolates of T. molitor larvae."</data>
