    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEALWORMS (TENEBRIO MOLITOR LARVAE)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"INSECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mealworm larvae, specifically Tenebrio molitor, demonstrate gut microbiomes capable of responding similarly to polystyrene and corn straw diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms are the larvae of Tenebrio molitor, a species known for their ability to ingest and biodegrade plastics such as PS and PE."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms are the larvae of Tenebrio molitor beetles and play a key role in the biodegradation of polystyrene by altering their gut microbiome and metabolome."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0f2fd4b2e978e6745e0dde602114a826&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a00d67f63d22d1959c8a565b6a86d22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb1740bb657b0f90c48ee5e6d75945ce</data>
