      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The anterior gut of mealworms is dominated by facultative anaerobes, including Lactococcus and Pantoa genera, as well as Bacillaceae family members."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6bd3778dedc6a0463017df9f8d6396eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POSTERIOR GUT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The posterior gut of mealworms is more diverse, featuring anaerobic bacteria from the Spiroplasma, Clostridium, and Enterobacter genera."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6bd3778dedc6a0463017df9f8d6396eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MOLECULAR WEIGHTS (MN)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Molecular weights are used to quantify the reduction in polymer size after biodegradation, with significant decreases observed for PE and PS."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6bd3778dedc6a0463017df9f8d6396eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FACULTATIVE ANAEROBES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Facultative anaerobes are bacteria that can survive in both oxygenated and oxygen-deprived environments, commonly found in the anterior gut of mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6bd3778dedc6a0463017df9f8d6396eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANAEROBES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Anaerobes are bacteria that thrive in oxygen-free environments, prevalent in the posterior gut of mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6bd3778dedc6a0463017df9f8d6396eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STANDARD DIET&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DIET"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A standard diet for mealworms typically includes bran and supports the growth of specific bacterial genera in their gut."&lt;SEP&gt;"Standard Diet refers to the fermented cassava yeasts fed to the control group of mealworms in the experiment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Standard diet refers to the control diet used in the experiment, typically consisting of yeast."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d6a80044bea074bdbcb68f489aa8af0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32f340b7166025be3c56178a94ae480d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bd3778dedc6a0463017df9f8d6396eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COLONY FORMING UNITS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Colony forming units are a measure of bacterial concentration, ranging from 10^3 to 10^6 per gut in mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6bd3778dedc6a0463017df9f8d6396eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MARINE ENVIRONMENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ECOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Marine environments are particularly affected by plastic pollution due to the recalcitrance of plastics, leading to harmful effects on wildlife."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6bd3778dedc6a0463017df9f8d6396eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COFEEDING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cofeeding involves providing mealworms with a combination of plastics and other food sources, such as bran, to enhance plastic degradation rates."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6bd3778dedc6a0463017df9f8d6396eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PE FRASS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PE Frass is a derivative of polyethylene showing altered molecular weight properties compared to original PE."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf662c8e784d14a3a4dba2e89041aa4a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PE + BRAN FRASS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PE + Bran Frass is a composite material derived from polyethylene combined with bran frass, exhibiting modified molecular weight reductions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf662c8e784d14a3a4dba2e89041aa4a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PS FRASS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PS Frass is a variant of polystyrene displaying changes in molecular weight properties."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf662c8e784d14a3a4dba2e89041aa4a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PS + BRAN FRASS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PS + Bran Frass represents a composite material formed by combining polystyrene with bran frass, resulting in adjusted molecular weight reductions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf662c8e784d14a3a4dba2e89041aa4a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MOLECULAR WEIGHT \(M_{W}\)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Molecular weight \(M_{w}\) represents the weight-average molecular mass of polymers, indicating the overall size distribution of polymer chains."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf662c8e784d14a3a4dba2e89041aa4a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MOLECULAR WEIGHT \(M_{N}\)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Molecular weight \(M_{n}\) denotes the number-average molecular mass of polymers, reflecting the average chain length of the polymer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf662c8e784d14a3a4dba2e89041aa4a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REDUCTION IN \(M_{W}\)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL REACTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Reduction in \(M_{w}\) refers to the process where the weight-average molecular weight of polymers decreases due to degradation or other processes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf662c8e784d14a3a4dba2e89041aa4a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REDUCTION IN \(M_{N}\)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL REACTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Reduction in \(M_{n}\) signifies the decrease in number-average molecular weight of polymers, often caused by chemical or biological degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf662c8e784d14a3a4dba2e89041aa4a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRAN FRASS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bran frass is a biological product derived from bran and insect frass, used as an additive in composites for altering material properties."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf662c8e784d14a3a4dba2e89041aa4a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INDIAN MEAL MOTHS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"INSECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Indian meal moths are omnivorous insect larvae that have been reported to degrade plastics, suggesting broader insect gut capabilities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-89ff8edff56325c22cfed3871f4fbf48</data>
    </node>
