      <data key="d2">chunk-c16dd402d0a926c1a975280e2b32e84e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PS (POLYSTYRENE FOAM)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PS is a type of plastic used as a diet in the experiment, with varying consumption rates depending on the species."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c16dd402d0a926c1a975280e2b32e84e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PU (POLYURETHANE FOAM)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PU is another type of plastic used as a diet in the experiment, consumed similarly by both superworms and yellow mealworms when normalized per unit mass."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c16dd402d0a926c1a975280e2b32e84e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CUMULATIVE NET WEIGHT CHANGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cumulative net weight change tracks the growth or loss of weight in larvae over time, reflecting their metabolic responses to diet."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c16dd402d0a926c1a975280e2b32e84e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HOLLOWS AND PITS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL FEATURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hollows and pits are physical changes observed in PS and PU foams after incubation with larvae, indicating plastic degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c16dd402d0a926c1a975280e2b32e84e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GEOGRAPHIC SOURCES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ECOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Geographic sources refer to the locations where test larvae were obtained, potentially influencing their plastic ingestion abilities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c16dd402d0a926c1a975280e2b32e84e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INITIAL AVERAGE WEIGHT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Initial average weight refers to the starting weight of larvae, which can influence their plastic consumption efficiency."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c16dd402d0a926c1a975280e2b32e84e</data>
    </node>
