    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BENZENE RING CLEAVAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL REACTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Benzene Ring Cleavage occurs in PS foam during digestion by larvae, leading to the disappearance of characteristic peaks in ATR-FTIR spectra."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-705bf68703e5d236b2ffabb7ecb3de5e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STUDENT'S T-TESTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"STATISTICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Student's t-tests are statistical tests used to determine significant differences between groups, such as plastic consumption rates among larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Student's t-tests are used to determine statistical significance in molecular weight reductions of LDPE."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b95a108327e39d37d20bdd99db541164&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705bf68703e5d236b2ffabb7ecb3de5e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CC STRETCH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CC Stretch refers to the carbon-carbon stretching vibrations observed in ATR-FTIR spectra, which decrease during plastic degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-705bf68703e5d236b2ffabb7ecb3de5e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;C-O STRETCH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNCTIONAL GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"C-O Stretch refers to the carbon-oxygen stretching vibrations observed in ATR-FTIR spectra, indicating changes in plastic structure during degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"C-O stretch indicates the presence of ester or ether groups formed during biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"C-O stretch is a functional group identified in ATR-FTIR analysis, indicating oxidation and depolymerization of plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7d0e4cb4324bc684ebb2ca6136c04ad0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-630e33352368a0c7f34d56ad45a38e56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705bf68703e5d236b2ffabb7ecb3de5e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;N-C=O STRETCH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"N-C=O Stretch is a characteristic absorption peak of PU foam, which disappears during degradation in the guts of larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-705bf68703e5d236b2ffabb7ecb3de5e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;−CH₂ STRETCH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"−CH₂ Stretch refers to the methylene group stretching vibrations observed in ATR-FTIR spectra, which weaken during plastic degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-705bf68703e5d236b2ffabb7ecb3de5e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;−OH STRETCH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"−OH Stretch refers to hydroxyl group vibrations observed in ATR-FTIR spectra, which disappear during plastic degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-705bf68703e5d236b2ffabb7ecb3de5e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CO STRETCH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CO Stretch refers to carbonyl group vibrations observed in ATR-FTIR spectra, which appear during plastic degradation as new functional groups form."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-705bf68703e5d236b2ffabb7ecb3de5e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIERARCHICAL CLUSTER ANALYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hierarchical Cluster Analysis further supports the differentiation of gut bacterial communities based on dietary plastic types."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hierarchical cluster analysis groups similar data points to understand relationships between gut microbial communities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hierarchical cluster analysis is a method used to group samples based on similarity in microbial community structure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hierarchical cluster analysis is a method used to group similar entities based on their characteristics, here applied to gut bacterial communities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a3f07da33b55bf8a25fe06beee23e90e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-476e13b69587aa4e81395e2fd00a9d5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df045e015825dac8935c9c6d8a402cda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df147b253e29abfa812d060407051e45</data>
