    <node id="&quot;BIT-26\(^{\MATHRM{T}}\)\">
      <data key="d0">BACTERIUM\</data>
      <data key="d1">BIT-26\(^{\mathrm{T}}\) is a bacterial strain characterized in the study as a novel species of the genus Mixta, identified using a polyphasic approach."&lt;SEP&gt;BIT-26\(^{\mathrm{T}}\) is a bacterial strain isolated from the gut of the plastic-eating mealworm Tenebrio molitor L. It is Gram-stain-negative, facultatively anaerobic, motile rods with peritrichous flagella."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-706b5d3a2fa68c3f52b58132d05b7165&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff28716c2f25b8550595e1f473add0c4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ERWINIA PIRIFORMIGRANS CFBP 5888\(^{\MATHRM{T}}\)\">
      <data key="d0">BACTERIUM\</data>
      <data key="d1">Erwinia piriformigrans CFBP 5888\(^{\mathrm{T}}\) is a bacterium that shows the highest 16S rRNA gene sequence similarity (97.4%) to the strain BIT-26\(^{\mathrm{T}}\)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-706b5d3a2fa68c3f52b58132d05b7165</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CITROBACTER SEDLAKII NBRC 105722\(^{\MATHRM{T}}\)\">
      <data key="d0">BACTERIUM\</data>
      <data key="d1">Citrobacter sedlakii NBRC 105722\(^{\mathrm{T}}\) has a 16S rRNA gene sequence similarity of 97.3% to the strain BIT-26\(^{\mathrm{T}}\)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-706b5d3a2fa68c3f52b58132d05b7165</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MIXTA CALIDA LMG 25383\(^{\MATHRM{T}}\)\">
      <data key="d0">BACTERIUM\</data>
      <data key="d1">Mixta calida LMG 25383\(^{\mathrm{T}}\) belongs to the genus Mixta and shows a 16S rRNA gene sequence similarity of 97.3% to the strain BIT-26\(^{\mathrm{T}}\)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-706b5d3a2fa68c3f52b58132d05b7165</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CRONOBACTER MUYTJENSII ATCC 51329\(^{\MATHRM{T}}\)\">
      <data key="d0">BACTERIUM\</data>
      <data key="d1">Cronobacter muytjensii ATCC 51329\(^{\mathrm{T}}\) has a 16S rRNA gene sequence similarity of 97.2% to the strain BIT-26\(^{\mathrm{T}}\)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-706b5d3a2fa68c3f52b58132d05b7165</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MIXTA THEICOLA QC88-366 \({ }^{\MATHRM{T}}\)\">
      <data key="d0">BACTERIUM\</data>
      <data key="d1">Mixta theicola QC88-366 \({ }^{\mathrm{T}}\) belongs to the genus Mixta and shows a 16S rRNA gene sequence similarity of 97.2% to the strain BIT-26\(^{\mathrm{T}}\)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-706b5d3a2fa68c3f52b58132d05b7165</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MIXTA TENEBRIONIS SP. NOV\">
      <data key="d0">BACTERIUM\</data>
      <data key="d1">Mixta tenebrionis sp. nov represents a novel species within the genus Mixta, isolated from the gut of the plastic-eating mealworm Tenebrio molitor L."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-706b5d3a2fa68c3f52b58132d05b7165</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TENEBRIO MOLITOR L\">
      <data key="d0">MICROORGANISM\</data>
      <data key="d1">Tenebrio molitor L is a plastic-eating mealworm whose gut harbors symbiotic bacteria involved in plastic degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-706b5d3a2fa68c3f52b58132d05b7165</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MIXTA\">
      <data key="d0">GENUS\</data>
      <data key="d1">Mixta is a bacterial genus that includes BIT-26\(^{\mathrm{T}}\), which has been identified as a novel species in this study."&lt;SEP&gt;Mixta is a genus within the family Erwiniaeae, established in 2018 by reclassifying four species from the genus Pantoea."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-706b5d3a2fa68c3f52b58132d05b7165&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff28716c2f25b8550595e1f473add0c4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ERWINIAEAE\">
      <data key="d0">FAMILY\</data>
      <data key="d1">Erwiniaeae is one of the families within the order Enterobacteriales and contains 14 genera including Mixta."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-706b5d3a2fa68c3f52b58132d05b7165</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENTEROBACTERIALES\">
      <data key="d0">ORDER\</data>
      <data key="d1">Enterobacteriales is an order of bacteria within the class Gammaproteobacteria, divided into seven families including Erwiniaeae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-706b5d3a2fa68c3f52b58132d05b7165</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GAMMAPROTEOBACTERIA\">
      <data key="d0">CLASS\</data>
      <data key="d1">Gammaproteobacteria is a class of bacteria containing the order Enterobacteriales."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-706b5d3a2fa68c3f52b58132d05b7165</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXIGUOBACTERIUM SP. STRAIN YT2\">
      <data key="d0">BACTERIUM\</data>
      <data key="d1">Exiguobacterium sp. strain YT2 is a plastic-degrading bacterium isolated from the mealworm's gut."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-706b5d3a2fa68c3f52b58132d05b7165</data>
    </node>
