      <data key="d0">GENE</data>
      <data key="d1">infB is one of the housekeeping genes used for phylogenetic analysis of the bacterial strain BIT-26\(^{\mathrm{T}}\)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-706b5d3a2fa68c3f52b58132d05b7165</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RPOB&quot;">
      <data key="d0">GENE</data>
      <data key="d1">rpoB is one of the housekeeping genes used for phylogenetic analysis of the bacterial strain BIT-26\(^{\mathrm{T}}\)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-706b5d3a2fa68c3f52b58132d05b7165</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYPHASIC APPROACH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">A polyphasic approach involves combining multiple methods, such as phenotypic, genotypic, and chemotaxonomic analyses, for bacterial classification."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-706b5d3a2fa68c3f52b58132d05b7165</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IN SILICO DNA–DNA HYBRIDIZATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">In silico DNA–DNA hybridization is a computational method used to estimate the relatedness between bacterial genomes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-706b5d3a2fa68c3f52b58132d05b7165</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AVERAGE NUCLEOTIDE IDENTITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Average nucleotide identity (ANI) is a measure of genome similarity used to differentiate bacterial species."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-706b5d3a2fa68c3f52b58132d05b7165</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHYLOGENETIC ANALYSES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">BIOLOGICAL PROCESS</data>
      <data key="d1">Phylogenetic analyses involve constructing evolutionary trees to study the relationships among organisms based on genetic data."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-706b5d3a2fa68c3f52b58132d05b7165</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHEMOTAXONOMIC DATA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Chemotaxonomic data refers to the chemical characteristics of an organism used for classification purposes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-706b5d3a2fa68c3f52b58132d05b7165</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MULTILOCUS SEQUENCE ANALYSIS (MLSA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A method for bacterial identification and phylogenetic studies using multiple gene loci."&lt;SEP&gt;"A method utilizing multiple gene loci for bacterial identification and phylogenetic studies."&lt;SEP&gt;Multilocus sequence analysis (MLSA) is a method that uses sequences from multiple housekeeping genes to determine the evolutionary relationships among organisms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-706b5d3a2fa68c3f52b58132d05b7165&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db0003a7244c51697d0129eb84b8e28e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENOME-BASED PHYLOGENIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">BIOLOGICAL PROCESS</data>
      <data key="d1">Genome-based phylogenies are constructed using whole-genome sequences to infer evolutionary relationships."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-706b5d3a2fa68c3f52b58132d05b7165</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SYMBIOTIC GUT BACTERIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">MICROORGANISMS</data>
      <data key="d1">Symbiotic gut bacteria are microorganisms residing in the digestive tract that interact with their host, often providing benefits such as aiding in digestion or degrading substances."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-706b5d3a2fa68c3f52b58132d05b7165</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;16S RRNA GENE\">
      <data key="d0">GENE\</data>
      <data key="d1">The 16S rRNA gene is used for phylogenetic analysis to classify and identify bacterial strains, including BIT-26\(^{\mathrm{T}}\)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ff28716c2f25b8550595e1f473add0c4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ATPD, GYRB, INFB, RPOB\">
      <data key="d0">GENE\</data>
      <data key="d1">These genes (atpD, gyrB, infB, rpoB) are used for constructing Maximum-likelihood trees through concatenated protein sequences to determine evolutionary relationships among bacterial species."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ff28716c2f25b8550595e1f473add0c4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRENNERIA ALNI NCPPB\(^{\MATHRM{T}}\)\">
      <data key="d0">BACTERIUM\</data>
      <data key="d1">Brenneria alni NCPPB\(^{\mathrm{T}}\) serves as an outgroup in the phylogenetic analysis to establish evolutionary relationships."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ff28716c2f25b8550595e1f473add0c4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MIXTA CALIDA 1400/07*, MIXTA GAVINIAE A18/07*, MIXTA TENEBRIONIS BIT-26*, MIXTA INTESTINALIS 2Y989B*, MIXTA THELICOLA QCSS-366*\">
      <data key="d0">BACTERIUM\</data>
