      <data key="d2">chunk-ff28716c2f25b8550595e1f473add0c4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TATUMELLA\">
      <data key="d0">GENUS\</data>
      <data key="d1">Tatumella is a bacterial genus that includes species compared to the novel strain BIT-26\(^{\mathrm{T}}\) for taxonomic classification."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ff28716c2f25b8550595e1f473add0c4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYPHASIC APPROACH\">
      <data key="d0">PROCESS\</data>
      <data key="d1">A polyphasic approach involves combining multiple methods (e.g., genetic sequencing, phenotypic analysis) for comprehensive taxonomic identification of bacterial strains."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ff28716c2f25b8550595e1f473add0c4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MAXIMUM-LIKELIHOOD TREE\">
      <data key="d0">BIOLOGICAL PROCESS\</data>
      <data key="d1">The Maximum-likelihood tree is a statistical method used to infer evolutionary relationships among bacterial species based on genetic sequences."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ff28716c2f25b8550595e1f473add0c4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BOOTSTRAP VALUES\">
      <data key="d0">BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT\</data>
      <data key="d1">Bootstrap values represent the statistical support for branches in phylogenetic trees, indicating the reliability of inferred evolutionary relationships."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ff28716c2f25b8550595e1f473add0c4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUBSTITUTIONS PER NUCLEOTIDE POSITION\">
      <data key="d0">BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE\</data>
      <data key="d1">This measure quantifies the rate of nucleotide changes in DNA sequences, providing insights into evolutionary distances between species."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ff28716c2f25b8550595e1f473add0c4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUBSTITUTIONS PER AMINO ACID POSITION\">
      <data key="d0">BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE\</data>
      <data key="d1">This measure quantifies the rate of amino acid changes in protein sequences, providing insights into evolutionary distances between species."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ff28716c2f25b8550595e1f473add0c4</data>
    </node>
