    <node id="&quot;16S RNA GENE PHYLOGENY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"16S RNA Gene Phylogeny refers to the study of bacterial relationships through analysis of the 16S rRNA gene sequences."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-014b72d0a2657cbc89c4dee5f2b32bba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MLSAPHYLOTYPING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Multilocus Sequence Analysis (MLSA) involves comparing multiple genetic loci for phylogenetic classification."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-014b72d0a2657cbc89c4dee5f2b32bba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COLONY PIGMENTATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Colony pigmentation refers to the color of bacterial colonies, which can vary among species."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-014b72d0a2657cbc89c4dee5f2b32bba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VOGES–PROSKAUER TEST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Voges–Proskauer test detects acetoin production from glucose fermentation, indicating metabolic activity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-014b72d0a2657cbc89c4dee5f2b32bba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INDOLE PRODUCTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Indole production involves the breakdown of tryptophan into indole, used to identify certain bacteria."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-014b72d0a2657cbc89c4dee5f2b32bba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CITRATE UTILIZATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Citrate utilization tests the ability of bacteria to use citrate as a carbon source."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-014b72d0a2657cbc89c4dee5f2b32bba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GELATINASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gelatinase is an enzyme that hydrolyzes gelatin, used to identify gelatin-degrading bacteria."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-014b72d0a2657cbc89c4dee5f2b32bba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ARGININE DIHYDROLASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Arginine dihydrolase is an enzyme involved in the degradation of arginine."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-014b72d0a2657cbc89c4dee5f2b32bba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ORNITHINE DECARBOXYLASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ornithine Decarboxylase is an enzyme that decarboxylates ornithine, distinguishing BIT-26T from closely related species in the genus Mixta."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ornithine decarboxylase catalyzes the decarboxylation of ornithine."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ornithine decarboxylase is an enzyme that catalyzes the conversion of ornithine to putrescine."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-146789a250a0dbaae0d8438de692e191&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d043948723ae25a365e297c98300be3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-014b72d0a2657cbc89c4dee5f2b32bba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SALICIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Salicin is a glycoside that BIT-26T can utilize for acid production."&lt;SEP&gt;"Salicin is a glycoside that serves as a substrate for bacterial metabolism."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8d043948723ae25a365e297c98300be3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-014b72d0a2657cbc89c4dee5f2b32bba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CELLOBIOSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cellobiose is a disaccharide that BIT-26T cannot utilize for acid production."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cellobiose is a disaccharide that can be utilized by certain bacteria."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8d043948723ae25a365e297c98300be3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-014b72d0a2657cbc89c4dee5f2b32bba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LACTOSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lactose is a disaccharide sugar that is metabolized by lactose-fermenting bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lactose is a disaccharide that BIT-26T can utilize for acid production."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8d043948723ae25a365e297c98300be3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-014b72d0a2657cbc89c4dee5f2b32bba</data>
