    <node id="&quot;FECUNDITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fecundity indicates the reproductive capacity of mealworms, measured by the number of eggs laid by females after mating."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fecundity refers to the reproductive capacity of T. molitor, which is significantly affected by pupal weight and possibly adult weight."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fecundity refers to the reproductive capacity of mealworms, measured by the number of eggs laid."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d6a80044bea074bdbcb68f489aa8af0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32f340b7166025be3c56178a94ae480d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd3cec3addc1bee202783dff1583ba54</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PREPUPAL PERIOD&quot;">
