    <node id="&quot;CRONOBACTER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cronobacter is a Gram-negative bacterial genus more abundant in PS samples, though inconsistently represented across resamples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cronobacter is a Gram-negative genus known for creating biofilms on plastic surfaces but not recorded in plastic breakdown."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cronobacter is a bacterial genus identified in the gut microbiota of polystyrene-fed larvae, associated with plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cronobacter is a bacterial genus significantly more abundant in PS samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cronobacter is a bacterial genus that appeared overrepresented in PS samples with a Log2-fold change of 5.8."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cronobacter is a genus of bacteria found in the gut microbiota of mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d9095195e9cf06b9887c03abde6284d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6ddf9dd30d7258964408f9a915d3478&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b4b45d826a6a7956015e680f5fb8ee6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1070f8c33eb8afcfcffac95df9012d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32f340b7166025be3c56178a94ae480d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-001e8f54368c9a236f702fd09cddf4a8</data>
    </node>
