    <node id="&quot;CATIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cation concentration in the insects' frass varies depending on the diet provided."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cations are positively charged ions measured in multivariate analysis to assess biodegradation parameters."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cations are positively charged ions, such as magnesium, sodium, and potassium, whose concentrations were measured in the insect frass."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cations such as potassium, sodium, magnesium, and calcium are involved in biochemical processes during PS biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a0d2f43eebe2309fba46c5335d76df56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6338d56b535220f260826703b0f7229&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-395b01f15fd97b70e2368941120e9a37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a708f09b97ac93da05bd1d20bdfe174</data>
