    <node id="&quot;MAGNESIUM (MG²⁺)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MINERAL"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Magnesium is an essential mineral that acts as a cofactor in various biochemical activities, including cellular energy production processes. It plays a crucial role in mitochondrial functions and energy metabolism."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5a708f09b97ac93da05bd1d20bdfe174</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SODIUM (NA⁺)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MINERAL"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sodium is a mineral involved in osmoregulation and excretion processes in insects, primarily through the action of V-ATPase and Na⁺/K⁺-ATPase enzymes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5a708f09b97ac93da05bd1d20bdfe174</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POTASSIUM (K⁺)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MINERAL"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Potassium is a mineral involved in osmoregulation and excretion processes in insects, working synergistically with NH₄⁺ and K⁺ to regulate ammonia transport."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5a708f09b97ac93da05bd1d20bdfe174</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;V-ATPASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"V-ATPase is an enzyme responsible for maintaining pH gradients across membranes and plays a key role in osmoregulation and ion transport."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5a708f09b97ac93da05bd1d20bdfe174</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NA⁺/K⁺-ATPASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Na⁺/K⁺-ATPase is an enzyme that regulates sodium and potassium levels across cell membranes, playing a vital role in osmoregulation and ion balance."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5a708f09b97ac93da05bd1d20bdfe174</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ELECTRON TRANSPORT CHAIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
