      <data key="d1">"PE-WC co-feed combines polyethylene and waxcomb, enhancing both biodegradation rates and survivability."&lt;SEP&gt;"PE-WC co-feed is a diet combining polyethylene and waxcomb, enhancing waxworm growth and biodegradation efficiency."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ab6b219720db5a6e3384c884c280984c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b25215becbc007a60f24b86a2d6aaf26</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENZYMES SYNTHESIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Enzyme synthesis involves the production of enzymes necessary for metabolic processes, including the degradation of polyethylene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ab6b219720db5a6e3384c884c280984c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NUTRIENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nutrients are essential substances required for the growth, development, and survival of organisms like waxworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b25215becbc007a60f24b86a2d6aaf26</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIFE CYCLE STAGES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Life cycle stages refer to the developmental phases of waxworms, including larva, pupa, moth, and egg."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b25215becbc007a60f24b86a2d6aaf26</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;C-H ROCKING ALKANES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNCTIONAL GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"C-H rocking alkanes are functional groups identified in PE through FTIR analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b25215becbc007a60f24b86a2d6aaf26</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;C-N STRETCHING ALIPHATIC AMINES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNCTIONAL GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"C-N stretching aliphatic amines are functional groups detected in control samples via FTIR analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b25215becbc007a60f24b86a2d6aaf26</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;N-O ASYMMETRIC STRETCHING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNCTIONAL GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"N-O asymmetric stretching refers to functional groups analyzed in positive controls using FTIR techniques."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b25215becbc007a60f24b86a2d6aaf26</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FIRST-GENERATION WAXWORMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LIFE STAGE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"First-generation waxworms are the initial cohort of larvae used in experiments involving PE degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b25215becbc007a60f24b86a2d6aaf26</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SECOND-GENERATION WAXWORMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LIFE STAGE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Second-generation waxworms are offspring of first-generation waxworms, reared under controlled conditions for further studies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b25215becbc007a60f24b86a2d6aaf26</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIO-MINERALIZATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bio-mineralization refers to the transformation of organic material into simpler forms through biological activity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b25215becbc007a60f24b86a2d6aaf26</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;A. GRISEA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Achoria grisea is the scientific name for lesser waxworms, which are capable of ingesting and degrading polyethylene as part of their diet."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b9bd8cf0d5102bbca724e0773be0eeae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;^1H NMR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Proton Nuclear Magnetic Resonance (^1H NMR) is employed to further confirm the presence of newly formed chemical groups in the egested frass of A. grisea larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b9bd8cf0d5102bbca724e0773be0eeae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNSATURATED HYDROCARBON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Unsaturated hydrocarbons are observed to increase during the biodegradation of polyethylene, indicating chemical transformation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b9bd8cf0d5102bbca724e0773be0eeae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALCOHOLIC GROUPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNCTIONAL GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Alcoholic groups appear in the egested frass, serving as evidence of the biodegradation process."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b9bd8cf0d5102bbca724e0773be0eeae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CENTRAL INSTRUMENTATION FACILITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
