      <data key="d2">chunk-b9bd8cf0d5102bbca724e0773be0eeae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TITANIA NANOTUBES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MATERIAL"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Titania nanotubes are used as photocatalysts in the degradation of low-density polyethylene films."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b9bd8cf0d5102bbca724e0773be0eeae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RHODOCOCCUS RHODOCHROUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A bacterium capable of metabolizing styrene, contributing to the biological breakdown of plastic compounds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rhodococcus rhodochrous is a thermophilic bacterium involved in the biodegradation of polyethylene through oxidized oligomers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ecf2c478d08c7bc8e491f630aa289881&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44e006d8af33633a06dac6789334329d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ACHORIA GRISEA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"INSECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Achoria grisea, referred to as the lesser wax moth, is compared biologically with Galleria mellonella in entomological studies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ecf2c478d08c7bc8e491f630aa289881</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MANGROVE SOIL MICROFLORA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mangrove soil microflora refers to the diverse microbial community found in mangrove ecosystems, which has been studied for its ability to degrade polythene materials."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ecf2c478d08c7bc8e491f630aa289881</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NIGER DELTA MANGROVE SWAMP&quot;">
