      <data key="d1">"The Niger Delta mangrove swamp is an ecosystem rich in biodiversity, where indigenous Bacillus species have been identified for their role in polyethylene degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ecf2c478d08c7bc8e491f630aa289881</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;13C-NMR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL REACTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"13C-NMR is a nuclear magnetic resonance technique used to study branching patterns in low-density polyethylene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ecf2c478d08c7bc8e491f630aa289881</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THERMO-OXIDATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Thermo-oxidation involves heat-induced oxidation of polymers, enhancing their biodegradability by microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thermo-oxidation refers to the chemical process involving heat-induced oxidation, affecting the degradation of environmentally exposed polyethylene films."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thermo-oxidation is a pretreatment process applied to enhance PE biodegradability."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ecf2c478d08c7bc8e491f630aa289881&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1006283f24aba2aa605f9e719f36cf9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-694aaaa7c2839ea048d46b6a2bb13748</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYTHENE CARRY BAGS&quot;">
