      <data key="d2">chunk-933de951613fc7eadfd14dde9bd18b2d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GELATIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROTEIN"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gelatin is a protein derived from collagen, used in the creation of biodegradable films blended with poly(vinyl alcohol) and studied for its physical properties."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c1d3c25b9affee2f535cb531a09a2384</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLY(VINYL ALCOHOL)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Poly(vinyl alcohol) (PVA) is a synthetic polymer used in combination with gelatin to create biodegradable films, where its type or concentration affects film properties."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c1d3c25b9affee2f535cb531a09a2384</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHOTO-OXIDATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Photo-oxidation is a chemical reaction involving light exposure that accelerates the degradation of polymers like polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Photo-oxidation is a pretreatment process applied to enhance PE biodegradability."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c1d3c25b9affee2f535cb531a09a2384&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-694aaaa7c2839ea048d46b6a2bb13748</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THERMALLY TREATED LOW-DENSITY POLYETHYLENE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Thermally treated low-density polyethylene undergoes changes that enhance its susceptibility to biodegradation by fungi such as Penicillium pinophilum and Aspergillus niger."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c1d3c25b9affee2f535cb531a09a2384</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYETHYLENE GLYCOL MODIFIED TIO2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polyethylene glycol modified TiO2 acts as a pro-oxidant additive, enhancing the photo-oxidation and subsequent biodegradation of polyethylene films."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c1d3c25b9affee2f535cb531a09a2384</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FRESHWATER ECOSYSTEMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ECOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Freshwater ecosystems are natural environments where microplastics pose significant risks to aquatic life and ecological balance."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c1d3c25b9affee2f535cb531a09a2384</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHYSIOCHEMICAL PROPERTIES&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-3bd104d06a1ede06701ecfa96bccc2c4</data>
      <data key="d1">"FTIR is used to analyze changes in the physiochemical properties of materials such as polyethylene during degradation."</data>
      <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COI SEQUENCE&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-5af82472112cbc9e76b1fd1ac6e8c54e</data>
      <data key="d1">"These kits read PCR amplicons, generating sequences for COI gene analysis."</data>
      <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PAPER&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-9f2303f3680e9313daac77bb7e27e7da</data>
      <data key="d1">"Paper is provided as a surface for larvae to spin cocoons and for female moths to lay eggs."</data>
