    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HOLE FORMATION&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-af5eb6a8326b4977801e2f7694a2c750</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hole formation on PE films serves as a visible indicator of the physical and biological degradation caused by A. grisella larvae."</data>
      <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;YELLOW AND DARK MEALWORMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Yellow and dark mealworms (Tenebrio molitor and Tenebrio obscurus) are insect larvae capable of biodegrading commercial polyethylene materials at a high rate."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-326a8dda1cdd196236b9c836192c76f1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRANCHING STRUCTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL FEATURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Branching structure, including short and long chain branches, influences the packing and crystallinity of polyethylene, affecting its biodegradability."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-326a8dda1cdd196236b9c836192c76f1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PY-GC/MS ANALYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL REACTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Py-GC/MS analysis confirms the breaking of the macromolecule backbone and formation of oxidized functional groups during biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-326a8dda1cdd196236b9c836192c76f1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RELATIVE DOMINANCE ANALYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Relative dominance analysis assesses the impact of various factors on the biodegradation of PE polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Relative dominance analysis is a statistical method used to determine the impact of different factors on the biodegradation process."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-326a8dda1cdd196236b9c836192c76f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-988ef111808996ddbe6e483d6505ab45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SHORT CHAIN BRANCHING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL FEATURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Short chain branching involves shorter side chains in polymers, influencing packing density and crystallinity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Short chain branching refers to the presence of short side chains in polyethylene, influencing its crystallinity and biodegradability."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-326a8dda1cdd196236b9c836192c76f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f75b58db5211fc7348ccca8206b9bbae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LONG CHAIN BRANCHING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL FEATURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Long chain branching involves longer side chains in polyethylene, affecting its packing and crystallinity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Long chain branching refers to extended side chains in polymers like LDPE, impacting crystallinity and degradation rates."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-326a8dda1cdd196236b9c836192c76f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f75b58db5211fc7348ccca8206b9bbae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INTERMOLECULAR FORCES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Intermolecular forces describe the attractions between polymer chains, influencing structure and stability."&lt;SEP&gt;"Intermolecular forces in polyethylene are influenced by its molecular structure, impacting its physical properties and biodegradability."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-326a8dda1cdd196236b9c836192c76f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f75b58db5211fc7348ccca8206b9bbae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ACINETOBACTER SP. NYZ450&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Acinetobacter sp. NyZ450 is part of a co-culture that reduces the weight of PE mulching film."&lt;SEP&gt;"Acinetobacter sp. NyZ450, isolated from mealworms ingesting polyethylene mulching film, forms biofilm and decomposes polyethylene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a1006283f24aba2aa605f9e719f36cf9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eadba0dcfe8eff9c8040ec5f17e1adb3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BACILLUS SP. NYZ451&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bacillus sp. NyZ451 is part of a co-culture that reduces the weight of PE mulching film."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a1006283f24aba2aa605f9e719f36cf9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PE WAX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PE Wax refers to low molecular weight PE, which can be degraded relatively quickly by bacterial consortia."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a1006283f24aba2aa605f9e719f36cf9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MECHANICAL PROPERTY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mechanical properties of polymers, such as tensile strength and flexibility, influence their susceptibility to biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a1006283f24aba2aa605f9e719f36cf9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRIBOLIUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"INSECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tribolium, a genus of darkling beetles, includes species whose larvae have been found to rapidly biodegrade plastics like PE and PS."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a1006283f24aba2aa605f9e719f36cf9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1, 2, 4-TRICHLOROBENZENE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"1, 2, 4-Trichlorobenzene is a solvent used in the extraction and analysis of residual PE from frass."&lt;SEP&gt;"1, 2, 4-trichlorobenzene is a solvent used for extracting residual PE from frass during the depolymerization process."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-30a7209d626a6319ba5600bea7f27299&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6afbb58ebe9108893daf7e65d59fac39</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROTON NUCLEAR MAGNETIC RESONANCE (1H NMR) SPECTROSCOPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"1H NMR analyzes chemical modifications and degraded functional groups in egested frass, using software like MestReNova for spectrum analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6afbb58ebe9108893daf7e65d59fac39</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;X-RAY DIFFRACTION INSTRUMENT&quot;">
