    <node id="&quot;DRIED WHEY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dried Whey is a dairy product derived from the liquid remaining after milk has been curdled and strained."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dried whey is a feed source used in the experiment, leading to moderate mortality rates."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dried whey is a feed type used in the experiment, contributing to measurable crude protein and fat content in larvae and excrement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dried whey is a milk-based product used as feed, influencing larval life cycles."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dried whey is a protein-rich feed with high carbohydrate and protein content."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dried whey is another type of feed tested for Tenebrio molitor larvae. While it reduces larval mortality, it slows down the developmental cycle rate."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b8a706f2bd66291a3ef925114ffd9300&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eed90a978852274ead3771418cd60bed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d01d291012bd548fc067e250ec39fba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbf28f07f3e46b29e447aae784667c29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a170da66288c73388872b8a43fa51e33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-531058c4540bd4e6a50d141db01d4d11</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RAW WARE POTATOES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
