    <node id="&quot;NITROGENOUS SUBSTANCES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRITIONAL COMPONENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nitrogenous substances are components analyzed in the study to assess the nutritional value of the larvae under different feeding conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrogenous substances are components measured in larvae and excrement, representing crude protein content."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrogenous substances include proteins and amino acids that impact insect growth and development."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrogenous substances include proteins and amino acids, which play a crucial role in larval growth and development."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrogenous substances were measured using the Kjeldahl method to assess the nutritional quality of larvae and their excreta."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a170da66288c73388872b8a43fa51e33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-531058c4540bd4e6a50d141db01d4d11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d01d291012bd548fc067e250ec39fba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba22196a59b67cbf67af7d76a039af1e</data>
