      <data key="d1">"Potatoes are a feed type that led to a fatty acid content of 236.0 g/kg dry matter in mealworm larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Potatoes are a nutrient-rich food source that resulted in the lowest mortality and no developmental defects in mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Potatoes represent a type of feed or dietary component used in the analysis of fatty acid proportions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Potatoes serve as a dietary component for mealworms, influencing their fatty acid composition and overall growth."</data>
