      <data key="d1">"C18:2, or Linoleic acid, is an essential omega-6 polyunsaturated fatty acid."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b8a706f2bd66291a3ef925114ffd9300</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;C18:3&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FATTY ACID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"C18:3 is a type of fatty acid whose concentration varies depending on the feed type given to the larvae, with notable differences observed in potato-fed samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"C18:3, or Alpha-linolenic acid, is an essential omega-3 polyunsaturated fatty acid."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ba22196a59b67cbf67af7d76a039af1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8a706f2bd66291a3ef925114ffd9300</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;C20:2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FATTY ACID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"C20:2 is a fatty acid that exhibits varying levels depending on the diet provided to the mealworm larvae, showing distinct patterns across different feeds."&lt;SEP&gt;"C20:2 is a fatty acid with varying content depending on the feed type, as observed in the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"C20:2 is a polyunsaturated fatty acid involved in various biological processes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a660790845c6a68ed38b428a7756fc84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba22196a59b67cbf67af7d76a039af1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8a706f2bd66291a3ef925114ffd9300</data>
    </node>
