      <data key="d0">"FATTY ACID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Linolenic Acid is an omega-3 fatty acid with a content range from 0.3% to 1.6% across various studies, but lower values were determined in this work."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a660790845c6a68ed38b428a7756fc84</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WHEY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DIET"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Whey is a dairy by-product used as a feed in the analysis of fatty acid proportions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Whey is a feed type that resulted in a fatty acid content of 179.9 g/kg dry matter in mealworm larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Whey is a nutrient-rich byproduct of cheese production, used as feed for mealworms, resulting in higher fatty acid contents compared to other feeds."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a660790845c6a68ed38b428a7756fc84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abb542a26376f51c3cd9247fe3d56854&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba22196a59b67cbf67af7d76a039af1e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MONOENOIC FATTY ACIDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FATTY ACID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Monoenoic Fatty Acids are unsaturated fatty acids with one double bond, representing the majority of fatty acids in the studied samples."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a660790845c6a68ed38b428a7756fc84</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYENE FATTY ACIDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FATTY ACID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polyene Fatty Acids are polyunsaturated fatty acids with multiple double bonds, showing a sum range from 21.3% (whey) to 26.7% (bran)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a660790845c6a68ed38b428a7756fc84</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUM OF SATURATED FA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Sum of Saturated FA represents the total saturated fatty acids in mealworm larvae, influenced by different feed types."&lt;SEP&gt;"The sum of saturated fatty acids represents a metabolic measure indicating the total amount of saturated fatty acids present in the larvae samples."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a660790845c6a68ed38b428a7756fc84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba22196a59b67cbf67af7d76a039af1e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUM OF MONOENOIC FA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Sum of Monoenoic FA refers to the total monounsaturated fatty acids in mealworm larvae, showing significant variation across different feeds."&lt;SEP&gt;"The sum of monoenoic fatty acids reflects a metabolic measure of the total monoene fatty acids in the larvae and their excrement."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a660790845c6a68ed38b428a7756fc84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba22196a59b67cbf67af7d76a039af1e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUM OF POLYENOIC FA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Sum of Polyenoic FA indicates the total polyunsaturated fatty acids in mealworm larvae, reflecting dietary impacts."&lt;SEP&gt;"The sum of polyenoic fatty acids serves as a metabolic measure for the total polyene fatty acids detected in the larvae and their excrement."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a660790845c6a68ed38b428a7756fc84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba22196a59b67cbf67af7d76a039af1e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TOTAL FA CONTENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Total FA Content measures the overall fatty acid content in mealworm larvae, providing insight into nutritional value."&lt;SEP&gt;"Total fatty acid content refers to the overall quantity of fatty acids measured in the larvae, influenced by the type of feed."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a660790845c6a68ed38b428a7756fc84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba22196a59b67cbf67af7d76a039af1e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FAEXC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"FAexc refers to the fatty acid content in excrement, used to calculate the proportion relative to fatty acid content in the body."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a660790845c6a68ed38b428a7756fc84</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FALAR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"FAlar denotes the fatty acid content in the larvae, used for calculating the excrement-to-body fatty acid ratio."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a660790845c6a68ed38b428a7756fc84</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FAD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"FAD is the calculated fatty acid proportion in excrement relative to the body, indicating dietary efficiency."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a660790845c6a68ed38b428a7756fc84</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;C10 ACID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FATTY ACID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"C10 Acid is a saturated fatty acid with notable proportions in excrement, especially when fed polystyrene or whey."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a660790845c6a68ed38b428a7756fc84</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;C17 ACID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FATTY ACID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"C17 Acid is a saturated fatty acid with a carbon chain length of 17, showing varying proportions across different feeds."&lt;SEP&gt;"C17 Acid shows trends similar to C10 Acid in its excrement-to-body ratio, influenced by diet."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a660790845c6a68ed38b428a7756fc84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abb542a26376f51c3cd9247fe3d56854</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;C18 ACID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FATTY ACID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"C18 Acid exhibits trends similar to C10 Acid, indicating dietary effects on fatty acid retention."&lt;SEP&gt;"C18 Acid is a saturated fatty acid with a carbon chain length of 18, exhibiting differing proportions in various feeds."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a660790845c6a68ed38b428a7756fc84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abb542a26376f51c3cd9247fe3d56854</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;C20 ACID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FATTY ACID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"C20 Acid displays an opposite trend compared to C10 and C17 Acids, highlighting dietary-specific variations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a660790845c6a68ed38b428a7756fc84</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SATURATED C10 ACID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FATTY ACID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Saturated C10 Acid is a fatty acid with a carbon chain length of 10, exhibiting varying proportions in different feeds such as polystyrene, whey, and potatoes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-abb542a26376f51c3cd9247fe3d56854</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SATURATED C20 ACID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FATTY ACID"</data>
