      <data key="d1">"Pseudomonadaceae is a bacterial family significantly more abundant in PS samples than in CT samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonadaceae is a family of bacteria commonly found in insect guts and involved in the degradation of various substances."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonadaceae is a family of bacteria reported to be active in insect guts, potentially involved in polystyrene degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonadaceae rises from absent to 7.68% in PP-fed groups, signifying its involvement in PP degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonadaceae is a family of bacteria identified in this study, accounting for 80% of strains in mealworm intestines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonadaceae is a family within Gammaproteobacteria identified in the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonadaceae is a family within Gammaproteobacteria, including species like Pseudomonas multiresinivorans, Pseudomonas nitroreducens, and Pseudomonas plecoglossicida."</data>
