      <data key="d1">"Aspergillus niger can degrade thermally oxidized high-density polyethylene isolated from plastic waste dumpsites."</data>
      <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MICROBIAL ASSISTED DEGRADATION&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-5f99668e767a56e2e64ece791653b952</data>
      <data key="d1">"Microbes assist in the degradation of high impact polystyrene (HIPS), enhancing its biodegradability."</data>
      <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMBINED OZONATION AND BIODEGRADATION&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-5f99668e767a56e2e64ece791653b952</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polymeric aromatic hydrocarbons in soil can be remediated using a combination of ozonation and biodegradation techniques."</data>
      <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PSEUDOMONAS SPECIES&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-5f99668e767a56e2e64ece791653b952</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pseudomonas species contribute to the biodegradation of low-density polythene (LDPE), enhancing its environmental breakdown."</data>
      <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ASPERGILLUS NIGER&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-5f99668e767a56e2e64ece791653b952</data>
      <data key="d1">"Aspergillus niger degrades thermally oxidized high-density polyethylene, contributing to plastic waste management."</data>
      <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ASPERGILLUS ORYZAE&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-5f99668e767a56e2e64ece791653b952</data>
      <data key="d1">"Aspergillus oryzae produces enzymes capable of degrading biodegradable plastics, supporting sustainable practices."</data>
      <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GLOEOPHYLLUM TRABEUM&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-5f99668e767a56e2e64ece791653b952</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gloeophyllum trabeum utilizes hydroquinone-driven Fenton chemistry to break down polystyrene sulfonate."</data>
      <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AZOTOBACTER BEIJERINCKII HM121&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-5f99668e767a56e2e64ece791653b952</data>
      <data key="d1">"Azotobacter beijerinckii HM121 produces enzyme hydroquinone peroxidase, enabling the enzymatic degradation of polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="POLYMERIC AROMATIC HYDROCARBONS&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-5f99668e767a56e2e64ece791653b952</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ozonation is used in combination with biodegradation to remediate polymeric aromatic hydrocarbons in soil."</data>
      <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PLASTIC WASTE&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-5f99668e767a56e2e64ece791653b952</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biodegradation processes help in breaking down plastic waste, reducing environmental pollution."</data>
      <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ETHYLENE VINYL ACETATE (EVA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ethylene Vinyl Acetate is a copolymer plastic used in the study to test its effects on larval growth and gut microbiomes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9d7500fe4985cb2b885f9eb244ed3c2e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GUT FUNGI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNGI"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gut fungi are fungal communities found in the gut microbiome, contributing to digestion and possibly plastic degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9d7500fe4985cb2b885f9eb244ed3c2e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STARVATION GROUP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONTROL GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The starvation group refers to larvae that were not fed any diet, used as a control to compare survival rates."&lt;SEP&gt;"The starvation group refers to yellow mealworms that were not fed any diet, used as a baseline to compare survival and growth."&lt;SEP&gt;"The starvation group represents yellow mealworms not fed any diet, used to compare weight changes and survival rates."&lt;SEP&gt;"The starvation group represents larvae that did not receive any food, used for comparison with microplastic-fed groups."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7d0e4cb4324bc684ebb2ca6136c04ad0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdc8398efba587929eebd0a0842f6e69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-444b8acd02a76616457012e1ac0db23b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d7500fe4985cb2b885f9eb244ed3c2e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYOLEFIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of plastic whose degradation shows slight similarities with copolymers in the gut microbial community structure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyolefin is a type of plastic used as an experimental feedstock in the study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3e34d58a20a707b35e8fcd5658ba2924&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-444b8acd02a76616457012e1ac0db23b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COPOLYMER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Copolymer is a type of plastic used as an experimental feedstock in the study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-444b8acd02a76616457012e1ac0db23b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EVA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"EVA (Ethylene Vinyl Acetate) is a type of plastic consumed by yellow mealworms, showing significant changes in Mn, Mw, and Mz during biodegradation via limited extent depolymerization."&lt;SEP&gt;"EVA (ethylene-vinyl acetate) is a foam plastic fed to yellow mealworms in one of the experimental groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"EVA refers to Ethylene Vinyl Acetate, a copolymer used in a variety of applications such as packaging and adhesives."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7d0e4cb4324bc684ebb2ca6136c04ad0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-444b8acd02a76616457012e1ac0db23b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7043eb8aa4221f396a5c65fb6493bd41</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;O-H BEND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNCTIONAL GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"O-H bend is a functional group identified in ATR-FTIR analysis, indicating oxidation and depolymerization of plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7d0e4cb4324bc684ebb2ca6136c04ad0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MORAXELLACEAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FAMILY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Moraxellaceae increases from absent to 13.29% in PP-fed groups, indicating its potential role in PP degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Moraxellaceae is a family of bacteria identified in this study, accounting for 80% of strains in mealworm intestines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Moraxellaceae is a family within Gammaproteobacteria identified in the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"Moraxellaceae is a family within Gammaproteobacteria, containing Acinetobacter septicus."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-10f59d5d10f08e8107f36bff5a4c93ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-476e13b69587aa4e81395e2fd00a9d5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eadba0dcfe8eff9c8040ec5f17e1adb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfd05eac1abc28ac416e6a56ccd6a9d6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PORPHYROMONADACEAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FAMILY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Porphyromonadaceae increases from 8.78% to 8.87% in EVA-fed groups, correlating with EVA foam degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-476e13b69587aa4e81395e2fd00a9d5a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PEDICOCCUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pedicoccus disappears in plastic-fed groups despite being dominant in bran-fed groups, indicating diet-specific changes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-476e13b69587aa4e81395e2fd00a9d5a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PU (POLYURETHANE)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PU is a plastic polymer linked to unclassified Enterobacteriaceae dominance and distinct fungal communities."&lt;SEP&gt;"PU is a plastic type associated with a high abundance of Enterobacteriaceae, indicating its role in shaping the gut microbiota for PU degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a3f07da33b55bf8a25fe06beee23e90e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-476e13b69587aa4e81395e2fd00a9d5a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EVA (ETHYLENE VINYL ACETATE)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"EVA is a plastic diet linked to increased abundances of Enterobacteriaceae and Porphyromonadaceae, suggesting their involvement in EVA degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-476e13b69587aa4e81395e2fd00a9d5a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNWEIGHTED UNIFRAC ANALYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Unweighted UniFrac Analysis is a method used to reveal distinguishable clusters associated with different consumed diets, highlighting dietary impacts on gut bacteria."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-476e13b69587aa4e81395e2fd00a9d5a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLASTIC INGESTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Plastic ingestion leads to significant changes in the gut bacterial community, altering the relative abundances of specific bacterial families and genera."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-476e13b69587aa4e81395e2fd00a9d5a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMMUNITY SHIFT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Community Shift describes the changes in gut bacterial composition due to different diets, particularly plastic types, affecting microbial diversity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-476e13b69587aa4e81395e2fd00a9d5a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RELATIVE ABUNDANCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Relative Abundance measures the proportion of specific bacterial taxa within the gut bacterial community, reflecting dietary influences."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-476e13b69587aa4e81395e2fd00a9d5a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CEREAL GRAINS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cereal grains are a source of nutrients like bran and fiber, commonly used in diets."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7043eb8aa4221f396a5c65fb6493bd41</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYMERIZATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polymerization is a chemical process that creates polymers such as PP, PU, and EVA."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7043eb8aa4221f396a5c65fb6493bd41</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ETHYLENE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ethylene is a chemical compound that forms the basis of EVA polymer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ethylene is a gaseous product formed during acetylene reduction assays, indicating nitrogen-fixing activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ethylene is a product of the acetylene reduction process and serves as an indicator of nitrogen-fixing activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ethylene is produced during acetylene reduction assays as a result of nitrogenase activity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-813b71242f366f10218c10631cd7dee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b12451ba2a22e6f74c543f982a0a7b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e37da2fbe64f85c50c36da45006f4c23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7043eb8aa4221f396a5c65fb6493bd41</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VINYL ACETATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Vinyl Acetate is a chemical compound that combines with ethylene to form EVA."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7043eb8aa4221f396a5c65fb6493bd41</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADHESIVE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Adhesives are substances like PU and EVA used for bonding materials together."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7043eb8aa4221f396a5c65fb6493bd41</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PACKAGING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Packaging is an application where materials like EVA and PP are extensively utilized."&lt;SEP&gt;"Packaging refers to the materials and methods used to wrap or protect products, often contributing to plastic waste."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0b50c5a85182344022614ffe10dc9382&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7043eb8aa4221f396a5c65fb6493bd41</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DYGONOMONAS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dygonomonas was a specific genus associated with EVA diet, indicating its role in EVA degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a3f07da33b55bf8a25fe06beee23e90e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MORTIERELLOMYCOTA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYLUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mortierellomycota is a fungal phylum present in the gut fungal community, though less dominant compared to Ascomycota and Basidiomycota."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a3f07da33b55bf8a25fe06beee23e90e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DEBAROMYCESACEAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FAMILY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Debaromycesaceae was the dominant family in bran-fed groups but decreased significantly in plastics-fed groups."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a3f07da33b55bf8a25fe06beee23e90e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPORIDIOBOLACEAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FAMILY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sporidiobolaceae became dominant in plastic-fed groups, particularly in EVA-fed groups."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a3f07da33b55bf8a25fe06beee23e90e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TREMELLACEAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FAMILY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tremellaceae was another dominant family in plastic-fed groups, showing significant differences among various plastic types."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a3f07da33b55bf8a25fe06beee23e90e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AUREOBASIDIACEAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FAMILY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Aureobasidiaceae was dominant in PU-fed groups, indicating its role in PU degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a3f07da33b55bf8a25fe06beee23e90e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPOROBACTERIACEAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FAMILY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sporobacteriaceae had a high relative abundance in EVA-fed groups, increasing significantly compared to bran-fed groups."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a3f07da33b55bf8a25fe06beee23e90e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EVA (ETHYLENE-VINYL ACETATE)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"EVA is a copolymer associated with Dygonomonas and unique fungal communities such as Sporobacteriaceae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a3f07da33b55bf8a25fe06beee23e90e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HYPHOPICHA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hyphopicha was dominant in bran-fed groups but decreased significantly in plastic-fed groups."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a3f07da33b55bf8a25fe06beee23e90e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OTUS (OPERATIONAL TAXONOMIC UNITS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A term used in microbiology to classify groups of closely related organisms based on sequence similarity."&lt;SEP&gt;"OTUs are used to measure species richness and diversity in microbial communities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a3f07da33b55bf8a25fe06beee23e90e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53ab7dd83bf51674598c6a5bdd146b90</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PP-FED GROUPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DIET"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Groups of yellow mealworms fed with polypropylene (PP) plastic, showing specific percentages of degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3e34d58a20a707b35e8fcd5658ba2924</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PU-FED GROUPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DIET"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Groups of yellow mealworms fed with polyurethane (PU) plastic, exhibiting higher microbial abundances and enzyme secretion for biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3e34d58a20a707b35e8fcd5658ba2924</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EVA-FED GROUPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DIET"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Groups of yellow mealworms fed with ethylene-vinyl acetate (EVA) copolymer, causing significant changes in gut microbial communities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3e34d58a20a707b35e8fcd5658ba2924</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRAN-FED GROUPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DIET"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Control group of yellow mealworms fed with bran, used as a baseline for comparison."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3e34d58a20a707b35e8fcd5658ba2924</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYESTER PLASTIC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of plastic composed of polyisocyanates and polyols, leading to greater enrichment of fungal colonies in the gut."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3e34d58a20a707b35e8fcd5658ba2924</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYISOCYANATES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A chemical component of polyester plastics that contributes to the enrichment of fungal colonies in the gut."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3e34d58a20a707b35e8fcd5658ba2924</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FUNGAL COMMUNITY RICHNESS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The diversity and abundance of fungi in the gut microbiome, observed to be higher in PU-fed groups."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3e34d58a20a707b35e8fcd5658ba2924</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CORE GUT FUNCTIONAL MICROBIOME&quot;">
