      <data key="d1">"Changes in water contact angle indicate alterations in surface properties of PP due to biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Water contact angle measures hydrophilicity, inversely related to microbial colonization on aged MPs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Water contact angle measures the hydrophobicity or hydrophilicity of plastic surfaces."&lt;SEP&gt;"Water contact angle measures the wettability and surface energy of the plastics tested."</data>
