    <node id="&quot;THIOL PEROXIDASE (TPX)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Thiol peroxidase (tpx) is an enzyme involved in oxidative stress response and identified in Enterobacter hormaechei LG3 during polystyrene degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a7cbc8be34e0de8aebc6fd547bacc627</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALKYL HYDROPEROXIDE REDUCTASE C (AHPC)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Alkyl hydroperoxide reductase C (ahpC) is an enzyme in the peroxidase family whose expression increases after Mi-PS treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alkyl hydroperoxide reductase C (ahpC) is an enzyme that helps in detoxifying reactive oxygen species and was identified in Enterobacter hormaechei LG3."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a7cbc8be34e0de8aebc6fd547bacc627&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f91980be083a0bf5b52d43a640e9d787</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BACTERIOFERRITIN COMIGRATORY PROTEIN (BCP)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROTEIN"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bacterioferritin comigratory protein (bcp) is a protein involved in iron storage and regulation, identified during polystyrene degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacterioferritin comigratory protein (bcp) is an enzyme in the peroxidase family whose expression increases after Mi-PS treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a7cbc8be34e0de8aebc6fd547bacc627&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f91980be083a0bf5b52d43a640e9d787</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIPID A&quot;">
      <data key="d0">|"LIPID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lipid A is a component of the outer membrane of Gram-negative bacteria, upregulated during polystyrene degradation by Enterobacter hormaechei LG3."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipid A is a toxic component of endotoxin found in opportunistic pathogens."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3a889b716cac361e6e04405777075076&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7cbc8be34e0de8aebc6fd547bacc627</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BACILLUS AMYLOLIQUEFACIENS SCGB1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A bacterial strain isolated from traditional Korean soybean-fermented foods capable of growing under anaerobic conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus amyloliquefaciens SCGB1 is a bacterium compared with Enterobacter hormaechei LG3 for its ability to degrade polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus amyloliquefaciens SCGB1 is a facultative gut bacterium used to confirm PS degradation capabilities in comparative studies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eafea2357c59ac6712f4d9ab41ac5d14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7cbc8be34e0de8aebc6fd547bacc627&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-050a4c71685bf71165985a79f528ed58</data>
    </node>
