      <data key="d1">"Strain SCGB1 is a bacterium belonging to the species Bacillus amyloliquefaciens and has been reported as both a PE- and PS-degrading organism."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d80979bb7e58b10bb558705b5d96fa99</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CFU CONCENTRATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CFU concentration measures the number of viable bacterial cells in a sample, indicating microbial growth and activity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d80979bb7e58b10bb558705b5d96fa99</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENTEROBACTER SP. STRAIN D1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Enterobacter sp. strain D1 is a bacterium capable of degrading PE under aerobic conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d80979bb7e58b10bb558705b5d96fa99</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENTEROBACTER CLOACAE AKS7&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Enterobacter cloacae AKS7 is a bacterium reported to degrade PE as a carbon source for cell growth under aerobic conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d80979bb7e58b10bb558705b5d96fa99</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LATE-INSTAR PS-FED LARVAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LIFE STAGE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Late-instar larvae refer to the developmental stage of insects, specifically those fed on polystyrene, providing a habitat for PS-degrading microorganisms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d80979bb7e58b10bb558705b5d96fa99</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VINYL ANAEROBIC CHAMBER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL FEATURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A vinyl anaerobic chamber is an apparatus designed to maintain anaerobic conditions for experiments requiring oxygen-free environments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d80979bb7e58b10bb558705b5d96fa99</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SHAKER INCUBATOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A shaker incubator is a device used to culture microorganisms under controlled temperature and agitation conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d80979bb7e58b10bb558705b5d96fa99</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STATIONARY INCUBATOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A stationary incubator is a device used to culture microorganisms without agitation, maintaining static conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d80979bb7e58b10bb558705b5d96fa99</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANAEROBIC INCUBATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Anaerobic incubation refers to the process of cultivating microorganisms in an oxygen-free environment, typically at 37°C."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-345c72af5aa26d5c4e06d7df5d8a1c85</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STERILE CONDITION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sterile condition refers to an environment free from microbial contamination, used as a control in experiments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-345c72af5aa26d5c4e06d7df5d8a1c85</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;E. HORMAECHEI LG3&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A specific bacterial strain isolated from mealworms, showing high anaerobic PS-degrading activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"E. hormaechei LG3 is a bacterial strain capable of forming biofilms and degrading PS films under anaerobic conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-345c72af5aa26d5c4e06d7df5d8a1c85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcc545cfe4d6e8e04c3698a149d4101a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;B. AMYLOLIQUEFACIENS SCGB1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A gut commensal bacterium with PS degradation activity, used for comparison with E. hormaechei LG3."&lt;SEP&gt;"B. amyloliquefaciens SCGB1 is another bacterial strain studied for its ability to degrade PS films."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-345c72af5aa26d5c4e06d7df5d8a1c85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcc545cfe4d6e8e04c3698a149d4101a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FIELD-EMISSION SCANNING ELECTRON MICROSCOPY (FE-SEM)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"FE-SEM is a high-resolution imaging technique used to observe the morphology of bacterial cells and PS films."&lt;SEP&gt;"FE-SEM is utilized for detailed visualization of bacterial morphology and surface interactions with PS films."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-345c72af5aa26d5c4e06d7df5d8a1c85</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CELL DENSITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cell density is a measure of the number of cells per unit volume, often determined by optical density at 600 nm (Abs600)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cell density refers to the number of cells per unit volume or area, used here to assess bacterial growth on PS films."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bfa1d3c9710e10c5eb533d8d791c93e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-345c72af5aa26d5c4e06d7df5d8a1c85</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;APPENDAGES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL FEATURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Appendages are structures such as pili or fimbriae that facilitate bacterial attachment to surfaces."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-345c72af5aa26d5c4e06d7df5d8a1c85</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CAVITIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL FEATURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cavities refer to depressions or voids formed on the PS film surface due to microbial degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-345c72af5aa26d5c4e06d7df5d8a1c85</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CELL ADHESION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL FUNCTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cell adhesion describes the ability of bacterial cells to attach to surfaces, such as PS films."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-345c72af5aa26d5c4e06d7df5d8a1c85</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FLUORESCENCE MICROSCOPIC IMAGES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fluorescence microscopy is employed to distinguish live (green) from dead (red) bacterial cells within biofilms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-345c72af5aa26d5c4e06d7df5d8a1c85</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GC ANALYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL REACTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gas chromatography (GC) analysis is used to quantify CO2 concentration as an indicator of PS film degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-345c72af5aa26d5c4e06d7df5d8a1c85</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SCGB1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"SCGB1 is a strain of B. amyloliquefaciens with reduced PS degradation activity under anaerobic conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"SCGB1 is a strain of Bacillus amyloliquefaciens used as a control in PS degradation experiments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f91980be083a0bf5b52d43a640e9d787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91523cdd8f510a966e9b301a0adb96b9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PEROXIDASE (EFEB)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Peroxidase (efeB) is an enzyme upregulated in LG3 when metabolizing Mi-PS, involved in aryl alcohol compound reactions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f91980be083a0bf5b52d43a640e9d787</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HYDROLASE (UBI GENES)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hydrolase (ubi genes) is an enzyme upregulated in LG3 when metabolizing Mi-PS, involved in aryl alcohol compound reactions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f91980be083a0bf5b52d43a640e9d787</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OXIDASE (YFIH)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Oxidase (yfiH) is an enzyme not upregulated in LG3 when metabolizing Mi-PS."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f91980be083a0bf5b52d43a640e9d787</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MONOXYGENASE (PAA GENES)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Monoxygenase (paa genes) is an enzyme not upregulated in LG3 when metabolizing Mi-PS."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f91980be083a0bf5b52d43a640e9d787</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THIOL PEROXIDASE (PXC)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Thiol peroxidase (pxc) is an enzyme in the peroxidase family whose expression increases after Mi-PS treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f91980be083a0bf5b52d43a640e9d787</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIPID A SYNTHESIS PATHWAY ENZYMES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Enzymes involved in lipid A synthesis pathway are upregulated in LG3 when metabolizing Mi-PS."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f91980be083a0bf5b52d43a640e9d787</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FLAGELLAR PROTEIN-CODING GENES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Flagellar protein-coding genes such as ycgR, flgH, and flp are downregulated in LG3 when using Mi-PS instead of maltose."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f91980be083a0bf5b52d43a640e9d787</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GLYCOLYTIC PATHWAY ENZYMES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Enzymes in the glycolytic pathway show downregulation in LG3 when using Mi-PS instead of maltose."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f91980be083a0bf5b52d43a640e9d787</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STERILE CONTROL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONTROL"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sterile control refers to experimental conditions without bacterial intervention, used as a baseline for comparison."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f91980be083a0bf5b52d43a640e9d787</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BUTYL RUBBER STOPPER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A butyl rubber stopper is used to seal the FMM medium containing Mi-PS for incubation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Butyl rubber stopper is used to seal the FMM medium bottles to maintain anaerobic conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f91980be083a0bf5b52d43a640e9d787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91523cdd8f510a966e9b301a0adb96b9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WCA VALUES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"WCA values (Water Contact Angle) are used to assess surface changes in PS films due to bacterial exposure."&lt;SEP&gt;"WCA values refer to water contact angle measurements reflecting changes in surface properties due to PS oxidation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f91980be083a0bf5b52d43a640e9d787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91523cdd8f510a966e9b301a0adb96b9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FLAGELLAR BRAKE PROTEIN (YCGR)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Flagellar brake protein (ycgR) is a gene downregulated in LG3 when using Mi-PS instead of maltose."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f91980be083a0bf5b52d43a640e9d787</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FLAGELLAR L-RING PROTEIN (FLGH)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Flagellar L-ring protein (flgH) is a gene downregulated in LG3 when using Mi-PS instead of maltose."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f91980be083a0bf5b52d43a640e9d787</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FLAGELLAR BIOSYNTHETIC PROTEIN (FLP)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Flagellar biosynthetic protein (flp) is a gene downregulated in LG3 when using Mi-PS instead of maltose."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f91980be083a0bf5b52d43a640e9d787</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HYDROXYL COMPOUNDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hydroxyl compounds are chemical entities identified via SPME/GC-MS analysis, indicating different degradation products."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-91523cdd8f510a966e9b301a0adb96b9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALIPHATIC AND AROMATIC ALCOHOLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Aliphatic and aromatic alcohols are degradation products observed in increased abundances during the PS biodegradation process."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-91523cdd8f510a966e9b301a0adb96b9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CO2 EMISSION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CO2 emission represents the release of carbon dioxide by bacterial strains during their metabolic processes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-91523cdd8f510a966e9b301a0adb96b9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FE-SEM IMAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"FE-SEM imaging involves using field-emission scanning electron microscopy to visualize structures like Mi-PS and bacterial cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-91523cdd8f510a966e9b301a0adb96b9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HYDROXYLASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hydroxylase is an enzyme upregulated during anaerobic PS biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-91523cdd8f510a966e9b301a0adb96b9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ISOBUTYRIC ACID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Isobutyric acid is a metabolite produced by SCGB1 under aerobic conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-91523cdd8f510a966e9b301a0adb96b9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ISOVALERIC ACID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Isovaleric acid is another metabolite produced by SCGB1 under aerobic conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-91523cdd8f510a966e9b301a0adb96b9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SULFATE (SO42-) &quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sulfate ions are utilized in anaerobic oxidation processes instead of oxygen."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-91523cdd8f510a966e9b301a0adb96b9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NITRATE (NO3-) &quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nitrate ions serve as electron acceptors in anaerobic respiration."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-91523cdd8f510a966e9b301a0adb96b9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NITRITE (NO2-) &quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nitrite ions also function as electron acceptors in anaerobic respiration."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-91523cdd8f510a966e9b301a0adb96b9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;METHYL 2-HYDROXYBENZOATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Methyl 2-Hydroxybenzoate is another intermediate in the anaerobic biodegradation pathway of styrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Methyl 2-hydroxybenzoate is another secondary product of PS degradation associated with LG3."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3a889b716cac361e6e04405777075076&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91523cdd8f510a966e9b301a0adb96b9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IPX, ABPC, BCP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"These genes encode peroxiredoxins and are substantially upregulated in LG3 after treatment with Mi-PS."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-91523cdd8f510a966e9b301a0adb96b9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPME/GC-MS ANALYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"SPME/GC-MS analysis is a method used to identify hydroxyl compounds from the degradation of Mi-PS."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-91523cdd8f510a966e9b301a0adb96b9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHROMATOGRAMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chromatograms are graphical representations of PS treated with strains, indicating different compounds."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-91523cdd8f510a966e9b301a0adb96b9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OXYGEN-LIMITED POSTERIOR GUT SECTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL FEATURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"This refers to the part of the mealworm gut where oxygen levels are low, favoring Enterobacter spp."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-91523cdd8f510a966e9b301a0adb96b9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;E. HORMAECHEI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"E. hormaechei is a species within the Enterobacter genus that can exist in various environments including insect and marine fish guts."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-91523cdd8f510a966e9b301a0adb96b9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;B. AMYLOLIQUEFACIENS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"B. amyloliquefaciens SCGB1 is a gut commensal bacterium with reduced PS degradation activity under anaerobic conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-91523cdd8f510a966e9b301a0adb96b9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DENITRIFICATION ENZYMES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Denitrification enzymes are involved in microbial nitrate reduction during anaerobic PS oxidation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-91523cdd8f510a966e9b301a0adb96b9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MI-PS DERIVATIVES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mi-PS derivatives are depolymerized products detected after anaerobic PS biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-91523cdd8f510a966e9b301a0adb96b9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANAEROBIC RESPIRATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Anaerobic respiration is a metabolic process occurring without oxygen, using alternative electron acceptors like nitrate or nitrite."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-91523cdd8f510a966e9b301a0adb96b9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICROBIAL NITRATE REDUCTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Microbial nitrate reduction is a process coupled with anaerobic PS oxidation, involving denitrification enzymes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-91523cdd8f510a966e9b301a0adb96b9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OXIDIZED LIPID MOLECULES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Oxidized Lipid Molecules are metabolites targeted by peroxiredoxins under anaerobic conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oxidized lipid molecules are substrates acted upon by peroxiredoxins like ipx, abpC, and bcp under anaerobic conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3a889b716cac361e6e04405777075076&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91523cdd8f510a966e9b301a0adb96b9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IPX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"ipx is a gene that encodes for peroxiredoxins, which have activity against oxidized lipid molecules under anaerobic conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3a889b716cac361e6e04405777075076</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ABPC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"abpC is a gene involved in the anaerobic biodegradation process of PS and its expression is upregulated upon treatment with Mi-PS."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3a889b716cac361e6e04405777075076</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BCP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"bcp is a gene encoding peroxiredoxins, showing increased expression after treatment with Mi-PS."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3a889b716cac361e6e04405777075076</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PEROXIREDOXINS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROTEIN"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Peroxiredoxins are proteins with enzymatic activity that help detoxify reactive oxygen species."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3a889b716cac361e6e04405777075076</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AROMATIC ALCOHOLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Aromatic Alcohols are metabolites produced during the anaerobic biodegradation of PS and styrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3a889b716cac361e6e04405777075076</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALIPHATIC ALCOHOLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Aliphatic Alcohols are metabolites significantly increased in strain LG3 under anaerobic conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3a889b716cac361e6e04405777075076</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;YCGR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"ycgR is a gene associated with cell motility whose expression is downregulated in LG3 treated with Mi-PS."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3a889b716cac361e6e04405777075076</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FLGH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"flgH is a gene related to flagellar assembly, showing reduced expression in LG3 upon Mi-PS treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3a889b716cac361e6e04405777075076</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FLHA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"FlhA is a gene involved in flagellar biosynthesis, with decreased expression in LG3 when exposed to Mi-PS."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3a889b716cac361e6e04405777075076</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIPXC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"lipxC is a gene involved in the biosynthesis pathway of Lipid A, upregulated in LG3 upon Mi-PS treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3a889b716cac361e6e04405777075076</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIPXD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"lipxD is another gene involved in the Lipid A biosynthesis pathway, showing increased expression in LG3."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3a889b716cac361e6e04405777075076</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENDOTOXIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TOXIN"</data>
