      <data key="d2">chunk-bfd05eac1abc28ac416e6a56ccd6a9d6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENTEROBACTER SOLI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Enterobacter soli is a bacterium isolated from mealworms' digestive tracts."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bfd05eac1abc28ac416e6a56ccd6a9d6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KLEBSIELLA GRIMMONTII&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Klebsiella grimmontii is a bacterium sensitive to salt, as indicated by its growth characteristics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bfd05eac1abc28ac416e6a56ccd6a9d6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLASTN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"BLASTN is a bioinformatics tool used for homology search of nucleotide sequences to identify bacterial strains."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bfd05eac1abc28ac416e6a56ccd6a9d6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEALWORM WEIGHT CHANGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"HEALTH MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mealworm Weight Change measures the reduction in weight of mealworms fed an EPS diet, indicating their ability to metabolize polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bfd05eac1abc28ac416e6a56ccd6a9d6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AUTOAGGREGATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A process observed in Acinetobacter strains, contributing to adhesion and degradation of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Autoaggregation is a mechanism by which certain bacterial strains attach to surfaces through self-aggregation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Autoaggregation is a process where bacteria clump together, affecting growth measurement as seen in Acinetobacter septicus."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c1bb645805a7158e2e18e95313565f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfd05eac1abc28ac416e6a56ccd6a9d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d4e1982efefa47339205e972562b51f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DOUBLING TIME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Doubling Time is a measure of bacterial growth rate, influenced by environmental factors like salt concentration."&lt;SEP&gt;"Doubling time is the time required for a bacterial population to double in size during exponential growth."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bfa1d3c9710e10c5eb533d8d791c93e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfd05eac1abc28ac416e6a56ccd6a9d6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;P. NITROREDUCENS MA77&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A bacterium whose growth is affected by salt concentration, isolated from the intestine of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"P. nitroreducens MA77 consistently exhibits polystyrene-degrading activity through cell adhesion, growth, and decomposition processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"P. nitroreducens MA77 demonstrates changes in polystyrene particles, suggesting effective degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"P. nitroreducens MA77 is a bacterial strain capable of adhering to polystyrene film."&lt;SEP&gt;"P. nitroreducens MA77 is a bacterial strain capable of degrading polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"P. nitroreducens MA77 is a bacterial strain that exhibits sensitivity to salt and has a doubling time of 113.4 minutes in LB medium during the exponential phase."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-07a91e5cf8b623163be09e14d1f4978e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfa1d3c9710e10c5eb533d8d791c93e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c1bb645805a7158e2e18e95313565f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-126ff1ea4b1c89f82a750386be59f926&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d4e1982efefa47339205e972562b51f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eadba0dcfe8eff9c8040ec5f17e1adb3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;A. TUMEFACIENS MA92&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A bacterium found in the digestive tract of mealworms with a polystyrene diet."&lt;SEP&gt;"A. tumefaciens MA92 exhibits high adhesion to polystyrene film but lacks clear evidence of degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"A. tumefaciens MA92 is a bacterial strain capable of adhering to polystyrene film."&lt;SEP&gt;"A. tumefaciens MA92 is a bacterial strain involved in the degradation of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"A. tumefaciens MA92 is a bacterial strain with a longer doubling time of 106.8 minutes in LB medium during the exponential phase."&lt;SEP&gt;"A. tumefaciens MA92 was isolated from insect intestines and considered capable of degrading polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-07a91e5cf8b623163be09e14d1f4978e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfa1d3c9710e10c5eb533d8d791c93e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c1bb645805a7158e2e18e95313565f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-126ff1ea4b1c89f82a750386be59f926&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d4e1982efefa47339205e972562b51f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eadba0dcfe8eff9c8040ec5f17e1adb3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;P. MULTIRESINIVORANS MA11&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A bacterium isolated from the intestine of mealworms, capable of degrading polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"P. multiresinivorans MA11 is a bacterial strain capable of degrading polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"P. multiresinivorans MA11 is a bacterial strain identified with high adhesion to polystyrene film and capable of producing micro-cracks on its surface."&lt;SEP&gt;"P. multiresinivorans MA11 is a bacterial strain that adheres well to polystyrene film."&lt;SEP&gt;"P. multiresinivorans MA11 is a bacterial strain with a doubling time of 113.4 minutes in LB medium during the exponential phase."&lt;SEP&gt;"P. multiresinivorans MA11 produces micro-cracks on the polystyrene film surface, indicating its degrading activity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-07a91e5cf8b623163be09e14d1f4978e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfa1d3c9710e10c5eb533d8d791c93e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c1bb645805a7158e2e18e95313565f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-126ff1ea4b1c89f82a750386be59f926&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d4e1982efefa47339205e972562b51f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eadba0dcfe8eff9c8040ec5f17e1adb3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;K. GRIMMONTII MA76&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"K. grimmontii MA76 is a bacterial strain with a doubling time of 113.4 minutes in LB medium during the exponential phase."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bfa1d3c9710e10c5eb533d8d791c93e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;P. PLECOGLOSSICIDA MA93&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A bacterium isolated from polyethylene plastic samples, capable of using paraffin as a carbon source."&lt;SEP&gt;"P. plecoglossicida MA93 is a bacterial strain capable of adhering to polystyrene film."&lt;SEP&gt;"P. plecoglossicida MA93 is a bacterial strain identified with high adhesion to polystyrene film."&lt;SEP&gt;"P. plecoglossicida MA93 is a bacterial strain with a doubling time of 106.8 minutes in LB medium during the exponential phase."&lt;SEP&gt;"P. plecoglossicida MA93 is a bacterial strain with the ability to break down polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"P. plecoglossicida MA93 was isolated from insect intestines and considered capable of degrading polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-07a91e5cf8b623163be09e14d1f4978e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfa1d3c9710e10c5eb533d8d791c93e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c1bb645805a7158e2e18e95313565f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-126ff1ea4b1c89f82a750386be59f926&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d4e1982efefa47339205e972562b51f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eadba0dcfe8eff9c8040ec5f17e1adb3</data>
    </node>
