    <node id="&quot;S. MARCESCENS MA42&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A bacterium identified as part of the intestinal microbiota of T. molitor that degrades polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"S. marcescens MA42 is a bacterial strain that adheres well to polystyrene film."&lt;SEP&gt;"S. marcescens MA42 is a bacterial strain with high adhesion to polystyrene film and produces micro-cracks on its surface."&lt;SEP&gt;"S. marcescens MA42 is a bacterial strain with the ability to degrade polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"S. marcescens MA42 produces micro-cracks on the polystyrene film surface and consistently exhibits polystyrene-degrading activity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-07a91e5cf8b623163be09e14d1f4978e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c1bb645805a7158e2e18e95313565f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-126ff1ea4b1c89f82a750386be59f926&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d4e1982efefa47339205e972562b51f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eadba0dcfe8eff9c8040ec5f17e1adb3</data>
