    <node id="&quot;A. SEPTICUS MA21&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A bacterium isolated from the intestine of mealworms, showing ability to degrade polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"A. septicus MA21 consistently exhibits polystyrene-degrading activity through cell adhesion, growth, and decomposition processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"A. septicus MA21 is a bacterial strain attached to the polystyrene film surface by autoaggregation."&lt;SEP&gt;"A. septicus MA21 is a bacterial strain that contributes to the breakdown of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"A. septicus MA21 is a bacterial strain that exhibits rapid polystyrene degradation, forming thick cell spots from the first day of culture."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-07a91e5cf8b623163be09e14d1f4978e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c1bb645805a7158e2e18e95313565f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-126ff1ea4b1c89f82a750386be59f926&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d4e1982efefa47339205e972562b51f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eadba0dcfe8eff9c8040ec5f17e1adb3</data>
    </node>
