    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIGESTIVE BIOFRAGMENTATION MODEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A model based on enzymatic surface degradation used to simulate the size-reduction process of plastic particles in the intestines of macroinvertebrates."&lt;SEP&gt;"A model developed to simulate the size reduction and distribution of plastics during digestion in organisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"A model simulating the size-reduction process of plastics during digestion by mealworms using parameters like biodegradation and grinding rates."&lt;SEP&gt;"A predictive model developed to simulate the size reduction and biodegradation of ingested plastics within mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Digestive Biofragmentation Model is a computational approach used to predict the time required for the removal of plastic particles by mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb1740bb657b0f90c48ee5e6d75945ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47e7fe379fcd6b17740bc4d953cd3b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84a8f1c256b1141b6bd2b404e817dfb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02e6f7bbb2c1ef92c57b423020b0cc5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0881f766e34a5d97ee711cd2edd793f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LASER LIGHT SCATTERING SIZER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A highly sensitive technology used to determine the size distribution of residual plastic particles after biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"A laser light scattering sizer is a tool used to measure particle sizes, with a detection limit of 10 nm in this study."&lt;SEP&gt;"The laser light scattering sizer is a highly sensitive analytical tool used to measure nanoparticle sizes in frass samples."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d0881f766e34a5d97ee711cd2edd793f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47e7fe379fcd6b17740bc4d953cd3b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84a8f1c256b1141b6bd2b404e817dfb7</data>
    </node>
