      <data key="d2">chunk-cb1740bb657b0f90c48ee5e6d75945ce</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CW VALUES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cw values represent the fraction of water-extracted organic components and salts in frass, indicating hydrophilic soluble substances."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-490fdb90ad8a65d35f3c2cd42a8c4c8e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CE VALUES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ce values indicate ethanol-extracted intermediates in frass, reflecting limited ethanol-soluble substances during plastic degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-490fdb90ad8a65d35f3c2cd42a8c4c8e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CO VALUES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Co values denote the content of residual PS or PE in frass, extracted using specific solvents like THF for PS and 1,2,4-TCB for PE."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-490fdb90ad8a65d35f3c2cd42a8c4c8e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MOLECULAR WEIGHTS (MW, MP, MS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Molecular weights are critical parameters used to assess the depolymerization of ingested plastics during biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-490fdb90ad8a65d35f3c2cd42a8c4c8e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1,2,4-TCB (1,2,4-TRICHLOROBENZENE)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"SOLVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"1,2,4-TCB is a solvent used to extract residual PE from frass samples for analysis."</data>
