      <data key="d1">"The extended simplified DEB model incorporates specific assumptions for holometabolous insects."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eee7e44e4c15567a057d7d295d240211</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENERGY CONDUCTANCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Energy conductance ($\nu$) quantifies the rate at which energy flows through an organism’s system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Energy conductance quantifies the rate at which energy is transferred through an organism."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eee7e44e4c15567a057d7d295d240211</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CRITICAL VALUE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Critical value is the threshold level of a metabolite that triggers developmental transitions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eee7e44e4c15567a057d7d295d240211</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KAPPA RULE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENETIC CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The kappa rule governs the mobilization flux of energy reserves within the DEB model framework."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eee7e44e4c15567a057d7d295d240211</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MORPHOLOGY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Morphology pertains to the structural features and form of an organism."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eee7e44e4c15567a057d7d295d240211</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SHAPE CHANGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Shape change refers to alterations in the physical structure of an organism during development."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eee7e44e4c15567a057d7d295d240211</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ISOMORPHISM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Isomorphism assumes no significant changes in shape during growth phases of an organism."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eee7e44e4c15567a057d7d295d240211</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DEB MODEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"DEB (Dynamic Energy Budget) Model is used to analyze the growth and energy allocation in T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"DEB Model is a process used to analyze changes in the development of T. molitor larvae based on reserve dynamics."&lt;SEP&gt;"DEB model (Dynamic Energy Budget) is a theoretical framework used to analyze the growth, reproduction, and energy allocation in organisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The DEB model is a dynamic energy budget model used to analyze energy flow and allocation in organisms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91831340731171413dc4c412a325e034&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a97d5b092508f2e837932274d6b3282</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RESERVES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Reserves refer to stored energy within the organism, utilized during periods of starvation when external food sources are insufficient."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reserves refer to the stored energy resources within the larvae that are utilized for growth and reproduction."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STRUCTURAL LENGTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Structural length describes the physical size of the larvae, which changes over time according to growth equations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VON BERTALANFFY GROWTH RATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Von Bertalanffy growth rate (\(\dot{r}_B\)) is a parameter describing the rate of growth in terms of structural length."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MAXIMUM BODY LENGTH (\(L_M\))&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL FEATURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Maximum body length is the largest attainable size of the larvae under given conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FEEDING CONDITIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DIET"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Feeding conditions refer to the different diets provided to the larvae groups, including oatmeal, PS (Styrofoam), and starvation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EGG PRODUCTION COST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The cost of making an egg is assumed constant in the DEB model, influencing reproduction dynamics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RESERVE DENSITY (\(E\))&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Reserve density represents the proportion of reserves in relation to total energy content."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SCALED RESERVE DENSITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Scaled reserve density is used as a parameter in equations describing structural length changes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STRUCTURAL LENGTH AT THE BEGINNING (\(L_0\))&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Initial structural length of larvae at the start of the experiment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MAXIMUM STRUCTURAL LENGTH ABOVE INITIAL (\(L_{M0}\))&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL FEATURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The additional maximum structural length beyond the initial length achieved during growth."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRIMARY DEB MODEL PARAMETERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENETIC CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Primary DEB model parameters include \([p_M]\), \([E_C]\), and \([E_m]\), which define key metabolic rates."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GROWTH RATE PARAMETER (\(\DOT{K}_M\))&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Growth rate parameter relates to the efficiency of converting assimilated energy into structural growth."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENERGY CONDUCTANCE (\(G\))&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL FUNCTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Energy conductance describes the organism's ability to allocate energy towards growth and reproduction."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FEEDING RATE (\(F\))&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DIET"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Feeding rate represents the intake of food resources, assumed constant for simplicity in the model."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ASSIMILATION EFFICIENCY (\(E\))&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Assimilation efficiency indicates how effectively consumed food is converted into reserves."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RESERVE ALLOCATION RATE (\(\DOT{R}\))&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Reserve allocation rate describes how reserves are distributed between growth and reproduction."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PS LARGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LIFE STAGE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Older and larger larvae compared to the PS group, with a mass range of 0.06–0.1 g each, fed with PS."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PS + OAT.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DIET"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Larvae fed with a combination of PS and crushed oatmeal, where oatmeal is provided every 10 days and removed after 24 hours."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PS + OAT. + VIT.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DIET"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Larvae fed with PS, vitamins, and minerals mixed with crushed oatmeal, provided every 10 days and removed after 24 hours."&lt;SEP&gt;"This dietary condition includes PS supplemented with oatmeal and vitamins, showing a similar survival rate to controls but limited pupation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a97d5b092508f2e837932274d6b3282</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VITAMINS AND MINERALS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Supplementary nutrients added to crushed oatmeal for larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\( L \)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Structural body length of the organism."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\( L_V \)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Volumetric body length of the organism."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\( L_W \)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL FEATURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Physical body length of the organism."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\( L_E \)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL FEATURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Volumetric length of the reserve in the organism."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\( R \), \( R_S \)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"REPRODUCTION RATE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Reproduction rate or scaled reproduction rate of the organism."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\( E \)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"SCALED RESERVE DENSITY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Amount of energy stored in the reserve."&lt;SEP&gt;"Scaled reserve density in the organism."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\( [E] \)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Reserve density in the organism."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\( E_R \)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENERGY MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Amount of energy in the reproduction buffer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\( [E_R] \)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Density of energy in the reproduction buffer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Energy density threshold required for pupation, measured as \( e^{-3} \)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\( F \)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"SCALED FUNCTIONAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A parameter representing the scaled functional response of the organism."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\( \DOT{V} \)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENERGY CONDUCTANCE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Energy conductance in the organism, measured as \( l^{-1} \)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\( K_M \)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"SOMATIC MAINTENANCE RATE COEFFICIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Somatic maintenance rate coefficient, with a control value \( k_{m0} \), measured as \( t^{-1} \)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\( G \)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENERGY INVESTMENT RATIO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Energy investment ratio, with a control value \( g_0 \)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\( \DOT{R}_M \), \( \DOT{R}_{SM} \)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MAXIMUM REPRODUCTION RATE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Maximum reproduction rate (at \( f = 1 \), \( L = L_m \)), with control values \( \dot{R}_{m0} \) and \( \dot{R}_{Sm0} \), measured as \( t^{-1} \)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\( L_M(E), L_{V0}(E) \)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BODY LENGTH PARAMETERS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Maximum structural/volumetric body lengths for given constant \( e \), used as parameters."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\( L_0, L_{V0} \)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"INITIAL BODY LENGTHS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Structural/volumetric lengths at the beginning of the experiment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\( L_{M0}, L_{VM0} \)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MAXIMUM BODY LENGTHS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Maximum structural/volumetric lengths above initial values."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\( L_P, L_{VP} \)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PUBERTY BODY LENGTHS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Structural/volumetric body lengths at puberty."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\( L_{EM} \)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MAXIMUM RESERVE LENGTH"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Maximum volumetric length of reserve for given \( L \) and \( e \)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\( L_{S0} \)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"STARVATION START LENGTH"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Structural body length at the beginning of starvation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\( L_{SURVIVE} \)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CRITICAL SURVIVAL LENGTH"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Critical structural length necessary for survival."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\( [P_M] \)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"VOLUME-SPECIFIC SOMATIC MAINTENANCE POWER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Volume-specific somatic maintenance power, measured as \( e^{-1} l^{-3} \)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\( [E_C] \)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"VOLUME-SPECIFIC COSTS FOR STRUCTURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Volume-specific costs for structure, measured as \( e^{-3} \)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\( [E_M] \)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MAXIMUM RESERVE DENSITY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Maximum reserve density, measured as \( e^{-3} \)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\( E_0, E_T \)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENERGY CONTENT MEASURES"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Energy content of a single egg and total number of eggs, measured as \( e \)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\( [E_0], [E_T] \)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENERGY DENSITY THRESHOLDS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Energy density thresholds for a single egg and total number of eggs, measured as \( e^{-3} \)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\( \KAPPA \)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FRACTION OF MOBILIZED RESERVES"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fraction of mobilized reserves allocated to the soma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\( \KAPPA_R \)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FRACTION OF ALLOCATED RESERVES"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fraction of allocated reserves fixed in eggs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\( R_B \)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"VON BERTALANFFY GROWTH RATE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Von Bertalanffy growth rate for given constant \( e \), used as a parameter, measured as \( t^{-1} \)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\( U_V \)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROPORTIONALITY COEFFICIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Proportionality coefficient equal to the constant ratio \( \frac{L_V}{L} \)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\( U_R \)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROPORTIONALITY COEFFICIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Proportionality coefficient equal to the constant ratio \( \frac{L_E}{L} \)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;L_V&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"L_V represents volumetric length, which is affected by changes in reserve density during starvation and is derived using equations related to reserves dynamics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-998b63e5349034d477c2087c139669ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;L^3_{EM}&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"L^3_{Em} denotes the maximum volume of reserves for specific conditions and depends on structural length L."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-998b63e5349034d477c2087c139669ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;E(T)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MARKER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"e(t) represents scaled reserve density, which is a function of time and indicates the proportion of reserve volume relative to its maximum value."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-998b63e5349034d477c2087c139669ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;F&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"f is a parameter representing the fraction of energy allocated towards reserves within the organism."&lt;SEP&gt;"f represents the food availability in the environment, which can decrease due to dietary changes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-998b63e5349034d477c2087c139669ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\DOT{V}&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"\dot{v} signifies the rate of energy assimilation or consumption by the organism."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-998b63e5349034d477c2087c139669ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;L_{S0}&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"L_{S0} refers to initial structural volume parameters used in the equation describing volumetric length change."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-998b63e5349034d477c2087c139669ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PS MASS LOSS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PS mass loss refers to the degradation of polystyrene by organisms over time, indicating their ability to metabolize plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-998b63e5349034d477c2087c139669ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;L^3&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"L^3 represents the structural volume of the organism, which plays a critical role in growth and energy allocation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-998b63e5349034d477c2087c139669ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;K_M&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"k_M is a parameter representing maintenance costs required for sustaining the organism's structure."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-998b63e5349034d477c2087c139669ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;G&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"g refers to the fraction of energy allocated towards somatic growth within the organism."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-998b63e5349034d477c2087c139669ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;E_R&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"E_R denotes the energy content of the reproduction buffer, which accumulates energy for future reproductive events."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-998b63e5349034d477c2087c139669ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;E_0&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"E_0 is a constant used to calculate the number of eggs, but it does not influence the amount of energy stored in the reproduction buffer."&lt;SEP&gt;"E_0 represents the energy content of a single egg, used as a reference for calculating reproductive investment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-998b63e5349034d477c2087c139669ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\KAPPA_R&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"\kappa_R signifies the proportion of energy from the reproduction buffer that is directly allocated to egg production."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-998b63e5349034d477c2087c139669ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;R_S&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MARKER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"R_S is the integrated scaled reproduction, representing the ratio of current reproduction buffer to the total possible energy for reproduction during the imago stage."&lt;SEP&gt;"R_S is the normalized density of the reproduction buffer, indicating its relative energy content compared to total reproductive potential."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-998b63e5349034d477c2087c139669ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;[E_T]&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"[E_T] represents the energy density of the total reproductive buffer available for future reproduction."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-998b63e5349034d477c2087c139669ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;[E_R]&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"[E_R] indicates the energy density of the reproduction buffer at any given time during development."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-998b63e5349034d477c2087c139669ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;E_R(T)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"E_R(t) represents the reproduction buffer (energy) density at time t, which is a measure of the energy available for reproduction in an organism."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;E_T&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"E_T is the reproduction buffer (energy) density threshold required for pupation, marking the critical energy level necessary for this biological transition."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;E_I&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"E_I is the total energy content of all eggs that can be produced during the imago stage, indicating reproductive potential."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;P(T)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROBABILITY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"P(t) is the probability of achieving the reproduction buffer density threshold after a given time t, described by a sigmoidal distribution curve."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;Τ&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TIME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"τ is the inflection point of the distribution curve, indicating the most likely time when pupation occurs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;P_M&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MAINTENANCE COST"</data>
      <data key="d1">"p_M is the somatic and maturity maintenance cost, which can increase due to toxicity or starvation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;E_C&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"COST"</data>
      <data key="d1">"E_C denotes the composition of structures and reserves within the organism, particularly in the context of dietary components."&lt;SEP&gt;"E_C represents the costs for structure and maintenance, which can increase due to toxic effects of the PS diet."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f71fddc259d51158d5c79f38bf41523f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;Κ&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ALLOCATION PARAMETER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"κ is the allocation parameter determining how energy is distributed between somatic growth and reproduction, which can change under starvation conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JAGER AND ZIMMER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"RESEARCHER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Jager and Zimmer are researchers who derived equation (19) related to reproduction buffer density thresholds."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LLANDRES ET AL.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"RESEARCHER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Llandres et al. described the reproduction buffer (energy) density threshold for pupation in their research."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RITZ&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"RESEARCHER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ritz proposed the log-logistic model used to describe the accumulated number of pupae as a sigmoidal distribution curve."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KOOIJMAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"RESEARCHER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Kooijman provided insights into the reaction of larvae to starvation, focusing on energy allocation and maintenance costs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOMATIC MAINTENANCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL FUNCTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Somatic maintenance involves the energy costs required for basic physiological functions in organisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Somatic maintenance refers to the energy required to maintain the body structures and functions of an organism."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5740f0973ff804cae61f6fc12f3e3753&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OOGENESIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Oogenesis is the process of egg formation, which was not directly observed in this study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TOXICITY OF PS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TOXIN"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The toxicity of polystyrene includes the harmful effects of its metabolites and impurities on organisms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INFLECTION POINT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The inflection point of a curve indicates where the curvature changes direction, used here to identify the most likely time of pupation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SIGMOIDAL DISTRIBUTION CURVE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICAL MODEL"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A sigmoidal distribution curve describes processes that start slowly, increase rapidly, and then level off, such as the accumulation of pupae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOG-LOGISTIC MODEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"STATISTICAL MODEL"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The log-logistic model is a type of sigmoid function used to model probabilities or proportions over time."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STARVATION RESPONSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Starvation response refers to the physiological and behavioral changes in organisms when exposed to insufficient food."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STRUCTURAL RESERVES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC COMPONENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Structural reserves are components of an organism's body that can be utilized as energy sources during starvation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KAPPA PARAMETER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PARAMETER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The kappa parameter determines how energy is allocated between somatic growth and reproduction in the DEB model."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ISOMORPHIC GROWTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Isomorphic growth describes consistent growth patterns without significant changes in shape or density."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5740f0973ff804cae61f6fc12f3e3753</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RESERVE DENSITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Reserve density ($e$) measures the energy reserves within the organism, which decrease during starvation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reserve density quantifies the energy reserves available in larvae for survival and growth."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5740f0973ff804cae61f6fc12f3e3753&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INEQUALITY (18)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Inequality (18) is a criterion used to assess whether larval energy reserves meet survival requirements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Inequality (18) is a criterion used to determine if reserves are sufficient for somatic maintenance in T. molitor larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5740f0973ff804cae61f6fc12f3e3753&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a97d5b092508f2e837932274d6b3282</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SHAPE COEFFICIENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Shape coefficient measures the geometric properties of mealworms during growth."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5740f0973ff804cae61f6fc12f3e3753</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SCALED RESERVE DENSITY E(T)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Scaled Reserve Density e(t) measures the energy reserves available for somatic maintenance and reproduction; insufficient levels hinder development."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9a97d5b092508f2e837932274d6b3282</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REPRODUCTION RATE R&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Reproduction Rate R indicates the reproductive capacity of T. molitor, influenced by scaled reserve density and feeding conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9a97d5b092508f2e837932274d6b3282</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MORALES-RAMOS ET AL.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"RESEARCH STUDY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Morales-Ramos et al. studied the effects of diet supplements on the development time and number of instars in T. molitor larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9a97d5b092508f2e837932274d6b3282</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONNAT ET AL.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"RESEARCH STUDY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Connat et al. observed that large larvae of T. molitor could complete larval development and moult to pupae during starvation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9a97d5b092508f2e837932274d6b3282</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REPRODUCTION BUFFER THRESHOLD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Reproduction Buffer Threshold is a measure indicating the energy reserves needed for reproduction and pupation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9a97d5b092508f2e837932274d6b3282</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VOLUMETRIC LENGTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Volumetric Length refers to the physical size increase in T. molitor larvae, used as a growth indicator."&lt;SEP&gt;"Volumetric length represents a measure of structural growth or reduction in the organism, affected by starvation and diet quality."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a97d5b092508f2e837932274d6b3282</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUM OF SQUARED ERRORS (SSE)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"SSE is a statistical measure used to evaluate the goodness of fit in the DEB model."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9a97d5b092508f2e837932274d6b3282</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ROOT MEAN SQUARE ERROR (RMSE)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"RMSE is another statistical measure used to assess the accuracy of the DEB model fitting."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9a97d5b092508f2e837932274d6b3282</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOOD AVAILABILITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DIET"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Food availability ($f$) represents the accessibility of nutrients to the organism, assumed to be zero during starvation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DEB MODEL PARAMETERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"DEB model parameters ($k_M$, $g$, $\hat{r}_B$, $L_{\text{Im}}$, etc.) are used to quantify physiological processes and responses in organisms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MOULT RESIDUES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRITIONAL COMPONENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Moult residues are discarded exoskeletal materials that may serve as a minor nutritional source for larvae under starvation conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DROPPINGS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"WASTE PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Droppings are fecal matter produced by organisms, providing minimal nutrition under starvation conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MACRO- AND MICROELEMENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Macro- and microelements are essential nutrients required for maintaining life, lacking in PS and contributing to larval starvation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PS + OAT. GROUP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EXPERIMENTAL GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The PS + oat group involves larvae fed with polyethylene supplemented with oats, showing partial inhibition of growth and reproduction."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PS + OAT. + VIT. GROUP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EXPERIMENTAL GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The PS + oat. + vit. group includes larvae fed with polyethylene, oats, and vitamins, exhibiting similar outcomes to the PS + oat group."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;L_IM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"L_Im represents a metabolic parameter related to larval growth or development, specifically the volumetric length in the context of T. molitor larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f71fddc259d51158d5c79f38bf41523f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;R̂&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"R̂ is a biological response parameter indicating changes in the reproduction buffer, reflecting reproductive potential."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f71fddc259d51158d5c79f38bf41523f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;R_B̂&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"r_B̂ represents a parameter associated with the rate of resource allocation towards reproduction."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f71fddc259d51158d5c79f38bf41523f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;P_M̂&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"p_M̂ refers to somatic maintenance, representing energy expenditure on maintaining body functions rather than growth or reproduction."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f71fddc259d51158d5c79f38bf41523f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MECHANISTIC MODEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mechanistic model is a method used to analyze and predict changes in larval growth and development under different feeding conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f71fddc259d51158d5c79f38bf41523f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALPHITOBIUS DIAPERINUS PANZER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"SPECIES"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Alphitobius diaperinus Panzer is a species belonging to the same family as T. molitor, studied for its metabolic response to starvation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f71fddc259d51158d5c79f38bf41523f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HAEMOLYMPH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL FEATURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Haemolymph is a fluid in insects analogous to blood, containing carbohydrates that sustain organs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Haemolymph is the circulatory fluid in insects, analogous to blood, containing nutrients and supporting the nervous system."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-91831340731171413dc4c412a325e034&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f71fddc259d51158d5c79f38bf41523f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NERVOUS SYSTEM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL SYSTEM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The nervous system in insects is sustained by carbohydrates present in the haemolymph."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-91831340731171413dc4c412a325e034</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEALWORM GUTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mealworm guts refer to the digestive system of mealworms, potentially involved in PS degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-91831340731171413dc4c412a325e034</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RESERVE DYNAMICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Reserve dynamics describe the changes in energy reserves like lipids and proteins in T. molitor larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-91831340731171413dc4c412a325e034</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STYRENE ANALOGUES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Styrene analogues are degradation products derived from polystyrene breakdown."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-33f35f87c2ff7792eb41bdd8debdb5f0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DYNAMIC ENERGY BUDGET&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dynamic energy budget models describe how organisms allocate energy for growth, reproduction, and maintenance throughout their life cycle."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-33f35f87c2ff7792eb41bdd8debdb5f0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COASTLINES OF THE NORTH-EAST PACIFIC OCEAN AND HAWAII&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The coastlines of the North-East Pacific Ocean and Hawaii are regions where styrene analogues from polystyrene degradation have been studied."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-33f35f87c2ff7792eb41bdd8debdb5f0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RECYCLING OF POLYSTYRENE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Recycling of polystyrene refers to methods used to convert waste polystyrene into reusable materials."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-33f35f87c2ff7792eb41bdd8debdb5f0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DYNAMIC ENERGY BUDGET FOR HOLOMETABOLOUS INSECTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"This concept models energy allocation in holometabolous insects like mealworms during their life cycle."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-33f35f87c2ff7792eb41bdd8debdb5f0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENTOMOLOGY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FIELD OF STUDY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Entomology is the scientific study of insects, including species like Tenebrio molitor."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-33f35f87c2ff7792eb41bdd8debdb5f0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CAMBRIDGE UNIVERSITY PRESS&quot;">
