      <data key="d3">136.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Biodegradation involves breaking down Polystyrene into simpler compounds, often facilitated by organisms such as mealworm larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodegradation involves the breakdown of polystyrene by microorganisms, making it an important ecological process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodegradation processes break down polystyrene into simpler compounds using enzymes and microbial activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodegradation processes involve the breakdown of polystyrene by microorganisms present in the gut of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene undergoes biodegradation, highlighting its potential for environmental decomposition."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene is subjected to biodegradation processes to evaluate its suitability for degradation by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene undergoes biodegradation processes, although it typically requires specialized conditions or microorganisms to break down effectively."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene undergoes biodegradation, demonstrating its susceptibility to microbial action."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodegradation is the process by which polystyrene is broken down into simpler compounds by bacteria present in the mealworms' guts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodegradation processes involve the breakdown of polystyrene by living organisms such as Tenebrio molitor Linnaeus larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodegradation is the biological process through which polystyrene is broken down into simpler compounds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodegradation is the process by which polystyrene is broken down by yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodegradation is the process through which polystyrene is broken down into simpler substances by bacterial strains like Klebsiella sp. WJ2020 and Cellulosimicrobium sp. WJ2025."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene undergoes biodegradation processes mediated by various microorganisms, highlighting its potential for environmental remediation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The process of biodegradation involves breaking down polystyrene into simpler substances by microorganisms, highlighting an environmentally friendly solution."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene undergoes biodegradation through the action of microorganisms like Tenebrio molitor larvae, breaking it down into simpler compounds."</data>
