    <edge source="&quot;GUT MICROBIOME&quot;" target="&quot;MEALWORMS&quot;">
      <data key="d3">137.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Changes in the gut microbiome diversity of mealworms depend on the type of provided PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms harbor a gut microbiome that actively participates in plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The gut microbiome of mealworms facilitates the biodegradation of plastics, indicating a symbiotic relationship between the two."&lt;SEP&gt;"The gut microbiome of mealworms plays a crucial role in facilitating the biodegradation of plastics like polyethylene and polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"The gut microbiome of mealworms is essential for the biodegradation of polystyrene, as evidenced by the effect of antibiotics on this process."&lt;SEP&gt;"The gut microbiome of mealworms contributes to their ability to biodegrade plastics like polyethylene and polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms harbor the gut microbiome, which plays a critical role in PS degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms harbor a gut microbiome that facilitates the breakdown of plastics, enhancing their ability to degrade them."&lt;SEP&gt;"The gut microbiome of mealworms plays a crucial role in their ability to degrade plastics like PE and PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms display distinct gut microbial profiles depending on their diet, with plastic-fed groups showing higher microbial diversity compared to bran-fed ones."&lt;SEP&gt;"The gut microbiome of mealworms plays a crucial role in the digestion and metabolism of consumed plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms rely on their gut microbiome to aid in the digestion and biodegradation of plastics like polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Gut Microbiome of mealworms plays a crucial role in the depolymerization and biodegradation of ingested plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"The gut microbiome of mealworms is altered by interactions with microplastics and nanoplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"The gut microbiome of mealworms plays a crucial role in the degradation of polystyrene microplastics, contributing to the observed molecular weight changes."</data>
