      <data key="d4">"Gut microbiota in Tenebrio molitor aids in digesting cell walls and detoxifying glucosides, contributing to the biodegradation of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor larvae utilize their gut microbiota to aid in the breakdown of recalcitrant plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"The gut microbiota of Tenebrio molitor plays a crucial role in its ability to digest and process various substrates, including polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"The gut microbiota of Tenebrio molitor plays a critical role in the biodegradation of polystyrene, enabling the insect to digest plastic materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"The gut microbiota of Tenebrio molitor plays a crucial role in the biodepolymerization of plastics and polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"The gut microbiota of Tenebrio molitor is studied for its response to environmental changes, indicating a relationship between the beetle's internal microbial community and external environmental factors."&lt;SEP&gt;"The gut microbiota of Tenebrio molitor plays a significant role in the insect's ability to degrade plastics, establishing a relationship between the host and its microbiota."&lt;SEP&gt;"The gut microbiota of Tenebrio molitor plays a critical role in digesting cellulose and detoxifying glucosides."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor harbors gut microbiota that play essential roles in digestion and detoxification processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Studies have investigated the gut microbiota of Tenebrio molitor larvae, indicating a relationship between the insect and its associated microorganisms."</data>
