    <edge source="&quot;TENEBRIO MOLITOR&quot;" target="&quot;POLYVINYL CHLORIDE (PVC)&quot;">
      <data key="d3">119.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"PVC biodegradation occurs in Tenebrio molitor larvae, demonstrating their ability to break down diverse plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"PVC is biodegraded by Tenebrio molitor larvae, demonstrating their capacity to process various plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor larvae degrade PVC, showcasing their versatility in plastic biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor larvae have been shown to biodegrade PVC, highlighting their potential in plastic waste management."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor contributes to the biodegradation of PVC, demonstrating its capability to handle various types of plastic waste."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyvinyl chloride (PVC) can be biodegraded by Tenebrio molitor larvae, showcasing their versatility in plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor has the potential to degrade polyvinyl chloride, contributing to its biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Studies have shown that Tenebrio molitor larvae can biodegrade PVC, indicating their potential role in managing this type of plastic waste."&lt;SEP&gt;"Yellow mealworms show the lowest conversion efficiency for PVC, preferring wheat bran instead due to its poor texture and limited digestibility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor larvae exhibit limited but notable abilities to degrade polyvinyl chloride through biodegradation processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor larvae demonstrate potential for PVC degradation through their metabolic pathways."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor larvae have demonstrated the ability to degrade PVC, indicating their potential role in plastic waste management."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor larvae have shown potential in biodegrading PVC, contributing to plastic waste management."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor larvae are capable of biodegrading PVC, demonstrating their potential in plastic waste management."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor larvae are capable of degrading polyvinyl chloride, showcasing their potential in addressing PVC waste."&lt;SEP&gt;"The larvae of Tenebrio mo