      <data key="d3">52.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Tenebrio molitor larvae are capable of consuming and depolymerizing LDPE, suggesting enzymatic or physical mechanisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor mealworms were placed in contact with LDPE substrates to evaluate their effectiveness in degrading the material."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor larvae can rapidly biodegrade LDPE, indicating a specialized enzymatic or microbial capability."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor larvae significantly degrade LDPE, reducing its molecular weight and altering its physical properties."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor larvae can degrade LDPE, expanding their role in breaking down various forms of PE."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor larvae fragment and biodegrade LDPE, with residual polymers excreted in frass."</data>
