    <edge source="&quot;T. MOLITOR&quot;" target="&quot;PS&quot;">
      <data key="d3">89.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"PS biodegradation by T. molitor larvae has been studied previously, providing insights into their survival and consumption patterns."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS undergoes depolymerization when ingested by T. molitor larvae, as indicated by changes in Mn and Mw."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. molitor consumes PS, leading to a statistically significant reduction in its mass over time."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. molitor exhibited increased Proteobacteria abundance when fed PS, consistent with findings in other studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Yellow mealworms (T. molitor) also contribute to the degradation of PS, showing similar efficiency as Z. atratus in this regard."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. molitor mealworms have been shown to efficiently utilize PS, with utilization rates varying based on geographical origin and dietary supplements."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. molitor larvae consume PS, leading to its depolymerization and biodegradation through gut microbiome activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. molitor's ability to oxidize PS was studied previously, providing context for its current role in PE biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. molitor larvae also consume PS but at a lower rate compared to T. obscurus, suggesting less efficient PS digestion."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. molitor larvae consumed PS, showing their capability to digest polystyrene as part of the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS consumption by T. molitor larvae leads to insufficient growth due to limited nutrient conversion into biomass."</data>
      <data key="d5">"biodegradation capability, comparative analysis"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation studies"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, feeding behavior"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, species-specific activity"&lt;SEP&gt;"consumption, biodegradation"&lt;SEP&gt;"depolymerization, ingestion"&lt;SEP&gt;"efficiency, consumption"&lt;SEP&gt;"microbial adaptation, dietary association"&lt;SEP&gt;"nutrient limitation"&lt;SEP&gt;"plastic degradation, biological activity"&lt;SEP&gt;"utilization efficiency, dietary influence"</data>
