    <edge source="&quot;PVC&quot;" target="&quot;MEALWORMS&quot;">
      <data key="d3">49.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Mealworms can also degrade PVC, highlighting their versatility in processing various types of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms consume PVC, further showcasing their capacity to degrade diverse plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms from Tai'an and Shenzhen alter the crystalline structure of PVC, while those from Guangzhou do not cause significant changes."&lt;SEP&gt;"PVC caused mealworms to lose mass due to the release of organic compounds like carboxylic acids and insufficient nutritional content."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms ingest PVC microplastics, resulting in PVC's biodegradation and molecular weight changes."&lt;SEP&gt;"PVC had a more significant negative impact on mealworm survival compared to PE and PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"PVC's smooth surface makes it difficult for mealworms to chew, leading to minimal mass loss despite being consumed slightly."</data>
      <data key="d5">"biodegradation, molecular alteration"&lt;SEP&gt;"digestibility, food availability"&lt;SEP&gt;"metabolism, structural change"&lt;SEP&gt;"nutrient exhaustion, survival"&lt;SEP&gt;"plastic degradation, adaptability"&lt;SEP&gt;"toxicity, nutrition"&lt;SEP&gt;"versatility, chemical resistance"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-9a27dff473ed210517e6461ad3e5d783&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe381daaa91bbff20758798e5baf82b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f267b48449a40d614a2f325799752dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff201df58dec460c49cd31920c29f11a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b0b175969d87b3be377f65b988d0a52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0491f3e96c1d355b8431b9d74868f63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ed721221326657b60aadb09faeeac92</data>
    </edge>
