    <edge source="&quot;BRAN&quot;" target="&quot;MEALWORMS&quot;">
      <data key="d3">129.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Bran cofeeding influences the biomass gain and plastic degradation efficiency of mealworms compared to those fed plastics alone."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bran is fed to mealworms in control experiments, contrasting with Styrofoam diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bran served as a food source for mealworms in control experiments, allowing comparison of survival rates and mass changes with those exposed to LDPE."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bran serves as a nutrient-rich diet for mealworms, promoting their growth compared to microplastic diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bran supplements the diet of mealworms, enhancing their growth and survival compared to a plastic-only diet."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms fed bran exhibit similar survival rates to those fed polyether-PU foam, suggesting bran serves as an effective control diet."&lt;SEP&gt;"The addition of bran improves the survival rate and PS consumption rate of mealworms, addressing the nutrient deficiency in PS alone."&lt;SEP&gt;"The diet of bran influences the gut microbial communities of mealworms, which in turn affects PS degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms were initially stabilized with bran feeding before being divided into bran-fed and EPS-fed groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms fed with bran experience significant weight gain, highlighting the importance of nutrients for growth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms fed on bran show better growth compared to those consuming PU Foam, indicating bran's higher nutritional value."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bran supplementation shifts the gut microbiome of mealworms, affecting bacterial populations and potentially enhancing biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bran provides better nutrition compared to plastics, enhancing mealworm viability and contrasting with the negative effects of plastic-only diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bran serves as a nutritional supplement supporting the growth and survival of mealworms while they consume polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms fed bran along with PS show improved survival rates compared to those fed PS alone."&lt;SEP&gt;"Supplementing mealworms with bran enhances their PS degradation rates, indicating the importance of added nutrition for biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms were also fed bran as a control group to compare with PS-fed groups."</data>
      <data key="d5">"comparison, dietary control"&lt;SEP&gt;"control diet, stabilization"&lt;SEP&gt;"control, comparison"&lt;SEP&gt;"diet comparison, nutritional adequacy"&lt;SEP&gt;"dietary effect, nutrient impact"&lt;SEP&gt;"dietary influence, microbial composition"&lt;SEP&gt;"dietary influence, microbial population"&lt;SEP&gt;"dietary relationship"&lt;SEP&gt;"nutrient source, control experiment"&lt;SEP&gt;"nutrient source, growth"&lt;SEP&gt;"nutrition, growth"&lt;SEP&gt;"nutrition, survival"&lt;SEP&gt;"nutrition, sustenance"&lt;SEP&gt;"nutritional enhancement, enzymatic activity"&lt;SEP&gt;"nutritional enhancement, growth improvement"&lt;SEP&gt;"nutritional supplementation, survival enhancement"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-2a214d2b1c90aeb78e6e8562679d4963&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e45f9527e7b07e945435dae572dc387&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-630e33352368a0c7f34d56ad45a38e56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0638e0fe93dc27e678672a164e6088c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e05bc34fccfca5e177064daf8346866&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04683827a8d88bc2fa28ae73ccc0714f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81552b76a273b31cc2bd9ed21ed7a919&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b0b175969d87b3be377f65b988d0a52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53dd546535ef4247004faab1fa475889&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2338bb97657d74ab5d8a444849037692&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9af0d95fd5f52d02b9cb33387951963&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1769c4becf46c99994cb7ced2bffda1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c818a01113d8c07554629cc5edfd28f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b387da8298c55673284dca93ea82fc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7a14229bceb339a4ca1baf0772b47ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05b7bf66b11c66f02e73a07fb823b8fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae42540a18795e5e2ad9054b7a0edfc3</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BRAN&quot;" target="&quot;MEALWORM LARVAE&quot;">
      <data key="d3">57.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Bran is used as a food source for mealworm larvae in combination with PE microplastics to support their growth and survival."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bran supplementation enhances the digestibility and physiological health of mealworm larvae when combined with PE microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bran supplementation improves the health of mealworm larvae by enhancing biomass and survival but reduces PE removal efficiency."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bran supplementation mitigates negative impacts caused by PE ingestion, improving survival and growth in mealworm larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Supplementing bran enhances the biomass levels and survival of mealworm larvae, indirectly affecting PE removal efficiency."&lt;SEP&gt;"The addition of bran to the diet enhanced the PE consumption rate and overall performance of mealworm larvae in plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworm larvae fed on bran showed steady weight increase followed by a decline, serving as a control for comparing plastic-fed groups."</data>
      <data key="d5">"control group, nutritional impact"&lt;SEP&gt;"dietary enhancement, health improvement"&lt;SEP&gt;"dietary enhancement, improved digestion"&lt;SEP&gt;"dietary supplementation, mitigation"&lt;SEP&gt;"nutrition, sustenance"&lt;SEP&gt;"nutritional enhancement"&lt;SEP&gt;"nutritional support, biodegradation impact"</data>
