    <edge source="&quot;MEALWORMS&quot;" target="&quot;EPS&quot;">
      <data key="d3">61.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"EPS is another plastic material evaluated for its suitability for mealworm consumption, with significant mass loss observed during experiments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms consumed EPS to study its degradation mechanisms and effects on larval development."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms degrade EPS, leading to changes in molecular weight and chemical properties."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms were fed EPS, which significantly altered their intestinal microbial flora compared to those fed bran."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms were used to digest EPS, demonstrating their ability to break down plastics under controlled lab conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms consumed EPS material, showing high PS consumption rates due to its lower density compared to other PS products."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms were fed exclusively with EPS after an initial period, highlighting the role of EPS as their sole energy source."</data>
