    <edge source="&quot;POLYSTYRENE&quot;" target="&quot;TENEBRIO OBSCURUS&quot;">
      <data key="d3">105.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Similar to Tenebrio molitor, Tenebrio obscurus larvae exhibit the ability to degrade polystyrene, highlighting the importance of these insects in plastic waste management."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio obscurus degrades polystyrene, highlighting its potential in plastic waste management."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio obscurus larvae, like Tenebrio molitor, have demonstrated the ability to biodegrade polystyrene, contributing to plastic waste management."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio obscurus larvae contribute to the biodegradation of polystyrene, highlighting their role in plastic breakdown."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio obscurus larvae contribute to the biodegradation of polystyrene plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio obscurus larvae are capable of degrading polystyrene, contributing to the biodegradation process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio obscurus has been shown to degrade polystyrene, indicating a biological relationship between the two."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio obscurus larvae contribute to the biodegradation of polystyrene, working synergistically with Tenebrio molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio obscurus has been shown to contribute to the biodegradation of polystyrene, demonstrating its role in breaking down this plastic substrate."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio obscurus larvae ingest polystyrene and contribute to its degradation through gut microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio obscurus participates in the biodegradation of polystyrene, offering insights into alternative methods for managing plastic waste."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio obscurus larvae (dark mealworms) have the ability to biodegrade polystyrene, similar to yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio obscurus larvae contribute to the biodegradation of polystyrene, expanding the range of plastic-degrading organisms."</data>
