      <data key="d3">138.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Galleria Mellonella bio-degrades polyethylene, showcasing its enzymatic capabilities to metabolize plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Galleria mellonella larvae possess the capability to bio-degrade polyethylene, contributing to plastic waste reduction."&lt;SEP&gt;"Greater wax moth larvae (Galleria mellonella) demonstrate significant potential in degrading polyethylene, contributing to plastic waste reduction."&lt;SEP&gt;"Galleria Mellonella larvae have been shown to harbor bacteria capable of degrading polyethylene, establishing a connection between the organism and the plastic."&lt;SEP&gt;"Galleria mellonella larvae interact with polyethylene, creating holes and contributing to its degradation through chewing and ingestion."&lt;SEP&gt;"Galleria mellonella larvae exhibit the ability to biodegrade polyethylene, showcasing a clear relationship between the insect and the plastic."&lt;SEP&gt;"Galleria mellonella larvae metabolize polyethylene, demonstrating their potential in plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Galleria mellonella larvae degrade polyethylene using enzymes present in their saliva, highlighting the potential of biological solutions for plastic waste management."&lt;SEP&gt;"Galleria mellonella larvae exhibit the ability to metabolize polyethylene, contributing to plastic waste management."&lt;SEP&gt;"Galleria mellonella caterpillars have the ability to biodegrade polyethylene, highlighting their role in plastic waste management."&lt;SEP&gt;"Galleria mellonella caterpillars have been shown to bio-degrade polyethylene, establishing a direct relationship between the two entities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Galleria mellonella larvae consume and degrade polyethylene, demonstrating a significant biological relationship."&lt;SEP&gt;"Galleria mellonella larvae possess the ability to bio-degrade polyethylene, highlighting the potential of biological methods for plastic waste management."&lt;SEP&gt;"Galleria mellonella demonstrates the ability to degrade polyethylene through enzymatic activity within its gut microbiota."&lt;SEP&gt;"Galleria mellonella has demonstrated the ability to bio-degrade polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Galleria mellonella caterpillars exhibit the ability to bio-degrade polyethylene, showcasing their potential in plastic waste management."</data>
