      <data key="d3">63.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"PET provides energy and carbon sources for T. molitor larvae, enabling their survival and growth."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. molitor larvae actively consumed PET microplastics, indicating their ability to digest or biodegrade this polymer as an energy source."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. molitor larvae degrade PET with much higher efficiency compared to other persistent plastics like PS and PE."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. molitor larvae demonstrate the ability to decompose PET polymers, suggesting enzymatic mechanisms for polymer breakdown."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. molitor larvae are fed PET polymers, leading to shifts in their gut microbiota composition and increased potential for PET degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. molitor larvae consume and metabolize PET, demonstrating a significant PET degradation rate and efficiency."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. molitor larvae degrade PET through enzymatic and microbial activities, influenced by molecular weight and other factors."</data>
