      <data key="d5">"energy management, metabolic balance"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;RESERVES&quot;" target="&quot;FEEDING RATE (\(F\))&quot;">
      <data key="d3">4.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Feeding rate determines the influx of energy into the system, directly impacting reserve accumulation and utilization."</data>
      <data key="d5">"dietary input, energy storage"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;STRUCTURAL LENGTH&quot;" target="&quot;VON BERTALANFFY GROWTH RATE&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The Von Bertalanffy growth rate governs changes in structural length over time, as described by the simplified DEB model equations."</data>
      <data key="d5">"growth dynamics, mathematical relationship"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;VON BERTALANFFY GROWTH RATE&quot;" target="&quot;MAXIMUM BODY LENGTH (\(L_M\))&quot;">
      <data key="d3">6.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Maximum body length is related to the Von Bertalanffy growth rate through specific parameters derived from the DEB model."</data>
      <data key="d5">"parameter interdependence, growth prediction"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;VON BERTALANFFY GROWTH RATE&quot;" target="&quot;GROWTH RATE PARAMETER (\(\DOT{K}_M\))&quot;">
      <data key="d3">6.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Growth rate parameter directly contributes to the calculation of Von Bertalanffy growth rate, linking metabolic efficiency with physical growth."</data>
      <data key="d5">"growth efficiency, metabolic interdependence"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;ENERGY CONDUCTANCE (\(G\))&quot;" target="&quot;RESERVE ALLOCATION RATE (\(\DOT{R}\))&quot;">
      <data key="d3">5.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Energy conductance affects how reserves are allocated, influencing both growth and reproduction rates."</data>
      <data key="d5">"resource distribution, biological prioritization"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;PS + OAT. + VIT.&quot;" target="&quot;VITAMINS AND MINERALS&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Vitamins and minerals are added to the PS + oat. + vit. diet, enhancing its nutritional value."</data>
      <data key="d5">"nutritional enhancement, dietary enrichment"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;\( L \)&quot;" target="&quot;\( L_V \)&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"\( L_V \) is related to \( L \) as it represents volumetric body length based on structural body length."</data>
      <data key="d5">"physical characteristics, body dimensions"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;\( L \)&quot;" target="&quot;\( L_W \)&quot;">
      <data key="d3">6.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"\( L_w \) represents physical body length, which is linked to structural body length \( L \)."</data>
      <data key="d5">"physical features, body dimensions"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;\( L_E \)&quot;" target="&quot;\( E \)&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"\( L_E \) relates to scaled reserve density \( e \), indicating the volumetric length of reserves."</data>
      <data key="d5">"reserve dynamics, energy storage"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;\( E \)&quot;" target="&quot;\( \DOT{V} \)&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Energy conductance \( \dot{v} \) affects the amount of energy in reserve \( E \)."</data>
      <data key="d5">"energy transport, storage"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;\( E \)&quot;" target="&quot;\( L_{EM} \)&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The maximum volumetric length of reserve \( L_{Em} \) relates to the energy in reserve \( E \)."</data>
      <data key="d5">"reserve dynamics, energy storage"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;\( [E_R] \)&quot;" target="&quot;\( E_0 \)&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The energy content of a single egg \( E_0 \) is connected to the energy density threshold for pupation \( [E_R] \)."</data>
      <data key="d5">"reproductive biology, developmental stages"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;\( F \)&quot;" target="&quot;\( R \)&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The scaled functional response \( f \) influences the reproduction rate \( R \)."</data>
      <data key="d5">"biological function, reproductive dynamics"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;\( K_M \)&quot;" target="&quot;\( [P_M] \)&quot;">
      <data key="d3">6.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The somatic maintenance rate coefficient \( k_M \) relates to volume-specific somatic maintenance power \( [p_M] \)."</data>
      <data key="d5">"maintenance processes, energy usage"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;\( G \)&quot;" target="&quot;\( \KAPPA \)&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The energy investment ratio \( g \) influences the fraction of mobilized reserves \( \kappa \)."</data>
      <data key="d5">"energy allocation, biological processes"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;\( L_{S0} \)&quot;" target="&quot;\( L_{SURVIVE} \)&quot;">
      <data key="d3">6.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The structural body length at the beginning of starvation \( L_{S0} \) correlates with the critical survival length \( L_{survive} \)."</data>
      <data key="d5">"starvation effects, survival thresholds"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;\( [E_C] \)&quot;" target="&quot;\( [E_M] \)&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The volume-specific costs for structure \( [E_c] \) are related to the maximum reserve density \( [E_m] \)."</data>
      <data key="d5">"structural costs, energy management"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;L_V&quot;" target="&quot;E(T)&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The volumetric length (L_V) decreases due to changes in scaled reserve density (e(t)) during starvation, reflecting the interdependence between structural preservation and energy reserves."</data>
      <data key="d5">"energy dynamics, metabolic adaptation"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-998b63e5349034d477c2087c139669ed</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;F&quot;" target="&quot;P_M&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Decreased food availability (f) can lead to increased somatic and maturity maintenance costs (p_M), reflecting the organism's response to environmental stress."</data>
      <data key="d5">"nutritional stress, maintenance costs"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;F&quot;" target="&quot;Κ&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Changes in κ may occur due to decreased food availability (f), altering energy allocation strategies under starvation conditions."</data>
      <data key="d5">"energy allocation, starvation"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;L^3&quot;" target="&quot;E_R&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Structural volume (L^3) influences the energy invested into the reproduction buffer (E_R), highlighting the trade-off between growth and reproduction."</data>
      <data key="d5">"energy partitioning, developmental trade-offs"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-998b63e5349034d477c2087c139669ed</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;E_R&quot;" target="&quot;R_S&quot;">
      <data key="d3">10.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The energy content of the reproduction buffer (E_R) directly affects the normalized reproduction buffer density (R_S), linking energy storage with reproductive readiness."</data>
      <data key="d5">"reproductive readiness, energy thresholds"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-998b63e5349034d477c2087c139669ed</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;E_0&quot;" target="&quot;E_I&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"E_0 is used to calculate the number of eggs but does not affect the energy stored in the reproduction buffer, indicating its role in quantifying reproductive output without influencing energy dynamics."</data>
      <data key="d5">"calculation, energy storage"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;R_S&quot;" target="&quot;E_I&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"R_S is scaled by E_I, showing the proportion of reproduction energy relative to the total possible energy for egg production during the imago stage."</data>
      <data key="d5">"reproductive scaling, energy"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;E_R(T)&quot;" target="&quot;E_T&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"E_R(t) represents the dynamic energy available for reproduction over time, while E_T is the fixed threshold needed for pupation, indicating a relationship between energy accumulation and developmental transitions."</data>
      <data key="d5">"biological process, threshold"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;E_R(T)&quot;" target="&quot;JAGER AND ZIMMER&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Jager and Zimmer's work involves the derivation of equations related to E_R(t), the reproduction buffer density over time."</data>
      <data key="d5">"research contribution, energy dynamics"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;E_T&quot;" target="&quot;LLANDRES ET AL.&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Llandres et al. described E_T, the reproduction buffer density threshold for pupation, contributing to understanding developmental transitions."</data>
      <data key="d5">"threshold determination, biological process"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;P(T)&quot;" target="&quot;RITZ&quot;">
      <data key="d3">10.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Ritz's log-logistic model is applied to describe P(t), the probability of achieving the reproduction buffer density threshold over time."</data>
      <data key="d5">"model application, probability"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;P(T)&quot;" target="&quot;SIGMOIDAL DISTRIBUTION CURVE&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The sigmoidal distribution curve models P(t), describing the accumulation of pupae over time with a characteristic S-shape."</data>
      <data key="d5">"mathematical modeling, biological process"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;Τ&quot;" target="&quot;INFLECTION POINT&quot;">
      <data key="d3">10.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The inflection point τ represents the most likely time of pupation, crucial for estimating developmental transitions."</data>
      <data key="d5">"mathematical concept, biological timing"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;P_M&quot;" target="&quot;E_C&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Increased p_M can be accompanied by increased E_C, indicating a broader impact of toxicity on metabolic costs."</data>
      <data key="d5">"toxicity, metabolic costs"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;P_M&quot;" target="&quot;SOMATIC MAINTENANCE&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Somatic maintenance costs are represented by p_M, indicating the energy required to maintain body structures and functions."</data>
      <data key="d5">"biological function, maintenance cost"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;E_C&quot;" target="&quot;TOXICITY OF PS&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The toxicity of PS affects E_C, the costs for structure and maintenance, highlighting the broader metabolic impacts of dietary toxins."</data>
      <data key="d5">"toxicity, metabolic cost"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;Κ&quot;" target="&quot;KOOIJMAN&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Kooijman's work focuses on the kappa parameter, which determines energy allocation strategies under starvation conditions."</data>
      <data key="d5">"energy allocation, starvation response"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SOMATIC MAINTENANCE&quot;" target="&quot;RESERVE DENSITY&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Somatic maintenance depends on sufficient reserve density to ensure larval survival and proper functioning."</data>
      <data key="d5">"energy expenditure, metabolic balance"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-5740f0973ff804cae61f6fc12f3e3753</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;ISOMORPHIC GROWTH&quot;" target="&quot;SHAPE COEFFICIENT&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The shape coefficient supports the concept of isomorphic growth, indicating consistent growth patterns in mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d5">"growth pattern, physical characteristic"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-5740f0973ff804cae61f6fc12f3e3753</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;RESERVE DENSITY&quot;" target="&quot;INEQUALITY (18)&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Inequality (18) evaluates whether reserve density meets the energetic demands for somatic maintenance."</data>
      <data key="d5">"mathematical modeling, biological constraint"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-5740f0973ff804cae61f6fc12f3e3753</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;RESERVE DENSITY&quot;" target="&quot;VOLUMETRIC LENGTH&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Decreased volumetric length correlates with reduced reserve density, indicating energy depletion during starvation."</data>
      <data key="d5">"metabolic response, structural change"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;INEQUALITY (18)&quot;" target="&quot;SCALED RESERVE DENSITY E(T)&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Inequality (18) determines whether the Scaled Reserve Density e(t) is sufficient for somatic maintenance and reproduction."</data>
      <data key="d5">"biological criterion, metabolic dependency"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-9a97d5b092508f2e837932274d6b3282</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SCALED RESERVE DENSITY E(T)&quot;" target="&quot;REPRODUCTION RATE R&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Decreased Scaled Reserve Density e(t) causes a reduction in Reproduction Rate R, impacting pupation."</data>
      <data key="d5">"metabolic correlation, reproductive limitation"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-9a97d5b092508f2e837932274d6b3282</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;FOOD AVAILABILITY&quot;" target="&quot;MOULT RESIDUES&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Moult residues contribute minimally to food availability during starvation, serving as an inadequate nutritional source."</data>
      <data key="d5">"nutritional contribution, survival strategies"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;FOOD AVAILABILITY&quot;" target="&quot;DROPPINGS&quot;">
      <data key="d3">6.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Droppings provide limited nutrition during starvation, insufficient to sustain larval growth and survival."</data>
      <data key="d5">"waste utilization, energy limitation"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;PS + OAT. GROUP&quot;" target="&quot;PS + OAT. + VIT. GROUP&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Both groups show similar outcomes despite vitamin supplementation, indicating that the diet remains insufficient for full recovery."</data>
      <data key="d5">"dietary sufficiency, physiological response"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;L_IM&quot;" target="&quot;R̂&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"A decrease in L_Im correlates with changes in R̂, suggesting that reduced growth impacts reproductive potential."</data>
      <data key="d5">"growth-reproduction tradeoff"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-f71fddc259d51158d5c79f38bf41523f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;R_B̂&quot;" target="&quot;P_M̂&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"An increase in p_M̂ would theoretically increase r_B̂, but this was not observed, implying other factors dominate physiological responses."</data>
      <data key="d5">"energy allocation"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-f71fddc259d51158d5c79f38bf41523f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;POLYSTYRENE (PS)&lt;&quot;|&gt;&quot;PS-FED LARVAE&quot;" target="&quot;POLYSTYRENE IS USED AS A NOVEL FEEDING SUBSTRATE TO STUDY ITS IMPACT ON LARVAL GROWTH AND DEVELOPMENT.&quot;">
      <data key="d3">2.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"novel diet, experimental variation"</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;\( R \)&quot;" target="&quot;\( \DOT{R}_M \)&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The maximum reproduction rate \( \dot{R}_m \) is linked to the reproduction rate \( R \)."</data>
      <data key="d5">"reproductive capacity, biological rates"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;\( L_0 \)&quot;" target="&quot;\( L_M(E) \)&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The maximum structural body length \( L_m(e) \) is related to the initial structural length \( L_0 \)."</data>
      <data key="d5">"growth patterns, structural development"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </edge>
  </graph>
